ME3","text":"Historia personalis ultra memoriam dilatatur, quia testimonium, analogia et dependentia ontologica partes identitatis fiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ME4","text":"Infantia ex regione innocentiae in formam initialem earumdem inordinationum quae societatem adultam regunt reclassificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ME5","text":"Educatio ex simplici transmissione scientiae in machinam mixtam facultatum utilium, coercitionis, gloriae et reproductionis moralis redescribitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ME6","text":"Lingua in instrumentum bonum et materiam variabiliter ordinatam dividitur; medium a turpitudine contenti separatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ME7","text":"Aestimatio actionis bifurcatur inter intentionem agentis et effectum a providentia ad utilitatem ordinatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ME8","text":"Dilatio baptismi ex prudentia pastorali in structuram possibilis licentiae peccandi denuo describitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ALT1","text":"Surface — Precatio, confessio originum, infantiae et pueritiae atque iudicium de studiis constituunt obiectum immediatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ALT2","text":"Structural — Familia, schola, conventiones linguae, disciplina, praemia socialia et praxis baptismalis appetitus atque facultates ordinant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Textus normas aestimationis ab honore, eloquentia et consuetudine ad conscientiam, ordinem amoris et usum donorum transfert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Subiectum creatum, in Deo contentum et per tempus mutabile sub aeterno Dei hodie persistit, quamvis sui principia memoria non teneat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT1","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad motum a theologia invocationis ad confessionem autobiographicam, criticam institutionis et conversionem facultatum restituendum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT2","text":"Cohaerentia systematis innititur distinctionibus inter creatorem et ordinatorem peccati, donum et abusum, intentionem et effectum, signum et materiam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT3","text":"Structura firmissima est ubi omnia bona ad Deum referuntur, peccatum autem ut ordinatio affectus ad creaturas definitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT4","text":"Relatio exacta inter cognitionem, invocationem et fidem interrogationibus aperitur et mediatione fidei solvitur operationaliter, non demonstratione epistemica completa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0003","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0004","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT5","text":"Iudicium de peccato infantili testimonio doctrinali, observatione aliorum infantium et analogia cum vita adulta nititur, non memoria directa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT6","text":"Commissura inter providentiam et culpam fragilis manet, quia Deus ex actibus pravis bonum elicit sine explicatione completa causalitatis concurrentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT7","text":"Critica scholae ab exemplis grammaticae et litterarum ad totum flumen moris humani transit, antithesi morali magis quam analysi institutionali exhaustiva sustentata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT8","text":"Aestimatio dilationis baptismi insoluta manet inter prudentiam matris de futuris tentationibus et analogiam sanitatis quae celerem mundationem postulat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0045","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT9","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat: a Deo ut principio per reconstructionem sui peccatoris ad dona recuperanda et in Deum finaliter ordinanda.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T141753642572Z_bc4660d4","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"BOOK ONE.","source_sha256":"d2efcc83225f47fbd20db3a607b387c9091a36ba0546d85c27aa22bc123c1baa","sha256":"6a35c69a52a2e9e085b9827ccbd6621500dd0ec5b172b5f76d666abcd6bf64bc","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:17:53.644111+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS1","text":"The text asks how a mortal human being, a sinner lacking memory of his own beginnings, can invoke, know, and praise God, while also truthfully confessing his life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS2","text":"The governing assertion is that all being and good are given by God, whereas sin arises from the disordered use of goods, until the heart returns to God and rests in him.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS3","text":"The argumentation is at once metaphysical, confessional, diagnostic, polemical, and reconstructive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS4","text":"The initial movement proceeds from the desire for praise through the circle of faith, invocation, and knowledge to the distinction between divine presence and spatial containment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS5","text":"The autobiographical movement proceeds from the absence of memory through testimony and analogy to the detection of sin in infancy and its continuation in adult life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS6","text":"The critical movement proceeds from childhood discipline to the structure of human custom, then to the distinction between good gifts, perverse uses, and providence, which orders even errors toward good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:A1","text":"All created being, life, and good are from God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:A2","text":"God fills all things by containing them, is wholly everywhere, and is not wholly contained by any thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:A3","text":"God, by immutable presence, contains all transitory time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:A4","text":"The human being is made for God and remains restless until he rests in God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:A5","text":"Invocation, which leads to knowledge and praise, begins from faith given by God, mediated through the Son and preaching.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:A6","text":"The human being, bearing mortality and sin, does not contend with God in judgment, but accuses himself under mercy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:A7","text":"God is the creator of natural things, but the orderer, not the author, of sins.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:A8","text":"Sin consists in seeking pleasure, sublimity, and truth in creatures while abandoning God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0078","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:A9","text":"The disordered mind is its own punishment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:A10","text":"God can use human errors and wicked intentions for the benefit of another without approving those acts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:A11","text":"Life prior to memory is known through testimony, analogy, and conjecture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:A12","text":"The weakness of an infant body does not establish the innocence of an infant mind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:A13","text":"Linguistic signs rest upon human convention and are learned from contextually repeated use.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:A14","text":"Created words and faculties remain good instruments, whose moral character depends on matter and use.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:A15","text":"Free curiosity for learning is more efficacious than fearful necessity, although necessity can restrain its course under law.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:A16","text":"Schooling establishes an order of values in which honor, wealth, and correctness of speech are preferred to divine commands.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:A17","text":"In the narrative, baptism is understood as salvific cleansing and remission of sins.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:A18","text":"The reported counsel delayed baptism because offenses after the washing were thought more serious and dangerous.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX1","text":"A creature is not the maker of its own being, life, or faculties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX2","text":"God is not introduced into the soul or the world as into an empty place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX3","text":"God is not distributed among creatures into greater and lesser parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0010","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX4","text":"God is not renewed by time, does not grow old, does not lack, nor does he change his counsel through changes in works.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX5","text":"Human speech cannot comprehend God, but silence about God is not thereby justified.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX6","text":"Infancy is not innocent because of the weakness of its limbs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX7","text":"A vice tolerated because it will perish with age does not thereby become good or slight.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX8","text":"An involuntary act does not become morally good merely from the goodness of the thing effected through it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX9","text":"The usefulness of discipline does not absolve the perversity of the teachers' intention.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX10","text":"Words are not accused as though they were the cause of error, nor are shameful tales necessary for learning words.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX11","text":"Grammatical correctness does not constitute rectitude of mind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0072","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX12","text":"Departure from God and return to him are not local motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX13","text":"The delay of baptism does not, from the intention of prudence alone, produce a certain benefit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0045","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:D1","text":"The circle between knowledge and invocation is opened not by perfect knowledge, but by antecedently given faith.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:D2","text":"A creature does not receive God as a vessel does, but itself exists because it is sustained by God and contained in him.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:D3","text":"Distance from God is the ordering of affection toward creatures, not spatial distance.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:D4","text":"Praise of God and self-accusation constitute one act of confession, because goodness is referred to the creator, while defect is referred to disordered will.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:D5","text":"Autobiographical identity extends beyond memory, because the same subject lived from God even in the time it cannot recall.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:D6","text":"Infantile desire displays the same form of disorder later unfolded in cupidity, envy, and domination.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:D7","text":"The difference between the vices of children and adults is principally a difference of instruments, rewards, and punishments, not of affective form.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0075","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:D8","text":"Scholastic coercion can produce useful knowledge, although neither the unwilling learner nor those compelling him thereby act well.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:D9","text":"Literary education is corrupted not through the signs themselves, but when good instruments serve fictions, lust, and glory.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:D10","text":"Socially enforced compacts of sounds can coexist with neglect of the divine covenant; knowledge of speech therefore does not entail conscience.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:D11","text":"The faculties of memory, speech, reading, and counting can be redirected toward God, because their goodness is not destroyed by perverse use.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:D12","text":"The delay of baptism can generate moral license before the washing, although maternal counsel intends to avoid the danger of future sins.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:D13","text":"The communication of signs makes inner will expressible and at the same time inserts the child into the authority of parents and elders.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD1","text":"Confession itself is an effect of providence, because the subject seeks God and states his errors through faith, memory, and language, all of which he has received.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD2","text":"Evil is not a created substance, but a disordering of goods, whose effects God orders without being the author of that same disordering.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD3","text":"The autobiographical person is founded not on memory alone, but on ontological continuity, social testimony, and the order of time under divine eternity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD4","text":"Infancy contains the microstructure of adult society: the desire for domination, rivalry, and injustice remain, while objects and powers increase.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBP:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD5","text":"Cultural education reproduces sin when it turns formal excellence into glory and tolerates or rewards ornately expressed vice.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBP:D9","CH_5P0L_LIBP:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD6","text":"The correction of education requires not the abolition of letters, but the conversion of linguistic faculties from vanity to truth and praise.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD7","text":"The counsel to defer the sacrament can establish a structure of permission to sin, although it arises from maternal providence and fear of future guilt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A18","CH_5P0L_LIBP:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD8","text":"Human responsibility is judged from the end of affection, while the usefulness of effects is referred to providence; intention and effect are therefore imputed on different grounds.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX1","text":"The system requires the falsity of evil as a thing created by God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX2","text":"The system does not admit that the subject is its own principle, possessor, or savior.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX3","text":"The goodness of an effect cannot prove the goodness of the intention or agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX4","text":"Social praise cannot be an index of truth or moral rectitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX5","text":"Infancy cannot constitute a morally exempt space.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX6","text":"Exhaustive memory is not a condition of personal identity or confession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX7","text":"Language in itself neither corrupts nor saves; the ordering of use renders judgment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX8","text":"Coercion cannot become morally good from the usefulness alone of the thing commanded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX9","text":"Education is not neutral, because it always directs faculties toward some order of love, honor, and truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:SNX1","text":"Speech adequate to God is unavailable, but absolute silence remains equally inadmissible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:SNX2","text":"No space outside God is given from which God may be called or to which the human being may depart; all alienation occurs within ontological dependence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:SNX3","text":"No innocent personal origin can be recovered by memory; the question of the beginning is already constituted under sin and forgetfulness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:SNX4","text":"Human custom cannot claim ultimate authority for itself, because its linguistic compacts are judged under the covenant of salvation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0071","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:SNX5","text":"Autonomous return is excluded: awakening, faith, invocation, faculties, and healing come from him to whom the human being returns.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:SNX6","text":"No neutral causal medium is provided in which divine providence and human guilt are exhaustively reconciled; the distinction operates without a complete mechanism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:FGS1","text":"The epistemic series is: preaching and the gift of faith → invocation → seeking → finding and knowledge → praise → rest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:FGS2","text":"The ontological schema is: God gives being → the creature is contained in God → God is not received spatially → divine presence coheres with incomprehensibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:FGS3","text":"The autobiographical schema is: lack of memory → testimony and analogy → reconstruction of infancy → detection of disorder → its continuation into later ages.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:FGS4","text":"The schema of sin is: good faculty → love of creature with abandonment of creator → disordered act → immanent punishment → confession under mercy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:FGS5","text":"The institutional schema is: useful signs → coercion and social reward → eloquence ordered toward glory → formally adorned vice → neglect of conscience.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:FGS6","text":"The schema of providence is: wicked human intention → mixed effect → divine appropriation for benefit → distinction between gift and abuse → conversion of faculties toward God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:FGS7","text":"The baptismal schema is: danger of death → request for cleansing → recovery of the body → delay owing to future guilt → implicit permission to sin → unresolved question of prudence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:AF1","text":"Desire for praise → circle of invocation and knowledge → antecedent faith → non-spatial presence of God → confession under mercy → diagnosis of disordered love → reorientation toward rest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:AF2","text":"Forgetfulness of origin → testimony about infancy → denial of innocence → schoolboyhood → inversion of cultural values → continuation of vices in adult life → recovery of gifts for divine use.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:AF3","text":"Baptism requested → cleansing delayed → reason of future danger → analogy of bodily wound → detection of license before the sacrament → final judgment suspended.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ME1","text":"The relation of God and world is transferred from a spatial map of container and contained to a map of ontological dependence and affective distance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ME2","text":"Praise of God and confession of sin are reduced from separate acts to one act of right attribution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ME3","text":"Personal history is extended beyond memory, because testimony, analogy, and ontological dependence become parts of identity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ME4","text":"Infancy is reclassified from a region of innocence into an initial form of the same disorders governing adult society.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ME5","text":"Education is redescribed from mere transmission of knowledge into a mixed machine of useful faculties, coercion, glory, and moral reproduction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ME6","text":"Language is divided into a good instrument and variably ordered matter; the medium is separated from the baseness of content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ME7","text":"The assessment of action bifurcates between the agent's intention and the effect ordered to benefit by providence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ME8","text":"The delay of baptism is redescribed from pastoral prudence into a structure of possible permission to sin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ALT1","text":"Surface — Prayer, confession of origins, infancy and childhood, and judgment concerning studies constitute the immediate object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ALT2","text":"Structural — Family, school, conventions of language, discipline, social rewards, and baptismal practice order desires and faculties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The text transfers norms of assessment from honor, eloquence, and custom to conscience, the order of love, and the use of gifts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The created subject, contained in God and mutable through time, persists under God's eternal today, although memory does not retain its own beginnings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement from the theology of invocation to autobiographical confession, critique of education, and conversion of faculties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT2","text":"The coherence of the system rests on distinctions between creator and orderer of sin, gift and abuse, intention and effect, sign and matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT3","text":"The structure is strongest where all goods are referred to God, while sin is defined as the ordering of affection toward creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT4","text":"The precise relation between knowledge, invocation, and faith is opened by questions and resolved operationally through the mediation of faith, not by complete epistemic demonstration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0003","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0004","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT5","text":"Judgment concerning infantile sin rests on doctrinal testimony, observation of other infants, and analogy with adult life, not on direct memory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT6","text":"The juncture between providence and guilt remains fragile, because God elicits good from wicked acts without a complete explanation of concurrent causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT7","text":"The critique of school passes from examples of grammar and literature to the whole current of human custom, supported more by moral antithesis than by exhaustive institutional analysis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT8","text":"The assessment of delaying baptism remains unresolved between a mother's prudence concerning future temptations and the analogy of health, which demands prompt cleansing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0045","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: from God as principle, through reconstruction of the sinful self, toward gifts to be recovered and finally ordered to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBP:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LIBP@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_5P0L_LIBP:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 01","title":"Book I.","context":"Chapter 01","original_title":"Liber Primus.","original_context":"Chapter 01"},"original_title":"Liber Primus.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS","layer":"CH","title":"Book II.","order":2,"parents":["RAW_5P0L_LIBS"],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LIBS@R001","sha256":"53fae835fcd11b94935b38920ac534ff97ebad1972a840dd26026e0dcb577ba6","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS1","text":"Textus quaerit cur furtum perpetratum delectaverit, cum neque necessitas neque fructus neque ipsa res furtiva causam delectationis praebeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS2","text":"Adolescentia non ut series actuum discretorum, sed ut dispersio animi ab uno bono in multitudinem concupiscentiarum constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS3","text":"Argumentatio a causis ordinariis peccati per bona inferiora appetitis procedit ad furtum, quod causam utilitariam eludit et malitiam ipsam quaestionem facit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS4","text":"Furtum explicatur ut imitatio perversa libertatis divinae, intensificata consortio simul peccantium et pudore ne minus impudens videatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS5","text":"Recordatio criminis in confessionem convertitur, qua culpa et abstinentia aequaliter misericordiae divinae attribuuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A1","text":"Deus est summum, verum et stabile bonum, extra quod nulla delectatio pura aut secura invenitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A2","text":"Peccatum oritur cum anima bona inferiora immoderate appetit et bona superiora deserit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A3","text":"Omne vitium speciem alicuius boni, potestatis, pulchritudinis, quietis, scientiae vel societatis imitatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A4","text":"Imitatio vitiosa bonum non creat, sed perfectionem divinam in formam imminutam et perversam convertit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A5","text":"Anima a Deo aversa in multa diffluit et sibi ipsa fit regio egestatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A6","text":"Furtum piri nec egestate nec suavitate fructus nec utilitate rei causatum fuit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A7","text":"In furto quaesita est transgressio legis, quia transgressio ipsa illicitam libertatis speciem praebuit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A8","text":"Malitia gratuita non est bonum positivum, sed amor defectus, ruinae et aversionis a firmamento divino.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A9","text":"Consortio peccantium cupiditas accenditur, quia communis impudentia damnum alienum in ludum et laudem mutat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A10","text":"Disciplina litteraria et eloquentia, si cultura cordis et castitatis non comitantur, adolescentem a dispersione non servant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A11","text":"Deus etiam per correptionem amarumque eventum agit, ut delectationes illicitae ad se ipsum referantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A12","text":"Non solum peccata commissa, sed etiam peccata non commissa, gratiae et misericordiae divinae imputanda sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX1","text":"Furtum non definitur appetitu pomorum, quia poma abundabant, meliora aderant, et rapina ad usum non ordinabatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX2","text":"Peccatum non est creatio boni autonomi, sed defectus boni et perversio boni creati.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX3","text":"Libertatem non efficit licentia faciendi quod non licet, quia talis licentia est captiva umbra omnipotentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX4","text":"Amicitia non est vera unitas, si societas eius in laetitia nocendi et in contagione turpitudinis consistit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX5","text":"Castitas et innocentia non sunt possessiones quas homo suis viribus sibi tribuere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX6","text":"Silentium divinum non est absentia divina, cum monitus matris et flagella vitae eandem vocem divinam mediantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX7","text":"Studium, honor domesticus et spes socialis non sufficiunt ad rectam formationem, si ad Deum et veritatem non referuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:D1","text":"Cum bona inferiora sint realiter bona sed non suprema, peccatum non res pulchras destruit, sed ordinem amoris dissolvit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:D2","text":"Furtum piri fit probatio extrema, quia ostendit voluntatem posse non rem appetere, sed statum contra legem se ponendi.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:D3","text":"Illicita voluptas libertatis ex eo nascitur quod anima, Deo subiecta, dominum suum fugere et potentiam sine potestate imitari conatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:D4","text":"Consortium non est tantum circumstantia exterior actus, sed causa formalis delectationis, quando solitarius actus idem non placeret.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:D5","text":"Pudor socialis invertitur: innocentia dedecus videtur, turpitudo gloria, et mendacium ad imitationem pravitatis adiungitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:D6","text":"Correctio divina non peccatum approbat, sed voluptatem illicitam amaritudine vulnerat, ut desiderium suum falsum agnoscat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:D7","text":"Recordatio peccati recte ordinata non ad amorem turpitudinis, sed ad amorem Dei et ad recollectionem animi dispersi tendit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:D8","text":"Qui minus graviter peccavit non minus misericordiae debitor est, quia etiam imminutio morbi a medico divino procedit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD1","text":"Ordo moralis non dividitur inter res bonas et res malas, sed inter amorem ordinate relatum ad summum bonum et amorem inferiorum bonorum absolutum.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD2","text":"Malum radicale non describitur ut substantia rivalis Deo, sed ut imminutio ontologica quae tamen voluntatem, societatem et memoriam efficaciter deformat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD3","text":"Societas prava potest mechanismum conversionis valorum efficere, quo damnum alienum, legis transgressio et simulatio turpitudinis in fontes honoris mutantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD4","text":"Confessio reordinat causalitatem moralem: agens culpam actuum propriorum retinet, sed liberationem et abstinentiam gratiae attribuit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD5","text":"Nulla aversio a Deo est absoluta, quia ipsa imitatio perversa bonorum divinorum persistentem dependentiam creaturae a creatore indicat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet exemplar quod peccatum ad ignorantiam rerum, ad necessitatem materialem vel ad calculum utilitatis redigit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet exemplar libertatis quod transgressionem legis pro actu sui-fundante accipit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet exemplar societatis quod consortium per se bonum putat, sine discrimine finis quo socii uniuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet exemplar virtutis quod innocentiam humanam a gratia separabilem et sibi sufficientem habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse debet exemplar educationis quod eloquentiam, studium et ascensum socialem pro cultura interiori substituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX1","text":"Systema non admittit locum extra Deum unde anima bonum stabile, quietem certam aut libertatem veram sibi comparare possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX2","text":"Systema non admittit malitiam tamquam principium autonomum, quia etiam deformitas vitiorum formas bonorum divinorum parasitice supponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX3","text":"Systema non admittit memoriam moralem neutralem, quia recordatio aut in delectationem criminis recidit aut in confessionem et conversionem ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:FGS1","text":"Aversio ab uno bono → dispersio in bona multa → imminutio facultatis discernendi dilectionem a libidine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:FGS2","text":"Apparens bonum inferius → appetitus immoderatus → desertio boni superioris → peccatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:FGS3","text":"Furtum sine utilitate → exclusio causae materialis → inquisitio delectationis ipsius transgressionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:FGS4","text":"Transgressio → imitatio perversa potentiae → libertas mutila → servitus et defectus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:FGS5","text":"Consortium peccantium → mutua inflammatio cupiditatis → pudor innocentiae → consolidatio actus et simulatio turpitudinis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:FGS6","text":"Recordatio criminis → confessio infirmitatis → agnitio gratiae in peccatis commissis et evitatis → amor Dei recollectus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AF1","text":"Adolescentiae libido et dispersio animi → defectus disciplinae spiritualis et moderaminis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AF2","text":"Defectus moderaminis → furtum quod nullum commodum externum explicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AF3","text":"Furtum inexplicabile per rem furtivam → distinctio inter bona quae vitia imitari conantur et malitiam quae defectum amat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AF4","text":"Malitia ut imitatio perversa libertatis → inventio consortii peccantium ut motoris affectivi actus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AF5","text":"Consortium et culpa recognita → confessio misericordiae quae culpam non delet ex memoria sed eius sensum transformat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:ME1","text":"Peccatum reclassificatur non ut amor rei intrinsece malae, sed ut amor inferioris boni extra ordinem summi boni positus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:ME2","text":"Furtum reclassificatur ex delicto proprietatis in experimentum perversae libertatis et in affectum socialiter productum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:ME3","text":"Amicitia bifurcatur in unitatem animorum ordinatam ad bonum et consortium contagiosum ordinatum ad nocendum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:ME4","text":"Educatio bifurcatur in acquisitionem eloquentiae externa et culturam cordis, quarum prima sine altera insufficienter formativa est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:ME5","text":"Abstinentia reclassificatur ex merito privato in beneficium gratiae, sicut remissio actuum commissorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:ALT1","text":"Surface — Textus examinatur adolescentiam libidinosam, furtum piri, monita parentum et consortium sodalium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:ALT2","text":"Structural — Mechanismus peccati consistit in aversione a bono supremo, appetitu inferiorum bonorum et deformatione sociali pudoris atque laudis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Quaestio de actu singulari transferitur ad investigationem generis desiderii quod transgressionem, imitationem et consortium producit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Creatura a Deo aversa non ad alteram stabilitatem transit, sed in defectum, dispersionem et egestatem temporalem decidit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam necessitatem qua peccatum ex inordinato amore bonorum inferiorum oritur et ad Deum reditus exigitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT2","text":"Explicatio furti sustinetur solum si transgressio, imitatio perversae libertatis et consortium peccantium simul retinentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT3","text":"Firmissimum systematis nexum constituit distinctio inter bonum creatum, cuius species vera manet, et usum eius inordinatum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT4","text":"Tensionem relinquit enuntiatio malitiae gratuita, quia textus simul omne peccatum aliquo bono apparenti moveri et furtum malitiam ipsam appetere affirmat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT5","text":"Tensionem relinquit relatio inter culpam voluntatis et gratiam divinam, quia agens proprie peccat, sed etiam imminutio peccati beneficio divino tribuitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT6","text":"Tensionem relinquit usus matrimonii tamquam remedii libidinis, cum idem matrimonium in ordine familiae etiam impedimentum spei litterariae describatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT7","text":"Restitutio motum textus servat, si recordatio non pro mera narratione praeteriti, sed pro operatione qua dispersio in confessionem et amor Dei convertitur accipitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T141902214233Z_f199e11d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"BOOK TWO.","source_sha256":"53fae835fcd11b94935b38920ac534ff97ebad1972a840dd26026e0dcb577ba6","sha256":"e8d4b418e82b14abb0a9fdceafcf0b5eef2c23fdc60c2a3d8b4f69a3c52dc34f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:19:02.216756+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS1","text":"The text asks why the committed theft delighted, when neither necessity nor gain nor the stolen thing itself supplied a cause of delight.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS2","text":"Adolescence is constituted not as a series of discrete acts, but as a dispersal of the soul from the one good into a multitude of desires.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS3","text":"The argument proceeds from the ordinary causes of sin through desired lower goods to theft, which evades a utilitarian cause and makes malice itself the question.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS4","text":"Theft is explained as a perverse imitation of divine freedom, intensified by the fellowship of those sinning together and by shame at appearing less shameless.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS5","text":"The recollection of the crime is converted into confession, by which guilt and abstinence alike are attributed to divine mercy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A1","text":"God is the highest, true, and stable good, apart from whom no pure or secure delight is found.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A2","text":"Sin arises when the soul immoderately desires lower goods and abandons higher goods.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A3","text":"Every vice imitates the appearance of some good, power, beauty, rest, knowledge, or fellowship.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A4","text":"Vicious imitation does not create good, but converts divine perfection into a diminished and perverse form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A5","text":"The soul turned away from God flows out into many things and becomes for itself a region of want.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A6","text":"The theft of the pear was caused neither by want, nor by the sweetness of the fruit, nor by the usefulness of the thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A7","text":"In theft, transgression of the law was sought, because transgression itself offered an illicit appearance of freedom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A8","text":"Gratuitous malice is not a positive good, but love of deficiency, ruin, and turning away from the divine foundation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A9","text":"In the fellowship of sinners, desire is inflamed, because shared shamelessness turns another's loss into sport and praise.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A10","text":"Literary training and eloquence, if they are not accompanied by cultivation of the heart and chastity, do not preserve the adolescent from dispersal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A11","text":"God acts even through correction and bitter outcome, so that illicit delights may be referred back to Himself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:A12","text":"Not only sins committed, but also sins not committed, must be attributed to divine grace and mercy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX1","text":"Theft is not defined by desire for the apples, because apples were abundant, better ones were present, and the robbery was not ordered to use.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0028","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX2","text":"Sin is not the creation of an autonomous good, but the privation of good and the perversion of created good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX3","text":"Freedom is not effected by the license to do what is not permitted, because such license is a captive shadow of omnipotence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX4","text":"Friendship is not true unity if its fellowship consists in the joy of harming and in the contagion of shamefulness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX5","text":"Chastity and innocence are not possessions that a human being can ascribe to himself by his own powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX6","text":"Divine silence is not divine absence, since a mother's warnings and the scourges of life mediate the same divine voice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX7","text":"Study, domestic honor, and social hope do not suffice for right formation if they are not referred to God and truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:D1","text":"Since lower goods are truly goods but not supreme, sin does not destroy beautiful things, but dissolves the order of love.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:D2","text":"The theft of the pear becomes an extreme test, because it shows that the will may desire not a thing, but the state of setting itself against the law.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:D3","text":"The illicit pleasure of freedom arises from this: that the soul, subject to God, attempts to flee its lord and to imitate power without authority.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:D4","text":"Fellowship is not merely an external circumstance of the act, but a formal cause of delight, when the same act would not please one acting alone.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:D5","text":"Social shame is inverted: innocence seems disgraceful, shamefulness glorious, and lying is added for the imitation of depravity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:D6","text":"Divine correction does not approve sin, but wounds illicit pleasure with bitterness, so that it may recognize its false desire.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:D7","text":"The rightly ordered recollection of sin tends not toward love of shamefulness, but toward love of God and the recollection of the dispersed soul.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:D8","text":"One who has sinned less gravely is no less a debtor to mercy, because even the diminution of sickness proceeds from the divine physician.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD1","text":"The moral order is not divided between good things and bad things, but between love ordered in relation to the highest good and absolute love of lower goods.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD2","text":"Radical evil is not described as a substance rival to God, but as an ontological diminution that nevertheless effectively deforms will, fellowship, and memory.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD3","text":"A depraved fellowship can effect a mechanism of value-conversion, by which another's loss, transgression of the law, and feigning of shamefulness are changed into sources of honor.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD4","text":"Confession reorders moral causality: the agent retains the guilt of his own acts, but attributes liberation and abstinence to grace.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD5","text":"No turning away from God is absolute, because even the perverse imitation of divine goods indicates the creature's enduring dependence upon the Creator.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:DNX1","text":"Any model that reduces sin to ignorance of things, material necessity, or a calculation of utility must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:DNX2","text":"Any model of freedom that takes transgression of the law as a self-founding act must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:DNX3","text":"Any model of fellowship that considers association good in itself, without distinguishing the end by which companions are united, must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:DNX4","text":"Any model of virtue that regards human innocence as separable from grace and self-sufficient must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:DNX5","text":"Any model of education that substitutes eloquence, study, and social ascent for inner cultivation must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX1","text":"The system admits no place outside God from which the soul could procure for itself stable good, certain rest, or true freedom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX2","text":"The system admits no malice as an autonomous principle, because even the deformity of vices parasitically presupposes forms of divine goods.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX3","text":"The system admits no neutral moral memory, because recollection either falls back into delight in crime or is ordered toward confession and conversion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:FGS1","text":"Turning away from the one good → dispersal into many goods → diminution of the capacity to distinguish love from lust.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:FGS2","text":"Apparent lower good → immoderate desire → abandonment of higher good → sin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:FGS3","text":"Theft without utility → exclusion of material cause → inquiry into the delight of transgression itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:FGS4","text":"Transgression → perverse imitation of power → mutilated freedom → servitude and deficiency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:FGS5","text":"Fellowship of sinners → mutual inflaming of desire → shame at innocence → consolidation of the act and feigning of shamefulness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:FGS6","text":"Recollection of crime → confession of weakness → recognition of grace in sins committed and avoided → recollected love of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AF1","text":"Adolescent lust and dispersal of soul → lack of spiritual discipline and restraint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AF2","text":"Lack of restraint → theft that no external advantage explains.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AF3","text":"Theft inexplicable through the stolen thing → distinction between goods that vices attempt to imitate and malice that loves deficiency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AF4","text":"Malice as a perverse imitation of freedom → discovery of the fellowship of sinners as the affective motor of the act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:AF5","text":"Fellowship and recognized guilt → confession of mercy that does not erase guilt from memory but transforms its meaning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:ME1","text":"Sin is reclassified not as love of a thing intrinsically evil, but as love of a lower good placed outside the order of the highest good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:ME2","text":"Theft is reclassified from an offense against property into an experiment in perverse freedom and a socially produced affect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:ME3","text":"Friendship bifurcates into a unity of souls ordered to the good and a contagious fellowship ordered to doing harm.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:ME4","text":"Education bifurcates into the acquisition of external eloquence and cultivation of the heart, the former of which is insufficiently formative without the latter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:ME5","text":"Abstinence is reclassified from private merit into a benefit of grace, just as is the remission of acts committed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text examines lustful adolescence, the theft of the pear, parental warnings, and the fellowship of companions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:ALT2","text":"Structural — The mechanism of sin consists in turning away from the highest good, the desire for lower goods, and the social deformation of shame and praise.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The question concerning a single act is transferred to an investigation of the kind of desire that produces transgression, imitation, and fellowship.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The creature turned away from God does not pass into another stability, but falls into deficiency, dispersal, and temporal want.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the necessity by which sin arises from the disordered love of lower goods and a return to God is required.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT2","text":"The explanation of the theft is sustained only if transgression, imitation of perverse freedom, and the fellowship of sinners are retained together.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT3","text":"The firmest link of the system is constituted by the distinction between created good, whose appearance remains true, and its disordered use.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT4","text":"The assertion of gratuitous malice leaves a tension, because the text simultaneously affirms that every sin is moved by some apparent good and that theft desires malice itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0020","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT5","text":"The relation between the guilt of the will and divine grace leaves a tension, because the agent properly sins, yet even the diminution of sin is attributed to divine benefit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT6","text":"The use of marriage as a remedy for lust leaves a tension, since the same marriage is also described, in the order of the family, as an impediment to literary hope.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0006","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the movement of the text if recollection is understood not as mere narration of the past, but as the operation by which dispersal is converted into confession and love of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBS:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LIBS@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_5P0L_LIBS:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 02","title":"Book II.","context":"Chapter 02","original_title":"Liber Secundus.","original_context":"Chapter 02"},"original_title":"Liber Secundus.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT","layer":"CH","title":"Book III.","order":3,"parents":["RAW_5P0L_LIBT"],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LIBT@R001","sha256":"3917f792d90af6b461a2bf901cb9a9d30d2d9bdb3ef63f8958acf46950645131","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS1","text":"Textus inquirit quomodo anima Deum nesciens appetat, appetitum in voluptates et errores convertat, atque ex ipsa aberratione ad veritatem praeparari possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS2","text":"Fames interior Dei, si non agnoscitur, amorem a creatore ad sensibilia, dolorem fictum, gloriam rhetoricam et doctrinam corpoream deflectit, quae animam non satiant sed exhauriunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS3","text":"Veritas affectu, consuetudine, specie facti aut nominibus sacris non mensuratur, sed Deo immutabili, ordine naturae et lege iustitiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS4","text":"Hortensius desiderium ab eloquentia ad sapientiam transfert, sed absentia nominis Christi et superbia adversus humilem Scripturam conversionem imperfectam relinquunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS5","text":"Reconstructio retrospectiva errores Manichaeorum dissolvit per Deum incorporeum, malum ut privationem boni, et iustitiam immutabilem quae diversa temporibus diversis distribuit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS6","text":"Misericordia divina ante confessionem operatur per poenas, excitationes intellectuales, preces Monnicae, somnium et correctionem prudenter dilatam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS7","text":"Argumentatio genealogica, diagnostica, polemica et reconstructiva ab effectibus amoris perversi ad causas ontologicas progreditur, deinde ad ordinem moralem et providentiam conversionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A1","text":"Deus est Veritas immutabilis, vita animarum et creator rectorque universi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2","text":"Anima, etiam sine desiderio conscio, Deo tamquam cibo incorruptibili indiget.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A3","text":"Bona creata amari possunt quia bona sunt, sed creatorem supplere nequeunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4","text":"Peccatum est conversio amoris a bono universali ad partem privatam immoderate possessam vel adhibitam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A5","text":"Misericordia vera miseriam auferri vult, non dolorem tamquam voluptatem retineri.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A6","text":"Malum non est substantia, sed privatio boni usque ad defectum essendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A7","text":"Deus est spiritus sine mole vel dimensionibus, totus ubique et nulli corpori aut animae creaturali idem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8","text":"Cognitio sensu corporis et phantasmate terminata Deum apprehendere nequit atque falsa infinita fabricatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A9","text":"Iustitia vera est lex Dei rectissima, ubique et semper eadem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","text":"Iustitia immutabilis diversa praecepta distribuit secundum tempora, regiones, officia et personas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A11","text":"Flagitia contra naturam semper damnanda sunt, violationes autem consuetudinum humanarum ex pacto civitatis vel gentis aestimantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A12","text":"Moralitas facti ex animo agentis, usu, tempore occulto et testimonio divino iudicatur, non ex sola specie externa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A13","text":"Praeceptum Dei, ut supremi rectoris, consuetudini et pacto humano praevalet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14","text":"Superbia intellectum a forma humili veritatis avertit et ad novitatem, eloquentiam atque apparentiam sapientiae inclinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A15","text":"Frequentia vocum veritatis et nominum divinorum praesentiam veritatis non praestat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16","text":"Misericordia divina confessionem antecedit atque etiam poena, mediatione et dilatione conversionem ordinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX1","text":"Intensitas amoris vel mutua fruitio corporalis bonitatem amoris non constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX2","text":"Dolor scenicis imaginibus excitatus misericordia non est, ubi nullum auxilium intenditur et dolor ipse delectat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX3","text":"Dolor aliquando approbari potest, sed numquam propter se amandus est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX4","text":"Humilitas stili Scripturae humilitatem vel indignitatem veritatis non significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX5","text":"Nomen philosophiae, veritatis, Christi aut Spiritus doctrinam veram per se non efficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX6","text":"Deus nec corpus, nec moles infinita, nec phantasma corporis, nec anima corporum est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX7","text":"Malum principium substantiale vel Deo coaeternum non est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX8","text":"Iustitia neque consuetudini locali reducitur neque uniformitatem praeceptorum per omnia tempora requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX9","text":"Similitudo externa facti peccatum aut iustitiam sine consideratione animi et temporis non probat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX10","text":"Peccatum Deum corrumpere non potest, nec fuga a Deo libertatem efficit; peccator se ipsum et societatem vulnerat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D1","text":"Fames Dei non agnita sensibilia tamquam alimenta quaerit; quia ea Deum supplere nequeunt, delectatio in maiorem inanitatem et dolorem transit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D2","text":"Theatrum misericordiam simulat, sed affectum in voluptatem doloris claudit quia spectatorem ad subveniendum non movet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D3","text":"Hortensius desiderium ab arte dicendi ad sapientiam transfert, sed sapientia sine Christo Augustinum totum rapere non potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D4","text":"Superbia Scripturam ex dignitate Ciceroniana metitur atque formam humilem respuit antequam eius interiora penetret.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5","text":"Coniunctio superbiae, imaginationis corporeae et nominum sacrorum Manichaeismum efficit apparentem satisfactionem desiderii veritatis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D6","text":"Fabula agnita ut ficta minus fallit quam doctrina ficta ut vera credita, quia distinctio inter imaginationem et assertionem servatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D7","text":"Quaestio Manichaea de origine mali dissolvitur, si malum privatio est et Deus incorporeus atque immutabilis intelligitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D8","text":"Diversitas praeceptorum divinorum patriarchis et praesentibus data mutationem iustitiae non probat, sed applicationem unius ordinis ad tempora diversa.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D9","text":"Facta specie similia moraliter differre possunt, si alius est animus, usus, articulus temporis vel mandatum divinum.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D10","text":"Peccatum contra Deum non est laesio divinae substantiae, sed deformatio naturae agentis et disruptio ordinis quo pars universo congruit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D11","text":"Monnicae emendatio interpretationis somnii directionem conversionis statuit: filius ad regulam matris accedet, non mater ad errorem filii.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12","text":"Episcopi recusatio disputationis errorem non tolerat, sed inflationem praesentem indocilem iudicat atque lectioni, tempori et precibus correctionem committit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD1","text":"Conversio requirit simul ordinationem amoris et mutationem modi cognoscendi, quia idem motus ad sensibilia et desiderium corrumpit et Deum in phantasma transformat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD2","text":"Error Manichaeus parasitatur bona quae corrumpit: desiderium veritatis, nomina divina, pulchritudinem creatam et misericordiae speciem.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD3","text":"Universalitas moralis non uniformitatem materialem, sed constantiam ordinis per applicationes temporaliter distinctas significat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4","text":"Genealogia lapsus duas causalitates coniungit: voluntas culpabiliter se ad exteriora convertit, dum misericordia antecedens eandem historiam ad reditum ordinat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5","text":"Mora conversionis absentiam Dei non indicat, quia Deus interior manet dum subiectum relationaliter peregrinatur, et ipsa dilatio instrumentum correctionis fit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX1","text":"Systema falsitatem dualismi requirit: malum non potest esse natura positiva contra bonum constituta.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX2","text":"Systema falsitatem reductionis ontologicae ad corpus requirit: realitas mensurabili mole non exhauritur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX3","text":"Systema falsitatem identitatis inter veritatem et splendorem sermonis requirit: stilus sublimis, copia librorum et nomina sacra possunt errorem tegere.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX4","text":"Systema simul conventionalismum moralem et uniformitatem sine temporum discrimine excludit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX5","text":"Systema falsitatem iudicii ex solo effectu visibili requirit, quia intentio et articulus temporis moralem speciem facti mutare possunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX6","text":"Systema falsitatem correctionis semper immediatae requirit: disputatio non prodest ubi superbia nondum capacitatem discendi admittit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX1","text":"Nulla desiderii neutralitas admittitur: appetitus aut ad fontem vitae ordinatur aut bonum creatum in substitutum falsum convertit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX2","text":"Creaturae exterioritas sibi sufficiens impossibilis est, quia recessus a Deo independentiam non parit sed defectum vitae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX3","text":"Nullum principium mali Deo coaevum, comparabile aut ipsum laedere capax admittitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX4","text":"Iudicium morale totale ex brevi praesentia humana praecluditur, quia ordo iustitiae nexus temporum et causarum excedit quos homo experitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX5","text":"Reditus per eandem superbiam quae errorem genuit impossibilis est; accessus ad veritatem inclinationem, confessionem et patientiam requirit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX6","text":"In hac narratione particulari finalis Augustini perditio per somnium et dictum episcopi praecluditur, quamvis haec praeclusio in legem universalem de omnibus filiis lacrimarum non convertatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:FGS1","text":"Fames Dei non agnita → amor amoris → proiectio ad sensibilia → voluptas mixta dolore → exinanitio → renovata fuga ad exteriora.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:FGS2","text":"Excitatio ad sapientiam → retentio criterii christiani → recusatio Scripturae humilis → quaestus corporeus veritatis → captatio per nomina sacra et phantasmata Manichaea.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:FGS3","text":"Quaestiones Manichaeae → correctio modi cognoscendi → Deus incorporeus → malum ut privatio → iustitia immutabilis cum distributione temporali → reclassificatio factorum moralium.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:FGS4","text":"Misericordia antecedens → poena et inquietudo → preces Monnicae → somnium directionis → dilatio disputationis → cognitio erroris per lectionem et tempus → reditus praenuntiatus.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:AF1","text":"Amor amoris → nexus libidinosus → voluptas doloris scenici → gloria rhetorica et societas perversa → Hortensiana conversio ad sapientiam → fastidium Scripturae → captatio Manichaea.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:AF2","text":"Quaestiones de malo, Deo et patriarchis → restitutio ontologiae et iustitiae → distinctio flagitiorum, facinorum et factorum apparentium → detectio absurditatis Manichaeae → intercessio Monnicae → promissio conversionis dilatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME1","text":"Amor ex intensitate affectus ad ordinem obiecti reclassificatur: quaestio decisiva non est quantum ametur, sed quid et quo ordine ametur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME2","text":"Misericordia a delectatione doloris separatur et per voluntatem subveniendi definitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME3","text":"Ordo cognitionis distinguit corpora vera, imaginationes corporum, phantasmata rerum nullarum et Deum qui omnes has classes transcendit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME4","text":"Oppositio inter legem universalem et varietatem historicam corruit; varietas praeceptorum fit modus applicationis legis immutabilis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME5","text":"Factum visibile ab actu morali separatur, quia intentio, officium, tempus et auctoritas possunt eandem speciem externam aliter constituere.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME6","text":"Haeresis non ut pura absentia veritatis, sed ut captatio parasitica per signa vera, desideria bona et phantasmata falsa describitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME7","text":"Mora conversionis ex signo desertionis in instrumentum providentiae et maturitatis epistemicae convertitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:ALT1","text":"Gradus superficiei continet amores Carthaginienses, spectacula, studia rhetorica, lectionem Hortensii, Manichaeismum et sollicitudinem Monnicae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:AF1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AF2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"h