timonium Dei certo agnoscatur intra capitulum nondum formaliter explicatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT5","text":"Iustitia immutabilis cum mandatis inusitatis cohaerere potest, sed occultatio causae mandati iudicium humanum dependentem ab auctoritate facit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0045","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT6","text":"Reiectio phantasmatum corporeorum et acceptio somnii divini tensionem epistemicam relinquunt, quia discretio utriusque ex effectu providentiali potius quam ex criterio generali pendet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0050","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0051","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT7","text":"Doctrina mali privativi cum activa seductione daemonum et flagellatione divina componitur, sed mediatio inter privationem, agentiam spiritualem et poenam rhetorice potius quam analytice exhibetur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0012","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT8","text":"Dictum episcopi de filio lacrimarum intra historiam Augustini vim propheticam accipit, sed ex eo propositio universalis sine excessu deduci non potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT9","text":"Restitutio servat verum motum textus: experientia miseriae → diagnosis desiderii → falsa sapientiae solutio → correctio ontologica et moralis → providentia reditus dilati.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:FGS1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T141932135654Z_90b27968","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"BOOK THREE.","source_sha256":"3917f792d90af6b461a2bf901cb9a9d30d2d9bdb3ef63f8958acf46950645131","sha256":"e04facd1edbf73fe42e4a8a8c5bcbda8487564baab61d29b374a708f0556ad9b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:19:32.137688+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumentative Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS1","text":"The text investigates how the soul, not knowing God, desires Him, turns desire into pleasures and errors, and can be prepared for truth from that very wandering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS2","text":"The soul's inner hunger for God, if unrecognized, diverts love from the creator toward sensible things, fictive sorrow, rhetorical glory, and corporeal doctrine, which do not satisfy the soul but exhaust it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS3","text":"Truth is not measured by feeling, custom, the appearance of a deed, or sacred names, but by immutable God, the order of nature, and the law of justice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS4","text":"Hortensius transfers desire from eloquence to wisdom, but the absence of Christ's name and pride against humble Scripture leave conversion incomplete.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS5","text":"Retrospective reconstruction dissolves the errors of the Manichaeans through incorporeal God, evil as the privation of good, and immutable justice that assigns different things at different times.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS6","text":"Divine mercy operates before confession through punishments, intellectual awakenings, Monnica's prayers, a dream, and correction prudently delayed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS7","text":"Genealogical, diagnostic, polemical, and reconstructive argumentation advances from the effects of perverse love to ontological causes, then to moral order and the providence of conversion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A1","text":"God is immutable Truth, the life of souls, and the creator and governor of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2","text":"The soul, even without conscious desire, needs God as incorruptible food.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A3","text":"Created goods can be loved because they are good, but they cannot replace the creator.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4","text":"Sin is the turning of love from the universal good to a private part possessed or used immoderately.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A5","text":"True mercy wishes misery to be removed, not sorrow to be retained as pleasure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A6","text":"Evil is not a substance, but the privation of good even unto a deficiency of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A7","text":"God is spirit without bulk or dimensions, wholly everywhere and identical with no body or created soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8","text":"Cognition bounded by bodily sense and phantasm cannot apprehend God and fabricates false infinities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A9","text":"True justice is God's most right law, the same everywhere and always.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","text":"Immutable justice distributes different precepts according to times, regions, offices, and persons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A11","text":"Shameful acts against nature are always to be condemned, whereas violations of human customs are assessed according to the compact of city or nation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0038","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A12","text":"The morality of a deed is judged by the agent's intention, usage, hidden time, and divine testimony, not by external appearance alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A13","text":"God's command, as that of the highest ruler, prevails over human custom and compact.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14","text":"Pride turns the intellect away from the humble form of truth and inclines it toward novelty, eloquence, and the appearance of wisdom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A15","text":"The frequency of words of truth and divine names does not ensure the presence of truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16","text":"Divine mercy precedes confession and orders conversion even through punishment, mediation, and delay.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX1","text":"The intensity of love or mutual bodily enjoyment does not constitute the goodness of love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX2","text":"Sorrow aroused by theatrical images is not mercy where no assistance is intended and sorrow itself delights.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX3","text":"Sorrow can sometimes be approved, but it must never be loved for its own sake.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX4","text":"The humility of Scripture's style does not signify the humility or unworthiness of truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX5","text":"The name of philosophy, truth, Christ, or Spirit does not in itself make doctrine true.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX6","text":"God is neither body, nor infinite bulk, nor phantasm of a body, nor the soul of bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX7","text":"Evil is not a substantial principle or one coeternal with God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX8","text":"Justice is neither reduced to local custom nor does it require uniformity of precepts through all times.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX9","text":"The external similarity of a deed does not establish sin or justice without consideration of intention and time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX10","text":"Sin cannot corrupt God, nor does flight from God produce freedom; the sinner wounds himself and society.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D1","text":"Unrecognized hunger for God seeks sensible things as food; because they cannot replace God, delight passes into greater emptiness and sorrow.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D2","text":"The theater simulates mercy, but encloses feeling within pleasure in sorrow because it does not move the spectator to render aid.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D3","text":"Hortensius transfers desire from the art of speaking to wisdom, but wisdom without Christ cannot wholly carry Augustine away.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D4","text":"Pride measures Scripture by Ciceronian dignity and rejects its humble form before penetrating its interior.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5","text":"The conjunction of pride, corporeal imagination, and sacred names makes Manichaeism an apparent satisfaction of the desire for truth.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D6","text":"A fable recognized as fictitious deceives less than fictitious doctrine believed true, because the distinction between imagination and assertion is preserved.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D7","text":"The Manichaean question concerning the origin of evil is dissolved if evil is understood as privation and God as incorporeal and immutable.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D8","text":"The diversity of divine precepts given to the patriarchs and to the present does not prove a change in justice, but the application of one order to different times.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D9","text":"Deeds similar in appearance can differ morally if the intention, use, juncture of time, or divine command is different.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D10","text":"Sin against God is not injury to the divine substance, but deformation of the agent's nature and disruption of the order by which a part accords with the universe.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D11","text":"The correction of Monnica's interpretation of the dream establishes the direction of conversion: the son will come to the mother's rule, not the mother to the son's error.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0051","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12","text":"The bishop's refusal of disputation does not tolerate error, but judges present inflation unteachable and entrusts correction to reading, time, and prayers.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD1","text":"Conversion requires at once the ordering of love and a change in the mode of knowing, because the same motion toward sensible things both corrupts desire and transforms God into a phantasm.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD2","text":"Manichaean error parasitizes the goods it corrupts: desire for truth, divine names, created beauty, and the appearance of mercy.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD3","text":"Moral universality signifies not material uniformity, but constancy of order through temporally distinct applications.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4","text":"The genealogy of the fall joins two causalities: the will culpably turns itself toward externals, while prevenient mercy orders the same history toward return.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5","text":"The delay of conversion does not indicate God's absence, because God remains within while the subject journeys relationally, and the delay itself becomes an instrument of correction.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX1","text":"The system requires the falsity of dualism: evil cannot be a positive nature constituted against good.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX2","text":"The system requires the falsity of ontological reduction to body: reality is not exhausted by measurable bulk.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX3","text":"The system requires the falsity of the identity between truth and splendor of speech: lofty style, an abundance of books, and sacred names can conceal error.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX4","text":"The system excludes both moral conventionalism and uniformity without distinction of times.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX5","text":"The system requires the falsity of judgment from visible effect alone, because intention and the juncture of time can alter the moral character of a deed.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX6","text":"The system requires the falsity of correction that is always immediate: disputation does not profit where pride does not yet admit the capacity for learning.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX1","text":"No neutrality of desire is admitted: appetite is either ordered toward the source of life or converts a created good into a false substitute.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX2","text":"The self-sufficient exteriority of the creature is impossible, because withdrawal from God produces not independence but deficiency of life.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX3","text":"No principle of evil coeval with God, comparable to Him, or capable of injuring Him is admitted.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX4","text":"Total moral judgment from brief human presence is precluded, because the order of justice exceeds the connections of times and causes that a human being experiences.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX5","text":"Return through the same pride that generated error is impossible; access to truth requires humility, confession, and patience.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX6","text":"In this particular narrative, Augustine's final perdition is precluded by the dream and the bishop's saying, although this preclusion is not converted into a universal law concerning all sons of tears.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:FGS1","text":"Unrecognized hunger for God → love of love → projection toward sensible things → pleasure mixed with sorrow → emptying → renewed flight toward externals.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:FGS2","text":"Awakening to wisdom → retention of the Christian criterion → rejection of humble Scripture → corporeal pursuit of truth → enticement by sacred names and Manichaean phantasms.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:FGS3","text":"Manichaean questions → correction of the mode of knowing → incorporeal God → evil as privation → immutable justice with temporal distribution → reclassification of moral deeds.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:FGS4","text":"Prevenient mercy → punishment and unrest → Monnica's prayers → dream of direction → delay of disputation → knowledge of error through reading and time → return foretold.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:AF1","text":"Love of love → lustful attachment → pleasure in theatrical sorrow → rhetorical glory and perverse society → Hortensian conversion to wisdom → distaste for Scripture → Manichaean enticement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:AF2","text":"Questions concerning evil, God, and the patriarchs → restoration of ontology and justice → distinction of shameful acts, criminal acts, and apparent deeds → detection of Manichaean absurdity → Monnica's intercession → promise of delayed conversion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME1","text":"Love is reclassified from intensity of feeling to the order of its object: the decisive question is not how much one loves, but what one loves and in what order.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME2","text":"Mercy is separated from delight in sorrow and defined through the will to render aid.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME3","text":"The order of cognition distinguishes true bodies, imaginations of bodies, phantasms of non-existent things, and God, who transcends all these classes.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME4","text":"The opposition between universal law and historical variety collapses; diversity of precepts becomes a mode of application of immutable law.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME5","text":"The visible deed is separated from the moral act, because intention, office, time, and authority can constitute the same external appearance differently.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME6","text":"Heresy is described not as a pure absence of truth, but as parasitic enticement through true signs, good desires, and false phantasms.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME7","text":"The delay of conversion is transformed from a sign of abandonment into an instrument of providence and epistemic maturity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:ALT1","text":"The surface level contains Carthaginian loves, spectacles, rhetorical studies, the reading of Hortensius, Manichaeism, and Monnica's concern.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:AF1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AF2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:ALT2","text":"The structural level joins inner hunger, conversion toward sensible things, pride, phantasmal cognition, and enticement through names.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:ALT3","text":"The metastrategic level transfers the criteria of judgment from feeling, eloquence, custom, and the appearance of a deed to the order of love, intention, times, and divine authority.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:ALT4","text":"The ontological and temporal level presupposes immutable and incorporeal God, privative evil, the dependent creature, and providence acting through delays.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to restore the sequence from perverse appetite through ontological error to moral correction and the providence of conversion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT2","text":"The system principally coheres, but the causal relation between the culpable conversion of the will and decisively prevenient divine mercy is not fully determined.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0012","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT3","text":"The strongest joint is the nexus between pride, corporeal cognition, rejection of Scripture, and Manichaean enticement.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT4","text":"The criterion by which an authentic divine command, a providential dream, or God's testimony may be certainly recognized is not yet formally explained within the chapter.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT5","text":"Immutable justice can cohere with unusual commands, but concealment of the reason for the command makes human judgment dependent on authority.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0032","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0034","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0045","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT6","text":"The rejection of corporeal phantasms and acceptance of the divine dream leave an epistemic tension, because the distinction between them depends on providential effect rather than on a general criterion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0050","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0051","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT7","text":"The doctrine of privative evil is combined with the active seduction of demons and divine scourging, but the mediation between privation, spiritual agency, and punishment is presented rhetorically rather than analytically.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0012","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT8","text":"The bishop's saying concerning the son of tears acquires prophetic force within Augustine's history, but no universal proposition can be deduced from it without excess.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the text's true movement: experience of misery → diagnosis of desire → false solution of wisdom → ontological and moral correction → providence of delayed return.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:FGS1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBT:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LIBT@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_5P0L_LIBT:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 03","title":"Book III.","context":"Chapter 03","original_title":"Liber Tertius.","original_context":"Chapter 03"},"original_title":"Liber Tertius.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ","layer":"CH","title":"Book IV.","order":4,"parents":["RAW_5P0L_LIBQ"],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ@R001","sha256":"1f988408904c4c8f116406ddf3380a228ab8d28d8373929d879ff7133b47dadd","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS1","text":"Textus quaerit quomodo ingenium acre, amicitia intensa et rectitudines particulares cum diuturno errore ac miseria cohaerere potuerint.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS2","text":"Bona creata perniciosa fiunt non natura sua, sed cum anima aversa a Deo ea tamquam fines stabiles amat vel interpretatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS3","text":"Distinctio generatrix opponit Deum incommutabilem creaturis mutabilibus, veritatem illuminantem menti participanti et amorem ordinatum fixationi in rebus caducis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS4","text":"Argumentatio confessionalis simul diagnostica, genealogica, polemica et reconstructiva est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS5","text":"Motus procedit ab errore culpabili ad mortem amici, a luctu ad ontologiam mutabilitatis, inde ad genealogiam erroris intellectualis et ad ordinem reditus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS6","text":"Restitutio animi non abolendo creaturas vel facultates, sed referendo amorem, cognitionem et dona ad Deum efficitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A1","text":"Deus est veritas et bonum incommutabile, cui proprietates non quasi accidentia subiecto insunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A2","text":"Omne bonum creatum, omne verum cognitum et omnis facultas intellectualis a Deo creatore procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A3","text":"Creatura temporalis per successionem partium constat, mutatur atque interit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A4","text":"Mens humana mutabilis est et veritatis per illuminationem particeps, non ipsa natura veritatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A5","text":"Sensus corporeus partes transeuntes capit, non totum simul neque rem incorpoream.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A6","text":"Amor animam rei dilectae alligat et in ea requiem quaerit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A7","text":"Diligere moriturum quasi non moriturum miseriam iam ante iacturam constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A8","text":"Vera amicitia exsistit tantum ubi Deus amantes sibi invicem caritate coniungit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A9","text":"Bonum creatum recte amatur in Deo et ad Creatorem refertur, non tamquam finis ab eo separatus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A10","text":"Aversio superba a Deo est radix perversitatis affectivae et intellectualis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A11","text":"Imaginatio corporea ad spiritualia translata phantasmata pro rebus constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A12","text":"Malum non est substantia, sed vitium motus, affectionis vel mentis mutabilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A13","text":"Error et peccatum ex voluntaria deviatione creaturae oriuntur, non ex necessitate siderum, materiae vel substantiae divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A14","text":"Consonantiae astrologicae possunt, secundum rationem senis medici ab Augustino receptam, sorte potius quam arte siderum oriri.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A15","text":"Laus socialis affectum audientis accendere potest, etiamsi res laudata ipsa non mutetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A16","text":"Celeritas intelligendi donum est cuius utilitas ex recto usu et fine, non ex sola possessione, pendet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A17","text":"Deus animam per media curare potest quae ipsa nondum plene intellegit vel voluntarie eligit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A18","text":"Vita divina incarnata mortem assumit atque vincit, ut homo ab exterioribus ad Deum redeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX1","text":"Rectitudo particularis conversionem integram non constituit, si finis actionis adhuc cupiditate vel superstitione regitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX2","text":"Astrologia non fit licita eo quod sacrificiis et precibus spirituum carere videatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX3","text":"Necessitas caelestis peccatorem a culpa non absolvit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX4","text":"Sacramentum non redditur inefficax sola absentia cognitionis consciae recipientis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX5","text":"Studia communia, mutua benevolentia et delectatio consortii ad veram amicitiam per se non sufficiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX6","text":"Mutatio loci, voluptas sensibilis et occupatio litteraria animam a se ipsa fugere neque dolorem radicaliter sanare possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX7","text":"Nulla creatura mutabilis est locus quietis imperturbabilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX8","text":"Deus non est corpus lucidum neque spatium lucis immensum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX9","text":"Deus decem praedicamentis quasi subiectum accidentium non continetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX10","text":"Malum non est substantia adversa Deo neque vita sui iuris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX11","text":"Mens humana non est pars substantiae divinae neque summum bonum incommutabile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX12","text":"Acumen dialecticum et scientia artium salutem aut sapientiam per se non efficiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX13","text":"Amor corporum, animarum et amicorum non abolendus, sed ordinandus est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D1","text":"Rectitudines locales cum perversitate totius vitae coexistere possunt, quia bonitas actus particularis ordinem finis universalis non necessario mutat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D2","text":"Astrologia, peccatum in necessitatem siderum transferens, hominem exculpat et Creatorem iustum implicite accusat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D3","text":"Praedictio vera artem astrologicam non probat, quia observatio particularis causalitatem artis a consonantia fortuita distinguere non potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D4","text":"Narratio conversionis amici effectum baptismi tamquam operationem divinam cognitionem explicitam praecedentem interpretatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D5","text":"Mors amici non tantum gaudium aufert, sed miseriam iam inclusam in amore mortalis tamquam immortalis manifestat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D6","text":"Fuga localis dolorem radicalem non removet, quia anima secum fert ordinem amoris quo ipsa sibi locus infelix facta est.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D7","text":"Successio temporis memorias et delectationes substituendo dolorem minuit, sed amicitiae extra Deum ordinatae causam futurorum dolorum servant.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D8","text":"Qui amicos in Deo amat ultimam amissionem non patitur, quia nexus amoris in eo fundatur qui non transit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D9","text":"Transitus partium defectus universi non est, sed condicio qua totum temporale per successionem constituitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D10","text":"Anima veritati nondum stabiliter inhaerens eundem hominem aliter amat secundum affectum laudantium, rebus ipsis immutatis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D11","text":"Imaginatio corporea cum superbia coniuncta mutabilitatem propriam in Deum transfert et vitium voluntatis in dualismum substantiarum transformat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D12","text":"Praedicamenta ad res creatas utilia falsitatem generant cum divina simplicitas quasi subiectum magnitudinis aut pulchritudinis tractatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D13","text":"Ingenium a fonte suo aversum veritates locales assequi potest, sed eas in superbiam, errorem metaphysicum et perniciem convertit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D14","text":"Incarnatio motum reditus ordinat per descensum humilem, mortis victoriam et recessionem a visu exteriori ad praesentiam interiorem.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD1","text":"Error moralis, luctus immoderatus, superstitiones et falsa metaphysica sunt diversi effectus eiusdem aversionis quae bonum creatum a fonte suo separat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D1","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D11","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD2","text":"Conversio non destruit amorem, sensum, amicitiam vel scientiam, sed eorum obiecta et fines secundum ordinem Creatoris et creaturae reconstituit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D8","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D9","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD3","text":"Miseria temporalis oritur cum anima permanentiam appetitam a partibus successive transeuntibus exigere conatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD4","text":"Possessio veritatis localis sapientiam non importat, quia ars recte intellecta cum falsa imagine Dei et perverso ordine amoris coexistere potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D10","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD5","text":"Confessio errata et dona retrospecte in laudem divinae misericordiae convertit, quia etiam media imperfecte intellecta intra processum curationis reponuntur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD6","text":"Reditus ad Deum non est ascensus autonomus, sed participatio motus Christi qui descendendo mortem vincit et hominem ad interiora revocat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A18","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D8","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD7","text":"Providentia divina et culpa humana simul retinentur: Deus per eventus curat, sed anima voluntarie avertitur et erroris poenam fert.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD8","text":"Auctoritas socialis errorem recursive propagat, quia anima ab opinionibus alienis mota doctrinam receptam amicis et discipulis tradit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX1","text":"Anima sibi ipsi principium veritatis, firmitatis aut salutis esse non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX2","text":"Usus facultatis a fine amoris separatim aestimari non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX3","text":"Nulla relatio ad rem finitam possessionem sine periculo amissionis praestat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX4","text":"Nulla pars sensibilis aut categoria creata legitimam totalizationem realitatis divinae praebet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX5","text":"Culpa in carnem, sidera, materiam vel divinam substantiam transferri non potest quin confessio et iustitia dissolvantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX6","text":"Nullum principium mali Deo coaeternum vel substantialiter oppositum admittitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX7","text":"Ascensus per superbam assimilationem ad Deum reditum efficere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX8","text":"Amicitia ut nexus mere dyadicus sufficientem firmitatis causam non habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX9","text":"Consensus laudantium criterium veritatis aut valoris intrinseci non constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX1","text":"Nullus locus exterior praesto est quo anima a corde suo aut a praesentia Dei effugiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX2","text":"Possessio permanens boni temporalis intra ipsum ordinem temporis impossibilis est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX3","text":"Nullum punctum epistemicum omnino extra participationem lucis divinae datur, etiam ubi cognoscens fontem cognitionis ignorat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX4","text":"Sanatio non consistit in restitutione praeteriti amissi, sed in reformatione rerum fluxarum sub bono permanente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX5","text":"Absentia Dei localis vel ontologica esse non potest; quod absentia videtur aversio cordis est, quae etiam fugiendo sub lege divina manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX6","text":"Firmitas autonoma subiecti excluditur: anima firma est tantum cum firmitas eius Deus est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS1","text":"Aversio a Deo superbiam generat; superbia donum creatum in cupiditatem, phantasma et doctrinam fallacem convertit; error inde se ipsum et alios reproducit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS2","text":"Amor boni temporalis ut finis stabilis fixationem parit; mutabilitas obiecti iacturam infert; iactura miseriam antecedentem manifestat; fuga exterior animam ad se vulneratam remittit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS3","text":"Sensus partis phantasma totius producit; phantasma Deum corporeum vel categoricum constituit; falsa imago dualismum et translationem culpae sustentat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS4","text":"Laus socialis affectum accendit; affectus auctoritatem rei substituit; auctoritas recepta doctrinam falsam corroborat; doctrina per docentem vel amicum propagatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS5","text":"Divina mediatio per admonitionem, sacramentum, eventum et successionem temporis falsam securitatem perturbat atque memoriam ad ulteriorem conversionem praeparat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS6","text":"Incarnatio per descensum mortem assumit, per abundantiam vitae mortem vincit, per absentiam visibilem cor ad praesentiam interiorem revocat et per humilitatem ascensum restituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS7","text":"Confessio effectus praesentis curationis ad errores praeteritos refert, ex eis principia aversionis extrahit et dona male usa ad fontem suum restituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AF1","text":"Textus a seductione mutua et rectitudinibus imperfectis ad astrologiam transit, cuius fatalismus moraliter et causaliter dissolvitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AF2","text":"Amicitia ad baptismum amici, baptismus ad mortem, mors ad luctum, luctus ad fugam sui et successio temporis ad consolationem imperfectam ducunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AF3","text":"Experientia luctus in doctrinam mutabilitatis creaturarum, ordinationis amoris et quietis in Deo convertitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AF4","text":"Quaestio pulchri et apti ad dependentiam a laude, inde ad imaginationem corpoream, dualismum, abusum categoriarum et vanitatem ingenii autonomi progreditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AF5","text":"Omnes lineae in necessitatem reditus humilis ad Deum tamquam bonum, veritatem et firmitatem animae conveniunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME1","text":"Rectitudo moralis non iam per actus singulos tantum, sed per ordinem finis totius vitae describitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME2","text":"Luctus ex accidente post amissionem in revelationem miseriae iam praesentis ante amissionem reclassificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME3","text":"Amicitia e nexu duorum affectuum in relationem triadicam per Deum constituentem transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME4","text":"Mutabilitas creaturarum non ut mera defectio, sed ut successio ordinata partium universi fit visibilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME5","text":"Astrologia e disciplina praedictiva in machinam exculpationis moralis et confusionis causalis reclassificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME6","text":"Malum e substantia adversa in corruptionem motuum et facultatum mutabilium transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME7","text":"Pulchritudo, amicitia et artes ex finibus autonomis in bona signantia atque ad Creatorem referenda convertuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME8","text":"Oppositio inter ingenium excellens et fidem simplicem corruit, quia tarditas intellectus cum recta orientatione tutior esse potest quam acumen aversum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME9","text":"Conversio ex motu spatiali vel ascensu superbo in reditum interiorem per humilitatem et mediationem divinam redescribitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ALT1","text":"Gradus superficiei confessiones erroris, astrologiae, mortis amici, luctus, scriptorum philosophicorum et artium intellectarum continet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ALT2","text":"Gradus structuralis unum mechanismum detegit quo aversio, fixatio amoris, auctoritas socialis et imaginatio corporea affectum atque cognitionem corrumpunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ALT3","text":"Gradus metastrategicus criterium quaerendi mutat: non amplius quaeritur quantum anima intelligat vel amet, sed ad quid intellectus et amor ordinentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ALT4","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis distinctione inter Creatorem incommutabilem et creaturam successive existentem limites sensus, amoris et praedicationis constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad motum ab experientia erroris et luctus ad doctrinam mutabilitatis, illuminationis et amoris ordinati restituendum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT2","text":"Cohaerentia firmissima est ubi mors amici structuram latentem amoris mortalis manifestat et ubi imaginatio corporea falsam metaphysicam generat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT3","text":"Dulcedo fletus explicite indeterminata manet; textus hypotheses proponit, sed quaestionem confessioni subordinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT4","text":"Refutatio empirica astrologiae analogia sortis nititur neque documentum certum, quod Augustinus eo tempore quaerebat, plene exhibet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT5","text":"Efficacia baptismi amici ex mutatione narrativa et interpretatione providentiali infertur, non per mechanismum sacramentalem formaliter explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT6","text":"Concordia inter providentiam divinam, quae eventus disponit, et voluntariam deviationem animae affirmatur potius quam causaliter resolvitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT7","text":"Definitio amicitiae verae per Deum cum reali vi consolatoria et bonis internis amicitiarum nondum ordinatarum tensionem servat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT8","text":"Possibilitas veritates artium cognoscendi dum cognoscens ipse a lumine aversus manet distinctionem inter cognitionem localem et illuminationem sapientialem postulat, sed non plene formalizat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT9","text":"Restitutio ordinem verum textus servat: confessio biographica in diagnosin amoris, ontologiae et cognitionis transit atque in reditum ad bonum incommutabile clauditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T141833427941Z_4e8ce3d3","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"BOOK FOUR.","source_sha256":"1f988408904c4c8f116406ddf3380a228ab8d28d8373929d879ff7133b47dadd","sha256":"fc0fcf3cc40ae16baeffebbd82af6cd11fe950b22e2310789fe259c150c777ed","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:18:33.429867+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS1","text":"The text asks how keen intellect, intense friendship, and particular rectitudes could cohere with prolonged error and misery.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS2","text":"Created goods become pernicious not by their nature, but when the soul turned away from God loves or interprets them as stable ends.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS3","text":"The generative distinction opposes the immutable God to mutable creatures, truth illuminating the participating mind to love ordered to fixation upon perishable things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS4","text":"The confessional argumentation is at once diagnostic, genealogical, polemical, and reconstructive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS5","text":"The movement proceeds from culpable error to the death of a friend, from grief to the ontology of mutability, thence to the genealogy of intellectual error and to the order of return.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS6","text":"The restoration of the soul is effected not by abolishing creatures or faculties, but by referring love, knowledge, and gifts to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A1","text":"God is immutable truth and good, in whom properties do not inhere as though accidents in a subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A2","text":"Every created good, every known truth, and every intellectual faculty proceeds from God the creator.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A3","text":"A temporal creature consists through the succession of parts, changes, and perishes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A4","text":"The human mind is mutable and shares in truth through illumination, not itself the nature of truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A5","text":"Bodily sense apprehends passing parts, not the whole at once nor an incorporeal thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A6","text":"Love binds the soul to the thing loved and seeks rest in it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A7","text":"To love what will die as though it would not die establishes misery even before the loss.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A8","text":"True friendship exists only where God joins those who love one another in charity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A9","text":"A created good is rightly loved in God and referred to the Creator, not as an end separate from him.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A10","text":"Proud turning away from God is the root of affective and intellectual perversity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A11","text":"Bodily imagination, transferred to spiritual things, constitutes phantasms as realities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A12","text":"Evil is not a substance, but a defect of movement, affection, or mutable mind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A13","text":"Error and sin arise from the voluntary deviation of the creature, not from the necessity of the stars, matter, or divine substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A14","text":"Astrological correspondences can, according to the reasoning of the old physician accepted by Augustine, arise from chance rather than from the art of the stars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A15","text":"Social praise can kindle the affection of the hearer, even if the thing praised itself does not change.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A16","text":"Quickness of understanding is a gift whose usefulness depends on right use and end, not on possession alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A17","text":"God can heal the soul through means that it itself does not yet fully understand or voluntarily choose.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A18","text":"Divine life incarnate assumes and conquers death, so that the human being may return from external things to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX1","text":"Particular rectitude does not constitute complete conversion if the end of action is still governed by cupidity or superstition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX2","text":"Astrology does not become permissible because it seems to lack sacrifices and prayers to spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX3","text":"Celestial necessity does not absolve the sinner from guilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX4","text":"A sacrament is not rendered ineffective by the mere absence of the recipient's conscious knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX5","text":"Shared studies, mutual goodwill, and delight in companionship do not by themselves suffice for true friendship.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX6","text":"Change of place, sensible pleasure, and literary occupation cannot enable the soul to flee from itself or radically heal pain.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX7","text":"No mutable creature is a place of undisturbed rest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX8","text":"God is neither a luminous body nor an immense space of light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX9","text":"God is not contained within the ten categories as though a subject of accidents.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX10","text":"Evil is neither a substance opposed to God nor a life existing in its own right.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX11","text":"The human mind is neither a part of the divine substance nor the immutable highest good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX12","text":"Dialectical acumen and knowledge of the arts do not by themselves produce salvation or wisdom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX13","text":"Love of bodies, souls, and friends is not to be abolished, but ordered.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D1","text":"Local rectitudes can coexist with the perversity of an entire life, because the goodness of a particular act does not necessarily alter the order of the universal end.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D2","text":"Astrology, transferring sin into the necessity of the stars, exculpates the human being and implicitly accuses the just Creator.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D3","text":"A true prediction does not prove astrological art, because a particular observation cannot distinguish the causality of the art from fortuitous correspondence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D4","text":"The narrative of the friend's conversion interprets the effect of baptism as a divine operation preceding explicit knowledge.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D5","text":"The death of a friend does not merely remove joy, but manifests the misery already enclosed in love of the mortal as immortal.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D6","text":"Local flight does not remove radical pain, because the soul carries with it the order of love by which it has made itself an unhappy place for itself.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D7","text":"The succession of time lessens pain by replacing memories and pleasures, but friendships ordered outside God preserve the cause of future pains.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D8","text":"One who loves friends in God does not suffer ultimate loss, because the bond of love is founded in him who does not pass away.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D9","text":"The passing of parts is not a defect of the universe, but the condition by which the temporal whole is constituted through succession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D10","text":"A soul not yet stably adhering to truth loves the same person differently according to the affection of those who praise, while the things themselves remain unchanged.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D11","text":"Bodily imagination joined with pride transfers its own mutability to God and transforms a defect of the will into a dualism of substances.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D12","text":"Categories useful for created things generate falsehood when divine simplicity is treated as though it were a subject of magnitude or beauty.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D13","text":"Intellect turned away from its source can attain local truths, but turns them into pride, metaphysical error, and ruin.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D14","text":"The Incarnation orders the movement of return through humble descent, victory over death, and withdrawal from exterior sight to interior presence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD1","text":"Moral error, immoderate grief, superstitions, and false metaphysics are diverse effects of the same turning away that separates a created good from its source.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D1","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D11","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD2","text":"Conversion does not destroy love, sense, friendship, or knowledge, but reconstitutes their objects and ends according to the order of Creator and creature.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D8","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D9","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD3","text":"Temporal misery arises when the soul attempts to demand desired permanence from parts that pass away successively.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD4","text":"Possession of local truth does not entail wisdom, because rightly understood art can coexist with a false image of God and a perverse order of love.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D10","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD5","text":"Confession retrospectively converts errors and gifts into praise of divine mercy, because even imperfectly understood means are situated within the process of healing.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD6","text":"Return to God is not an autonomous ascent, but participation in the movement of Christ, who by descending conquers death and recalls the human being to interior things.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A18","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D8","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD7","text":"Divine providence and human guilt are retained together: God heals through events, but the soul voluntarily turns away and bears the penalty of error.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD8","text":"Social authority propagates error recursively, because a soul moved by the opinions of others hands down received doctrine to friends and pupils.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX1","text":"The soul cannot be for itself the principle of truth, stability, or salvation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX2","text":"The use of a faculty cannot be assessed separately from the end of love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX3","text":"No relation to a finite thing affords possession without the danger of loss.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX4","text":"No sensible part or created category provides a legitimate totalization of divine reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX5","text":"Guilt cannot be transferred to flesh, stars, matter, or divine substance without confession and justice being dissolved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX6","text":"No principle of evil coeternal with God or substantially opposed to him is admitted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX7","text":"Ascent through proud assimilation to God cannot effect return.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX8","text":"Friendship as a merely dyadic bond has no sufficient cause of stability.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX9","text":"The consensus of those who praise does not constitute a criterion of truth or intrinsic value.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX1","text":"No external place is available to which the soul may escape from its own heart or from the presence of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX2","text":"Permanent possession of a temporal good within the order of time itself is impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX3","text":"No epistemic point wholly outside participation in divine light is given, even where the knower is ignorant of the source of knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX4","text":"Healing does not consist in the restoration of the lost past, but in the reformation of transient things under the permanent good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX5","text":"The absence of God cannot be local or ontological; what appears to be absence is the turning away of the heart, which even in fleeing remains under divine law.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX6","text":"The autonomous stability of the subject is excluded: the soul is stable only when God is its stability.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS1","text":"Turning away from God generates pride; pride converts a created gift into cupidity, phantasm, and false doctrine; error thereafter reproduces itself and others.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS2","text":"Love of a temporal good as a stable end produces fixation; the mutability of the object brings loss; loss manifests antecedent misery; external flight sends the soul back to itself wounded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS3","text":"Sense of a part produces a phantasm of the whole; the phantasm constitutes a corporeal or categorical God; the false image sustains dualism and the transfer of guilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS4","text":"Social praise kindles affection; affection substitutes for the authority of the thing; received authority reinforces false doctrine; doctrine is propagated through teacher or friend.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS5","text":"Divine mediation through admonition, sacrament, event, and the succession of time unsettles false security and prepares memory for further conversion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS6","text":"The Incarnation through descent assumes death, through abundance of life conquers death, through visible absence recalls the heart to interior presence, and through humility restores ascent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS7","text":"Confession refers the effects of present healing to past errors, extracts from them the principles of turning away, and restores misused gifts to their source.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AF1","text":"The text moves from mutual seduction and imperfect rectitudes to astrology, whose fatalism is dissolved morally and causally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AF2","text":"Friendship leads to the baptism of the friend, baptism to death, death to grief, grief to flight from oneself, and the succession of time to imperfect consolation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AF3","text":"The experience of grief is converted into a doctrine of the mutability of creatures, the ordering of love, and rest in God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AF4","text":"The question of the beautiful and the fitting proceeds to dependence on praise, thence to bodily imagination, dualism, abuse of categories, and the vanity of autonomous intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AF5","text":"All lines converge upon the necessity of humble return to God as the good, truth, and stability of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME1","text":"Moral rectitude is described no longer through individual acts alone, but through the order of the end of the whole life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME2","text":"Grief is reclassified from an accident after loss into the revelation of misery already present before loss.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME3","text":"Friendship is transferred from a bond of two affections into a triadic relation constituted through God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME4","text":"The mutability of creatures becomes visible not as mere deficiency, but as the ordered succession of the parts of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME5","text":"Astrology is reclassified from a predictive discipline into a mechanism of moral exculpation and causal confusion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME6","text":"Evil is transferred from an opposing substance into the corruption of mutable movements and faculties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME7","text":"Beauty, friendship, and the arts are converted from autonomous ends into signifying goods to be referred to the Creator.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME8","text":"The opposition between outstanding intellect and simple faith collapses, because slowness of understanding with right orientation can be safer than turned-away acumen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME9","text":"Conversion is redescribed from spatial movement or proud ascent into interior return through humility and divine mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ALT1","text":"The surface level contains confessions of error, astrology, the death of a friend, grief, philosophical writings, and understood arts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ALT2","text":"The structural level uncovers a single mechanism by which turning away, fixation of love, social authority, and bodily imagination corrupt affection and knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ALT3","text":"The metastrategic level changes the criterion of inquiry: no longer is it asked how much the soul understands or loves, but to what intellect and love are ordered.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ALT4","text":"The ontological and temporal level, through the distinction between immutable Creator and successively existing creature, establishes the limits of sense, love, and predication.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement from the experience of error and grief to the doctrine of mutability, illumination, and ordered love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT2","text":"The coherence is strongest where the death of the friend manifests the hidden structure of mortal love and where bodily imagination generates false metaphysics.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT3","text":"The sweetness of weeping remains explicitly indeterminate; the text proposes hypotheses, but subordinates the question to confession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT4","text":"The empirical refutation of astrology relies upon the analogy of chance and does not fully furnish the certain proof that Augustine sought at that time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT5","text":"The efficacy of the friend's baptism is inferred from narrative change and providential interpretation, not formally explained through a sacramental mechanism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT6","text":"The concord between divine providence, which disposes events, and the voluntary deviation of the soul is affirmed rather than causally resolved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT7","text":"The definition of true friendship through God retains tension with the real consolatory force and internal goods of friendships not yet ordered.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT8","text":"The possibility of knowing the truths of the arts while the knower himself remains turned away from light requires a distinction between local knowledge and sapiential illumination, but does not fully formalize it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT9","text":"The restoration preserves the true order of the text: biographical confession passes into a diagnosis of love, ontology, and knowledge, and concludes in return to the immutable good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LIBQ@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_5P0L_LIBQ:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 04","title":"Book IV.","context":"Chapter 04","original_title":"Liber Quartus.","original_context":"Chapter 04"},"original_title":"Liber Quartus.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2","layer":"CH","title":"Book V.","order":5,"parents":["RAW_5P0L_LI_2"],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LI_2@R001","sha256":"ad01d54dc311ae6ec909351a96e9bc6a3309f4788772721971b76ab371fe763f","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS1","text":"Argumentatio quaerit quomodo auctoritas Manichaeorum dissolvatur et inquisitio veri ad Ecclesiam Catholicam nondum plene creditam transferatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS2","text":"Comparatio doctrinae cum ratione, experientia et exegesi ostendit Manichaeismum falsum, Catholicam autem fidem saltem defensibilem esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS3","text":"Argumentatio confessionalis, diagnostica, genealogica et reconstructiva est, quia errorem ex condicionibus epistemicis, moralibus et providentialibus resolvit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS4","text":"Motus primus procedit a scientia creaturarum ad examen magistri, ab examine ad ruinam auctoritatis, a ruina ad remissionem vinculi sectarii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS5","text":"Motus secundus procedit ab imaginatione corporea et excusatione culpae ad impassam doctrinalem, deinde per migrationes causis mixtis effectas ad auditionem Ambrosii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS6","text":"Terminus non est plena conversio, sed desertio Manichaeorum, defensibilitas Catholica, dubitatio Academica et status catechumeni donec certius criterium elucescat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A1","text":"A Deo averti non est eius praesentiam effugere, sed a se ipso discedere sub Deo semper praesente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A2","text":"Confessio subiectum iam cognitum ad agnitionem culpae, laudem et sanationem convertit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A3","text":"Vera de creatura per numeros, ordinem temporum et visibiles attestationes cognosci possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A4","text":"Beatitudo non ex scientia creaturarum, sed ex cognitione, glorificatione et gratiarum actione erga Deum oritur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A5","text":"Veritas et falsitas a cultu vel ruditate sermonis independent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A6","text":"Confessio ignorantiae epistemice melior est quam pertinax assertio rei ignoratae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A7","text":"Auctoritas plenariam praesentiam divinam sibi vindicans rationem etiam falsarum assertionum examinabilium reddere debet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A8","text":"Doctrina Manichaeorum cosmologiam rationibus et observationibus adversam cum religiosis suis fabulis coniungit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A9","text":"Impossibilitas substantiam spiritalem cogitandi imaginationem ad moles corporeas, dualismum et falsam fidei Catholicae effigiem cogit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A10","text":"Totum ego agit et peccat; natura aliena intra hominem posita culpam eius suscipere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A11","text":"Reconciliatio per crucem veram incarnationem et mortem Christi, non phantasma carnis, praesupponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A12","text":"Expositio spiritalis Scripturarum objectiones ex sola litterali acceptione ortas dissolvere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A13","text":"Possibilitas doctrinam defendendi nondum eius veritatem aut victoriam demonstrat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A14","text":"Augustinus tunc censet modum verum quaerendi ab auctoritate divina petendum esse neque philosophiam sine Christo curationi animae sufficere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A15","text":"Narratio retrospectiva providentiam causas externas, cupiditates perversas et actiones nescientium ad salutarem directionem ordinare affirmat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A16","text":"Deus petitionem immediatam negare potest ut cardinem profundioris desiderii ordine temporali impleat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX1","text":"Confessio Deum de statu confitentis non informat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX2","text":"Iniquus praesentiam Dei mutatione loci effugere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX3","text":"Praedictio siderum et cognitio mundi neque pietatem neque beatitudinem constituunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX4","text":"Eloquium ornatum veritatem non efficit, sicut sermo incompositus falsitatem non efficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX5","text":"Ignorantia rerum naturalium per se fidem non destruit, nisi ad doctrinam pietatis referatur et pertinaciter affirmetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX6","text":"Falsitas astronomica religionis iudicium non effugit ubi tamquam auctoritate divina traditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX7","text":"Modestia Fausti circa propriam imperitiam doctrinam sectae non verificat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX8","text":"Malum non est natura aliena cui peccator propriam actionem imputare possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX9","text":"Fides Catholica non est doctrina Dei figura humana corporaliter terminati.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX10","text":"Refutatio objectionum Manichaearum non constituit adhuc probationem plenam Catholicismi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX11","text":"Dubitatio Academica permanentiam in doctrina iam infirmata non iustificat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX12","text":"Negatio petitionis Monicae non significat eius orationem contemptam esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D1","text":"Comparatio cosmologiae Manichaeae cum rationibus numerorum et testimoniis visibilibus discrepantiam doctrinalem facit examinabilem.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D2","text":"Falsitas in rebus examinabilibus fit crisis auctoritatis, quia eadem doctrina plenitudinem divinae auctoritatis sibi vindicat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A7","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D3","text":"Faustus suavitate sermonis delectare potest, sed munus magistri promissi implere nequit, cum quaestiones structurales sectae explicare non possit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D4","text":"Philosophi possunt Manichaeis veriora de mundo dicere et tamen Creatorem non invenire neque ex scientia sua beati fieri.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D5","text":"Imaginatio omnis realitatis ut molis corporeae generat duas substantias oppositas, Christologiam phantasticam et repulsam fidei Catholicae male intellectae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A9","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D6","text":"Externalizatio peccati sanationem impedit, quia subiectum quod culpam negat confessionem necessariam recusat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D7","text":"Exegesis Ambrosii destruit persuasionem Scripturas omnino indefensibiles esse, sed nondum cogit Augustinum Catholicam doctrinam veram iudicare.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A12","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D8","text":"Manichaeismus relinquendus est, dum Ecclesia Catholica tamquam locus provisionalis inquisitionis retinetur sine assensu definitivo.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D9","text":"Attentio ad formam sermonis potest praeter intentionem auditorem materiae verae aperire, quia verba et res separari causaliter non semper possunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D10","text":"Licentia scholasticorum, ambitio, cupiditas lucri et auxilia Manichaeorum fiunt instrumenta migrationis quae Augustinum ad Ambrosium perducit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D11","text":"Recuperatio corporis a febre non est salus perfecta, sed conservatio temporalis subiecti cui salus spiritualis postea danda est.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D12","text":"Petitio Monicae ne filius naviget negatur, ut desiderium eius profundius de salute filii per ipsam navigationem promoveatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD1","text":"Conversio epistemica incipit non a probatione positiva novi systematis, sed a degradatione certitudinis veteris per discrepantiam, defectum magistri et exegesim aemulam.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:D1","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD2","text":"Rhetorica est medium causaliter efficax sed epistemice neutrum: apud Faustum errorem vestit, apud Ambrosium veritatem praeter intentionem auditoris transmittit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD3","text":"Providentia non ponitur ut causa concurrens inter alias, sed ut ordinatio superior quae causas moraliter mixtas ad finem ab agentibus ignoratum dirigit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D10","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD4","text":"Plena conversio requirit simul mutationem criterii epistemici, ontologiae corporis et spiritus, doctrinae responsabilitatis atque interpretationis Scripturae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A9","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD5","text":"Dubitatio fit intervallum productivum inter sectam iam falsam et Ecclesiam nondum demonstratam, non autem terminus sufficiens inquisitionis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD6","text":"Reditus ad Deum implicat reditum subiecti ad unitatem sui, quia alienatio a Deo, divisio culpae et recusatio confessionis eundem nexum constituunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse debet doctrinam occultam ab erroribus examinabilibus immunem manere, ubi utraque eidem auctoritati divinae attribuitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse debet defectum systematis sola eloquentia vel adventu magistri perfectioris sanari posse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse debet scientiam naturalem aut nullius valoris aut per se salutarem esse; ea vera et refutatoria esse potest sine beatitudine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse debet corporeitatem totum ambitum entis exhaurire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse debet divisionem agentis in ego innocens et naturam peccantem responsabilitatem conservare posse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:DNX6","text":"Falsum esse debet suspensionem iudicii modum quaerendi et auctoritatem veram per se praebere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:DNX7","text":"Falsum esse debet providentiam tantum per intentiones rectas, causas perspicuas et petitiones statim impletas operari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX1","text":"Systema exigit ut malum neque substantia sui iuris neque pars Dei sit, quamquam huius exclusionis ontologia positiva nondum praebetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX2","text":"Conversio autonoma et sibi perfecte perspicua excluditur, quia subiectum neque causas veras itineris neque finem earum dum movetur cognoscit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX3","text":"Accessus immediatus ad veritatem excluditur; creaturae, magistri, Scriptura, exegesis, Ecclesia et oratio omnes functionem mediationis exercent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX4","text":"Certitudo totalis non est condicio primi motus conversionis, quia argumentatio procedit per refutationem asymmetricam et habitationem provisionalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX5","text":"Probatio positiva verae auctoritatis divinae adhuc abest, atque haec absentia statum catechumeni et continuationem quaestionis ordinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:FGS1","text":"Aversio a Deo → caecitas → discessio a se → impossibilitas se vel Deum inveniendi, praesentia Dei tamen permanente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:FGS2","text":"Separatio eloquentiae a veritate → comparatio assertionum cum ratione et visibilibus testimoniis → detectio discrepantiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:FGS3","text":"Discrepantia examinabilis + praetensio divina + defectus magistri promissi → ruina fidei in auctoritatem Manichaeam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:FGS4","text":"Ruina auctoritatis + imaginatio corporea + externalizatio culpae → desertio interna sectae sine possessione alternativa positiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:FGS5","text":"Motiva perversa + pressiones externae + ordinatio providentialis → Roma → Mediolanum → accessus ad Ambrosium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:FGS6","text":"Auditio propter formam → ingressus inseparabilis rerum → exegesis spiritalis → defensibilitas Scripturae et Catholicismi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:FGS7","text":"Falsitas Manichaeorum + nondum probata victoria Catholica + insufficientia philosophiae sine Christo → dubitatio ordinata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:FGS8","text":"Dubitatio ordinata → desertio sectae → catechumenatus provisionalis → exspectatio criterii certioris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:AF1","text":"Omnipraesentia Dei → distinctio scientiae a beatitudine → distinctio eloquentiae a veritate → examen auctoritatis Manichaeae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:AF2","text":"Exspectatio Fausti → confessio eius imperitiae → defectus solutionis → remissio vinculi sectarii → migratio causis mixtis effecta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:AF3","text":"Impassa imaginationis corporeae → auditio Ambrosii → dissolutio objectionum litteralium → defensibilitas Catholica → dubitatio Academica → catechumenatus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME1","text":"Auctoritas religiosa denuo describitur ut examinabilis, ubi assertiones suas in agrum rationis et observationis extendit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME2","text":"Veritas propositionis, forma sermonis, pietas loquentis et beatitudo cognoscentis in axes distinctos distribuuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME3","text":"Ignorantia non amplius solo obiecto iudicatur, sed modo quo agnoscitur, occultatur aut auctoritate divina affirmatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME4","text":"Malum ab externa substantia ad divisionem et responsabilitatem subiecti reclassificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME5","text":"Catholicismus ex caricatura corporea et scripturaliter indefensibili in candidatum rationaliter defensibilem transit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME6","text":"Scepticismus ex doctrina finali in instrumentum dissolutionis et spatium transitionis convertitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME7","text":"Providentia ex interventu manifesto in ordinationem latentem causarum mixtarum et responsionum dilatarum transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME8","text":"Conversio ex actu singulari in seriem dissolutionis auctoritatis, mutationis ontologicae, recognitionis culpae et relocationis ecclesialis reconfiguratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ALT1","text":"Surface — Fausti imperitia, migratio Romam et Mediolanum, morbus, auditio Ambrosii et desertio Manichaeorum constituunt obiecta immediata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ALT2","text":"Structural — Relatio inter auctoritatem, probationem, rhetoricam, exegesim, responsabilitatem et institutionem ecclesialem conversionem generat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Quaestio mutatur ab electione inter doctrinas ad inventionem criterii, modi quaerendi et loci provisionalis inquisitionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Argumentatio praesupponit realitatem spiritalem non spatialem, unitatem agentis moralis, providentiam supra intentiones particulares et impletionem finis per moram.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam ruinam auctoritatis Manichaeae, impassam materialisticam et transitum ad catechumenatum provisionalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT2","text":"Ontologia positiva substantiae spiritalis nondum determinatur; tantum necessitas eius et defectus imaginationis corporeae apparent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT3","text":"Criterium quo vera auctoritas divina inter auctoritates aemulas agnoscatur nondum plene constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT4","text":"Structura firmissima est in distinctionibus inter veritatem et eloquentiam, scientiam et beatitudinem, ignorantiam confessam et falsitatem auctoritative assertam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT5","text":"Commissura fragilis inter errores cosmologicos et falsitatem religionis tantum tenet quia secta utrumque sub eadem praetensione divina coniungit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT6","text":"Modestia Fausti extrapolationem ab eius imperitia ad falsitatem totius sectae temperat; vis rupturae potius ex munere promisso non impleto provenit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT7","text":"Eloquium tamquam criterium repudiatur, sed tamquam causa ingressus veritatis retinetur; distinctio inter valorem epistemicum et efficaciam causalem tensionem tantum partialiter solvit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0026","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0061","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT8","text":"Providentia perversis causis utitur sine explicatione plena relationis inter ordinationem divinam et culpabilitatem humanam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT9","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat, quia capitulum non ad conversionem completam, sed ad desertionem sectae, suspensionem iudicii et repositionem ecclesialem pervenit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T142039075353Z_efffdf2d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"BOOK FIVE.","source_sha256":"ad01d54dc311ae6ec909351a96e9bc6a3309f4788772721971b76ab371fe763f","sha256":"1dd304c900643ce20fba91bb9f0b88260d6a70fb3f5cebb0eabd374f18db8f0e","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:20:39.077374+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS1","text":"The argument seeks how the authority of the Manichaeans is dismantled and the inquiry into truth transferred to the Catholic Church, not yet fully believed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS2","text":"Comparison of doctrine with reason, experience, and exegesis shows Manichaeism to be false, while the Catholic faith is at least defensible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS3","text":"The argument is confessional, diagnostic, genealogical, and reconstructive, because it resolves error from epistemic, moral, and providential conditions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS4","text":"The first movement proceeds from knowledge of creatures to examination of the teacher, from examination to the collapse of authority, and from collapse to the loosening of the sectarian bond.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS5","text":"The second movement proceeds from bodily imagination and the excuse of guilt to a doctrinal impasse, then through migrations brought about by mixed causes to the hearing of Ambrose.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS6","text":"The terminus is not full conversion, but the abandonment of the Manichaeans, the defensibility of Catholicism, Academic doubt, and the status of catechumen until a more certain criterion becomes clear.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A1","text":"To turn away from God is not to escape His presence, but to depart from oneself beneath God ever present.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A2","text":"Confession turns a subject already known toward acknowledgment of guilt, praise, and healing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A3","text":"Truths concerning creatures can be known through numbers, the order of times, and visible attestations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A4","text":"Blessedness arises not from knowledge of creatures, but from knowledge, glorification, and thanksgiving toward God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A5","text":"Truth and falsehood are independent of the refinement or roughness of speech.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A6","text":"Confession of ignorance is epistemically better than the stubborn assertion of an unknown matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A7","text":"An authority claiming for itself the full presence of the divine must also render its false assertions examinable by reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A8","text":"The doctrine of the Manichaeans joins a cosmology contrary to rational arguments and observations with its religious fables.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A9","text":"The inability to think spiritual substance compels imagination toward bodily masses, dualism, and a false image of the Catholic faith.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A10","text":"The whole self acts and sins; an alien nature placed within a human being cannot assume that person's guilt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A11","text":"Reconciliation through the cross presupposes the true incarnation and death of Christ, not a phantom of flesh.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A12","text":"The spiritual exposition of the Scriptures can dissolve objections arising from a merely literal understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A13","text":"The possibility of defending a doctrine does not yet demonstrate its truth or victory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A14","text":"Augustine then judges that the true way of seeking must be obtained from divine authority and that philosophy without Christ does not suffice for the healing of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A15","text":"The retrospective narrative affirms that providence orders external causes, perverse desires, and the actions of the unaware toward a salvific direction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:A16","text":"God can deny an immediate petition in order to fulfill, in temporal order, the hinge of a deeper desire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX1","text":"Confession does not inform God about the state of the one confessing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX2","text":"The wicked person cannot escape God's presence by a change of place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX3","text":"Prediction of the stars and knowledge of the world constitute neither piety nor blessedness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX4","text":"Ornate speech does not produce truth, just as unpolished speech does not produce falsehood.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX5","text":"Ignorance of natural matters does not in itself destroy faith, unless it is referred to a doctrine of piety and stubbornly asserted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX6","text":"Astronomical falsehood does not escape religious judgment where it is handed down as by divine authority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX7","text":"Faustus's modesty concerning his own incompetence does not verify the doctrine of the sect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX8","text":"Evil is not an alien nature to which the sinner can impute his own action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX9","text":"The Catholic faith is not a doctrine of God as a human figure bounded bodily.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX10","text":"The refutation of Manichaean objections does not yet constitute a full proof of Catholicism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX11","text":"Academic doubt does not justify remaining in a doctrine already weakened.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX12","text":"The denial of Monica's petition does not signify that her prayer was despised.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D1","text":"Comparison of Manichaean cosmology with numerical calculations and visible testimonies makes doctrinal discrepancy examinable.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D2","text":"Falsehood in examinable matters becomes a crisis of authority, because the same doctrine claims for itself the fullness of divine authority.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A7","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D3","text":"Faustus may delight by the sweetness of his speech, but he cannot fulfill the office of the promised teacher, since he cannot explain the structural questions of the sect.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D4","text":"Philosophers can say truer things about the world than the Manichaeans and yet fail to find the Creator or become blessed from their knowledge.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D5","text":"The imagination of all reality as bodily mass generates two opposed substances, a phantasmal Christology, and rejection of a misunderstood Catholic faith.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A9","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D6","text":"The externalization of sin impedes healing, because the subject who denies guilt refuses the necessary confession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D7","text":"Ambrose's exegesis destroys the conviction that the Scriptures are altogether indefensible, but does not yet compel Augustine to judge Catholic doctrine true.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A12","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D8","text":"Manichaeism must be abandoned, while the Catholic Church is retained as a provisional place of inquiry without definitive assent.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D9","text":"Attention to the form of speech can, beyond intention, open the hearer to true matter, because words and things cannot always be causally separated.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D10","text":"The licentiousness of students, ambition, desire for gain, and Manichaean assistance become instruments of migration that bring Augustine to Ambrose.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D11","text":"Recovery of the body from fever is not perfect salvation, but the temporal preservation of a subject to whom spiritual salvation is later to be given.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:D12","text":"Monica's petition that her son not sail is denied, so that her deeper desire for her son's salvation may be advanced through the very voyage.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD1","text":"Epistemic conversion begins not from the positive proof of a new system, but from the degradation of certainty in the old through discrepancy, the failure of the teacher, and rival exegesis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:D1","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD2","text":"Rhetoric is a causally effective but epistemically neutral medium: in Faustus it clothes error; in Ambrose it transmits truth beyond the hearer's intention.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD3","text":"Providence is not posited as one concurrent cause among others, but as a higher ordering that directs morally mixed causes toward an end unknown to the agents.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D10","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD4","text":"Full conversion requires at once a change of epistemic criterion, of the ontology of body and spirit, of the doctrine of responsibility, and of the interpretation of Scripture.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A9","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD5","text":"Doubt becomes a productive interval between a sect already false and a Church not yet demonstrated, but not a sufficient terminus of inquiry.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD6","text":"Return to God entails the subject's return to the unity of itself, because alienation from God, division of guilt, and refusal of confession constitute the same nexus.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:DNX1","text":"It must be false that hidden doctrine remains immune from examinable errors, where both are attributed to the same divine authority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:DNX2","text":"It must be false that the defect of a system can be healed by eloquence alone or by the arrival of a more perfect teacher.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:DNX3","text":"It must be false that natural knowledge is either of no value or salutary in itself; it can be true and refutatory without conferring blessedness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:DNX4","text":"It must be false that corporeality exhausts the whole scope of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:DNX5","text":"It must be false that the division of the agent into an innocent self and a sinning nature can preserve responsibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:DNX6","text":"It must be false that suspension of judgment can of itself provide a mode of seeking and true authority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:DNX7","text":"It must be false that providence operates only through right intentions, evident causes, and petitions fulfilled at once.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX1","text":"The system requires that evil be neither a self-subsisting substance nor a part of God, although the positive ontology of this exclusion is not yet provided.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX2","text":"Autonomous conversion, perfectly transparent to itself, is excluded, because the subject knows neither the true causes of the journey nor their end while it is moving.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX3","text":"Immediate access to truth is excluded; creatures, teachers, Scripture, exegesis, the Church, and prayer all perform a mediating function.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX4","text":"Total certainty is not the condition of the first movement of conversion, because the argument proceeds through asymmetric refutation and provisional dwelling.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX5","text":"Positive proof of true divine authority is still absent, and this absence orders the status of catechumen and the continuation of inquiry.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:FGS1","text":"Turning away from God → blindness → departure from oneself → inability to find oneself or God, while God's presence nevertheless remains.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:FGS2","text":"Separation of eloquence from truth → comparison of assertions with reason and visible testimonies → detection of discrepancy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:FGS3","text":"Examinable discrepancy + divine claim + failure of the promised teacher → collapse of faith in Manichaean authority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:FGS4","text":"Collapse of authority + bodily imagination + externalization of guilt → internal abandonment of the sect without possession of a positive alternative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:FGS5","text":"Perverse motives + external pressures + providential ordering → Rome → Milan → access to Ambrose.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:FGS6","text":"Hearing because of form → inseparable entry of things → spiritual exegesis → defensibility of Scripture and Catholicism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:FGS7","text":"Falsehood of the Manichaeans + Catholic victory not yet proven + insufficiency of philosophy without Christ → ordered doubt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:FGS8","text":"Ordered doubt → abandonment of the sect → provisional catechumenate → expectation of a more certain criterion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:AF1","text":"God's omnipresence → distinction of knowledge from blessedness → distinction of eloquence from truth → examination of Manichaean authority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:AF2","text":"Expectation of Faustus → confession of his incompetence → failure of solution → loosening of the sectarian bond → migration produced by mixed causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:AF3","text":"Impasse of bodily imagination → hearing of Ambrose → dissolution of literal objections → defensibility of Catholicism → Academic doubt → catechumenate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME1","text":"Religious authority is redescribed as examinable where it extends its assertions into the field of reason and observation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME2","text":"The truth of a proposition, the form of speech, the piety of the speaker, and the blessedness of the knower are distributed across distinct axes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME3","text":"Ignorance is no longer judged by its object alone, but by the manner in which it is acknowledged, concealed, or affirmed by divine authority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME4","text":"Evil is reclassified from an external substance to the division and responsibility of the subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME5","text":"Catholicism passes from a bodily caricature and scripturally indefensible position into a rationally defensible candidate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME6","text":"Skepticism is transformed from a final doctrine into an instrument of dissolution and a space of transition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME7","text":"Providence is transferred from manifest intervention into a hidden ordering of mixed causes and delayed responses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME8","text":"Conversion is reconfigured from a singular act into a series of the dissolution of authority, ontological change, acknowledgment of guilt, and ecclesial relocation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ALT1","text":"Surface — Faustus's incompetence, migration to Rome and Milan, illness, the hearing of Ambrose, and abandonment of the Manichaeans constitute the immediate objects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ALT2","text":"Structural — The relation among authority, proof, rhetoric, exegesis, responsibility, and ecclesial institution generates conversion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The question changes from choosing among doctrines to discovering a criterion, a mode of seeking, and a provisional place of inquiry.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The argument presupposes a non-spatial spiritual reality, the unity of the moral agent, providence above particular intentions, and fulfillment of an end through delay.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the collapse of Manichaean authority, the materialist impasse, and the transition to provisional catechumenate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT2","text":"The positive ontology of spiritual substance is not yet determined; only its necessity and the defect of bodily imagination appear.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT3","text":"The criterion by which true divine authority is recognized among rival authorities is not yet fully established.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT4","text":"The firmest structure lies in the distinctions between truth and eloquence, knowledge and blessedness, confessed ignorance and falsehood authoritatively asserted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT5","text":"The fragile joint between cosmological errors and the falsehood of religion holds only because the sect joins both under the same divine claim.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT6","text":"Faustus's modesty tempers extrapolation from his incompetence to the falsehood of the whole sect; the force of the rupture arises rather from the promised office left unfulfilled.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT7","text":"Eloquence is rejected as a criterion, but retained as a cause of truth's entry; the distinction between epistemic value and causal efficacy only partially resolves the tension.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0026","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0061","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0063","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT8","text":"Providence uses perverse causes without a full explanation of the relation between divine ordering and human culpability.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement, because the chapter reaches not complete conversion but abandonment of the sect, suspension of judgment, and ecclesial repositioning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_2:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LI_2@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_5P0L_LI_2:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 05","title":"Book V.","context":"Chapter 05","original_title":"Liber Quintus.","original_context":"Chapter 05"},"original_title":"Liber Quintus.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3","layer":"CH","title":"Book VI.","order":6,"parents":["RAW_5P0L_LI_3"],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LI_3@R001","sha256":"e9ea9c9e1c2b7056848d2e4e0c7bccfed67d654290500381e34cbc0268e4400b","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS1","text":"Textus quaerit quomodo animus, falsitate Manichaeorum liberatus sed veritati nondum assensus, ad fidem et conversionem adduci possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS2","text":"Impedimenta doctrinalia per doctrinam Ambrosii et auctoritatem Scripturae solvuntur, sed conversio differtur quia voluntas consuetudine, ambitione et concupiscentia ligatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS3","text":"Argumentatio confessionalis, diagnostica, reconstructiva et theologica eventus praeteritos tamquam operationes providentiae interpretatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS4","text":"Motus epistemicus procedit a desperatione veritatis ad dissolutionem falsae imaginis fidei catholicae, deinde ad legitimam necessitatem credendi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS5","text":"Motus moralis procedit a detectione falsi gaudii ad agnitionem servitutis voluntatis et insufficientiae virium propriarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS6","text":"Casus Alypii demonstrant correctionem, captivitatem et disciplinam iudicii per mediationes ab agentibus non intentas produci posse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS7","text":"Clausura non est conversio perfecta, sed constitutio condicionum quibus dilatio intolerabilis et gratia necessaria fiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A1","text":"Deus ordinem creaturarum et eventuum providentia regit, etiam agentibus ignaris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A2","text":"Anima extra Deum stabilem requiem et sanitatem invenire non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A3","text":"Mens a Deo aversa veritatem extra se et sub imaginibus corporeis quaerit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A4","text":"Doctrina catholica Deum forma humana aut spatio locali non terminat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A5","text":"Apparentia litteralis Scripturae sensum spiritualem et sacramentalem non exhaurit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A6","text":"Actio humana cotidiana necessario fide testium de rebus non visis innititur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A7","text":"Ratio infirma ad veritatem liquidam sola pervenire non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A8","text":"Fides auctoritate sustentata mentem ad veritatem cognoscendam purgat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A9","text":"Auctoritas Scripturae per gentes diffusa voluntati divinae ut per eam Deus credatur et quaeratur attribuitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A10","text":"Bona saecularia neque verum gaudium neque securitatem stabilem praestant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11","text":"Correctio intellectus habitum cupiditatis per se non dissolvit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A12","text":"Postulatio certitudinis demonstrativae ante omnem fidem impedit medicinam qua facultas cognoscendi sanatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A13","text":"Providentia verba non intenta et casus adversos in instrumenta correctionis convertere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A14","text":"Animus propriae firmitati confidens sub impulsu sensuum et multitudinis facile capitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A15","text":"Continentia stabilisque virtus dono divino, non solis viribus propriis, constant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A16","text":"Iudicium ex solis apparentiis ad damnationem innocentis labi potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A17","text":"Amicitia et honestas propter se dilectae ordinem bonorum voluptati corporali non reducibilem manifestant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A18","text":"Mors et iudicium futurum dilationem conversionis in periculum practicum vertunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX1","text":"Relictus Manichaeismus non est iam adepta fides catholica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX2","text":"Deus neque corpus humanum neque imago corporea in loco circumscripta est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX3","text":"Littera Scripturae non est tota Scripturae significatio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX4","text":"Fides catholica non definitur temeraria promissione scientiae quae postea fabulas credendas imponat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX5","text":"Suspensio assensus falsitatem vitat, sed veritatem neque possidet neque sanitatem constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX6","text":"Pietas neque voluptati rituali neque consuetudini hereditariae immobiliter adhaeret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX7","text":"Hilaritas mendici non est verum gaudium, sed sollicitudo ambitiosi est etiam ab illa hilaritate remotior.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX8","text":"Eruditio ad placendum hominibus ordinata non est sapientia neque ministerium doctrinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX9","text":"Desiderium matrimonii Augustini non est principaliter amor ordinis coniugalis, sed continuatio concupiscentiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX10","text":"Consortium philosophicum sine renuntiatione domesticis cupiditatibus non est vita sapientiae stabilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX11","text":"Praesentia corporis clausis oculis non efficit libertatem animi a spectaculo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX12","text":"Continentia non est facultas quam voluntas ex se certo possidet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX13","text":"Impetus animae somniantis non est eo ipso revelatio divina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX14","text":"Mors corporis non accipitur ut certa consumptio vitae animae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D1","text":"Prior accusatio fidei catholicae obiectum suum non attigerat, quia figmentum corporeum pro doctrina catholica oppugnabat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D2","text":"Apparens absurditas Scripturae desinit esse directa probatio falsitatis ubi interpretatio litteralis non habetur exhaustiva; interpretatio spiritualis tamen possibilitatem veritatis aperit, nondum veritatem demonstrat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D3","text":"Obiectio universalis contra credere sibi contradicit, quia vita ordinaria innumeris testimoniis non inspectis necessario credit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D4","text":"Fides medicinalis non cognitionem abolet, sed condicionem efficit qua intellectus infirmus ad cognitionem perduci possit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D5","text":"Defectus colloquii privati cum Ambrosio correctionem non impedit, quia praedicatio publica sufficit ad dissolvendas calumnias doctrinales.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D6","text":"Post dissolutionem anthropomorphismi et literalismi, principale impedimentum conversionis ab intellectu ad voluntatem consuetudine ligatam transfertur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D7","text":"Ambitio miseriam auget quia requiem quaerit per bona transitoria quae finem appetitus praestare non possunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D8","text":"Correctio Alypii per exemplum Circensium et captivitas eius in amphitheatro ostendunt receptionem moralem plus ab habitu et fiducia animi quam ab intentione exterioris agentis pendere.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D9","text":"Falsa comprehensio Alypii disciplinam iudicialem efficit, quia evidentia circumstantialis culpam manifestam simulare potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D10","text":"Propositum matrimonii et consilium vitae communis conversionem non efficiunt, quia ordinem novum instituere conantur sine radice concupiscentiae amputata.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D11","text":"Substitutio alterius concubinae demonstrat dolorem separationis non sanari, sed consuetudinem sub forma transitoria conservari.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D12","text":"Hypothesis beatitudinis ex perpetua voluptate corporali deficit, quia ipsa vita voluptuosa amicitiam gratuitam et bonum honestatis adhuc requirit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D13","text":"Dilatio conversionis non est mora neutra, sed continuatio servitutis sub tempore mortis incertae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD1","text":"Processus cognitionis est recursivus: aliqua fides requiritur ut mens sanetur ad iudicandum id cui ante sanationem assentiri dubitat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A12","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD2","text":"Conversio epistemica conversionem moralem antecedit: falsae accusationes corruunt antequam voluntas ab obiectis suis avelli possit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:D1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD3","text":"Mediatio moralis est non linearis: idem subiectum verbo fortuito corrigi, spectaculo sociali capi et adversitate ad prudentiam erudiri potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A16","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD4","text":"Honores, matrimonium et otium commune fiunt mechanismi dilationis quando appetitus saecularis sub nova dispositione servatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D10","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD5","text":"Retrospectus confessionalis casum, impedimentum, errorem et frustratum consilium intra unam ordinationem providentialem totalizat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD6","text":"Incertitudo mortis interrogationem speculativam in necessitatem decisionis sub cognitione incompleta convertit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A12","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A18","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX1","text":"Ratio a fide et auctoritate prorsus autonoma sufficiens esse non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX2","text":"Recta doctrina sola voluntatem convertitam efficere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX3","text":"Desiderium sibi ipsi perfecte perspicuum non est, quia libido se matrimonium, ambitio se felicitatem et dilatio se prudentiam nominare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX4","text":"Ambitus socialis moraliter neutralis non est; multitudo, amicitia et auctoritas habitum animi formant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX5","text":"Auctoritas et libertas simpliciter adversae non sunt, quia auctoritas medicinalis a falsa imagine liberare potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX6","text":"Casus tamquam eventus sine ordine finali intra interpretationem confessionalem excluditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX7","text":"Tempus dilationis vacuum non est, quia consuetudinem corroborat et morti subiacet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX8","text":"Bona divina et saecularia tamquam fines aequales componi non possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX1","text":"Vera absentia Dei excluditur; absentia experta constituitur ut caecitas animae coram praesentia occulta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX2","text":"Positio stabilis inter falsitatem relictam et conversionem recusatam non datur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX3","text":"Subiectum se ipsum per scientiam aut voluntatem sui iuris redimere non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX4","text":"Beatitudo intra totalitatem bonorum finitorum, etiam sine metu amissionis imaginatam, impossibilis habetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX5","text":"Certitudo transformationem antecedens indisponibilis est; postulatio eius ipsum iter transformationis claudit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:FGS1","text":"Prima operatio procedit: aversio a Deo → inquisitio exterior → imaginatio corporea → simulacrum doctrinae catholicae → accusatio falsa.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:FGS2","text":"Secunda operatio procedit: praedicatio Ambrosii → remotio anthropomorphismi → exegesis spiritualis → dissolutio absurditatum apparentium → veritas possibilis sed nondum assensa.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:FGS3","text":"Tertia operatio procedit: necessitas cotidiana testimonii → legitimatio credendi → auctoritas Scripturae → fides medicinalis → intellectus purgabilis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A9","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:FGS4","text":"Quarta operatio procedit: appetitus beatitudinis → honor, lucrum et connubium → anxietas → comparatio falsorum gaudiorum → detectio miseriae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:FGS5","text":"Quinta operatio procedit: clarificatio intellectus + consuetudo concupiscentiae → voluntas divisa → consilia compromissoria → procrastinatio → servitus aucta.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D10","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D11","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:FGS6","text":"Sexta operatio procedit: verbum aut eventus non intentus + dispositio recipientis → correctio aut captivitas → memoria medicinalis → humilitas iudicii et fiducia Dei.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A16","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:FGS7","text":"Ultima operatio procedit: mors et iudicium + insufficientia virium propriarum → clausura dilationis → necessitas gratiae → conversio imminens sed nondum effecta.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A18","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AF1","text":"Desperatio veritatis → Manichaeismus relictus sine fide catholica → calumniae doctrinales dissolutae → credere rehabilitatum → impedimentum ad voluntatem translatum → gratia necessaria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AF2","text":"Appetitus beatitudinis → cursus saecularis → anxietas et falsum gaudium → consilia media → ruptura consiliorum → procrastinatio → metus mortis et iudicii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AF3","text":"Indoles moralis Alypii → captivitas socialis → correctio involuntaria → fiducia sui → nova captivitas → liberatio et disciplina iudicii → aptatio ad munus futurum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME1","text":"Fides catholica ab obiecto quasi refutato in doctrinam nondum intellectam reclassificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME2","text":"Oppositio inter fidem et cognitionem solvitur, quia fides fit condicio medicinalis cognitionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME3","text":"Distinctio litterae et spiritus apparentem absurditatem in quaestionem gradus interpretationis transfert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME4","text":"Problema conversionis ab errore doctrinali ad habitum voluntatis et concupiscentiae relocatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME5","text":"Gaudium non amplius sola affectione mensuratur, sed fonte, obiecto et modo acquisitionis distinguitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME6","text":"Casus et influentia socialis ex circumstantiis exterioribus in mechanismos formationis moralis et providentiae convertuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME7","text":"Honor, matrimonium et otium commune ex solutionibus possibilibus in formas dilationis sub desiderio non sanato reclassificantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME8","text":"Tempus inquisitionis ex spatio neutro deliberationis in medium servitutis crescentis sub morte incerta mutatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ALT1","text":"In gradu superficiei, Augustinus Manichaeismum relinquit, Ambrosium audit, fidem catholicam minus absurdum iudicat et conversionem tamen differt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ALT2","text":"In gradu structurali, auctoritas, interpretatio, consuetudo, multitudo et disciplina providentiae intellectum atque voluntatem diversis modis formant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ALT3","text":"In gradu metastrategico, quaestio mutatur ab exigentia demonstrationis antecedentis ad electionem auctoritatis quae mentem sanare et vitam ordinare possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ALT4","text":"In gradu ontologico et temporali, Deus non localis et semper praesens opponitur animae dispersae, temporali, mortali et tamen ad vitam post mortem ordinatae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT1","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad restitutionem nexus inter correctionem doctrinalem, necessitatem fidei, servitutem voluntatis et operationem gratiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT2","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat: falsitas prius solvitur, auctoritas deinde rehabilitatur, impedimentum postremo in voluntate deprehenditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT3","text":"Pars firmissima est demonstratio quod prior polemica anthropomorphismum fictum, non doctrinam catholicam, oppugnaverat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT4","text":"Nexus inter testimonium cotidianum et legitimam necessitatem credendi firmus est, sed non per se determinat cui auctoritati credendum sit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT5","text":"Transitus ab auctoritate Scripturae late diffusa ad eius institutionem divinam criterio independente non plene explicatur et vi confessionali comprimitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT6","text":"Fides proponitur ut medicina rationis, sed divina auctoritas medicinae partim ex fide antecedenti in providentiam recognoscitur; circulus ut therapeuticus exhibetur, non formaliter solvitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT7","text":"Providentia eventus ordinat et tamen agentibus culpam vel meritum relinquit, sed relatio inter causalitatem divinam et responsabilitatem humanam nondum formaliter explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT8","text":"Obedientia Monnicae auctoritatem ecclesiasticam confirmat, sed effectus prohibitionis ex amore personali erga Ambrosium saltem partim pendet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT9","text":"Matrimonium ut bonum legitimum admittitur et simul ut tegumentum libidinis fungitur; criterium utriusque usus implicite, non complete, determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT10","text":"Machina ad necessitatem conversionis et gratiae pervenit, non ad conversionem ipsam; haec incompletio est terminus structuralis libri, non defectus restitutionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T142113942391Z_eea8a4c6","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"BOOK SIX.","source_sha256":"e9ea9c9e1c2b7056848d2e4e0c7bccfed67d654290500381e34cbc0268e4400b","sha256":"10c43f0b129545b75173448b076b49cc5fb1f64e947e73d7201e6d5e468a47ec","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:21:13.943447+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS1","text":"The text asks how the mind, freed from Manichaean falsehood yet not having assented to truth, may be led to faith and conversion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS2","text":"Doctrinal impediments are resolved through Ambrose's teaching and the authority of Scripture, but conversion is delayed because the will is bound by habit, ambition, and concupiscence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS3","text":"Confessional, diagnostic, reconstructive, and theological argumentation interprets past events as operations of providence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS4","text":"The epistemic movement proceeds from despair of truth to the dissolution of a false image of the Catholic faith, then to the legitimate necessity of believing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS5","text":"The moral movement proceeds from the detection of false joy to recognition of the bondage of the will and the insufficiency of one's own powers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS6","text":"Alypius's cases demonstrate that correction, captivity, and the discipline of judgment can be produced through mediations unintended by their agents.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS7","text":"The conclusion is not perfect conversion, but the establishment of conditions under which delay becomes intolerable and grace necessary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A1","text":"God governs the order of creatures and events by providence, even when agents are unaware.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A2","text":"The soul cannot find stable rest and health outside God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A3","text":"The mind turned away from God seeks truth outside itself and beneath bodily images.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A4","text":"Catholic doctrine does not delimit God by human form or local space.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A5","text":"The literal appearance of Scripture does not exhaust its spiritual and sacramental meaning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A6","text":"Everyday human action necessarily rests on faith in witnesses concerning unseen things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A7","text":"Weak reason cannot by itself attain clear truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A8","text":"Faith supported by authority purifies the mind for knowing truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A9","text":"The authority of Scripture, spread among the nations, is attributed to the divine will, so that through it God may be believed and sought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A10","text":"Secular goods provide neither true joy nor stable security.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11","text":"Correction of the intellect does not by itself dissolve the habit of desire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A12","text":"The demand for demonstrative certainty before all faith obstructs the medicine by which the capacity for knowing is healed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A13","text":"Providence can turn unintended words and adverse events into instruments of correction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A14","text":"A mind trusting in its own firmness is easily captured under the impulse of the senses and the multitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A15","text":"Continence and steadfast virtue consist in divine gift, not in one's own powers alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A16","text":"Judgment from appearances alone can fall into the condemnation of the innocent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A17","text":"Friendship and honesty loved for their own sake disclose an order of goods irreducible to bodily pleasure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:A18","text":"Death and future judgment turn delay in conversion into a practical danger.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX1","text":"Manichaeism having been abandoned is not yet Catholic faith attained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX2","text":"God is neither a human body nor a bodily image circumscribed in a place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX3","text":"The letter of Scripture is not the whole meaning of Scripture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX4","text":"Catholic faith is not defined by a rash promise of knowledge that later imposes fables to be believed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX5","text":"Suspension of assent avoids falsehood, but neither possesses truth nor establishes health.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX6","text":"Piety adheres immovably neither to ritual pleasure nor to hereditary custom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX7","text":"The cheerfulness of the beggar is not true joy, but the anxiety of the ambitious man is still further removed even from that cheerfulness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX8","text":"Learning ordered toward pleasing men is neither wisdom nor a ministry of teaching.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX9","text":"Augustine's desire for marriage is not principally love of the order of marriage, but the continuation of concupiscence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX10","text":"A philosophical fellowship without renouncing domestic desires is not a stable life of wisdom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX11","text":"The presence of the body with closed eyes does not effect the mind's freedom from the spectacle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX12","text":"Continence is not a capacity that the will certainly possesses of itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX13","text":"The impulse of the dreaming soul is not thereby a divine revelation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX14","text":"The death of the body is not received as the certain extinction of the soul's life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D1","text":"The earlier accusation against the Catholic faith had not reached its object, because it attacked a bodily fabrication in place of Catholic doctrine.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D2","text":"The apparent absurdity of Scripture ceases to be direct proof of falsehood when literal interpretation is not held exhaustive; spiritual interpretation nevertheless opens the possibility of truth, not yet demonstrating truth.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D3","text":"The universal objection against believing contradicts itself, because ordinary life necessarily trusts countless unexamined testimonies.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D4","text":"Medicinal faith does not abolish knowledge, but makes possible the condition in which weak intellect can be led to knowledge.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D5","text":"The lack of private conversation with Ambrose does not impede correction, because public preaching suffices to dissolve doctrinal calumnies.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D6","text":"After the dissolution of anthropomorphism and literalism, the principal impediment to conversion is transferred from the intellect to the will bound by habit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D7","text":"Ambition increases misery because it seeks rest through transitory goods that cannot provide the end of desire.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D8","text":"Alypius's correction through the example of the Circus Games and his captivity in the amphitheater show that moral reception depends more on habit and confidence of mind than on the intention of the external agent.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D9","text":"Alypius's false apprehension produces judicial discipline, because circumstantial evidence can simulate manifest guilt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D10","text":"The intention of marriage and the plan of common life do not effect conversion, because they attempt to establish a new order without the root of concupiscence having been cut off.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D11","text":"The substitution of another concubine demonstrates that the pain of separation is not healed, but that habit is preserved under a transitory form.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D12","text":"The hypothesis of happiness from perpetual bodily pleasure fails, because even the pleasurable life itself still requires gratuitous friendship and the good of honesty.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:D13","text":"Delay in conversion is not neutral postponement, but continuation of bondage under the time of uncertain death.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD1","text":"The process of knowledge is recursive: some faith is required for the mind to be healed so as to judge that to which it doubts whether to assent before healing.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A12","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD2","text":"Epistemic conversion precedes moral conversion: false accusations collapse before the will can be torn away from its objects.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:D1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD3","text":"Moral mediation is non-linear: the same subject can be corrected by a chance word, captured by a social spectacle, and instructed in prudence by adversity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A16","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD4","text":"Honors, marriage, and common leisure become mechanisms of delay when secular desire is preserved under a new arrangement.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D10","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD5","text":"Confessional retrospection totalizes chance, impediment, error, and frustrated plan within a single providential ordering.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD6","text":"The uncertainty of death transforms speculative inquiry into the necessity of decision under incomplete knowledge.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A12","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A18","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX1","text":"Reason wholly autonomous from faith and authority cannot be sufficient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX2","text":"Right doctrine alone cannot bring about a converted will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX3","text":"Desire is not perfectly transparent to itself, because lust can call itself marriage, ambition can call itself happiness, and delay can call itself prudence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX4","text":"The social environment is not morally neutral; the multitude, friendship, and authority shape the habit of the mind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX5","text":"Authority and freedom are not simply opposed, because medicinal authority can liberate from a false image.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX6","text":"Chance as an event without final order is excluded within confessional interpretation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX7","text":"The time of delay is not empty, because it reinforces habit and is subject to death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX8","text":"Divine and secular goods cannot be composed as equal ends.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX1","text":"The true absence of God is excluded; experienced absence is constituted as the soul's blindness before hidden presence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX2","text":"No stable position is given between abandoned falsehood and refused conversion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX3","text":"The subject cannot redeem itself through knowledge or self-governing will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX4","text":"Happiness within the totality of finite goods, even imagined without fear of loss, is held impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX5","text":"Certainty preceding transformation is unavailable; its demand closes the very path of transformation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:FGS1","text":"The first operation proceeds: turning away from God → external inquiry → bodily imagination → simulacrum of Catholic doctrine → false accusation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:FGS2","text":"The second operation proceeds: Ambrose's preaching → removal of anthropomorphism → spiritual exegesis → dissolution of apparent absurdities → truth possible but not yet assented to.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:FGS3","text":"The third operation proceeds: everyday necessity of testimony → legitimation of believing → authority of Scripture → medicinal faith → intellect capable of purification.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A9","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:FGS4","text":"The fourth operation proceeds: desire for happiness → honor, profit, and marriage → anxiety → comparison of false joys → detection of misery.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:FGS5","text":"The fifth operation proceeds: clarification of intellect + habit of concupiscence → divided will → compromising plans → procrastination → increased bondage.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D10","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D11","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:FGS6","text":"The sixth operation proceeds: unintended word or event + disposition of the recipient → correction or captivity → medicinal memory → humility of judgment and trust in God.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A16","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:FGS7","text":"The final operation proceeds: death and judgment + insufficiency of one's own powers → closure of delay → necessity of grace → conversion imminent but not yet effected.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A18","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AF1","text":"Despair of truth → Manichaeism abandoned without Catholic faith → doctrinal calumnies dissolved → believing rehabilitated → impediment transferred to the will → grace necessary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AF2","text":"Desire for happiness → secular career → anxiety and false joy → intermediate plans → collapse of plans → procrastination → fear of death and judgment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:AF3","text":"Alypius's moral character → social captivity → involuntary correction → self-confidence → new captivity → liberation and discipline of judgment → adaptation to a future office.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME1","text":"Catholic faith is reclassified from an object seemingly refuted into a doctrine not yet understood.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME2","text":"The opposition between faith and knowledge is dissolved, because faith becomes a medicinal condition of knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME3","text":"The distinction between letter and spirit transfers apparent absurdity into a question of the level of interpretation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME4","text":"The problem of conversion is relocated from doctrinal error to the habit of will and concupiscence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME5","text":"Joy is no longer measured by affection alone, but distinguished by source, object, and mode of acquisition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME6","text":"Chance and social influence are transformed from external circumstances into mechanisms of moral formation and providence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME7","text":"Honor, marriage, and common leisure are reclassified from possible solutions into forms of delay under unhealed desire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME8","text":"The time of inquiry is transformed from a neutral space of deliberation into a medium of growing bondage under uncertain death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ALT1","text":"At the surface level, Augustine abandons Manichaeism, listens to Ambrose, judges the Catholic faith less absurd, and nevertheless delays conversion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ALT2","text":"At the structural level, authority, interpretation, habit, the multitude, and the discipline of providence form intellect and will in different ways.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ALT3","text":"At the metastrategic level, the question changes from the demand for prior demonstration to the choice of an authority able to heal the mind and order life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:ALT4","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, the non-local and ever-present God is opposed to the scattered, temporal, mortal soul, yet one ordered toward life after death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to reconstruct the connection between doctrinal correction, the necessity of faith, the bondage of the will, and the operation of grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT2","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: falsehood is first dissolved, authority is then rehabilitated, and the impediment is finally discovered in the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT3","text":"The strongest part is the demonstration that the earlier polemic had attacked a fictitious anthropomorphism, not Catholic doctrine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT4","text":"The connection between everyday testimony and the legitimate necessity of believing is firm, but does not by itself determine which authority should be believed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT5","text":"The transition from the widely diffused authority of Scripture to its divine institution is not fully explained by an independent criterion and is compressed by confessional force.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT6","text":"Faith is proposed as the medicine of reason, but the divine authority of the medicine is recognized partly from prior faith in providence; the circle is presented as therapeutic, not formally resolved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT7","text":"Providence orders events and yet leaves agents blame or merit, but the relation between divine causality and human responsibility is not yet formally explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT8","text":"Monnica's obedience confirms ecclesiastical authority, but the effect of the prohibition depends at least in part on her personal love for Ambrose.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT9","text":"Marriage is admitted as a legitimate good and at the same time functions as a covering for lust; the criterion of either use is determined implicitly, not completely.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT10","text":"The mechanism arrives at the necessity of conversion and grace, not at conversion itself; this incompleteness is the structural terminus of the book, not a defect of reconstruction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LI_3@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_5P0L_LI_3:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 06","title":"Book VI.","context":"Chapter 06","original_title":"Liber Sextus.","original_context":"Chapter 06"},"original_title":"Liber Sextus.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4","layer":"CH","title":"Book VII.","order":7,"parents":["RAW_5P0L_LI_4"],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LI_4@R001","sha256":"3131845c166a65439e15e7699620c04a78a9ef54802d7a7fac603ac6009ce47a","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS1","text":"Textus solvere conatur quomodo malum esse possit, si Deus est incommutabile summum bonum et omnium naturarum creator.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS2","text":"Malum constituitur non substantia, sed privatio boni et perversio voluntatis a bono superiore ad inferiora.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS3","text":"Argumentatio diagnostica, reductiva et reconstructiva exemplaria corporea, dualistica, astrologica et intellectualistica successive excludit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS4","text":"Motus primus a contradictionibus incorruptibilitatis Dei ad reiectionem substantiae malae et causalitatis astralis procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS5","text":"Motus secundus ab interiori ascensu ad veritatem incorpoream transit, deinde ex infirmitate adhesionis necessitatem mediationis elicit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS6","text":"Clausura Platonicam cognitionem patriae a Christiana via humilitatis, gratiae et liberationis distinguit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A1","text":"Deus summum et optimum bonum est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A2","text":"Incorruptibile ac incommutabile corruptibili ac mutabili verissime praeferuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A3","text":"Voluntas et potentia Dei idem sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4","text":"Nulla natura est nisi a Deo creata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5","text":"Quidquid est, inquantum est, bonum est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A6","text":"Corruptio non nocet nisi bonum minuendo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A7","text":"Omnimoda privatio boni rei esse aufert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A8","text":"Creaturae finitae, mutabiles et inaequales unum ordinem constituunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A9","text":"Res parti non conveniens potest in se bona et alteri parti congrua esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A10","text":"Voluntas propria eadem certitudine cognoscitur qua vita propria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A11","text":"Culpa actui voluntario, poena passioni involuntariae competit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A12","text":"Iudicium de mutabilibus normam incommutabilem supra mentem mutabilem requirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13","text":"Veritas incommutabilis neque spatiis continetur neque a mente creata efficitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A14","text":"Conspectus veritatis non sufficit ad stabilem veritatis fruitionem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A15","text":"Superbia et consuetudo carnalis mentem a viso bono retrahunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A16","text":"Libri Platonicorum aeternitatem Verbi ostendunt, incarnationis autem humilitatem et redemptionem non tradunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17","text":"Incarnatio Christi et gratia Scripturarum intellectum humiliant, sanant et ad fruitionem ducunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A18","text":"Eadem astrorum configuratio cum contrariis vitae eventibus componi potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX1","text":"Deus neque figura humana neque corpus per infinita spatia diffusum est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX2","text":"Spatiis carere non idem est ac nihil esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX3","text":"Natura tenebrarum Deo coaeterna aut nociva constitui non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX4","text":"Malum ex materia increata quam Deus corrigere non potuerit oriri non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX5","text":"Divinatio astrologica ars causaliter certa non est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX6","text":"Inconvenientia localis creaturam malam secundum substantiam non facit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX7","text":"Cognitio Platonicorum neque salutem neque stabilem Dei fruitionem per se confert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX8","text":"Christus non est tantum homo sapientissimus perfectiore participatione praeditus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX9","text":"Christus non est Deus carne indutus sine anima et mente humana.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX10","text":"Falsitas non est res creata, sed aestimatio qua aliquid putatur esse quod non est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:D1","text":"Deus corrumpi, violari aut mutari nullo modo potest; alioquin aliquid eo melius cogitari posset.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:D2","text":"Certamen Manichaeum aut Deum corruptibilem facit aut causam certaminis tollit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3","text":"Malum substantia esse non potest, quia omnis substantia aliquod bonum habet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:D4","text":"Creaturae esse participant: sunt quia a Deo sunt, sed non sunt ipsum esse quia mutabiles sunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","text":"Iniquitas est voluntatis aversio a summo bono et conversio ad inferiora.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:D6","text":"Mala particularia bonitatem universi non destruunt, quia eadem res alibi congrua et in se bona esse potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","text":"Ascensus a sensibilibus ad mentem iudicantem veritatem incommutabilem demonstrat, sed infirmitatem contemplantis non sanat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A12","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8","text":"Platonici terminum itineris ostendunt, Christus autem et gratia viam, robur et adhesionem praebent.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A16","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:D9","text":"Vera astrologorum praedictio arti attribui non potest, ubi eadem signa eventus contrarios patiuntur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD1","text":"Theoria mali tres gradus componit: malum ontologice est privatio, moraliter voluntatis perversio, poenaliter passio iusto iudicio ordinata.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD2","text":"Reiectio dualismi et determinismi simul bonitatem creatoris et responsabilitatem creaturae tuetur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD3","text":"Cognitio salutaris duplicem operationem requirit: veritatem conspicere et subiectum sanari ut visae veritati adhaereat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD4","text":"Incarnatio veritatem ontologice superiorem in viam anthropologice congruam convertit, quia humilitas superbiam sanat et infirmum ad superiora levat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD5","text":"Ordo universalis omnem discordiam creatam intra bonitatem totius includit et exterioritatem ontologicam mali excludit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD6","text":"Creatio non succedit otio divino intra tempus, quia ipsa temporum spatia ab operatione manentis Dei dependent.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX1","text":"Falsum esse oportet esse et spatialiter extendi converti.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX2","text":"Falsum esse oportet praesentiam Dei corporibus secundum magnitudinem dividi.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX3","text":"Falsum esse oportet creaturam inferiorem posse summum bonum invito Deo mutare.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX4","text":"Falsum esse oportet malum rationem positivam sui in aliqua natura habere.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX5","text":"Falsum esse oportet mentem mutabilem autonomam mensuram veritatis esse.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A12","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX6","text":"Falsum esse oportet cognitionem termini facultatem perveniendi et permanendi secum ferre.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A16","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX7","text":"Falsum esse oportet causas astrales culpam a voluntate ad ordinem externum transferre posse.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX8","text":"Falsum esse oportet displicentiam partis iudicium sufficiens de bonitate totius praebere.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A9","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SNX1","text":"Systema nullum ontologicum extra ordinem a Deo creatum admittit unde malum irruere possit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SNX2","text":"Systema transitum a ratione superba ad stabilem Dei possessionem sine humiliatione et mediatione praecludit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SNX3","text":"Systema causam positivam primae voluntatis malae admittere non potest, quia talis causa aut natura bona esset aut dualismum restitueret.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SNX4","text":"Ante tempus et extra creaturam nulla regio substantialis relinquitur in qua Deus, materia et malum quasi res coordinatae collocentur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS1","text":"Machina invariantes statuit: Deus est summum bonum, incorruptibilis, omnipotens et creator omnis naturae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS2","text":"Exemplaria corporea, dualistica et astrologica contra invariantes probantur atque contradictione eliminantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS3","text":"Iter cognitionis a sensibilibus per animam et rationem ad normam incommutabilem supra mentem ascendit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A12","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS4","text":"Esse a Deo derivatum bonitatem implicat; corruptio bonum minuit; privatio totalis esse tollit; igitur malum substantia non est.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A7","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS5","text":"Malum morale localizatur in motu voluntatis quo subiectum a superiore ordine ad inferiora detorquetur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS6","text":"Inconvenientiae particulares in ordinem totius referuntur, quo bonitas creaturarum sine aequalitate earum servatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A9","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS7","text":"Visio veritatis infirmitatem contemplantis detegit; infirmitas superbiam et consuetudinem indicat; haec diagnosis mediationem humilem requirit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS8","text":"Veritas Platonica a Scriptura recipitur, sed per incarnationem, confessionem et gratiam in viam liberationis convertitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A16","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:AF1","text":"Motus principalis procedit: imaginatio corporea → contradictio incorruptibilitatis → reiectio dualismi → quaestio voluntatis → ascensus ad veritatem incorpoream → definitio mali ut privationis → insufficientia visionis → Christus mediator → gratia Paulina.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS7","CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:AF2","text":"Submotus astrologicus procedit: eadem signa → eventus contrarii → defectus artis → restitutio causalitatis voluntariae et providentiae occultae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A18","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D9","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME1","text":"Infinitas Dei a magnitudine spatiali ad eminentiam incorpoream et causalitatem omnitenentem transfertur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME2","text":"Malum ex genere substantiarum in genus privationum et motuum voluntatis reclassificatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME3","text":"Interrogatio unde malum ab origine materialis rei ad defectionem agentis voluntarii convertitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME4","text":"Oppositio bonum–malum ut conflictus duarum naturarum corruit et ordine graduum boni substituitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME5","text":"Philosophia et revelatio non ut duae cosmologiae aequales, sed ut visio termini et via sanans distinguuntur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A16","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME6","text":"Cognitio dividitur in demonstrationem obiecti, capacitatem videndi et facultatem permanendi in viso.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A12","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME7","text":"Astrologia a causa rerum ad coniecturam sine potestate explicativa reclassificatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A18","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME8","text":"Haeresis fit instrumentum differentiale quo limites doctrinae de Christo manifestantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ALT1","text":"Gradus superficiei continet quaestionem originis mali, dissolutionem opinionum priorum et transitum a Platonicis ad Paulum.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ALT2","text":"Gradus structuralis componit participationem essendi, corruptionem ut privationem, ordinem universi et voluntatem ut locum culpae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ALT3","text":"Gradus metastrategicus discernit inter doctrinam quae obiectum ostendit et mediationem quae subiectum ad obiectum idoneum efficit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ALT4","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis verum esse in immutabilitate collocat, creaturas participatione subsistere statuit et tempora operationi Dei subordinat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad reicienda exemplaria corporea et dualistica, ad malum privative definiendum et ad mediationem Christi introducendam.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT2","text":"Structura interne cohaeret dum gradus ontologicus, moralis et poenalis mali distincti manent.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT3","text":"Firmissimae commissurae sunt reductio Manichaeorum et deductio qua substantia mali ex logica corruptionis excluditur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT4","text":"Origo primae voluntatis malae nondum plene determinatur: perversio voluntatis describitur, sed causa primae defectionis positiva non redditur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT5","text":"Bonitas universi praesupponit omnes inconvenientias particulares in ordine totali congruentiam habere, quam textus exemplis confirmat sed universaliter non demonstrat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D6","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT6","text":"Tractatio astrologiae inter sortem et occultam providentiam tensionem servat, nisi sors ad solum defectum artis humanae restringatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D9","CH_5P0L_LI_4:AF2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT7","text":"Transitus a visione intellectuali ad necessitatem mediatoris experientia infirmitatis firmatur potius quam deductione ontologica completa.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT8","text":"Distinctio inter Verbum immutabile et totum hominem in Christo limites errorum constituit, sed modum unionis nondum formaliter explicat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT9","text":"Restitutio motum verum servat: exclusio falsarum ontologiarum praecedit theoriam privationis, quam sequitur correctio soteriologica intellectus.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AF1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T142143627488Z_522ae3e5","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"BOOK SEVEN.","source_sha256":"3131845c166a65439e15e7699620c04a78a9ef54802d7a7fac603ac6009ce47a","sha256":"f47f33d898cf050785d713997b30beb4f5a7de8f2252b21c9809d425c1b8bc6f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:21:43.629366+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumentative Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS1","text":"The text endeavors to resolve how evil can exist if God is the immutable highest good and creator of all natures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS2","text":"Evil is constituted not as a substance, but as a privation of good and a perversion of the will from the higher good toward lower things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS3","text":"The diagnostic, reductive, and reconstructive argument successively excludes corporeal, dualistic, astrological, and intellectualist models.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS4","text":"The first movement proceeds from the contradictions of God's incorruptibility to the rejection of evil substance and astral causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS5","text":"The second movement passes from an inward ascent to incorporeal truth, then infers from the weakness of adhesion the necessity of mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS6","text":"The conclusion distinguishes Platonic knowledge of the homeland from the Christian way of humility, grace, and liberation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0080","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A1","text":"God is the highest and best good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A2","text":"The incorruptible and immutable are most truly preferred to the corruptible and mutable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A3","text":"God's will and power are the same.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4","text":"No nature exists unless created by God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5","text":"Whatever is, insofar as it is, is good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A6","text":"Corruption harms only by diminishing good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A7","text":"The complete privation of good removes a thing's being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A8","text":"Finite, mutable, and unequal creatures constitute one order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A9","text":"A thing unsuitable to one part can be good in itself and fitting to another part.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A10","text":"One's own will is known with the same certainty as one's own life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A11","text":"Fault belongs to voluntary action, punishment to involuntary suffering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A12","text":"Judgment concerning mutable things requires an immutable norm above the mutable mind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0069","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13","text":"Immutable truth is neither contained by spaces nor produced by a created mind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A14","text":"The sight of truth does not suffice for stable enjoyment of truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A15","text":"Pride and carnal habit draw the mind back from the good it has seen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A16","text":"The books of the Platonists show the eternity of the Word, but do not convey the humility of the incarnation and redemption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17","text":"The incarnation of Christ and the grace of the Scriptures humble, heal, and lead the understanding to enjoyment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:A18","text":"The same configuration of the stars can coincide with contrary events of life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX1","text":"God is neither a human figure nor a body diffused through infinite spaces.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX2","text":"To lack spatial extension is not the same as to be nothing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX3","text":"A nature of darkness coeternal with God or harmful to God cannot be posited.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0009","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX4","text":"Evil cannot arise from uncreated matter that God could not correct.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX5","text":"Astrological divination is not a causally certain art.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX6","text":"Local unsuitability does not make a creature evil according to substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX7","text":"Knowledge of the Platonists confers neither salvation nor stable enjoyment of God by itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX8","text":"Christ is not merely a most wise man endowed with more perfect participation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX9","text":"Christ is not God clothed in flesh without a human soul and mind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0076","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX10","text":"Falsehood is not a created thing, but an estimation by which something is thought to be that is not.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:D1","text":"God can in no way be corrupted, violated, or changed; otherwise something better than him could be conceived.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:D2","text":"The Manichaean conflict either makes God corruptible or removes the cause of the conflict.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3","text":"Evil cannot be a substance, because every substance has some good.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:D4","text":"Creatures participate in being: they are because they are from God, but they are not being itself because they are mutable.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0053","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","text":"Iniquity is the will's turning away from the highest good and turning toward lower things.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:D6","text":"Particular evils do not destroy the goodness of the universe, because the same thing can be fitting elsewhere and good in itself.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","text":"The ascent from sensible things to the mind judging demonstrates immutable truth, but does not heal the weakness of the contemplator.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A12","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8","text":"The Platonists show the destination of the journey, but Christ and grace provide the way, strength, and adhesion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A16","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:D9","text":"A true prediction by astrologers cannot be attributed to their art where the same signs admit contrary events.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD1","text":"The theory of evil combines three levels: ontologically, evil is privation; morally, a perversion of the will; penally, suffering ordered by just judgment.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD2","text":"The rejection of dualism and determinism simultaneously preserves the goodness of the creator and the responsibility of the creature.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD3","text":"Salvific knowledge requires a twofold operation: to behold truth and for the subject to be healed so as to adhere to the truth beheld.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD4","text":"The incarnation converts ontologically higher truth into an anthropologically fitting way, because humility heals pride and raises the weak toward higher things.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD5","text":"The universal order includes every created discord within the goodness of the whole and excludes the ontological exteriority of evil.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD6","text":"Creation does not succeed divine repose within time, because the very intervals of times depend upon the operation of the abiding God.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX1","text":"It must be false that to be is convertible with being spatially extended.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX2","text":"It must be false that God's presence in bodies is divided according to magnitude.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX3","text":"It must be false that a lower creature can change the highest good against God's will.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX4","text":"It must be false that evil has a positive rationale of itself in any nature.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX5","text":"It must be false that the mutable mind is an autonomous measure of truth.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A12","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0069","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX6","text":"It must be false that knowledge of the destination carries with it the capacity to arrive and remain there.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A16","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0080","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX7","text":"It must be false that astral causes can transfer fault from the will to an external order.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX8","text":"It must be false that the displeasure of a part provides a sufficient judgment concerning the goodness of the whole.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A9","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SNX1","text":"The system admits no ontological outside beyond the order created by God from which evil could break in.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SNX2","text":"The system precludes passage from proud reason to stable possession of God without humbling and mediation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SNX3","text":"The system cannot admit a positive cause of the first evil will, because such a cause would either be a good nature or restore dualism.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:SNX4","text":"Before time and outside creation, no substantial region remains in which God, matter, and evil might be placed as though coordinated things.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS1","text":"The engine establishes invariants: God is the highest good, incorruptible, omnipotent, and creator of every nature.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS2","text":"Corporeal, dualistic, and astrological models are tested against the invariants and eliminated by contradiction.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS3","text":"The path of knowledge ascends from sensible things through soul and reason to an immutable norm above the mind.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A12","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS4","text":"Being derived from God entails goodness; corruption diminishes good; total privation removes being; therefore evil is not a substance.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A7","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS5","text":"Moral evil is localized in the movement of the will by which the subject is twisted from the higher order toward lower things.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS6","text":"Particular unsuitabilities are referred to the order of the whole, through which the goodness of creatures is preserved without their equality.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A9","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS7","text":"The vision of truth reveals the weakness of the contemplator; weakness indicates pride and habit; this diagnosis requires humble mediation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS8","text":"Platonic truth is received from Scripture, but through incarnation, confession, and grace is converted into a way of liberation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A16","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:AF1","text":"The principal movement proceeds: corporeal imagination → contradiction of incorruptibility → rejection of dualism → question of the will → ascent to incorporeal truth → definition of evil as privation → insufficiency of vision → Christ the mediator → Pauline grace.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS7","CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:AF2","text":"The astrological submovement proceeds: same signs → contrary events → failure of the art → restoration of voluntary causality and hidden providence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A18","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D9","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME1","text":"God's infinity is transferred from spatial magnitude to incorporeal eminence and all-sustaining causality.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME2","text":"Evil is reclassified from the genus of substances into the genus of privations and movements of the will.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME3","text":"The question whence evil is converted from the origin of a material thing to the falling away of a voluntary agent.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME4","text":"The opposition good–evil as a conflict of two natures collapses and is replaced by an order of degrees of good.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME5","text":"Philosophy and revelation are distinguished not as two equal cosmologies, but as a vision of the destination and a healing way.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A16","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0080","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME6","text":"Knowledge is divided into demonstration of the object, capacity to see, and ability to remain in what is seen.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A12","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME7","text":"Astrology is reclassified from a cause of things to conjecture without explanatory power.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A18","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME8","text":"Heresy becomes a differential instrument through which the boundaries of doctrine concerning Christ are made manifest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ALT1","text":"The surface level contains the question of the origin of evil, the dissolution of prior opinions, and the transition from the Platonists to Paul.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ALT2","text":"The structural level combines participation in being, corruption as privation, the order of the universe, and the will as the locus of fault.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ALT3","text":"The metastrategic level discerns between doctrine that shows the object and mediation that renders the subject suited to the object.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:ALT4","text":"The ontological and temporal level locates true being in immutability, establishes that creatures subsist by participation, and subordinates times to God's operation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reject corporeal and dualistic models, to define evil privatively, and to introduce the mediation of Christ.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT2","text":"The structure coheres internally so long as the ontological, moral, and penal levels of evil remain distinct.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT3","text":"The strongest joints are the reduction of the Manichaeans and the deduction by which the substance of evil is excluded from the logic of corruption.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT4","text":"The origin of the first evil will is not yet fully determined: the perversion of the will is described, but no positive cause of the first falling away is given.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0066","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT5","text":"The goodness of the universe presupposes that all particular unsuitabilities have fittingness in the total order, which the text confirms by examples but does not demonstrate universally.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D6","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT6","text":"The treatment of astrology retains a tension between chance and hidden providence, unless chance is restricted to the mere failure of human art.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D9","CH_5P0L_LI_4:AF2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT7","text":"The transition from intellectual vision to the necessity of a mediator is strengthened by the experience of weakness rather than by a complete ontological deduction.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT8","text":"The distinction between the immutable Word and the whole human being in Christ establishes the limits of errors, but does not yet formally explain the mode of union.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: the exclusion of false ontologies precedes the theory of privation, which is followed by the soteriological correction of the understanding.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AF1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_4:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LI_4@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_5P0L_LI_4:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 07","title":"Book VII.","context":"Chapter 07","original_title":"Liber Septimus.","original_context":"Chapter 07"},"original_title":"Liber Septimus.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO","layer":"CH","title":"Book VIII.","order":8,"parents":["RAW_5P0L_LIBO"],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LIBO@R001","sha256":"267cc000c2a7946985c91899b81d4742e72222aa2370546b2152e28108a0d445","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS1","text":"Textus quaerit quomodo homo de Deo iam certus vitam temporalem mutare nequeat et qua operatione voluntas divisa ad conversionem integram perducatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS2","text":"Conversio non ut acquisitio novae doctrinae, sed ut sanatio et liberatio voluntatis consuetudine divisae per gratiam constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS3","text":"Argumentatio confessionalis simul est reconstructiva, genealogica, diagnostica, polemica adversus dualismum Manichaeum et strategica circa exemplorum vim.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS4","text":"Motus procedit a certitudine metaphysica ad impotentiam practicam, ab exemplis alienarum conversionum ad sui accusationem, atque a genealogia consuetudinis ad discrimen voluntatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS5","text":"Conflictus interior in unius animae voluntates partiales resolvitur, ne in duas naturas vel substantias contrarias transferatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS6","text":"Crisis consummatur cum admonitio exterior per Scripturam in praeceptum personale recipitur, dubitatio solvitur et voluntas ad renuntiationem temporalium integratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A1","text":"Augustino iam certum est omnem substantiam a Deo incorruptibili per Verbum provenire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2","text":"Certitudo de Deo per se nec stabilitatem in Deo nec rectam institutionem vitae temporalis efficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A3","text":"Eadem anima potest bonum aeternum veritate praeponere et bonum temporale familiaritate retinere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","text":"Voluntas perversa generat libidinem, libido consuetudinem, consuetudo non repugnata necessitatem servitutis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A5","text":"Vis consuetudinis praesens ex voluntariis actibus orta est atque involuntariam passionem cum imputabilitate coniungit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6","text":"Contrariae voluntates sunt partes incompletae unius voluntatis aegrotantis, non operationes duarum naturarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A7","text":"In actu qui sola voluntate perficitur, integre velle est iam facere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A8","text":"Gratia Dei per Iesum Christum sola catenam consuetudinis rumpit et voluntatem sanat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A9","text":"Narrationes conversionum alienarum sunt media quibus Deus imitationem accendit, excusationes dissolvit et subiectum sibi ipsi opponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A10","text":"Conversio Victorini per publicam professionem ecclesialem timorem auctoritatis paganae vincit et fidem socialiter agnoscibilem facit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A11","text":"Plena Augustini conversio secum fert abdicationem spei saecularis et consilii coniugalis, non solam mutationem opinionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A12","text":"Gaudium creaturae de re perdita ac reddita augetur secundum magnitudinem praecedentis periculi vel molestiae, Deo tamen invariabili.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A13","text":"Conversio hominis late noti maiorem effectum communem producit quia plures movet et pluribus exemplum praebet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14","text":"Admonitio Scripturae, cum ut sibi divinitus directa recipitur, potest voluntati praeceptum determinatum et securitatem finalem praebere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX1","text":"Mora conversionis non amplius ex incertitudine veritatis explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX2","text":"Duae voluntates adversantes duas animas vel naturas contrarias non probant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX3","text":"Omnis deliberatio non est certamen inter principium bonum et principium malum, quia voluntates plures omnes bonae vel omnes malae esse possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX4","text":"Consuetudo non est vis ab agente origine aliena.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX5","text":"Involuntaria consuetudinis violentia agentem ab antecedenti responsabilitate non eximit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX6","text":"Conversio non est motus localis aut opus corporis, sed integratio voluntatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX7","text":"Eruditio, eloquentia et dignitas socialis conversionem neque efficiunt neque eius mensuram constituunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX8","text":"Sola praesentia intra parietes ecclesiae Christianum non constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0012","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX9","text":"Fides secreta quae confessionem metu hominum recusat formam publicae conversionis nondum implet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX10","text":"Maius gaudium de nobili converso non oritur ex maiori dignitate personae coram Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX11","text":"Coniugium universaliter prohibitum non est, quamquam continentia Augustino ut via melior proponitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX12","text":"Continentia propria subiecti virtute effici non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX13","text":"Formulae morae, velut promissum conversionis futurae, non sunt decisionis initium determinatum, sed continuatio servitutis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:D1","text":"Sublata dubitatione metaphysica, impedimentum conversionis ex ordine cognitionis ad ordinem voluntatis transfertur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:D2","text":"Subiectum catenam patitur quam ipse per actus antecedentes fabricavit; servitus igitur simul est passio praesens et effectus culpae praeteritae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:D3","text":"Conflictus carnis et spiritus exprimit inaequalem unius animae adhaesionem bonis contrariis, non divisionem substantiae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:D4","text":"Exempla Victorini, Antonii et aulicorum demonstrant conversionem statim possibilem esse atque vetustatem excusationum Augustini in accusationem sui convertunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:D5","text":"Gratia voluntatem non substituit, sed eam ab incomplete volendo ad actum integralem perducit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:D6","text":"Publica conversio personae auctoritate praeditae instrumenta pristinae dominationis in instrumenta confessionis et imitationis convertit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:D7","text":"Maius gaudium de Victorino ex magnitudine liberationis et multiplicatione effectuum nascitur, non ex favore divitibus aut nobilibus concesso.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:D8","text":"Liberatio gratiae veritatem cognitam in novum ordinem vitae temporalis traducit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:D9","text":"Exemplum Antonii praebet formam interpretativam qua vox fortuita et lectio occurrens in admonitionem divinam personalem convertuntur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD1","text":"Psychologia moralis textus temporaliter construitur: idem subiectum per actus suos sedimentatur, dividitur et sanatur, sine mutatione in duas substantias.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD2","text":"Responsabilitas et dependentia a gratia non excluduntur: homo causam servitutis participat, sed principium liberationis sibi solus praebere nequit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD3","text":"Conversio est eventus punctiformis ex longa accumulatione mediationum ortus: exempla, pudor, autoaccusatio et Scriptura ad unum actum integrum comprimuntur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD4","text":"Conversio efficit circuitum exemplaritatis: conversus publice visibilis alios accendit, quorum conversio gaudium et vim imitativam ulterius multiplicat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD5","text":"Scriptura vim decisivam non tantum ex significatione generali, sed ex receptione temporali ut verbum nunc subiecto directum acquirit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD6","text":"Dilatio non conservat statum neutrum, sed consuetudinem veterem roborat; momentum conversionis ideo oppositionem inter nunc et indefinitum postea instituit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX1","text":"Ratio doctrinaliter illuminata non est causa sufficiens actionis rectae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX2","text":"Malum morale non requirit substantiam malam, alteram mentem aut principium ontologice contrarium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX3","text":"Necessitas consuetudinis non est necessitas naturalis ab initio data.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX4","text":"Gratia non est coactio externa quae voluntatem supervacaneam reddit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX5","text":"Conversio mere privata et socialiter invisibilis non complet formam confessionis quam exempla textus postulant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX6","text":"Mora deliberativa non est innocentia, quia ipsa retentio veteris vitae effectum electionis habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX7","text":"Continentia non est mera sterilitas vel subtractio voluptatis, sed forma fecundae vitae in Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX8","text":"Variatio gaudii in creaturis mutationem scientiae aut essentiae divinae non implicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SNX1","text":"Nullum ego neutrum extra voluntates contendentes stat; subiectum in utraque adest, quamquam se magis cum voluntate approbata identificat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SNX2","text":"Nullus terminus stabilis inter conversionem et non-conversionem datur, quia voluntas semiplena actum qui integrum velle requirit perficere nequit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SNX3","text":"Voluntas non possidet fundamentum autonomum ex quo se ipsam a propria divisione extrahat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SNX4","text":"Futurum indefinitum non praebet spatium conversioni reservatum, sed praesentem recusationem abscondit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SNX5","text":"Salus non clauditur intra conscientiam singularem, quia confessio, exemplum, auctoritas et gaudium ecclesiale ad ipsam operationem conversionis pertinent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:FGS1","text":"Prima operatio dissonantiam constituit: certitudo de Deo → instabilitas vitae → translatio quaestionis a cognitione ad voluntatem.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:FGS2","text":"Secunda operatio servitutem genealogice generat: voluntas perversa → libido → consuetudo → necessitas → voluntas divisa.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:FGS3","text":"Tertia operatio exempla in iudicium sui convertit: narratio alienae conversionis → possibilitas praesentis mutationis → ruina excusationum → pudor.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:FGS4","text":"Quarta operatio conflictum ontologice restringit: voluntates adversantes → partialitas utriusque → una anima aegrotans → exclusio dualismi.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:FGS5","text":"Quinta operatio limen decisionis producit: autoaccusatio → exhaustio argumentorum → horror amissionis consuetudinis → incapax voluntas semiplena → imploratio liberationis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:FGS6","text":"Sexta operatio voluntatem claudit: vox admonens → exemplar Antonii → lectio apostolica → praeceptum personale → securitas → actus integer.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:FGS7","text":"Ultima operatio eventum socialiter stabilit: renuntiatio temporalium → communicatio Alypio et Monicae → gaudium commune → incorporatio ecclesialis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:AF1","text":"Motus principalis est: certitudo metaphysica → displicentia vitae temporalis → exempla conversionis → autoaccusatio → diagnosis voluntatis divisae → gratia mediata per Scripturam → voluntas integra → renuntiatio et gaudium ecclesiale.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:AF2","text":"Ramus polemicus est: experientia voluntatum contrariarum → experimenta plurium voluntatum bonarum vel malarum → impossibilitas binarii dualismi → una anima variis desideriis distenta.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:AF3","text":"Ramus socialis est: fides secreta → confessio publica → victoria super timorem auctoritatis → gaudium multitudinis → auctoritas conversa in exemplum salutis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME1","text":"Quaestio conversionis ex oppositione inter fidem et incredulitatem ad oppositionem inter veritatem cognitam et voluntatem non integram transfertur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME2","text":"Consuetudo denuo describitur ut necessitas historice a subiecto producta, non ut natura fixa aut vis omnino externa.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME3","text":"Conflictus interior ex argumento pro dualismo in indicium partialitatis unius animae reclassificatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME4","text":"Professio publica non ut ornamentum fidei privatae, sed ut ruptura timoris socialis et effectus conversionis visibilis apparet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME5","text":"Nobilitas convertitur ex privilegio spirituali in facultatem multiplicandi exemplum, testimonium et gaudium commune.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME6","text":"Scriptura ex deposito propositionum in eventum allocutionis temporalis et personalis reordinatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D9","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME7","text":"Tempus deliberationis ex spatio neutro in mechanismum servitutis mutatur, dum nunc decisivum indefinito postea opponitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ALT1","text":"Gradus superficiei conversionem Augustini ex conflictibus, narrationibus, lacrimis, lectione apostolica et renuntiatione saeculari exhibet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ALT2","text":"Gradus structuralis mechanismum quo voluntas consuetudinem gignit, consuetudo voluntatem dividit et exempla divisionem intolerabilem faciunt explicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ALT3","text":"Gradus metastrategicus confessionem publicam, auctoritatem socialem et narrationem exemplarem in instrumenta propagationis conversionis transformat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ALT4","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis unam animam creatam, malum non substantializatum, Deum invariabilem, habitum sedimentatum et conversionem ut transitum decisivum inter vetus et novum constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT1","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad motum a certitudine sine conversione ad voluntatem per gratiam integratam restituendum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT2","text":"Structura firmissima est genealogia voluntatis perversae, libidinis, consuetudinis et necessitatis, cum analysi voluntatum partialium coniuncta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT3","text":"Systema interne cohaeret quatenus epistemicam certitudinem, moralem responsabilitatem, impotentiam praesentem et necessitatem gratiae distinguit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT4","text":"Relatio causalis inter actionem gratiae et actum voluntatis non plene formalizatur: gratia voluntatem sanat, sed modus huius efficientiae narratione potius quam analysi definitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT5","text":"Interpretatio vocis ut mandati divini analogia Antonii et praeparatione interiori nititur, sine criterio generali quo admonitio divina a casu distinguatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT6","text":"Refutatio Manichaeorum valide infirmat illationem a pluralitate voluntatum ad pluralitatem substantiarum, sed doctrinam poenae ex peccato liberiori et Adamica origine amplius probatam non reddit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT7","text":"Incrementum gaudii et invariabilitas divina per gaudium in creaturis componuntur, sed relatio inter locutionem affectivam de Deo et immutabilitatem eius compressa manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT8","text":"Relatio inter fidem interiorem, praesentiam ecclesialem et confessionem publicam per Victorinum ostenditur, non tamen in regulam universalem omnino determinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT9","text":"Praestantia continentiae in casu Augustini cum licitudine coniugii componitur, sed limes inter vocationem personalem et ordinem universalem imperfecte explicitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT10","text":"Restitutio servat verum motum textus: cognitio iam acquisita → servitus voluntatis → exempla et pudor → diagnosis anti-dualistica → interventus gratiae → actus conversionis → stabilizatio communis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T141719131608Z_c8061cd0","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"BOOK EIGHT.","source_sha256":"267cc000c2a7946985c91899b81d4742e72222aa2370546b2152e28108a0d445","sha256":"8b251ad5747ad9462aa539c49eb7911a0435324dc53e2c2f344316a14099a535","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:17:19.133639+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS1","text":"The text asks how a man already certain of God is unable to change his temporal life and by what operation a divided will is brought to complete conversion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS2","text":"Conversion is constituted not as the acquisition of a new doctrine, but as the healing and liberation by grace of a will divided by habit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS3","text":"The confessional argument is at once reconstructive, genealogical, diagnostic, polemical against Manichaean dualism, and strategic concerning the force of examples.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS4","text":"The movement proceeds from metaphysical certainty to practical impotence, from examples of others' conversions to self-accusation, and from the genealogy of habit to the crisis of the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS5","text":"The inner conflict is resolved into partial wills of one soul, lest it be transferred into two contrary natures or substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS6","text":"The crisis is consummated when an external admonition through Scripture is received as a personal command, doubt is dissolved, and the will is integrated toward the renunciation of temporal things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A1","text":"For Augustine it is already certain that every substance proceeds from the incorruptible God through the Word.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2","text":"Certainty about God does not of itself produce either stability in God or the right ordering of temporal life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A3","text":"The same soul can prefer the eternal good in truth and retain the temporal good through familiarity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","text":"A perverse will generates lust, lust habit, and habit, when not resisted, the necessity of bondage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A5","text":"The present force of habit arose from voluntary acts and joins involuntary suffering with imputability.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6","text":"Contrary wills are incomplete parts of one diseased will, not operations of two natures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A7","text":"In an act accomplished by the will alone, to will wholly is already to do.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0052","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A8","text":"The grace of God through Jesus Christ alone breaks the chain of habit and heals the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A9","text":"Narratives of others' conversions are means by which God kindles imitation, dissolves excuses, and sets the subject against himself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A10","text":"Victorinus's conversion, through public ecclesial profession, overcomes fear of pagan authority and makes faith socially recognizable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A11","text":"Augustine's full conversion entails the renunciation of secular hope and of the plan for marriage, not a mere change of opinion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0076","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A12","text":"The joy of a creature over what was lost and restored increases according to the magnitude of the preceding danger or distress, while God nevertheless remains unchangeable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A13","text":"The conversion of a widely known man produces a greater common effect because it moves more people and provides an example to more people.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14","text":"The admonition of Scripture, when received as divinely directed to oneself, can provide the will with a determinate command and final assurance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX1","text":"The delay of conversion is no longer explained by uncertainty of truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX2","text":"Two opposing wills do not prove two souls or contrary natures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX3","text":"Not every deliberation is a contest between a good principle and an evil principle, since multiple wills can all be good or all be evil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX4","text":"Habit is not a force alien in origin to the agent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX5","text":"The involuntary violence of habit does not exempt the agent from antecedent responsibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX6","text":"Conversion is not a local movement or a work of the body, but the integration of the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX7","text":"Learning, eloquence, and social rank neither effect conversion nor constitute its measure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX8","text":"Mere presence within the walls of a church does not make one a Christian.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0012","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX9","text":"Secret faith that refuses confession from fear of men does not yet fulfill the form of public conversion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX10","text":"Greater joy over a converted nobleman does not arise from the person's greater dignity before God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX11","text":"Marriage is not universally forbidden, although continence is proposed to Augustine as a better way.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX12","text":"Continence cannot be effected by the subject's own strength.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX13","text":"Formulas of delay, such as a promise of future conversion, are not a determinate beginning of decision but a continuation of bondage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:D1","text":"Once metaphysical doubt has been removed, the obstacle to conversion is transferred from the order of knowledge to the order of the will.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:D2","text":"The subject suffers the chain that he himself fashioned through antecedent acts; bondage is therefore at once present suffering and the effect of past guilt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:D3","text":"The conflict of flesh and spirit expresses the unequal adherence of one soul to contrary goods, not a division of substance.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:D4","text":"The examples of Victorinus, Antony, and the courtiers demonstrate that conversion is immediately possible and turn the antiquity of Augustine's excuses into self-accusation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:D5","text":"Grace does not substitute for the will, but brings it from willing incompletely to integral action.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:D6","text":"The public conversion of a person endowed with authority turns the instruments of former domination into instruments of confession and imitation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:D7","text":"Greater joy over Victorinus arises from the magnitude of his liberation and the multiplication of its effects, not from favor granted to the rich or noble.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:D8","text":"The liberation of grace translates known truth into a new ordering of temporal life.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:D9","text":"The example of Antony provides an interpretive form by which a chance voice and an encountered reading are transformed into a personal divine admonition.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD1","text":"The moral psychology of the text is temporally constructed: the same subject is sedimented, divided, and healed through his acts, without changing into two substances.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD2","text":"Responsibility and dependence on grace are not mutually exclusive: man participates in the cause of his bondage, but cannot by himself provide the principle of liberation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD3","text":"Conversion is a punctiform event arising from a long accumulation of mediations: examples, shame, self-accusation, and Scripture are compressed into one integral act.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD4","text":"Conversion produces a circuit of exemplarity: the publicly visible convert kindles others, whose conversion further multiplies joy and imitative force.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD5","text":"Scripture acquires decisive force not only from its general meaning, but from temporal reception as a word now directed to the subject.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD6","text":"Delay does not preserve a neutral state, but strengthens the old habit; the moment of conversion therefore establishes an opposition between now and an indefinite later.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX1","text":"Doctrinally enlightened reason is not a sufficient cause of right action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX2","text":"Moral evil does not require an evil substance, another mind, or an ontologically contrary principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX3","text":"The necessity of habit is not a natural necessity given from the beginning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX4","text":"Grace is not an external compulsion that renders the will superfluous.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX5","text":"A merely private and socially invisible conversion does not complete the form of confession demanded by the text's examples.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX6","text":"Deliberative delay is not innocence, because the very retention of the old life has the effect of a choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX7","text":"Continence is not mere sterility or the subtraction of pleasure, but a form of fruitful life in God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX8","text":"Variation of joy in creatures does not imply a change in divine knowledge or essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SNX1","text":"No neutral self stands outside the contending wills; the subject is present in both, although he identifies himself more with the approved will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SNX2","text":"No stable boundary between conversion and non-conversion is given, because a half-full will cannot perform an act requiring whole willing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SNX3","text":"The will does not possess an autonomous foundation from which it may draw itself out of its own division.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SNX4","text":"The indefinite future does not provide a space reserved for conversion, but conceals present refusal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:SNX5","text":"Salvation is not enclosed within individual consciousness, because confession, example, authority, and ecclesial joy belong to the very operation of conversion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:FGS1","text":"The first operation establishes dissonance: certainty about God → instability of life → transfer of the question from knowledge to will.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:FGS2","text":"The second operation genealogically generates bondage: perverse will → lust → habit → necessity → divided will.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:FGS3","text":"The third operation turns examples into self-judgment: narrative of another's conversion → possibility of present change → collapse of excuses → shame.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:FGS4","text":"The fourth operation ontologically restricts conflict: opposing wills → partiality of each → one diseased soul → exclusion of dualism.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:FGS5","text":"The fifth operation produces the threshold of decision: self-accusation → exhaustion of arguments → horror at the loss of habit → incapable half-full will → imploration of liberation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0054","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:FGS6","text":"The sixth operation closes the will: admonishing voice → example of Antony → apostolic reading → personal command → assurance → integral act.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:FGS7","text":"The final operation socially stabilizes the event: renunciation of temporal things → communication to Alypius and Monica → common joy → ecclesial incorporation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:AF1","text":"The principal movement is: metaphysical certainty → dissatisfaction with temporal life → examples of conversion → self-accusation → diagnosis of the divided will → grace mediated through Scripture → integral will → renunciation and ecclesial joy.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:AF2","text":"The polemical branch is: experience of contrary wills → experiences of multiple good or evil wills → impossibility of binary dualism → one soul stretched by various desires.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:AF3","text":"The social branch is: secret faith → public confession → victory over fear of authority → joy of the multitude → authority converted into an example of salvation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME1","text":"The question of conversion is transferred from the opposition between faith and unbelief to the opposition between known truth and an unintegrated will.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME2","text":"Habit is redescribed as a necessity historically produced by the subject, not as a fixed nature or an entirely external force.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME3","text":"Inner conflict is reclassified from an argument for dualism into an indication of the partiality of one soul.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME4","text":"Public profession appears not as an ornament of private faith, but as a rupture with social fear and a visible effect of conversion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME5","text":"Nobility is converted from a spiritual privilege into the capacity to multiply example, testimony, and common joy.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME6","text":"Scripture is reordered from a repository of propositions into an event of temporal and personal address.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D9","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME7","text":"The time of deliberation is changed from a neutral space into a mechanism of bondage, while the decisive now is opposed to an indefinite later.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ALT1","text":"The surface level presents Augustine's conversion through conflicts, narratives, tears, apostolic reading, and secular renunciation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ALT2","text":"The structural level explains the mechanism by which the will generates habit, habit divides the will, and examples make the division intolerable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ALT3","text":"The metastrategic level transforms public confession, social authority, and exemplary narrative into instruments for the propagation of conversion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:ALT4","text":"The ontological and temporal level establishes one created soul, unsubstantialized evil, an unchangeable God, sedimented habit, and conversion as a decisive passage between old and new.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement from certainty without conversion to a will integrated through grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT2","text":"The most robust structure is the genealogy of perverse will, lust, habit, and necessity, joined with the analysis of partial wills.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT3","text":"The system coheres internally insofar as it distinguishes epistemic certainty, moral responsibility, present impotence, and the necessity of grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT4","text":"The causal relation between the action of grace and the act of the will is not fully formalized: grace heals the will, but the mode of this efficacy is defined by narrative rather than analysis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT5","text":"The interpretation of a voice as a divine command rests on the analogy of Antony and inner preparation, without a general criterion by which divine admonition may be distinguished from chance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0071","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT6","text":"The refutation of the Manichaeans powerfully weakens the inference from a plurality of wills to a plurality of substances, but does not render the doctrine of punishment from freer sin and Adamic origin more fully proven.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0057","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT7","text":"The increase of joy and divine invariability are reconciled through joy in creatures, but the relation between affective speech about God and his immutability remains compressed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0018","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0021","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT8","text":"The relation between inner faith, ecclesial presence, and public confession is shown through Victorinus, yet is not wholly determined as a universal rule.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT9","text":"The superiority of continence in Augustine's case is reconciled with the lawfulness of marriage, but the boundary between personal vocation and universal order is imperfectly explicated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT10","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text: knowledge already acquired → bondage of the will → examples and shame → anti-dualistic diagnosis → intervention of grace → act of conversion → common stabilization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0075","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBO:P0076","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LIBO@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_5P0L_LIBO:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 08","title":"Book VIII.","context":"Chapter 08","original_title":"Liber Octavus.","original_context":"Chapter 08"},"original_title":"Liber Octavus.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN","layer":"CH","title":"Book IX.","order":9,"parents":["RAW_5P0L_LIBN"],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LIBN@R001","sha256":"69cb9f95dc17f316dbc7e2220f97fd0427af7651d6466bb9f56960bda51f30c3","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS1","text":"Quaestio centralis est quomodo liberatio interior a voluntate divisa in renuntiationem, baptismum, communionem ecclesialem et mortis intelligentiam traducatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS2","text":"Liberatio efficitur cum Deus voluntatem ligatam excitat, falsas delectationes vera suavitate expellit et bona humana sibi tamquam fonti restituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS3","text":"Argumentatio confessionalis, reconstructiva, polemica et eschatologica effectus conversionis ad gratiam, providentiam et misericordiam tamquam principia refert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS4","text":"Motus procedit a vinculis ruptis ad professionem depositam, deinde ad formationem, baptismum, vitam ecclesialem, contemplationem aeternitatis et mortem Monicae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS5","text":"Narratio Monicae eandem structuram probat: disciplina, correctio, virtus et reconciliatio non merita autonoma, sed dona providentiae sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS6","text":"Argumentatio in precem terminatur, quia nec conversio nec vita laudabilis necessitatem misericordiae, sacrificii Christi et intercessionis ecclesialis tollit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A1","text":"Deus solus est bonum immutabile, summa suavitas et lux interior qua homo illuminatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A2","text":"Voluntas peccato et consuetudine ligata se ipsa liberare non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3","text":"Misericordia Dei vincula rumpit et liberum arbitrium ad consensum excitat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A4","text":"Conversio consistit in recusatione voluntatis perversae et consensu voluntati divinae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A5","text":"Bona sensibilia et temporalia desiderium dispergunt neque bono aeterno comparari possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A6","text":"Liberatio cordis separationem externam antecedere atque eius tempus et modum regere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7","text":"Scriptura, sacramenta, cantus et communio Ecclesiae instrumenta divinae illuminationis et sanationis sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","text":"Providentia etiam morbum, conflictum, contumeliam et perturbationem ad effectus salutares convertere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9","text":"Retributio moralis voluntatem agentis respicit, non solum effectum quem providentia ex actu producit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A10","text":"Omne bonum humanum et omne meritum laudabile donum Dei est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A11","text":"Baptismus peccata antecedentia remittit et hominem in vitam ecclesialem regenerat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A12","text":"Regeneratio sacramentalis possibilitatem culpae posterioris neque necessitatem misericordiae aufert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A13","text":"Sapientia aeterna facta non est, non mutatur et solo praesenti aeterno subsistit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A14","text":"Mens temporalis Sapientiam aeternam breviter attingere potest, sed ad verba et successionem revertitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A15","text":"Consuetudo affectiva post correctionem intellectus et voluntatis permanere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A16","text":"Mors fidelis non est annihilatio; resurrectio locum sepulturae et distantiam corporalem relativam facit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17","text":"Sacrificium et intercessio Christi fundamentum remissionis, spei et memoriae liturgicae defunctorum sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX1","text":"Libertas non est possessio delectationum veterum, sed gaudium quod earum amissionem iam non timet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX2","text":"Renuntiatio professionis non debet fieri ut ruptura publica qua magnitudo convertentis spectetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX3","text":"Professio rhetorica non est ministerium legis et pacis, sed mercatus verborum quibus furor forensis instruitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX4","text":"Infirmitas corporis conversionem non efficit, quamvis legitimam discessus excusationem praebeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX5","text":"Peccatum non procedit ex natura aliena gentis tenebrarum, sed ad voluntatem peccantis refertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX6","text":"Bonum verum neque extra hominem in rebus visibilibus quaeritur neque ab homine tamquam fonte luminis producitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX7","text":"Christi caro et mors non sunt phantasma Manichaeum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX8","text":"In exemplari vitae aeternae Deus non auditur per linguam, angelum, sonitum, imaginem aut similitudinem, sed per se ipsum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX9","text":"Virtutes Monicae non exponuntur ut opera quibus ipsa se formaverit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX10","text":"Mors fidelis neque misera exstinctio est neque sepultura patria ad resurrectionem necessaria est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX11","text":"Fides luctum tamquam desperationem vetat, non autem lacrimas coram Deo emissas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX12","text":"Vita laudabilis neque innocentiam absolutam neque ius ad salutem sine misericordia constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D1","text":"Vera suavitas veteres voluptates non sola prohibitione, sed delectationis ordine inverso expellit; inde amissio ante timenda fit gaudium.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D2","text":"Discessus usque ad ferias dilatus cum conversione congruit, quia libertas interior iam perfecta modum externae separationis sine iactantia ordinat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D3","text":"Morbus pulmonis causa primaria renuntiationis non est, sed eventus contingens quem providentia in excusationem veracem assumit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D4","text":"Repudiato dualismo Manichaeo, memoria peccati in iram adversus propriam voluntatem et in responsabilitatem moralem convertitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D5","text":"Lectio Psalmorum verba externa in recognitionem interiorem transfert atque desiderium a temporalibus ad lumen aeternum dirigit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D6","text":"Conversio voluntatis maturitatem intellectualem statim non confert, quia scripta Cassiciacensia vestigia superbiae servant et lectio Isaiae adhuc differtur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D7","text":"Baptismus conversionem privatam in regenerationem communem Augustini, Alypii et Adeodati traducit atque sollicitudinem vitae praeteritae removet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D8","text":"Cantus communis veritatem per sensum et affectum infundit atque Ecclesiam sub pressione politica et haeretica sustinet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D9","text":"Sanationes quas narratio precibus aut reliquiis coniungit functionem signorum obtinent: fidem confirmant et persecutionis impetum comprimunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D10","text":"Contumelia ancillae Monicam corrigit sine merito corrigentis, quia effectus salutaris a providentia, culpa autem ab intentione inimica aestimatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D11","text":"Patientia, castitas, prudentia domestica et opus pacis in Monica praesentiam Dei manifestant, non sufficientiam moralem sui ipsius.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D12","text":"Ascensus Ostiensis sensibilia, caelum et ipsam mentem transcendit, Sapientiam breviter attingit ac deinde necessario ad sonum finitum revertitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D13","text":"Contemplatio aeternitatis et impleta spes conversionis filii desiderium Monicae vitae terrestris, patriae sepulturae et ulterioris morae dissolvunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D14","text":"Dolor Augustini non procedit ex opinione annihilationis, sed ex abruptione consuetudinis qua duae vitae affective cohaeserant.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D15","text":"Laudatio Monicae in orationem pro peccatis transit, quia dona bona ius contra iudicium non efficiunt et spes in Christo ac misericordia ponitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD1","text":"Confessio totam narrationem in redistributionem causalitatis convertit: homo actus patitur et consentit, sed initium, medicina, fructus et consummatio Deo attribuuntur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2","text":"Conversio est processus multistratus, quia liberatio voluntatis professionem, intellectum, affectum, sacramentum et consuetudinem diversis temporibus transformat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD3","text":"Oppositio inter successionem temporalem et praesentiam aeternam ordinat simul renuntiationem, contemplationem, mortem et memoriam.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4","text":"Providentia asymmetricam causalitatem instituit: malus affectus vel adversus eventus bonum producere potest, quin voluntas mala propter effectum absolvatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD5","text":"Mediatio ecclesialis et exemplar apophaticum non sunt alternativa aequalia: signa sunt necessaria viatori, sed in visione desiderata ab immediata Dei praesentia superantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD6","text":"Vincula familiaria non destruuntur, sed ex possessione temporali in communionem ecclesialem, memoriam liturgicam et spem resurrectionis transferuntur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D13","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD7","text":"Narratio sanctitatis necessario in intercessionem desinit, quia quo plura bona apparent, eo planius eorum ratio doni, non debiti, constituitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX1","text":"Systema falsam requirit doctrinam secundum quam subiectum autonomum conversionis suae initium et causam sufficientem praebet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX2","text":"Systema excludit conversionem uno decreto consummatam, cuius intellectus, habitus et affectus nullam ulteriorem formationem requirant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX3","text":"Systema excludit dualismum quo culpa in substantiam alienam transfertur et voluntas propria absolvitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX4","text":"Systema excludit aequationem inter effectum bonum et intentionem bonam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX5","text":"Neque mediatio ecclesialis sine transformatione interiori neque interioritas privata sine sacramento et communione sufficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX6","text":"Recta doctrina dolorem et consuetudinem affectivam automatice non dissolvit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX7","text":"Virtus humana nullum debitum efficit quo Deus misericordiam ex iustitia meriti praestare cogatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX1","text":"Nulla creatura, delectatio, professio, imago, vox aut institutum potest ultimus terminus desiderii esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2","text":"Immediata possessio stabilis Sapientiae aeternae intra vitam temporalem indisponibilis manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX3","text":"Plena transparentia sui, memoriae et providentiae negatur; narratio causam ultimam confitetur sine omnibus mediis occultis cognitis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX4","text":"Nulla ratio meritorum humanorum iudicium claudit aut misericordiam supervacaneam facit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX5","text":"Patria terrestris, successus saecularis, propinquitas corporalis et sepultura familiaris formam patriae ultimae praebere non possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX6","text":"Peregrinatio ad pacem aeternam immunitatem praesentem a vulnerabilitate, separatione et luctu non concedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:FGS1","text":"Prima operatio hanc seriem habet: miseria recognita → misericordia irrumpens → vincula rupta → voluntas concordans → delectationes veteres expulsae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:FGS2","text":"Transitus vocationalis sic generatur: liberatio cordis → remotio cupiditatis → mora prudentialis → excusatio providentialiter data → professio deposita.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:FGS3","text":"Formatio conversionis sequitur: otium Cassiciacense → Scriptura et disputatio → reliquiae superbiae detectae → instructio ecclesialis → Baptismus.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:FGS4","text":"Incorporatio ecclesialis sequitur: sacramentum et cantus → veritas per sensus infusa → affectus pietatis → communitas sub adversitate corroborata.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:FGS5","text":"Lectura providentiae sequitur: eventus ambiguus → effectus salutaris → distinctio effectus ab intentione → culpa agenti, bonum Deo tributum.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:FGS6","text":"Ascensus contemplativus sequitur: sensibilia transcensa → mens ingressa → mens transcensa → Sapientia breviter tacta → reditus ad verba temporalia.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passag