"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT1","text":"Axiomata sufficiunt ad restituendam seriem a liberatione voluntatis ad intercessionem pro defuncta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT2","text":"Structura interne cohaeret quia conversionem, providentiam, virtutem, contemplationem et mortem eadem ratione doni ordinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT3","text":"Firmissima commissura est relatio inter attributum bonum humanum et gratiarum actionem Deo debitam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT4","text":"Relatio causalis inter gratiam determinantem et liberum arbitrium consentientem affirmatur, sed non plene formaliter explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT5","text":"Distinctio inter providentiam bonum producentem et voluntatem malam culpabilem servatur, quamvis modus concursus nondum solvatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT6","text":"Remissio baptismalis et debitum post baptismum cohaerere possunt, sed limes exactus culpae posterioris non elaboratur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT7","text":"Immediatio contemplativa desideratur, dum tota vita temporalis mediationibus ecclesialibus nititur; relatio utriusque per statum viatoris tantum componitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT8","text":"Luctus primum quasi mollities coercetur, deinde lacrimis coram Deo sanatur; discrimen inter affectum carnalem et dolorem recte ordinatum manet mobile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0067","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0069","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0082","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT9","text":"Sanationes, status defunctorum et effectus eschatologici auctoritate testimonii, Scripturae et fidei nituntur potius quam probatione interna completa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT10","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat: liberatio → mediatio ecclesialis → reinterpretatio providentiae → transcensus temporalis → luctus → misericordia et communio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T141648975355Z_ddbc0b70","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"BOOK NINE.","source_sha256":"69cb9f95dc17f316dbc7e2220f97fd0427af7651d6466bb9f56960bda51f30c3","sha256":"5d7cc1151cf5f74b973e7db7e82a639fd8078da70be20c9f43d5c7724639a16b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:16:48.977177+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS1","text":"The central question is how interior liberation from a divided will is translated into renunciation, baptism, ecclesial communion, and an understanding of death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS2","text":"Liberation is effected when God awakens the bound will, expels false delights through true sweetness, and restores human goods to himself as their source.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS3","text":"The confessional, reconstructive, polemical, and eschatological argument refers the effects of conversion to grace, providence, and mercy as principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS4","text":"The movement proceeds from broken bonds to the relinquished profession, then to formation, baptism, ecclesial life, contemplation of eternity, and Monica's death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS5","text":"The narrative of Monica proves the same structure: discipline, correction, virtue, and reconciliation are not autonomous merits, but gifts of providence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS6","text":"The argument ends in prayer, because neither conversion nor a praiseworthy life removes the need for mercy, Christ's sacrifice, and ecclesial intercession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A1","text":"God alone is the immutable good, supreme sweetness, and interior light by which man is illuminated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A2","text":"The will bound by sin and habit cannot liberate itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3","text":"God's mercy breaks bonds and awakens free will to consent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A4","text":"Conversion consists in rejecting the perverse will and consenting to the divine will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A5","text":"Sensible and temporal goods scatter desire and cannot be compared with the eternal good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A6","text":"Liberation of the heart can precede external separation and govern its time and manner.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7","text":"Scripture, sacraments, chants, and the communion of the Church are instruments of divine illumination and healing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","text":"Providence can turn even illness, conflict, insult, and disturbance toward salutary effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9","text":"Moral retribution regards the will of the agent, not only the effect that providence produces from the act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0045","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A10","text":"Every human good and every praiseworthy merit is a gift of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A11","text":"Baptism remits preceding sins and regenerates man into ecclesial life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A12","text":"Sacramental regeneration removes neither the possibility of subsequent guilt nor the necessity of mercy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A13","text":"Eternal Wisdom was not made, does not change, and subsists in the eternal present alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0056","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A14","text":"The temporal mind can briefly touch eternal Wisdom, but returns to words and succession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A15","text":"Affective habit can remain after the correction of intellect and will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A16","text":"The death of the faithful is not annihilation; resurrection renders the place of burial and bodily distance relative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17","text":"Christ's sacrifice and intercession are the foundation of remission, hope, and the liturgical remembrance of the dead.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX1","text":"Freedom is not possession of former delights, but joy that no longer fears their loss.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX2","text":"The renunciation of one's profession ought not to occur as a public rupture by which the convert's greatness is displayed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX3","text":"The rhetorical profession is not a ministry of law and peace, but a marketplace of words by which forensic fury is equipped.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX4","text":"Bodily infirmity does not effect conversion, although it provides a legitimate excuse for departure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX5","text":"Sin does not proceed from an alien nature of a race of darkness, but is referred to the will of the sinner.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX6","text":"True good is sought neither outside man in visible things nor produced by man as a source of light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX7","text":"Christ's flesh and death are not a Manichaean phantom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX8","text":"In the exemplar of eternal life, God is heard not through language, angel, sound, image, or likeness, but through himself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX9","text":"Monica's virtues are not set forth as works by which she formed herself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0041","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX10","text":"The death of the faithful is neither a miserable extinction nor is burial in one's homeland necessary for resurrection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX11","text":"Faith forbids grief as despair, but not tears shed before God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX12","text":"A praiseworthy life establishes neither absolute innocence nor a right to salvation without mercy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D1","text":"True sweetness expels former pleasures not by prohibition alone, but by an inverted order of delight; hence what was formerly to be feared as loss becomes joy.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D2","text":"Departure delayed until the holidays accords with conversion, because interior freedom already perfected orders the manner of external separation without boasting.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D3","text":"Illness of the lungs is not the primary cause of renunciation, but a contingent event that providence assumes as a truthful excuse.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D4","text":"Once Manichaean dualism has been repudiated, memory of sin is transformed into anger against one's own will and into moral responsibility.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D5","text":"The reading of the Psalms transfers external words into interior recognition and directs desire from temporal things toward eternal light.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D6","text":"Conversion of the will does not immediately confer intellectual maturity, because the Cassiciacum writings retain traces of pride and the reading of Isaiah is still deferred.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D7","text":"Baptism translates the private conversion into the shared regeneration of Augustine, Alypius, and Adeodatus, and removes anxiety concerning past life.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D8","text":"Common chant instills truth through sense and affection and sustains the Church under political and heretical pressure.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D9","text":"The healings that the narrative connects with prayers or relics have the function of signs: they confirm faith and check the onslaught of persecution.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D10","text":"The insult of a maidservant corrects Monica without merit on the corrector's part, because the salutary effect is assessed as from providence, but guilt as from hostile intention.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D11","text":"Patience, chastity, domestic prudence, and the work of peace in Monica manifest God's presence, not her own moral self-sufficiency.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D12","text":"The Ostian ascent transcends sensible things, heaven, and the mind itself, briefly touches Wisdom, and then necessarily returns to finite sound.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D13","text":"Contemplation of eternity and the fulfilled hope of her son's conversion dissolve Monica's desire for earthly life, burial in her homeland, and further delay.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D14","text":"Augustine's sorrow does not proceed from the opinion of annihilation, but from the breaking of the habit by which two lives had affectively adhered together.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:D15","text":"The praise of Monica passes into prayer for sins, because good gifts do not effect a right against judgment, and hope is placed in Christ and mercy.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD1","text":"Confession transforms the whole narrative into a redistribution of causality: man undergoes and consents to acts, but beginning, remedy, fruit, and consummation are attributed to God.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2","text":"Conversion is a multilayered process, because liberation of the will transforms profession, intellect, affection, sacrament, and habit at different times.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD3","text":"The opposition between temporal succession and eternal presence orders together renunciation, contemplation, death, and memory.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4","text":"Providence establishes asymmetric causality: an evil affection or adverse event can produce good, without the evil will being absolved on account of the effect.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD5","text":"Ecclesial mediation and the apophatic exemplar are not equal alternatives: signs are necessary for the wayfarer, but in the desired vision they are surpassed by God's immediate presence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD6","text":"Familial bonds are not destroyed, but are transferred from temporal possession into ecclesial communion, liturgical remembrance, and hope of resurrection.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D13","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD7","text":"The narrative of holiness necessarily ends in intercession, because the more goods appear, the more clearly their character as gift, not debt, is established.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX1","text":"The system rejects the false doctrine according to which the autonomous subject provides the beginning and sufficient cause of its own conversion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX2","text":"The system excludes a conversion consummated by a single decree, whose intellect, habit, and affection require no further formation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX3","text":"The system excludes a dualism by which guilt is transferred to an alien substance and one's own will is absolved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX4","text":"The system excludes the equation of a good effect with a good intention.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0045","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX5","text":"Neither ecclesial mediation without interior transformation nor private interiority without sacrament and communion suffices.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX6","text":"Right doctrine does not automatically dissolve sorrow and affective habit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0068","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0072","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX7","text":"Human virtue creates no debt by which God may be compelled to bestow mercy according to the justice of merit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX1","text":"No creature, delight, profession, image, voice, or institution can be the ultimate end of desire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2","text":"Immediate stable possession of eternal Wisdom remains unavailable within temporal life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0059","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX3","text":"Full transparency of self, memory, and providence is denied; the narrative confesses the ultimate cause without knowing all the hidden means.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX4","text":"No reckoning of human merits closes judgment or renders mercy superfluous.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX5","text":"An earthly homeland, secular success, bodily proximity, and family burial cannot provide the form of the ultimate homeland.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0060","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX6","text":"Pilgrimage toward eternal peace does not grant present immunity from vulnerability, separation, and grief.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:FGS1","text":"The first operation has this sequence: recognized misery → irrupting mercy → broken bonds → concordant will → former delights expelled.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:FGS2","text":"The vocational transition is generated thus: liberation of the heart → removal of desire → prudential delay → providentially given excuse → profession relinquished.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:FGS3","text":"The formation of conversion follows: Cassiciacum leisure → Scripture and disputation → remnants of pride detected → ecclesial instruction → Baptism.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:FGS4","text":"Ecclesial incorporation follows: sacrament and chant → truth infused through the senses → affection of piety → community strengthened under adversity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:FGS5","text":"The reading of providence follows: ambiguous event → salutary effect → distinction of effect from intention → guilt attributed to the agent, good to God.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:FGS6","text":"The contemplative ascent follows: sensible things transcended → mind entered → mind transcended → Wisdom briefly touched → return to temporal words.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0057","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:FGS7","text":"The process of mourning follows: non-annihilating death + broken habit → restrained sorrow → sorrow over sorrow → tears before God → mitigation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:FGS8","text":"The soteriological closure follows: praiseworthy life → goods as gifts → possible debt → Christ's sacrifice → mercy → remembrance at the altar and prayer of readers.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:AF1","text":"Bonds of the will → liberating grace → renunciation of profession → Cassiciacum formation → Baptism → ecclesial communion → return to Africa → Monica's death → intercession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:AF2","text":"External goods → interior light → mind transcending itself → touch of eternal presence → desired failure of signs → return to temporal speech.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:AF3","text":"Monica's virtues → attribution of gifts to God → denial of absolute innocence → confession of debt → Christ's mercy → common liturgical remembrance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0087","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME1","text":"Conversion is redescribed from an autonomous act of the subject into freedom awakened by grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME2","text":"The rhetorical profession is reclassified from a neutral art into a mechanism of marketplace, ambition, and forensic armament.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME3","text":"The opposition of exterior and interior distinguishes dispersive temporal goods from the light received inwardly from God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME4","text":"Conversion is expanded from a closed moment into a temporal process of will, intellect, sacrament, habit, and affection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME5","text":"Moral causality is divided between the agent's intention and the effect that providence produces from the act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME6","text":"The Church becomes at once an apparatus of knowledge, affective formation, solidarity, and resistance under coercion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME7","text":"Death is transferred from local annihilation into temporal separation within the hope of resurrection and liturgical communion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME8","text":"Holy life is reordered from an argument of merit into matter for thanksgiving and intercession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:ALT1","text":"Altitude 1 — Surface — The relinquishment of profession, Cassiciacum leisure, Baptism, return, Monica's life, the Ostian conversation, death, mourning, and prayer constitute the manifest sequence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:ALT2","text":"Altitude 2 — Structural — Grace works through will, habit, ecclesial institution, sacrament, Scripture, affection, and providence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:ALT3","text":"Altitude 3 — Metastrategic — Confession orders memory so that causality is transferred from ego to God and readers are changed from spectators into intercessors.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0041","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:ALT4","text":"Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal — Reality is divided between mutable creatures in succession and present eternal Wisdom, whose touch is now brief, but whose possession is eschatological.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0057","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to restore the sequence from liberation of the will to intercession for the deceased woman.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT2","text":"The structure coheres internally because it orders conversion, providence, virtue, contemplation, and death according to the same logic of gift.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT3","text":"The strongest joint is the relation between attributed human good and thanksgiving owed to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0085","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT4","text":"The causal relation between determining grace and consenting free will is affirmed, but not fully formally explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT5","text":"The distinction between providence producing good and culpable evil will is preserved, although the mode of concurrence is not yet resolved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0045","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT6","text":"Baptismal remission and debt after baptism can cohere, but the exact limit of subsequent guilt is not elaborated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT7","text":"Contemplative immediacy is desired, while the whole temporal life rests upon ecclesial mediations; the relation of the two is reconciled only through the state of the wayfarer.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT8","text":"Mourning is first restrained as though it were weakness, then healed by tears before God; the distinction between carnal affection and rightly ordered sorrow remains mobile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0067","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0069","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0082","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT9","text":"Healings, the state of the dead, and eschatological effects rest upon the authority of testimony, Scripture, and faith rather than upon complete internal proof.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT10","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: liberation → ecclesial mediation → reinterpretation of providence → temporal transcendence → mourning → mercy and communion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0068","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBN:P0089","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LIBN@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_5P0L_LIBN:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 09","title":"Book IX.","context":"Chapter 09","original_title":"Liber Nonus.","original_context":"Chapter 09"},"original_title":"Liber Nonus.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD","layer":"CH","title":"Book X.","order":10,"parents":["RAW_5P0L_LIBD"],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LIBD@R001","sha256":"aaeef876066edc8f1bbfb7cd0b9f120af6092469ef2042499002e8d21c7e0ff8","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS1","text":"Textus quaerit quo fructu homo, Deo iam omnia cognoscente et sibi ipsi non plene noto, praesentem statum suum Deo et hominibus confiteatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS2","text":"Confessio veritatem in corde efficit, bona Deo tribuit, vulnera manifestat et auditores caritate coniunctos ad gratiarum actionem atque intercessionem convertit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS3","text":"Quaestio quid homo amet cum Deum amat cognitionem constituit ut ascensum per signa creata et facultates interiores ad veritatem supra mentem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS4","text":"Scrutinium memoriae simul condicionem quaerendi et agnoscendi aperit atque ostendit animam nec se comprehendere nec Deum velut obiectum intra se collocare posse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS5","text":"Appetitus universalis vitae beatae ad gaudium, deinde ad gaudium de veritate reducitur, sed amor veritatis divisione voluntatis corrumpitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS6","text":"Examen praesentis status per triplicem cupiditatem ostendit vitam continuam esse tentationem, cuius vires, fines et intentiones subiecto saepe latent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS7","text":"Impotentia continentiae autonomae et defectus mediatorum falsorum ad misericordiam divinam et Christum verum mediatorem ducunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0170","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS8","text":"Argumentatio est confessiva, apophatica, introspectiva, diagnostica et soteriologica; additamentum editoriale eandem structuram ad polemicam adversus iudicium ad hominem transfert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0173","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0175","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","text":"Deus totam conscientiam hominis cognoscit et iudicat, homo autem nec se ipsum totum cognoscit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A2","text":"Confessio veritatem coram Deo facit, cum malum sibi displicere et bonum non sibi sed Deo tribuere significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A3","text":"Confessio publica apud auditores caritate coniunctos gratiarum actionem pro bonis et intercessionem pro malis generat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A4","text":"Ratio interior sensuum nuntios iudicat et creaturas tamquam effectus Conditoris interpretatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","text":"Deus est veritas incommutabilis et vita animae, supra mentem mutabilem praesidens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6","text":"Memoria imagines sensibilium, res intelligibiles, notiones affectionum et proprias operationes diversis modis continet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A7","text":"Vis memoriae et animi propriam comprehensionem excedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A8","text":"Quaestio et agnitio rei aliquam eius notitiam retentam praesupponunt; quod omnino deletum est quaeri non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A9","text":"Appetitus universalis vitae beatae communem aliquam eius notitiam implicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A10","text":"Vita beata est gaudium ad Deum, de Deo et propter Deum, id est gaudium de veritate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A11","text":"Homo veritatem amat cum rem amatam confirmat, sed eam odit cum propriam falsitatem manifestat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12","text":"Creaturae bonae sunt, sed in laqueos vertuntur cum pro fine habentur aut usum necessarium et pium excedunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0114","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","text":"Vita praesens continua tentatio est, in qua vires, motiva et perseverantia hominis sibi incerta manent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0099","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14","text":"Concupiscentia carnis, concupiscentia oculorum et ambitio saeculi animam a Deo in voluptatem, vanam cognitionem et propriam excellentiam dispergunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0132","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0142","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","text":"Continentia animam ex multiplici dispersione in unitatem recti amoris colligit et donum Dei est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16","text":"Misericordia divina facultatem ad imperata praebet, languores sanat et imperfecta perficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","text":"Mediator reconciliationis mortalitatem cum hominibus et iustitiam cum Deo coniungere debet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18","text":"Christus, mortalis cum hominibus et iustus cum Deo, morte voluntaria sacerdos et sacrificium factus reconciliationem atque spem sanationis efficit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0170","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX1","text":"Confessio non est informatio Deo antea ignota neque solus strepitus vocis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX2","text":"Auditores humani nec cor confitentis immediate cognoscunt nec eius languores sanant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX3","text":"Homo non est iudex ultimus sui ipsius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX4","text":"Creaturae Deum indicant, sed nulla creatura est Deus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX5","text":"Deus non est corpus, qualitas sensibilis, vis vegetativa aut facultas sensitiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX6","text":"Deus non est imago corporalis, affectio, memoria, animus mutabilis aut res in loco memoriae inclusa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX7","text":"Res disciplinarum et rationes mathematicae non sunt imagines per sensus corporales invectae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX8","text":"Discere intelligibilia non est simpliciter aliena verba recipere, sed dispersa intus colligere et agnoscere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX9","text":"Vita beata non est quodlibet gaudium neque sola delectatio nominis eius.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0082","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX10","text":"Immunditia moralis non in cibo vel creatura ipsa, sed in cupiditate inordinata consistit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0114","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX11","text":"Curiositas non fit scientia vera eo solo quod appetitum experiendi nomine cognitionis tegit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0132","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0134","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX12","text":"Laus humana non est mensura bonitatis nec finis operis boni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0143","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0144","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX13","text":"Status conversus non tollit tentationem neque certitudinem de futura perseverantia praestat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0118","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX14","text":"Angeli, daemones, visiones curiosae et artes magicae reconciliationem cum Deo non efficiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0164","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0167","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX15","text":"Verbum, qua Deo aequale est, non est medius; Christus qua homo mediator est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX16","text":"Fuga in solitudinem non constituit solutionem vocationis, conflictus aut infirmitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0172","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D1","text":"Confessio non cognitionem Dei auget, sed subiectum intra veritatem divinae cognitionis ordinat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D2","text":"Publicatio confessionis tantum per caritatem et fructum communem iustificatur, non per curiositatem de vita aliena.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D3","text":"Examen sui necessario provisionale manet, quia is qui examinat proprias vires et motiva non plene videt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D4","text":"Creaturae theologice loquuntur tantum rationi quae earum speciem cum veritate interiore confert; amor subiciens iudicium impedit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D5","text":"Memoria est via necessaria quaerendi Deum, sed non terminus neque essentia eius.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D6","text":"Animus sibi praesens est sine plena sui comprehensione; proximitas subiecti non efficit transparantiam.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D7","text":"Deus in memoria invenitur quatenus veritas agnoscitur, sed principium huius agnitionis supra memoriam et supra subiectum manet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D8","text":"Consensus universalis circa beatitudinem non efficit consensum circa veram eius rationem neque voluntatem sufficientem ad eam adipiscendam.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D9","text":"Falsitas persistit quia homo veritatem vult ut electiones suas confirmet, sed eam recusat ut ipsum corrigat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D10","text":"Triplex tentatio tres modos exhibet quibus bonum creatum ex medio in finem illicitum mutatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0143","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D11","text":"Delectatio sensibilis legitima manet dum rationem sequitur et ad pietatem servit; peccaminosa fit cum rem significatam antecedit aut excludit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D12","text":"Incertitudo virium et perpetuitas tentationis mandatum continentiae in orationem pro dono convertunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0099","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D13","text":"Continentia non est mera privatio voluptatis, sed reintegratio amorum dispersorum sub uno fine.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D14","text":"Amor laudis difficillime probatur per absentiam, quia laus bonae vitae comes esse potest nec sine corruptione vitae deliberate removetur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0147","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D15","text":"Vana gloria recursive se instaurat, quia homo etiam de contemptu laudis gloriari potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0155","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D16","text":"Christus solus condiciones mediationis implet et ideo desperationem quam distantia inter peccatorem et Deum generat removet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0170","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D17","text":"Additamentum editoriale ex sermone Augustini structuram confessionis ad polemicam transfert: vitia ministri praeterita gratiam extollunt, causam catholicam non destruunt, et iudicium ad hominem scientiam cordis non praebet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0173","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0174","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD1","text":"Epistemologia interior et soteriologia eandem formam habent: descensus in se non autonomiam, sed dependentiam a veritate supra se detegit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD2","text":"Memoria limen est inter praesentiam et transcendentiam: sine ea Deus agnosci non potest, sed in ea Deus essentialiter aut spatialiter contineri non potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0065","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0089","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0092","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD3","text":"Appetitus beatitudinis simul vestigium veritatis et locus aberrationis est, quia finis communiter notus per gaudia falsa substitui potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD4","text":"Triplex cupiditas structuram captationis complet: sensus ab usu ad voluptatem, cognitio a sapientia ad experimentum, societas a caritate ad excellentiam privatam traducuntur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0143","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD5","text":"Confessio machina therapeutica recursiva est: eandem opacitatem quam manifestat numquam exhaurit, sed eam in orationem, correctionem et communionem convertit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0152","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD6","text":"Gratia actionem humanam non substituit, sed resistendi facultatem dat; ipsa resistentia simul donum receptum et vulnus residuum manifestat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD7","text":"Ascensus ad veritatem distantiam cognoscendam facit, sed eam non superat; mediatio Christi solvit discontinuum quod introspectio tantum detegere potuit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD8","text":"Subiectum christianum temporaliter inter sanationem iam incohatam et pacem nondum consummatam constituitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX1","text":"Ut confessionis necessitas constet, falsa esse debet plena sui transparentia et facultas hominis se ipsum definitive iudicandi.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX2","text":"Ut ascensus interior constet, falsa esse debet sufficientia sensus ad Deum vel veritatem ultimam cognoscendam.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX3","text":"Ut memoriae analysis constet, falsa esse debet memoria tamquam archivum mere passivum imaginum sensibilium.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX4","text":"Ut miseria voluntatis explicetur, falsum esse debet desiderium boni semper efficere rectam cognitionem, electionem et possessionem eius.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX5","text":"Ut doctrina moderationis constet, falsa esse debet intrinseca malitia corporis, sensuum et creaturarum.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0114","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0125","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX6","text":"Ut ratio gratiae constet, falsum esse debet mandatum divinum autonomam facultatem oboediendi praesupponere.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0113","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX7","text":"Ut diagnosis superbiae constet, falsum esse debet laudem humanam statum moralem laudati fideliter manifestare.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0146","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0149","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0150","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX8","text":"Ut incarnatio necessaria sit, falsa esse debet quaelibet superioritas spiritualis ad veram mediationem sufficere.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX9","text":"Ut confessio praesentis status permaneat, falsa esse debet perfectio stabilis hominis intra vitam mortalem.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0118","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX1","text":"Systema subiectum autonomum excludit: homo nec mensura, nec unitas, nec iudex, nec medicus sufficiens sui est.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX2","text":"Possessio Dei ut obiecti localis, sensibilis aut mentaliter inclusi structuraliter praecluditur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX3","text":"In vita praesenti nullus medius locus securus datur, quia prosperitas, adversitas, sensus, cognitio et relatio socialis materiam tentationis praebent.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0099","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0132","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX4","text":"Innocentia praesens tamquam fundamentum spei indisponibilis est; sola misericordia spem sustinet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX5","text":"Veritas et mendacium ut bona aeque possidenda simul consistere non possunt; conatus utrumque retinendi Deum amittit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0162","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX6","text":"Ascensus superbus ad Deum impossibilis est, quia superbia mediatores sibi similes eligit et separationem quam superare vult reproducit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX7","text":"Confessio praesentis hominis clausuram definitivam non admittit, quia subiectum inter cognitionem partialem, tentationem futuram et sanationem nondum completam manet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0099","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS1","text":"Machina confessionis procedit: omniscientia divina plus opacitas sui → confessio ut effectio veritatis → auditio caritatis → gratiarum actio et intercessio.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS2","text":"Machina ascensus procedit: signa sensibilia → iudex interior → exclusio corporis et potentiarum communium animalibus → memoria → excessus memoriae supra comprehensionem sui → veritas supra mentem.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS3","text":"Machina beatitudinis procedit: quaestio requirit notitiam retentam → omnes beatitudinem quaerunt → beatitudo ad gaudium reducitur → gaudia discernuntur → verum gaudium est gaudium de veritate → veritas est Deus.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS4","text":"Machina tentationis procedit: bonum creatum → usus necessarius aut pius → voluptas, experimentum vel laus finem usurpat → anima dispergitur → intentio sibi obscuratur → infirmitas confitetur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0134","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0143","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS5","text":"Machina continentiae procedit: mandatum → impotentia detecta → petitio doni → facultas divinitus data → recollectio partialis → nova tentatio → renovata petitio misericordiae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS6","text":"Machina mediationis procedit: distantia peccatoris a Deo → defectus mediationis propriae et daemonicae → coniunctio mortalitatis et iustitiae requisita → Christus homo mediator → mors voluntaria → reconciliatio et sanatio.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0164","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0170","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS7","text":"Circuitus totius libri est: gratia elevat → consuetudo et cupiditas deprimunt → confessio discrimen aperit → misericordia iterum colligit → pax plenaria in futurum differtur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AF1","text":"Deus iam cognoscit → utilitas confessionis problematizatur → caritas distinguit auditorem a curioso → confessio praesentis status fit actus communis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AF2","text":"Amor Dei interrogatur → creaturae ut Deus excluduntur → facultates corporis transcenduntur → memoria exploratur → veritas supra memoriam invenitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AF3","text":"Quaestio de inventione requirit memoriam → appetitus universalis beatitudinis detegitur → beatitudo a gaudio falso distinguitur → gaudium de veritate cum Deo identificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AF4","text":"Praesentia Dei agnoscitur → distantia per consuetudinem explicatur → vita tota tentatio constituitur → triplex cupiditas per actus cotidianos examinatur → fiducia sui dissolvitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AF5","text":"Dispersio requirit continentiam → continentia requirit donum → superbia producit mediatores falsos → Christus humilis mediator demonstratur → desperatio in spem sanationis et vitam pro Christo mutatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0170","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0172","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME1","text":"Confessio ex relatione rerum occultarum in operationem veritatis coram Deo et communitate caritatis reclassificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME2","text":"Memoria ex archivo imaginum in campum ontologice multiplicem mutatur, qui cognitionem, identitatem et temporalitatem sustinet sed subiectum excedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME3","text":"Interiorem sequi non significat in immanentia claudi, quia intimum subiecti ad veritatem supra subiectum aperitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME4","text":"Oppositio simplicis corporis mali et spiritus boni corruit; quaestio primaria fit ordo usus, fruitionis et amoris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0114","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME5","text":"Quaestio beatitudinis a consensu circa nomen ad distinctionem gaudii veri, gaudii falsi et voluntatis divisae transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME6","text":"Voluptas, curiositas et ambitio sub una forma cupiditatis ordinantur tamquam modi quibus attentionem bonum creatum captivam facit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0132","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0142","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME7","text":"Continentia ex suppressionis autonomae exemplari in recollectionem gratia effectam convertitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME8","text":"Mediatio ex mera superioritate spirituali in coniunctionem structuralem mortalitatis humanae et iustitiae divinae reconstituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME9","text":"Identitas christiana non ut status perfectus, sed ut compositio donorum receptorum, vulnerum persistentium et consummationis futurae describitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ALT1","text":"**Altitude 1 — Surface:** Confessio praesentis status, exploratio memoriae et examen tentationum constituunt obiecta immediata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ALT2","text":"**Altitude 2 — Structural:** Relationes inter sensum, memoriam, rationem, veritatem, cupiditatem et gratiam mechanismum internum constituunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ALT3","text":"**Altitude 3 — Metastrategic:** Textus introspectionem privatam in orationem, iudicium intentionum, communionem caritatis et resistentiam gratia sustentatam convertit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0152","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ALT4","text":"**Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal:** Subiectum creatum et mutabile a veritate incommutabili dependet atque inter conversionem praeteritam, tentationem praesentem et pacem futuram temporaliter suspenditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT1","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad restituendos confessionis, ascensus interioris, memoriae, beatitudinis, tentationis, gratiae et mediationis nexus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT2","text":"Systema firmissime cohaeret ubi omniscientiam Dei cum opacitate sui, triplicem cupiditatem cum dispersione et continentiam cum dono coniungit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT3","text":"Transitus inter notitiam universalem veritatis vel beatitudinis et primam cognitionem personalem Dei nondum plene determinatur: Deus antequam discatur in memoria non est, sed sine notitia retenta quaeri non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0065","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0089","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT4","text":"Paradoxum memoriae oblivionis explicite insolutum manet; certitudo actus retinetur sine sufficienti ratione mechanismi repraesentationis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0060","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0062","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT5","text":"Ascensus a corpore ad animam et ab anima ad Deum hierarchiam valoris praesupponit quam capitulum adhibet potius quam integre demonstrat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT6","text":"Assertio omnes beatitudinem et veritatem velle cum odio veritatis componitur per voluntatem divisam, sed diversa significatio verbi velle onus solutionis sustinet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0084","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0086","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT7","text":"Responsabilitas mali et totalis dependentia boni a gratia simul affirmantur, sed modus exactus cooperationis inter voluntatem et donum non formaliter explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0104","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0113","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT8","text":"Terminus inter necessitatem et voluptatem, utilitatem cantus et captationem sensus, curam proximi et amorem laudis intentione discernitur, quae ipsa subiecto incerta est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT9","text":"Clausura christologica interne congruit condicionibus mediatoris, sed incarnationis et redemptionis praemissis revelatis nititur quae ex analysi memoriae sola non derivantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT10","text":"Restitutio motum verum servat; additamentum editoriale anti-Donatisticum applicationem polemicam praebet, non novam praemissam generatricem libri.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0173","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T141615388325Z_c9b6260a","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"BOOK TEN.","source_sha256":"aaeef876066edc8f1bbfb7cd0b9f120af6092469ef2042499002e8d21c7e0ff8","sha256":"197e419162da6cf7c5265453f7af67399abad9cabd5bd5a7690197c5b6375c2b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:16:15.390286+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumentative Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS1","text":"The text asks to what end a man, though God already knows all things and he himself is not fully known to himself, confesses his present condition to God and to men.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS2","text":"Confession effects truth in the heart, attributes goods to God, makes wounds manifest, and turns hearers joined by charity toward thanksgiving and intercession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS3","text":"The question of what a man loves when he loves God establishes knowledge as an ascent through created signs and interior faculties to truth above the mind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS4","text":"The investigation of memory at once discloses the condition of seeking and recognizing and shows that the soul can neither comprehend itself nor place God within itself as an object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0065","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS5","text":"The universal desire for the blessed life is reduced to joy, then to joy in truth, but love of truth is corrupted by the division of the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0086","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS6","text":"Examination of the present condition through the threefold desire shows that life is a continuous temptation, whose powers, limits, and intentions often remain hidden from the subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS7","text":"The impotence of autonomous continence and the failure of false mediators lead to divine mercy and Christ the true mediator.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0170","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS8","text":"The argumentation is confessional, apophatic, introspective, diagnostic, and soteriological; the editorial addition transfers the same structure to polemic against ad hominem judgment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0173","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0175","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}]},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","text":"God knows and judges the whole consciousness of man, but man does not know even himself in his entirety.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A2","text":"Confession makes truth before God, insofar as it signifies that evil displeases one and that good is attributed not to oneself but to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A3","text":"Public confession among hearers joined by charity generates thanksgiving for goods and intercession for evils.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A4","text":"The inner reason judges the messages of the senses and interprets creatures as effects of the Creator.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","text":"God is immutable truth and the life of the soul, presiding above the mutable mind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6","text":"Memory contains, in different ways, images of sensible things, intelligible things, notions of affections, and its own operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0038","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A7","text":"The power of memory and of mind exceeds its own comprehension.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A8","text":"The seeking and recognition of a thing presuppose some retained knowledge of it; what has been wholly erased cannot be sought.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A9","text":"The universal desire for the blessed life implies some common knowledge of it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0075","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A10","text":"The blessed life is joy toward God, in God, and because of God, that is, joy in truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A11","text":"Man loves truth when it confirms a thing loved, but hates it when it reveals his own falsity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12","text":"Creatures are good, but turn into snares when they are held as an end or exceed necessary and pious use.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0114","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","text":"Present life is a continuous temptation, in which a man's powers, motives, and perseverance remain uncertain to himself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0099","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14","text":"The concupiscence of the flesh, the concupiscence of the eyes, and worldly ambition scatter the soul from God into pleasure, vain knowledge, and self-exaltation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0132","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0142","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","text":"Continence gathers the soul from manifold dispersion into the unity of right love and is a gift of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16","text":"Divine mercy provides the capacity for what is commanded, heals infirmities, and perfects what is imperfect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","text":"The mediator of reconciliation must join mortality with men and justice with God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18","text":"Christ, mortal with men and just with God, having become priest and sacrifice by voluntary death, effects reconciliation and hope of healing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0170","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX1","text":"Confession is not information previously unknown to God, nor mere noise of voice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX2","text":"Human hearers neither know the heart of the confessor immediately nor heal his infirmities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX3","text":"Man is not the ultimate judge of himself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX4","text":"Creatures indicate God, but no creature is God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX5","text":"God is not a body, a sensible quality, a vegetative power, or a sensitive faculty.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX6","text":"God is not a bodily image, an affection, memory, a mutable mind, or a thing enclosed in a place of memory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0092","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX7","text":"The objects of disciplines and mathematical relations are not images brought in through bodily senses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0041","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX8","text":"To learn intelligible things is not simply to receive foreign words, but to gather together and recognize what is scattered within.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX9","text":"The blessed life is not any joy whatsoever, nor mere delight in its name.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0082","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX10","text":"Moral uncleanness consists not in food or the creature itself, but in disordered desire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0114","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX11","text":"Curiosity does not become true knowledge merely because it covers the desire of experiencing with the name of knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0132","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0134","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX12","text":"Human praise is not the measure of goodness nor the end of a good work.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0143","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0144","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX13","text":"A converted state neither removes temptation nor guarantees certainty about future perseverance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0118","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX14","text":"Angels, demons, curious visions, and magical arts do not effect reconciliation with God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0164","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0167","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX15","text":"The Word, insofar as it is equal to God, is not a mediator; Christ, insofar as he is man, is mediator.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX16","text":"Flight into solitude does not constitute a solution to vocation, conflict, or infirmity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0172","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D1","text":"Confession does not increase God's knowledge, but orders the subject within the truth of divine knowledge.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D2","text":"Publication of confession is justified only through charity and common benefit, not through curiosity about another's life.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D3","text":"Self-examination necessarily remains provisional, because the one who examines his own powers and motives does not fully see them.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D4","text":"Creatures speak theologically only to reason that compares their appearance with interior truth; a subjecting love impedes judgment.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D5","text":"Memory is a necessary path for seeking God, but not his terminus or essence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D6","text":"The mind is present to itself without fully comprehending itself; the proximity of the subject does not produce transparency.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D7","text":"God is found in memory insofar as truth is recognized, but the principle of this recognition remains above memory and above the subject.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0089","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D8","text":"Universal consensus concerning blessedness does not produce consensus concerning its true account, nor a will sufficient to attain it.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D9","text":"Falsity persists because man wants truth to confirm his choices, but rejects it in order not to correct himself.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0086","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D10","text":"Threefold temptation exhibits three modes by which created good is changed from a means into an illicit end.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0143","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D11","text":"Sensible delight remains legitimate so long as it follows reason and serves piety; it becomes sinful when it precedes or excludes the thing signified.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0121","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D12","text":"Uncertainty about one's powers and the perpetuity of temptation turn the command of continence into prayer for a gift.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0099","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D13","text":"Continence is not mere deprivation of pleasure, but the reintegration of scattered loves under one end.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D14","text":"Love of praise is most difficultly tested by its absence, because praise can be a companion of a good life and is not deliberately removed without corruption of life.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0147","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D15","text":"Vain glory recursively reestablishes itself, because a man can glory even in contempt for praise.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0155","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D16","text":"Christ alone fulfills the conditions of mediation and therefore removes the despair generated by the distance between sinner and God.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0170","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:D17","text":"The editorial addition transfers from Augustine's discourse the structure of confession to polemic: the past vices of a minister magnify grace, do not destroy the Catholic cause, and ad hominem judgment provides no knowledge of the heart.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0173","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0174","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD1","text":"Interior epistemology and soteriology have the same form: descent into oneself discloses not autonomy but dependence on truth above oneself.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD2","text":"Memory is the threshold between presence and transcendence: without it God cannot be recognized, but in it God cannot be contained essentially or spatially.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0065","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0089","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0092","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD3","text":"The desire for blessedness is at once a trace of truth and a site of error, because an end commonly known can be substituted by false joys.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0086","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD4","text":"Threefold desire completes the structure of capture: sense is led from use to pleasure, knowledge from wisdom to experience, and society from charity to private excellence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0143","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD5","text":"Confession is a recursive therapeutic machine: it never exhausts the very opacity it discloses, but converts it into prayer, correction, and communion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0152","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD6","text":"Grace does not replace human action, but gives the capacity to resist; resistance itself simultaneously manifests the gift received and the residual wound.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD7","text":"Ascent to truth makes the distance known, but does not overcome it; Christ's mediation resolves the discontinuity that introspection could only disclose.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD8","text":"The Christian subject is temporally constituted between healing already begun and peace not yet consummated.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX1","text":"For the necessity of confession to hold, complete self-transparency and man's capacity definitively to judge himself must be false.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX2","text":"For interior ascent to hold, the sufficiency of sense for knowing God or ultimate truth must be false.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX3","text":"For the analysis of memory to hold, memory as a merely passive archive of sensible images must be false.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0038","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX4","text":"For the misery of the will to be explained, the desire for good must not always effect right knowledge, choice, and possession of it.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX5","text":"For the doctrine of moderation to hold, the intrinsic evilness of body, senses, and creatures must be false.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0114","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0125","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX6","text":"For the account of grace to hold, it must be false that divine command presupposes an autonomous capacity to obey.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0113","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX7","text":"For the diagnosis of pride to hold, it must be false that human praise faithfully manifests the moral state of the praised person.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0146","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0149","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0150","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX8","text":"For the incarnation to be necessary, it must be false that any spiritual superiority suffices for true mediation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX9","text":"For confession of the present state to remain, stable human perfection within mortal life must be false.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0118","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX1","text":"The system excludes the autonomous subject: man is neither the sufficient measure, nor unity, nor judge, nor physician of himself.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX2","text":"Possession of God as a local, sensible, or mentally enclosed object is structurally precluded.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX3","text":"In the present life no secure middle ground is given, because prosperity, adversity, sense, knowledge, and social relation provide material for temptation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0099","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0125","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0132","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0142","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX4","text":"Present innocence is unavailable as a foundation of hope; mercy alone sustains hope.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX5","text":"Truth and falsehood cannot coexist as goods equally to be possessed; the attempt to retain both loses God.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0162","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX6","text":"Proud ascent to God is impossible, because pride chooses mediators like itself and reproduces the separation it seeks to overcome.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX7","text":"Confession of present man admits no definitive closure, because the subject remains between partial knowledge, future temptation, and healing not yet complete.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0099","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS1","text":"The machine of confession proceeds: divine omniscience plus self-opacity → confession as the effecting of truth → hearing of charity → thanksgiving and intercession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS2","text":"The machine of ascent proceeds: sensible signs → inner judge → exclusion of body and powers shared with animals → memory → excess of memory beyond self-comprehension → truth above the mind.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS3","text":"The machine of blessedness proceeds: seeking requires retained knowledge → all seek blessedness → blessedness is reduced to joy → joys are discerned → true joy is joy in truth → truth is God.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS4","text":"The machine of temptation proceeds: created good → necessary or pious use → pleasure, experience, or praise usurps the end → the soul is scattered → intention is obscured to itself → infirmity is confessed.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0134","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0143","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS5","text":"The machine of continence proceeds: command → impotence disclosed → request for a gift → divinely given capacity → partial recollection → new temptation → renewed request for mercy.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS6","text":"The machine of mediation proceeds: sinner's distance from God → failure of self-mediated and demonic mediation → required conjunction of mortality and justice → Christ the man mediator → voluntary death → reconciliation and healing.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0164","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0170","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS7","text":"The circuit of the whole book is: grace raises up → habit and desire cast down → confession discloses the crisis → mercy gathers again → full peace is deferred to the future.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0160","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AF1","text":"God already knows → the utility of confession is problematized → charity distinguishes the hearer from the curious person → confession of the present state becomes a communal act.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AF2","text":"Love of God is questioned → creatures as God are excluded → bodily faculties are transcended → memory is explored → truth above memory is found.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AF3","text":"The question of finding requires memory → the universal desire for blessedness is disclosed → blessedness is distinguished from false joy → joy in truth is identified with God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0082","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AF4","text":"God's presence is recognized → distance is explained through habit → the whole of life is constituted as temptation → threefold desire is examined through daily acts → self-confidence is dissolved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0096","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:AF5","text":"Dispersion requires continence → continence requires gift → pride produces false mediators → Christ the humble mediator is demonstrated → despair is changed into hope of healing and life for Christ.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0170","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0172","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME1","text":"Confession is reclassified from a report of hidden things into an operation of truth before God and the community of charity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME2","text":"Memory is changed from an archive of images into an ontologically multiple field that sustains knowledge, identity, and temporality but exceeds the subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME3","text":"To follow the inner does not mean to be enclosed in immanence, because the innermost of the subject is opened to truth above the subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME4","text":"The opposition of simply evil body and good spirit collapses; the primary question becomes the order of use, enjoyment, and love.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0114","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0129","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME5","text":"The question of blessedness is transferred from consensus about the name to the distinction of true joy, false joy, and divided will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0082","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME6","text":"Pleasure, curiosity, and ambition are ordered under one form of desire as modes by which created good holds attention captive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0103","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0132","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0142","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME7","text":"Continence is converted from a model of autonomous suppression into a recollection effected by grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME8","text":"Mediation is reconstituted from mere spiritual superiority into a structural conjunction of human mortality and divine justice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME9","text":"Christian identity is described not as a perfect state, but as a composition of received gifts, persistent wounds, and future consummation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ALT1","text":"**Altitude 1 — Surface:** Confession of the present state, exploration of memory, and examination of temptations constitute the immediate objects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ALT2","text":"**Altitude 2 — Structural:** The relations among sense, memory, reason, truth, desire, and grace constitute the internal mechanism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ALT3","text":"**Altitude 3 — Metastrategic:** The text converts private introspection into prayer, judgment of intentions, communion of charity, and resistance sustained by grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0104","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0152","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:ALT4","text":"**Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal:** The created and mutable subject depends on immutable truth and is temporally suspended between past conversion, present temptation, and future peace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to reconstruct the connections of confession, interior ascent, memory, blessedness, temptation, grace, and mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0098","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT2","text":"The system coheres most firmly where it joins God's omniscience with self-opacity, threefold desire with dispersion, and continence with gift.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT3","text":"The transition between universal knowledge of truth or blessedness and the first personal knowledge of God is not yet fully determined: God is not in memory before he is learned, but cannot be sought without retained knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0065","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0089","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT4","text":"The paradox of memory and forgetfulness remains explicitly unresolved; certainty of the act is retained without a sufficient account of the mechanism of representation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0059","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0060","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0062","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT5","text":"The ascent from body to soul and from soul to God presupposes a hierarchy of value that the chapter employs rather than fully demonstrates.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT6","text":"The assertion that all desire blessedness and truth is reconciled with hatred of truth through the divided will, but the different meaning of the word “to will” bears the burden of the solution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0073","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0084","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0086","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT7","text":"Responsibility for evil and total dependence of good on grace are affirmed together, but the exact mode of cooperation between will and gift is not formally explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0101","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0104","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0113","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT8","text":"The boundary between necessity and pleasure, the usefulness of song and the capture of sense, care for one's neighbor and love of praise, is discerned by intention, which itself is uncertain to the subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0123","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0150","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT9","text":"The Christological closure is internally congruent with the conditions of the mediator, but rests on revealed premises of incarnation and redemption that are not derived from analysis of memory alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0094","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0166","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0169","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT10","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement; the anti-Donatist editorial addition provides a polemical application, not a new generative premise of the book.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LIBD:P0173","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LIBD@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_5P0L_LIBD:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 10","title":"Book X.","context":"Chapter 10","original_title":"Liber Decimus.","original_context":"Chapter 10"},"original_title":"Liber Decimus.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU","layer":"CH","title":"Book XI.","order":11,"parents":["RAW_5P0L_LIBU"],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LIBU@R001","sha256":"f4d906c4c36b982d923ff934978d6af7e9b6cee261909064d6a48a37ea3514ae","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS1","text":"Textus quaerit quomodo creatio temporalis cum aeternitate divina componatur et quid sit tempus quod mens experitur atque metitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS2","text":"Deus extra omnem successionem in Verbo coaeterno omnia, etiam tempora, creat; temporis autem mensurabilis ratio in praesentibus animae operationibus reperitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS3","text":"Argumentatio est exegetica, metaphysica, diagnostica, apophatica et reconstructiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS4","text":"Confessio non informativa in petitionem illuminationis transit, qua sensus Scripturae per interiorem veritatem quaeritur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS5","text":"Mutabilitas creaturae ad causam increatam, haec ad Verbum aeternum, Verbum autem ad distinctionem inter aeternitatem et successionem ducit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS6","text":"Obiectio de eo quod Deus ante creationem faciebat dissolvitur ostendendo ipsam notionem temporis ante tempora contradictionem continere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS7","text":"Analysis praesentis, memoriae, attentionis et exspectationis tempus in distentionem animi transfert, quae deinde in quaestionem collectionis animae ad Deum convertitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A1","text":"Confessio Deo omniscienti scientiam non addit, sed affectum confitentis et legentis ad Deum excitat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2","text":"Certitudo de veritate dicti non a lingua vel sono loquentis, sed a veritate stabili intus iudicante et divinitus aperiente pendet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A3","text":"Principium in quo caelum et terra facta sunt est Verbum, Filius, Sapientia et Veritas Dei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A4","text":"Res mutabilis, quia facta est et antequam esset operari non potuit, sui ipsius causa esse nequit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A5","text":"Deus causa est omnis creaturae atque omnium condicionum artis creatae, etiam materiae, corporis, animi, instrumenti, mundani loci et temporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A6","text":"Verbum Deo coaeternum omnia simul et sempiterne dicit, nullo eius elemento cedente vel succedente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A7","text":"Initia et fines rerum temporalium secundum aeternam rationem fiunt, sine nova voluntate aut mutatione in Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A8","text":"Aeternitas divina tota praesens manet, successione caret, et nullum tempus ei coaeternum est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A9","text":"Quod omnino non est neque videri neque mensurari potest; praeteritum autem iam non est et futurum nondum est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A10","text":"Praesens, si extenditur, in praeteritum et futurum dividitur; si indivisibile est, spatio caret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A11","text":"Tempus non est motus corporis, quia tam motus quam quies tempore mensurantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12","text":"Praeterito, praesenti et futuro respondent tres operationes praesentes animae: memoria, attentio sive contuitus, et exspectatio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A13","text":"Mens, cum tempus metitur, praesentem affectionem sive vestigium a rebus transeuntibus relictum metitur, non ipsas res iam absentes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","text":"In actione temporali attentio id quod exspectatur in id quod memoratur continuo transfert.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A15","text":"Deus futura et praeterita cognoscit atque creaturas efficit sine variatione cognitionis et sine distentione actionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16","text":"Distentio vitae humanae terminum suum normativum habet in collectione ad unum Deum per Mediatorem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX1","text":"Confessio non est narratio qua Deus aliquid prius ignotum cognoscat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX2","text":"Veritas Scripturae non constituitur praesentia corporali Moysis, lingua Hebraea, translatione Latina aut sono exteriori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX3","text":"Creatio divina non est artificium humanum quod formam materiae iam existenti imponat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX4","text":"Verbum creatorium non est vox temporalis syllabis successive sonantibus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX5","text":"Quaestio quid Deus ante tempora faceret non designat condicionem realem, quia ubi tempus non erat nullum erat «tunc».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX6","text":"Aeternitas non est tempus infinitum neque interminabilis annorum series.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX7","text":"Praeteritum et futurum, qua praeteritum et futurum, non sunt entia praesentia in occultis locis reposita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX8","text":"Praesens temporale non potest esse longum, quia omnis extensio eius in partes non praesentes solvitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX9","text":"Tempus non est circuitus solis, lunae, siderum aut cuiuslibet corporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX10","text":"Tempora non mensurantur ut res iam peractae vel nondum existentes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX11","text":"Cognitio divina non est memoria et praescientia creaturae ad infinitam amplitudinem aucta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX12","text":"Aporia non solvitur responsione ioculari, falsitate utili aut simulatione scientiae ubi ignorantia manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D1","text":"Confessio simul exercitium affectus et modus cognitionis est, quia mentem ad fontem illuminationis dirigit potius quam Deum informat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D2","text":"Genesis Christologice legitur: formula «in principio» actum creationis per Verbum aeternum constituit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D3","text":"Creatio ex nihilo sequitur, quia nulla materia, regio vel potentia a Deo non facta ante actum creatorium praesupponi potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D4","text":"Novitas creaturae novam voluntatem in Deo non postulat, quia effectus temporalis secundum rationem aeternam ex Verbo immutabili procedit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D5","text":"Quaestio «quid Deus ante creationem faciebat?» falso praesupponit tempus a creatione independens et ideo semanticam condicionem propriae responsionis destruit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D6","text":"Aeternitas et tempus non differunt quantitate durationis, sed modo praesentiae: aeternitas stat, tempus successione transit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D7","text":"Tria tempora proprie reformulantur ut praesens memoriae, praesens attentionis et praesens exspectationis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D8","text":"Praedictio futura non videt rem nondum existentem, sed ex causis, signis vel conceptionibus iam praesentibus futurum enuntiat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D9","text":"Mensuratio temporis fit per comparationem vestigiorum praesentium in animo, non per apprehensionem motus cum tempore identificati.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D10","text":"Longum futurum est longa exspectatio futuri, et longum praeteritum est longa memoria praeteriti.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D11","text":"Eadem conversio ex exspectatione per attentionem in memoriam syllabam, canticum, actionem, vitam et saeculum ordinat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D12","text":"Scientia et actio divina tempore non mensurantur, quamvis effectus cogniti et producti temporaliter ordinentur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D13","text":"Quia vita temporalis per multa in memoriam et exspectationem dispergitur, conversio ad Deum ut transitus a distentione ad intentionem describitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD1","text":"Exegesis primi versus in censuram condicionum temporalium transit, quia creatio recte cogitari nequit nisi vis praesupposita vocabulorum «ante», «tunc» et «incipere» examinetur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD2","text":"Discrimen Creatoris et creaturae simul ontologicum, temporale, causale et epistemicum est: creatura mutatur et distenditur, Deus autem manet et sine distentione efficit atque cognoscit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD3","text":"Usus communis trium temporum retineri potest, dummodo eius grammatica non convertatur in ontologiam praeteriti et futuri quasi praesentium rerum.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD4","text":"Tempus mensurabile neque res caelestis autonoma neque mera fictio est, sed relatio praesentis animi ad impressiones successionis creatae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD5","text":"Structura temporalis est recursive inclusiva: minima transitio soni eandem formam habet ac actio, vita singularis et historia humana.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD6","text":"Analysis temporis fit anthropologia spiritualis, quia distentio non solum mensurationem explicat sed etiam dispersionem vitae in multa constituit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD7","text":"Cognitio progreditur per exclusionem exemplarium impossibilium et in confessione residuae ignorantiae terminatur, non in comprehensione exhaustiva.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX1","text":"Praedicata temporalia de Deo et creatura univoce dici non possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX2","text":"Creatio novitatem effectus admittit, sed deliberationem, mutationem consilii aut novam inclinationem in Deo excludit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX3","text":"Causalitas non requirit semper tempus prius, materiam praevium aut locum externum in quo effectus producatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX4","text":"Auctoritas exterior locutoris, etiam Moysis, sine iudicio veritatis interioris certitudinem non constituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX5","text":"Familiaritas vocabuli «tempus» scientiam naturae temporis non praestat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX6","text":"Tempus non est receptaculum independens in quo Deus, creatio et anima successive collocentur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX7","text":"Memoria et exspectatio res absentes non restituunt ut praesentes; tantum praesentia vestigia et intentiones continent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX8","text":"Ratio creata sine illuminatione et sine confessione limitis sui mysterium aeternitatis aut temporis dominari non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX1","text":"Nullus datur prospectus temporalis extra creationem ex quo Deus ante mundum collocari possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX2","text":"Nullum tempus, nulla materia, nullus locus et nulla creatura stat iuxta Deum ut alterum coaeternum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX3","text":"Creaturae non competit praesens quod simul durationem integram possideat et omni transitu careat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX4","text":"Anima temporalis sibi ipsi perfecte praesens non est, quia inter memoriam, attentionem et exspectationem distrahitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX5","text":"Praeteritum et futurum nullum proprium repositorium habent; absentia eorum ipsam structuram memoriae et exspectationis ordinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX6","text":"Essentia temporis et modus quo aeternitas successionem efficit comprehensioni positivae plenae indisponibiles manent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:FGS1","text":"Machina hermeneutica sic procedit: omniscientia Dei → confessio non informativa → affectus excitatus → petitio illuminationis → iudicium veritatis interioris → intellectus Scripturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:FGS2","text":"Machina creationis sic procedit: mutabilitas rei → facticitas → impossibilitas autocausationis → causa increata → exclusio materiae et loci praevii → creatio ex nihilo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:FGS3","text":"Machina Verbi sic procedit: vox temporalis excluditur → Verbum coaeternum statuitur → omnia simul dicuntur → effectus secundum rationem aeternam temporaliter fiunt → immutabilitas Dei servatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:FGS4","text":"Obiectio de actione divina ante mundum sic dissolvitur: «ante» praesupponit tempus → tempus est creatum → tempus ante tempus est impossibile → quaestio caret referente reali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:FGS5","text":"Reductio temporum sic procedit: praeteritum iam non est + futurum nondum est + praesens extensum dividitur → tria tempora substantialia corruunt → memoria, attentio et exspectatio praesentia substituuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:FGS6","text":"Discrimen motus et temporis sic producitur: motus variari vel cessare potest → motus et quies mensurantur → mensura ab utroque differt → tempus non est motus corporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:FGS7","text":"Mensuratio sic operatur: res transit → affectionem in animo relinquit → attentio vestigium praesens retinet et comparat → proportio durationis enuntiatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:FGS8","text":"Clausura anthropologica sic procedit: exspectatio → attentio → memoria → multiplicatio huius circuitus in vita → distentio animi → conversio per Mediatorem → intentio et collectio ad unum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:AF1","text":"Confessio non informativa → petitio intelligentiae → iudicium veritatis interioris → lectio Verbi ut Principii → creatio ex nihilo → distinctio Verbi aeterni a voce temporali → dissolutio temporis ante creationem → analysis trium temporum → exclusio motus ut temporis essentiae → mensuratio vestigiorum in animo → distentio vitae → desiderium collectionis in Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME1","text":"Creatio non amplius collocatur in tempore praevio, sed ipsum tempus intra ordinem creatum redigitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME2","text":"Oppositio aeternitatis et temporis a differentia quantitatis ad differentiam inter praesentiam stabilem et successionem mutabilem transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME3","text":"«Principium» a solo termino chronologico ad Verbum aeternum, quod simul causa creationis et magister interior est, reclassificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME4","text":"Praeteritum, praesens et futurum ex tribus regionibus rerum in tres modos praesentis animae convertuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME5","text":"Motus caelestis ex essentia temporis in obiectum tempore mensuratum demovetur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME6","text":"Mensuratio temporis ab apprehensione rei transeuntis ad comparationem affectionum praesentium in memoria transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME7","text":"Vita humana ut structura temporalis recursive dispersa describitur, non ut simplex series eventuum exteriorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME8","text":"Lingua communis de tribus temporibus retinetur pragmatice, sed eius ontologia litteralis revocatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ALT1","text":"Altitude 1 — Surface — Obiectum immediatum est intellectus sententiae «In principio fecit Deus caelum et terram» atque responsio quaestioni quid Deus ante creationem faceret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ALT2","text":"Altitude 2 — Structural — Structura causalis distinguit Creatorem, Verbum coaeternum, ordinem creatum et operationes animae quibus successio apprehenditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ALT3","text":"Altitude 3 — Metastrategic — Textus controversiam non responsione intra grammaticam adversarii vincit, sed praesuppositionem temporalem quaestionis destruit et vocabula communia semanticis limitibus subicit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ALT4","text":"Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal — Realitas divina ut praesens immutabile, creatura ut mutabilis dependentia, et vita temporalis ut distentio inter memoriam, attentionem et exspectationem constituuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT1","text":"Axiomata proposita sufficiunt ad restituendam concatenationem a confessione et exegesi ad creationem, tempus, mensurationem et collectionem spiritualem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT2","text":"Nondum plene determinatur utrum tempus ontologice ipsa affectio animi sit an tantum per affectionem animi mensurari possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT3","text":"Doctrina vestigii explicat quid post transitum mensuretur, sed non perfecte explicat unde proportionalitas communis et certitudo mensurae oriatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT4","text":"Tensio manet inter praesens omni spatio carens et attentionem praesentem quae perdurare atque translationem futuri in praeteritum efficere dicitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT5","text":"Ratio aeterna novitatem effectuum sine mutatione Dei servat, sed productionem successionis ex causa omnino non successiva positive non explicat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT6","text":"Possibilitas creaturae «supra tempora» admittitur, sed modus quo talis creatura nec temporalis nec Deo coaeterna sit indeterminatus manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT7","text":"Firmissima pars systematis est dissolutio temporis ante tempora atque distinctio temporis a motu corporali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT8","text":"Transitus a distentione descriptiva ad collectionem normativam per Mediatorem praemissis theologicis, precatione et auctoritate Scripturae nititur, non ex sola analysi temporis deducitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT9","text":"Restitutio verum motum textus servat: exemplaria falsa excluduntur, aporia temporis in animam transfertur, et solutio phenomenologica in confessionem limitis atque desiderium aeternitatis clauditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T142006025285Z_bd7e3efd","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"BOOK ELEVEN.","source_sha256":"f4d906c4c36b982d923ff934978d6af7e9b6cee261909064d6a48a37ea3514ae","sha256":"ec58aa156919c2cc090d6c05e9f26e3e646ec3540d050d3aba57e277b4fb2b4e","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:20:06.026214+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS1","text":"The text asks how temporal creation may be reconciled with divine eternity and what time is that the mind experiences and measures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS2","text":"God, outside all succession, creates all things, including times, in the coeternal Word; but the basis of measurable time is found in the present operations of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS3","text":"The argument is exegetical, metaphysical, diagnostic, apophatic, and reconstructive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS4","text":"Non-informative confession passes into a petition for illumination, by which the meaning of Scripture is sought through interior truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS5","text":"The mutability of the creature leads to the uncreated cause, this to the eternal Word, and the Word to the distinction between eternity and succession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS6","text":"The objection concerning what God was doing before creation is dissolved by showing that the very notion of time before times contains a contradiction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS7","text":"The analysis of the present, memory, attention, and expectation transfers time into the distention of the mind, which is then converted into the question of the soul's gathering to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A1","text":"Confession adds no knowledge to God, who knows all things, but stirs the affection of the one confessing and reading toward God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2","text":"Certainty concerning the truth of what is said depends not on the language or sound of the speaker, but on stable truth judging within and divinely disclosing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A3","text":"The beginning in which heaven and earth were made is the Word, the Son, the Wisdom, and the Truth of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A4","text":"A mutable thing, because it was made and could not act before it existed, cannot be the cause of itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A5","text":"God is the cause of every creature and of all conditions of created art, including matter, body, soul, instrument, worldly place, and time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A6","text":"The Word coeternal with God says all things simultaneously and everlastingly, with no element of it passing away or succeeding another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A7","text":"The beginnings and ends of temporal things occur according to eternal reason, without new will or change in God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A8","text":"Divine eternity remains wholly present, lacks succession, and no time is coeternal with it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A9","text":"What is not at all cannot be either seen or measured; but the past is no longer, and the future is not yet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A10","text":"The present, if extended, is divided into past and future; if indivisible, it lacks duration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A11","text":"Time is not the motion of a body, because both motion and rest are measured by time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12","text":"To past, present, and future correspond three present operations of the soul: memory, attention or regard, and expectation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A13","text":"When the mind measures time, it measures a present affection or trace left by passing things, not the things themselves now absent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","text":"In temporal action, attention continuously transfers what is expected into what is remembered.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A15","text":"God knows future and past things and brings creatures about without variation of knowledge and without distention of action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16","text":"The distention of human life has its normative end in gathering to the one God through the Mediator.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX1","text":"Confession is not a narration by which God comes to know something previously unknown.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX2","text":"The truth of Scripture is not constituted by the bodily presence of Moses, the Hebrew language, a Latin translation, or an exterior sound.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX3","text":"Divine creation is not a human craft that imposes form upon already existing matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX4","text":"The creative Word is not a temporal voice sounding forth syllables successively.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX5","text":"The question of what God was doing before times does not designate a real condition, because where time was not, there was no «then».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX6","text":"Eternity is not infinite time nor an endless series of years.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX7","text":"Past and future, as past and future, are not beings present and stored away in hidden places.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX8","text":"The temporal present cannot be long, because all its extension is dissolved into non-present parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX9","text":"Time is not the circuit of the sun, moon, stars, or of any body whatever.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX10","text":"Times are not measured as things already completed or not yet existing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX11","text":"Divine knowledge is not creaturely memory and foreknowledge increased to infinite magnitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX12","text":"The aporia is not resolved by a joking answer, a useful falsehood, or a pretense of knowledge where ignorance remains.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D1","text":"Confession is at once an exercise of affection and a mode of cognition, because it directs the mind to the source of illumination rather than informing God.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D2","text":"Genesis is read Christologically: the formula «in principio» establishes the act of creation through the eternal Word.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D3","text":"Creation ex nihilo follows, because no matter, region, or power not made by God can be presupposed before the creative act.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D4","text":"The novelty of the creature does not require a new will in God, because the temporal effect proceeds according to eternal reason from the immutable Word.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D5","text":"The question «what was God doing before creation?» falsely presupposes time independent of creation and therefore destroys the semantic condition of its own answer.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D6","text":"Eternity and time differ not in quantity of duration but in mode of presence: eternity stands still; time passes in succession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D7","text":"The three times are properly reformulated as the present of memory, the present of attention, and the present of expectation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D8","text":"Prediction of the future does not see a thing not yet existing, but announces the future from causes, signs, or conceptions already present.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D9","text":"The measurement of time occurs through comparison of present traces in the mind, not through apprehension of motion identified with time.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D10","text":"A long future is a long expectation of the future, and a long past is a long memory of the past.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D11","text":"The same conversion from expectation through attention into memory orders a syllable, a song, an action, a life, and an age.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D12","text":"Divine knowledge and action are not measured by time, although known and produced effects are temporally ordered.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:D13","text":"Because temporal life is dispersed through many things into memory and expectation, conversion to God is described as passage from distention to intention.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD1","text":"The exegesis of the first verse passes into a critique of temporal conditions, because creation cannot be rightly thought unless the presupposed force of the words «ante», «tunc», and «incipere» is examined.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD2","text":"The distinction between Creator and creature is at once ontological, temporal, causal, and epistemic: the creature changes and is distended, whereas God remains and acts and knows without distention.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD3","text":"The common use of the three times may be retained, provided that its grammar is not converted into an ontology of past and future as though they were present things.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD4","text":"Measurable time is neither an autonomous celestial thing nor a mere fiction, but a relation of the present mind to impressions of created succession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD5","text":"Temporal structure is recursively inclusive: the smallest transition of sound has the same form as an action, an individual life, and human history.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD6","text":"The analysis of time becomes spiritual anthropology, because distention not only explains measurement but also constitutes the dispersion of life into many things.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD7","text":"Knowledge progresses through the exclusion of impossible models and terminates in confession of residual ignorance, not in exhaustive comprehension.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX1","text":"Temporal predicates cannot be said univocally of God and creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX2","text":"Creation admits novelty of effects, but excludes deliberation, change of plan, or new inclination in God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX3","text":"Causality does not always require prior time, pre-existing matter, or an external place in which an effect may be produced.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX4","text":"The external authority of a speaker, even Moses, does not establish certainty without the judgment of interior truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX5","text":"Familiarity with the word «time» does not furnish knowledge of the nature of time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX6","text":"Time is not an independent receptacle in which God, creation, and the soul are successively placed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX7","text":"Memory and expectation do not restore absent things as present; they contain only present traces and intentions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX8","text":"Created reason, without illumination and without confession of its own limit, cannot master the mystery of eternity or time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX1","text":"No temporal perspective outside creation is given from which God could be situated before the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX2","text":"No time, no matter, no place, and no creature stands alongside God as another coeternal being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX3","text":"The creature cannot possess a present that simultaneously possesses an entire duration and lacks all passage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX4","text":"The temporal soul is not perfectly present to itself, because it is distracted among memory, attention, and expectation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX5","text":"Past and future have no proper repository; their absence orders the very structure of memory and expectation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX6","text":"The essence of time and the manner in which eternity brings about succession remain unavailable to full positive comprehension.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:FGS1","text":"The hermeneutical machine proceeds thus: God's omniscience → non-informative confession → stirred affection → petition for illumination → judgment of interior truth → understanding of Scripture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:FGS2","text":"The machine of creation proceeds thus: mutability of a thing → facticity → impossibility of self-causation → uncreated cause → exclusion of prior matter and place → creation ex nihilo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:FGS3","text":"The machine of the Word proceeds thus: temporal voice is excluded → the coeternal Word is established → all things are said simultaneously → effects occur temporally according to eternal reason → God's immutability is preserved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:FGS4","text":"The objection concerning divine action before the world is dissolved thus: «before» presupposes time → time is created → time before time is impossible → the question lacks a real referent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:FGS5","text":"The reduction of times proceeds thus: the past is no longer + the future is not yet + the extended present is divided → the three substantial times collapse → present memory, attention, and expectation are substituted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:FGS6","text":"The distinction of motion and time is produced thus: motion can vary or cease → motion and rest are measured → the measure differs from both → time is not the motion of a body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:FGS7","text":"Measurement operates thus: a thing passes → it leaves an affection in the mind → attention retains and compares the present trace → a proportion of duration is stated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:FGS8","text":"The anthropological closure proceeds thus: expectation → attention → memory → multiplication of this circuit in life → distention of the mind → conversion through the Mediator → intention and gathering to the one.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:AF1","text":"Non-informative confession → petition for understanding → judgment of interior truth → reading of the Word as Principle → creation ex nihilo → distinction of the eternal Word from temporal voice → dissolution of time before creation → analysis of the three times → exclusion of motion as the essence of time → measurement of traces in the mind → distention of life → desire for gathering in God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME1","text":"Creation is no longer situated in prior time, but time itself is reduced within the created order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME2","text":"The opposition of eternity and time is transferred from a difference of quantity to a difference between stable presence and mutable succession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME3","text":"«Principium» is reclassified from a merely chronological term to the eternal Word, which is at once the cause of creation and the interior teacher.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME4","text":"Past, present, and future are converted from three regions of things into three modes of the soul's present.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME5","text":"Celestial motion is demoted from the essence of time to an object measured by time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME6","text":"The measurement of time is transferred from apprehension of a passing thing to comparison of present affections in memory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME7","text":"Human life is described as a recursively dispersed temporal structure, not as a simple series of exterior events.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME8","text":"Common language about the three times is retained pragmatically, but its literal ontology is revoked.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ALT1","text":"Altitude 1 — Surface — The immediate object is the understanding of the sentence «In principio fecit Deus caelum et terram» and the answer to the question of what God was doing before creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ALT2","text":"Altitude 2 — Structural — The causal structure distinguishes the Creator, the coeternal Word, the created order, and the operations of the soul by which succession is apprehended.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ALT3","text":"Altitude 3 — Metastrategic — The text does not overcome the controversy by an answer within the adversary's grammar, but destroys the temporal presupposition of the question and subjects common words to semantic limits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:ALT4","text":"Altitude 4 — Ontological/Temporal — Divine reality as immutable present, the creature as mutable dependence, and temporal life as distention among memory, attention, and expectation are established.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT1","text":"The proposed axioms suffice to reconstruct the concatenation from confession and exegesis to creation, time, measurement, and spiritual gathering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT2","text":"It is not yet fully determined whether time is ontologically the affection of the mind itself or can only be measured through the affection of the mind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT3","text":"The doctrine of the trace explains what is measured after passage, but does not perfectly explain whence common proportionality and certainty of measurement arise.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT4","text":"A tension remains between a present lacking all duration and present attention, which is said to endure and to bring about the transfer of the future into the past.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT5","text":"Eternal reason preserves the novelty of effects without change in God, but does not positively explain the production of succession from a cause wholly without succession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT6","text":"The possibility of a creature «above times» is admitted, but the manner in which such a creature is neither temporal nor coeternal with God remains indeterminate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT7","text":"The strongest part of the system is the dissolution of time before times and the distinction of time from bodily motion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT8","text":"The passage from descriptive distention to normative gathering through the Mediator rests upon theological premises, prayer, and the authority of Scripture; it is not deduced from analysis of time alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the text's true movement: false models are excluded, the aporia of time is transferred into the soul, and the phenomenological solution concludes in confession of limit and desire for eternity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LIBU@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_5P0L_LIBU:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 11","title":"Book XI.","context":"Chapter 11","original_title":"Liber Undecimus.","original_context":"Chapter 11"},"original_title":"Liber Undecimus.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5","layer":"CH","title":"Book XII.","order":12,"parents":["RAW_5P0L_LI_5"],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LI_5@R001","sha256":"bd1f95d96150461bad1f613e0b60c117bba0d5603c92126cea88923a8dd110f9","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS1","text":"Textus quaerit qua ratione initium Geneseos creationem, informitatem, ordinem et absentiam temporis simul significare possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS2","text":"Caelum principaliter creaturam intellectualem Deo contemplando inhaerentem, terra autem materiam informem ex qua mundus corporeus formatur significat, sine exclusione aliorum sensuum verorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS3","text":"Argumentatio a reconstructione metaphysica creationis ad disciplinam hermeneuticam pluralitatis verae procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS4","text":"Conceptus tenebrarum et informitatis per privationem purgatur, ut materia neque nihil neque corpus monstruose formatum intelligatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS5","text":"Ex relatione inter formam, mutationem et tempus deducuntur duae creaturae temporibus carentes: una perfecte formata per inhaesionem, altera penitus informis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS6","text":"Disputatio de re creata in disputationem de sensu Scripturae transit per distinctionem inter veritatem rerum et intentionem historicam Moysi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS7","text":"Incertitudo de singulari intentione humana resolvitur non exclusione sensuum verorum, sed veritate communi, caritate interpretum et amplitudine intentionis Spiritus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A1","text":"Deus aeternus est, nec substantia, scientia aut voluntas eius temporalem vicissitudinem patiuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A2","text":"Omnis natura vel substantia quae Deus non est a Deo facta est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A3","text":"Omnis creatura ex nihilo, non ex substantia Dei neque ex materia coaeterna, facta est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A4","text":"Omnis creatura, quia non est idipsum quod Deus, mutabilitatem habet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A5","text":"Verbum sive Sapientia increata est Principium coaeternum in quo Deus omnia creat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A6","text":"Materia informis est aliquid prope nihil, capax tamen formarum ex quibus mundus constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A7","text":"Informitas perfecta omni specie actuali, ordine et variatione formata caret.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A8","text":"Tempora ex ordinatis mutationibus motuum et formarum fiunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A9","text":"Ubi nulla est varietas motuum aut formarum, nulla est vicissitudo temporis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A10","text":"Caelum caeli est creatura intellectualis formata, Deo non coaeterna et natura mutabilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A11","text":"Inhaesio continua creaturae intellectualis Deo impedit ne eius mutabilitas in mutationem actualem exeat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A12","text":"Aliquid altero prius esse potest aeternitate, tempore, electione aut origine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A13","text":"Scriptura divina vera est et falsum Spiritui vel ministro veraci attribui non potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A14","text":"Sermo Scripturae paucus et humilis diversis intellectus gradibus divinitus accommodatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","text":"Eadem verba Scripturae plures sensus vere significatos sustinere possunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A16","text":"Veritas rei et intentio historica scriptoris sunt diversa obiecta cognitionis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A17","text":"Caritas est finis et norma legitimi usus Scripturae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A18","text":"Spiritus sanctus novit et per verba revelat quidquid veri posteris aperiendum est, etiamsi minister humanus unum tantum sensum cogitaverit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX1","text":"Tenebrae non sunt substantia positiva, sed absentia lucis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX2","text":"Materia informis non est omnino nihil, quia iam formari potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX3","text":"Informitas non est congeries formarum foedarum, insolitarum aut perturbatarum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX4","text":"Materia informis neque forma intelligibilis, sicut vita vel iustitia, neque res sensibilis actu est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX5","text":"Creatio neque ex substantia divina neque ex subiecto increato et Deo coaeterno procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX6","text":"Sapientia creata sive caelum intellectuale non est Sapientia increata per quam omnia facta sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX7","text":"Carentia temporis in creatura non est coaeternitas cum Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX8","text":"Prioritas materiae respectu formae non est necessario prioritas temporalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0102","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX9","text":"Silentium Geneseos de productione alicuius rei non probat eam a Deo non esse factam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX10","text":"Deus non creat ad modum corporis vel hominis nova voluntate moti, neque eius dictum est sonus temporaliter transiens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX11","text":"Pluralitas sensuum verorum non est admissio falsitatis, contradictionis arbitrariae aut indifferentiae interpretativae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX12","text":"Incertitudo de cogitatione Moysi neque veritatem rerum infirmat neque contentionem de intentione eius iustificat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D1","text":"Tenebrae super abyssum nihil materiae addunt, sed statum eius nondum illuminatum et formatum significant.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D2","text":"Materia informis concipienda est subtractione omnis formae actualis, non fictione formarum deformium.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D3","text":"Formatio capacitatem materiae in species ordinatas actualizat, quarum mutationes tempora mundi constituunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D4","text":"Duae creaturae extra vicissitudinem dierum intelliguntur: intellectualis quia non mutatur, informis quia nondum habet quo mutetur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A7","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A9","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D5","text":"Creatura intellectualis aeternitatem participat per inhaesionem, sed coaeterna Deo non est, quia facta et mutabilis manet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D6","text":"Materia ante dies et ante formas est origine, non intervallo temporis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A7","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A9","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D7","text":"Locutio «In principio» potest simul ad Sapientiam increatam et ad ordinem originis creaturarum referri.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A12","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D8","text":"Nomina caeli et terrae possunt diversas totalitates creatas vel diversas conditiones earum designare, dummodo sensus prolatus verus sit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D9","text":"Veritas de creatione, forma et tempore certius cognosci potest quam cogitatio singularis quam Moyses scribendo habuit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D10","text":"Assertio exclusiva de intentione Moysi caret fundamento, ubi plures sensus veri adsunt et mens auctoris directe non videtur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D11","text":"Interpretes sensuum diversorum concordare possunt, si veritatem communem potius quam proprietatem sententiae sequuntur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D12","text":"Humilitas superficiei Scripturae fidem rudium sustinet, dum brevitas eius eruditis plures nexus veros aperit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D13","text":"Plenitudo sensuum divinorum non pendet ab eo quod minister humanus omnes sensus conscie perspexerit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A16","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D14","text":"Interpres unum sensum verum, certum et bonum eligere potest, salva intentione qua sensum ministri quaerit et alios sensus veros non excludit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A16","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A17","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD1","text":"Tempus non est receptaculum primarium creationis, sed effectus mutationis actualis in creaturis formatis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A9","CH_5P0L_LI_5:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD2","text":"Ordo creatus duos limites temporibus carentes habet: plenitudinem formae Deo inhaerentem et defectum formae prope nihil.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:D4","CH_5P0L_LI_5:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_5:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD3","text":"Initium Geneseos structuram dependentiae ontologicae potius quam seriem momentorum ante mundum describit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:D4","CH_5P0L_LI_5:D6","CH_5P0L_LI_5:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD4","text":"Omissio narrativa numquam convertit creaturam in principium ontologice independens, quia universitas creati ex nihilo a Deo pendet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD5","text":"Auctoritas Scripturae agrum sensuum verorum multiplicat, sed eum veritate divina et exclusione falsi circumscribit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD6","text":"Inaccessibilitas intentionis humanae interpretationem non dissolvit, sed ab exclusivismo ad pluralitatem veritate et caritate limitatam transfert.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:D9","CH_5P0L_LI_5:D10","CH_5P0L_LI_5:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD7","text":"Simplicitas pedagogica et profunditas speculativa sunt operationes eiusdem sermonis canonici, non gradus inter se repugnantes.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_5:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX1","text":"Exemplar temporis tamquam spatii per se existentis, in quo etiam informitas et Deus locentur, falsum esse debet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX2","text":"Necessaria conversio omnis mutabilitatis possibilis in mutationem actualem excluditur, alioquin caelum intellectuale temporibus carere non posset.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX3","text":"Aequatio realitatis cum forma actuali falsa esse debet, alioquin materia informis aut nihil aut iam formata esset.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX4","text":"Informitas ut principium positivum mali vel chaos Deo adversum tacite excluditur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX5","text":"Praesuppositio qua nihil a Deo factum est nisi cuius factio expresse narratur repudianda est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX6","text":"Praesuppositio qua veritas unicum tantum sensum verbalem requirit falsa esse debet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX7","text":"Intentio conscia ministri humani non potest totum ambitum significationis divinae exhaurire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX8","text":"Veritas non potest privatim possideri vel ex origine interpretis auctoritatem accipere, quia supra omnes mentes communis manet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SNX1","text":"Cogitatio informitatis omnino imaginibus formatis carens indisponibilis manet; materia tantum per abstractionem et negationem specierum attingitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SNX2","text":"Actus interior Moysi, qui interpretationem univocam definitive confirmaret, ab interpretibus non videtur et etiam testimonio eius apparenti crederetur potius quam immediate cognosceretur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0087","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SNX3","text":"Nullum «ante tempus» temporaliter repraesentabile admittitur; origo prae-temporalis narrari potest tantum quasi prioritas esset successio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0104","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SNX4","text":"Clausura exhaustiva Scripturae praecluditur, quia finita inquisitio neque omnes sensus veros neque totam profunditatem verborum comprehendere potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0110","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:FGS1","text":"Deus incommutabilis in Verbo + nulla materia coaeterna → creatio ex nihilo → creatura a Deo dissimilis et mutabilis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:FGS2","text":"Capacitas formarum sine specie → absentia ordinis et variationis → absentia temporis → receptio formarum → mutationes ordinatae → dies et mundus temporalis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:FGS3","text":"Creatura intellectualis formata + mutabilitas naturalis + inhaesio continua Deo → nulla mutatio actualis → participatio aeternitatis sine coaeternitate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:FGS4","text":"Distinctio aeternitatis, temporis, electionis et originis → prioritas materiae origine → lectio non chronologica initii Geneseos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:FGS5","text":"Verba pauca et profunda → sensus candidati multiplices → examen veritatis → exclusio falsi → retentio plurium sensuum verorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:FGS6","text":"Veritas rei cognoscibilis + intentio Moysi non directe cognoscibilis + plenitudo Spiritus → recusatio monopolii interpretativi → concordia caritatis → electio unius sensus veri sine clausura ceterorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AF1","text":"Motus ontologicus procedit: obscuritas verborum → purgatio informitatis → creatio ex nihilo → duplex creatura temporibus carens → distinctio originis a tempore.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AF2","text":"Motus disputativus procedit: obiectio interpretum → consensus de veris metaphysicis → multiplicatio lectionum → distinctio rei ab intentione → imminutio certitudinis de mente Moysi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AF3","text":"Motus hermeneuticus procedit: incertitudo intentionis humanae → amplitudo intentionis Spiritus → veritas communis → caritas → electio non exclusiva sensus veri.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0113","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME1","text":"«Caelum» et «terra» ex nominibus univoce physicis in signa plurium ordinum creati reclassificantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0099","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME2","text":"Informitas et tenebrae ex entitatibus imaginatis in limites privativos formae et illuminationis convertuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME3","text":"Tempus ex medio universali in effectum mutationum ordinatarum rerum formatarum transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME4","text":"Carentia temporis bifariam describitur: supra vicissitudinem per inhaesionem formae, infra vicissitudinem per defectum formae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME5","text":"Oppositio «prius–posterius» in quattuor rationes separatur, unde ordo originis sine successione temporali cogitari potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME6","text":"Interpretatio ex certamine pro unico sensu in agrum pluralitatis verae, falsitate exclusa et caritate ordinata, transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME7","text":"Intentio auctoris humani manet norma quaerenda, sed desinit esse obiectum eadem certitudine cognoscibile ac veritas rerum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME8","text":"Humilitas sermonis canonici ex simplicitate conceptus in mechanismum accommodationis et fecunditatis semanticæ reclassificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ALT1","text":"Gradus superficiei verba «caelum», «terra», «tenebrae» et «in principio» immediate interpretatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ALT2","text":"Gradus structuralis creationem ex nihilo, capacitatem materiae, receptionem formarum, mutationem et productionem temporis connectit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ALT3","text":"Gradus metastrategicus contentionem de sensu in distinctionem inter veritatem, intentionem, auctoritatem et caritatem reconstituit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ALT4","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis Deum incommutabilem, creaturam mutabilem, participationem aeternitatis et tempus emergens distinguit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT1","text":"Axiomata ontologica et hermeneutica sufficiunt ad utrumque motum argumentationis restituendum: interpretationem creationis et disciplinam pluralitatis sensuum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT2","text":"Cohaerentia interna maxime nititur distinctionibus inter mutabilitatem et mutationem, inter originem et tempus, atque inter veritatem rei et intentionem scriptoris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT3","text":"Firmissima deductio est quod sine variatione formarum non sit tempus, unde duplex carentia temporis intelligitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT4","text":"Status materiae informis manet incomplete determinatus, quia aliquid esse et omni specie actuali carere affirmatur per notionem capacitatis quae ulterius non resolvitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT5","text":"Textus inter persuasionem Moysen omnia vera sensisse et concessionem eum fortasse unum sensum cogitavisse fluctuat; plenitudo Spiritus commissuram tuetur, non ambiguitatem tollit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0110","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT6","text":"Plures attributiones eorundem nominum verae declarantur, sed norma qua sensus diversi simul compatibiles potius quam tantum separatim veri sint non plene formalizatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT7","text":"Accommodatio sermonis et amplitudo intentionis divinae auctoritate theologica et analogia potius quam demonstratione independenter conclusa sustentantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT8","text":"Restitutio servat motum verum textus ab ontologia formae et temporis ad epistemicam modestiam, pluralitatem veram et concordiam caritatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T142217714180Z_7d315246","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"BOOK TWELVE.","source_sha256":"bd1f95d96150461bad1f613e0b60c117bba0d5603c92126cea88923a8dd110f9","sha256":"a0a9f9ef06453a4e28e859a9b92073466b3de27e471710380da7f9152f6f3c49","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:22:17.715701+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS1","text":"The text asks by what account the beginning of Genesis can signify simultaneously creation, formlessness, order, and the absence of time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS2","text":"Heaven principally signifies the intellectual creature adhering to God by contemplating Him, while earth signifies formless matter from which the corporeal world is formed, without excluding other true senses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS3","text":"The argument proceeds from a metaphysical reconstruction of creation to a hermeneutical discipline of true plurality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS4","text":"The concepts of darkness and formlessness are purified through privation, so that matter may be understood as neither nothing nor a monstrously formed body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS5","text":"From the relation among form, change, and time are deduced two creatures lacking times: one perfectly formed through adherence, the other utterly formless.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS6","text":"The discussion of the created thing passes into a discussion of the sense of Scripture through the distinction between the truth of things and Moses' historical intention.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS7","text":"Uncertainty concerning a singular human intention is resolved not by excluding true senses, but by common truth, the charity of interpreters, and the breadth of the Spirit's intention.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A1","text":"God is eternal, and neither His substance, knowledge, nor will undergo temporal change.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A2","text":"Every nature or substance that is not God has been made by God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0028","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A3","text":"Every creature has been made from nothing, not from God's substance nor from matter coeternal with Him.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A4","text":"Every creature, because it is not the very same thing as God, possesses mutability.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A5","text":"The Word, or uncreated Wisdom, is the coeternal Beginning in which God creates all things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A6","text":"Formless matter is something close to nothing, yet capable of the forms from which the world is constituted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A7","text":"Perfect formlessness lacks every actual species, order, and formed variation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A8","text":"Times arise from ordered changes of motions and forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A9","text":"Where there is no variety of motions or forms, there is no succession of time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A10","text":"The heaven of heaven is an intellectual creature, formed, not coeternal with God, and mutable by nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A11","text":"The continuous adherence of the intellectual creature to God prevents its mutability from issuing into actual change.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0030","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A12","text":"One thing can be prior to another in eternity, time, choice, or origin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0101","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A13","text":"Divine Scripture is true, and falsehood cannot be attributed to the Spirit or to a truthful minister.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A14","text":"The sparse and humble speech of Scripture is divinely accommodated to diverse levels of understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","text":"The same words of Scripture can support several truly signified senses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A16","text":"The truth of the thing and the historical intention of the writer are distinct objects of knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A17","text":"Charity is the end and norm of the legitimate use of Scripture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0062","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:A18","text":"The Holy Spirit knows and reveals through words whatever truth is to be disclosed to posterity, even if the human minister thought of only one sense.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX1","text":"Darkness is not a positive substance, but the absence of light.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX2","text":"Formless matter is not altogether nothing, because it can already be formed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX3","text":"Formlessness is not a heap of ugly, unfamiliar, or disordered forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX4","text":"Formless matter is neither an intelligible form, such as life or justice, nor an actual sensible thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX5","text":"Creation proceeds neither from divine substance nor from an uncreated subject coeternal with God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0058","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX6","text":"Created wisdom, or the intellectual heaven, is not the uncreated Wisdom through which all things were made.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX7","text":"The lack of time in a creature is not coeternity with God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX8","text":"The priority of matter with respect to form is not necessarily temporal priority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0102","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX9","text":"Genesis' silence concerning the production of some thing does not prove that it was not made by God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX10","text":"God does not create in the manner of a body or a human being moved by a new will, nor is His utterance a sound passing temporally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX11","text":"The plurality of true senses is not an admission of falsehood, arbitrary contradiction, or interpretive indifference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX12","text":"Uncertainty concerning Moses' thought neither weakens the truth of things nor justifies contention about his intention.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D1","text":"Darkness over the abyss adds nothing to matter, but signifies its state as not yet illuminated and formed.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D2","text":"Formless matter must be conceived through the subtraction of every actual form, not through the fiction of deformed forms.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D3","text":"Formation actualizes matter's capacity into ordered species, whose changes constitute the times of the world.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D4","text":"Two creatures are understood outside the succession of days: the intellectual because it does not change, the formless because it does not yet possess that by which it might change.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A7","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A9","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D5","text":"The intellectual creature participates in eternity through adherence, but is not coeternal with God, because it remains made and mutable.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D6","text":"Matter is before days and before forms by origin, not by an interval of time.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A7","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A9","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D7","text":"The expression «In principio» can refer simultaneously to uncreated Wisdom and to the order of the origin of creatures.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A12","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D8","text":"The names heaven and earth can designate diverse created totalities or their diverse conditions, provided that the proposed sense is true.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0068","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0069","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D9","text":"Truth concerning creation, form, and time can be known more certainly than the particular thought Moses had while writing.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D10","text":"An exclusive assertion concerning Moses' intention lacks foundation where several true senses are present and the author's mind is not directly seen.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D11","text":"Interpreters of diverse senses can agree if they follow common truth rather than ownership of an opinion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D12","text":"The humility of Scripture's surface sustains the faith of the unlearned, while its brevity opens several true connections to the learned.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D13","text":"The fullness of divine senses does not depend upon the human minister's having consciously discerned all senses.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A16","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:D14","text":"An interpreter can choose one true, certain, and good sense, while preserving the intention by which he seeks the minister's sense and does not exclude other true senses.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A16","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A17","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD1","text":"Time is not the primary receptacle of creation, but an effect of actual change in formed creatures.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A9","CH_5P0L_LI_5:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD2","text":"The created order has two limits lacking times: the fullness of form adhering to God and the defect of form close to nothing.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:D4","CH_5P0L_LI_5:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_5:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD3","text":"The beginning of Genesis describes a structure of ontological dependence rather than a series of moments before the world.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:D4","CH_5P0L_LI_5:D6","CH_5P0L_LI_5:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0104","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD4","text":"Narrative omission never turns a creature into an ontologically independent principle, because the whole of creation depends on God from nothing.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A3","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD5","text":"The authority of Scripture multiplies the field of true senses, but circumscribes it by divine truth and the exclusion of falsehood.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD6","text":"The inaccessibility of human intention does not dissolve interpretation, but transfers it from exclusivism to a plurality limited by truth and charity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:D9","CH_5P0L_LI_5:D10","CH_5P0L_LI_5:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD7","text":"Pedagogical simplicity and speculative profundity are operations of the same canonical speech, not mutually conflicting levels.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_5:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX1","text":"The model of time as a space existing in itself, in which even formlessness and God are located, must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX2","text":"The necessary conversion of every possible mutability into actual change is excluded; otherwise the intellectual heaven could not lack times.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX3","text":"The equation of reality with actual form must be false; otherwise formless matter would be either nothing or already formed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX4","text":"Formlessness as a positive principle of evil or as chaos opposed to God is tacitly excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0075","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX5","text":"The presupposition that nothing was made by God unless its making is expressly narrated must be rejected.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX6","text":"The presupposition that truth requires only one verbal sense must be false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX7","text":"The conscious intention of the human minister cannot exhaust the whole scope of divine signification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX8","text":"Truth cannot be privately possessed or receive authority from an interpreter's origin, because it remains common above all minds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0087","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SNX1","text":"The thought of formlessness entirely devoid of formed images remains unavailable; matter is attained only through abstraction and the negation of species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SNX2","text":"Moses' inner act, which would definitively confirm a univocal interpretation, is not seen by interpreters and would be believed even on the basis of his apparent testimony rather than immediately known.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0087","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SNX3","text":"No temporally representable «before time» is admitted; pre-temporal origin can be narrated only as though priority were succession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0104","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:SNX4","text":"The exhaustive closure of Scripture is precluded, because finite inquiry can comprehend neither all true senses nor the whole depth of the words.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0110","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:FGS1","text":"Immutable God in the Word + no coeternal matter → creation from nothing → creature unlike God and mutable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:FGS2","text":"Capacity for forms without species → absence of order and variation → absence of time → reception of forms → ordered changes → days and temporal world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:FGS3","text":"Formed intellectual creature + natural mutability + continuous adherence to God → no actual change → participation in eternity without coeternity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:FGS4","text":"Distinction of eternity, time, choice, and origin → priority of matter by origin → non-chronological reading of the beginning of Genesis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:FGS5","text":"Few and profound words → multiple candidate senses → examination of truth → exclusion of falsehood → retention of several true senses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:FGS6","text":"Knowable truth of the thing + Moses' intention not directly knowable + fullness of the Spirit → rejection of interpretive monopoly → concord of charity → choice of one true sense without closure upon the others.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AF1","text":"The ontological movement proceeds: obscurity of words → purification of formlessness → creation from nothing → two creatures lacking times → distinction of origin from time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0101","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AF2","text":"The disputative movement proceeds: objection of interpreters → consensus concerning true metaphysical matters → multiplication of readings → distinction of the thing from intention → diminution of certainty concerning Moses' mind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:AF3","text":"The hermeneutical movement proceeds: uncertainty of human intention → breadth of the Spirit's intention → common truth → charity → non-exclusive choice of a true sense.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0085","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0113","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME1","text":"«Caelum» and «terra» are reclassified from univocally physical names into signs of multiple orders of creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0099","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME2","text":"Formlessness and darkness are converted from imagined entities into privative limits of form and illumination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME3","text":"Time is transferred from a universal medium into an effect of the ordered changes of formed things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME4","text":"The lack of time is described in two ways: above succession through adherence to form, below succession through defect of form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0034","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME5","text":"The opposition «prius–posterius» is separated into four accounts, whence an order of origin without temporal succession can be conceived.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME6","text":"Interpretation is transferred from contest over a single sense into a field of true plurality, with falsehood excluded and ordered by charity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME7","text":"The intention of the human author remains a norm to be sought, but ceases to be an object knowable with the same certainty as the truth of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME8","text":"The humility of canonical speech is reclassified from simplicity of conception into a mechanism of accommodation and semantic fecundity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0091","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ALT1","text":"The surface level immediately interprets the words «caelum», «terra», «tenebrae», and «in principio».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0098","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ALT2","text":"The structural level connects creation from nothing, matter's capacity, reception of forms, change, and the production of time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ALT3","text":"The metastrategic level reconstitutes the contention concerning sense into a distinction among truth, intention, authority, and charity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:ALT4","text":"The ontological and temporal level distinguishes immutable God, mutable creature, participation in eternity, and emergent time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0028","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT1","text":"The ontological and hermeneutical axioms suffice to reconstruct both movements of the argument: the interpretation of creation and the discipline of the plurality of senses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT2","text":"Internal coherence depends most greatly upon the distinctions between mutability and change, between origin and time, and between the truth of the thing and the writer's intention.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0102","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT3","text":"The strongest deduction is that without variation of forms there is no time, whence the twofold lack of time is understood.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT4","text":"The status of formless matter remains incompletely determined, because that it is something and lacks every actual species is affirmed through a notion of capacity that is not further resolved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT5","text":"The text fluctuates between the persuasion that Moses perceived all true things and the concession that he may have thought of one sense; the fullness of the Spirit preserves the joint, but does not remove the ambiguity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0110","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT6","text":"Several attributions of the same names are declared true, but the norm by which diverse senses are simultaneously compatible rather than merely separately true is not fully formalized.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0106","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0109","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT7","text":"The accommodation of speech and the breadth of divine intention are sustained by theological authority and analogy rather than established independently by demonstration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0090","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the text's true movement from the ontology of form and time to epistemic modesty, true plurality, and the concord of charity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LI_5:P0112","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LI_5@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_5P0L_LI_5:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 12","title":"Book XII.","context":"Chapter 12","original_title":"Liber Duodecimus.","original_context":"Chapter 12"},"original_title":"Liber Duodecimus.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0","layer":"CH","title":"Book XIII.","order":13,"parents":["RAW_5P0L_LDT0"],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LDT0@R001","sha256":"71aca36a3b4fbe8072a0368646810e7162fe84eff4275bdfa7029cbaf7b84b2b","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS1","text":"Textus quaerit quo nexu bonitas Dei non indigentis, formatio creaturae, insinuatio Trinitatis, sanctificatio Ecclesiae et requies aeterna ex Genesi intelligantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS2","text":"Omne esse, formari, illuminari, bene vivere et quiescere creaturae ex gratuita operatione Dei procedit, qui nullo creato bono eget.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS3","text":"Argumentatio metaphysicam creationis, exegesim trinitariam, allegoriam ecclesialem et refutationem dualismi in unum systema reconstructivum coniungit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS4","text":"Motus initialis a gratia praeveniente ad distinctionem Dei sufficientis et creaturae dependentis, deinde ad formationem per Verbum et elevationem per Spiritum procedit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS5","text":"Ordo Geneseos in ordinem ecclesialem convertitur: illuminatio, auctoritas Scripturae, discretio fidelium, opera misericordiae, ministeria spiritualia, sacramenta, continentia et renovatio mentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0130","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS6","text":"Motus finalis a bonitate singulorum ad bonitatem totius, ab operibus temporalibus ad sabbatum sine vespera, et a divina operatione in nobis ad divinam quietem in nobis transit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A1","text":"Deus solus simpliciter atque incommutabiliter est, scit et vult, eiusque beatitudo et quies ab essentia eius non differunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A2","text":"Deus nullo bono creato eget neque creatione vel perfectione creaturarum perficitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A3","text":"Omne creatum esse ex bonitate gratuita Dei accipit, nullo merito creaturae antecedente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A4","text":"Creatura de nihilo, non de substantia Dei neque de materia Deo extranea, producitur; materia informis ipsa quoque concreatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0127","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A5","text":"In creatura aliud est esse et aliud formatum esse; in spiritu creato aliud est vivere et aliud sapienter ac beate vivere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6","text":"Creatura informis per Verbum revocatur ad unitatem, conversione formatur et illuminatione fit conformis Deo sine aequalitate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7","text":"Spiritus sanctus, ut donum et caritas, amorem infundit quo creatura vel sursum ad Deum vel deorsum ad inferiora fertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A8","text":"Creatura rationalis nullo bono quod Deo minus est, ne ipsa quidem sibi, ad beatam requiem satiatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A9","text":"Quidquid aliquo modo est, in quantum est, bonum est; singula bona sunt, universitas ordinata bona valde est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A10","text":"Res sunt quia Deus aeternaliter eas videt; creatura autem temporaliter eas videt quia sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0140","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A11","text":"Scriptura verbis temporalibus aeternum Verbum ministrat atque intellectui humano auctoritatem superiorem praebet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A12","text":"Pater, Filius et Spiritus sanctus in primis Geneseos verbis in aenigmate leguntur, sine divisione unius creatoris.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13","text":"Recta cognitio donorum Dei fit per Spiritum Dei, ita ut Deus in creatura cognoscat, videat et loquatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A14","text":"Expositio ordinem creationis atque narrationis Geneseos tamquam figuram formationis et sanctificationis Ecclesiae legit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0130","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15","text":"Sanctificatio ecclesialis secundum capacitatem progreditur a conversione initiali per disciplinam, opera et imitationem ad renovatum iudicium mentis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A16","text":"Spiritualis homo iudicat signa, interpretationes et mores corrigibiles sub auctoritate Scripturae, non ipsam Scripturam neque occulta iudicia Dei.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A17","text":"Una res intelligibilis multipliciter enuntiari et una enuntiatio multipliciter vere intelligi potest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A18","text":"Renovatio temporalis manet sub fide et spe donec opera transeant et creatura in sabbato aeterno requiescat in Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX1","text":"Cultus et ministerium creaturae neque lassitudinem Dei levant neque potestatem eius supplent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX2","text":"Creatura neque de divina substantia neque de natura hostili, increata et Deo contraria, constituitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0116","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0127","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX3","text":"Creatura neque esse, neque illuminari, neque beatificari antecedenti merito promeretur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX4","text":"Esse non est idem ac pulchrum esse, nec vivere idem ac sapienter vel beate vivere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX5","text":"Malum non est natura positiva Deo coaeterna, sed aversio, privatio luminis et inordinatus motus boni creati.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0116","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX6","text":"Spiritum aquis superferri non significat motum localem neque eminentiam soli Spiritui secundum divinitatem propriam.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX7","text":"Nulla copia quae Deus non est creaturae rationali plenitudo est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX8","text":"Esse, nosse et velle in mente humana non sunt ipsa Trinitas, sed exercitatio analogica quae distantiam potius quam comprehensionem ostendit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX9","text":"Lectio allegorica naturas rerum proprie considerandas non abolet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX10","text":"Successio verborum et dierum in Scriptura successionem cognitionis, voluntatis vel actionis in Deo non imponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0113","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0114","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX11","text":"Multiplicitas verarum intelligentiarum non est fallacia errorum neque licentia sensuum indiscriminatorum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0093","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX12","text":"Formula qua spiritualis omnia iudicat non extenditur ad auctoritatem Scripturae, status hominum occultos aut destinum eorum qui foris sunt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX13","text":"Requies Dei neque cessationem operationis neque mutationem temporalem in Deo significat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0138","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D1","text":"Invocatio Dei iam responsio est bonitati quae desiderium inspiravit, vocantem praevenit et aversum convertit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D2","text":"Prioritas informitatis ad formam ontologica vel expositionis est, non necessario intervallum temporale, quia materia et forma sine mora produci possunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0127","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D3","text":"Spiritus creatus aversione non desinit esse vel moveri, sed lumen amittit et motus eius fit mors, obscuritas atque dissimilitudo.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D4","text":"Verbum Fiat lux vitam illuminabilem praesupponit, sed tam vita quam illuminatio eadem gratia gratuita sustentantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5","text":"Amor est pondus creaturae: cupiditas deicit ad inquietudinem, caritas autem per Spiritum elevat ad locum proprium, qui est requies in Deo.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D6","text":"Spiritus singulariter superferri dicitur non quia Pater et Filius eminentia careant, sed quia donum caritatis proprie exprimit requiem et elevationem creaturae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D7","text":"In mente una esse, nosse et velle inseparabiliter distincta sunt; haec unitas distincta ad Trinitatem dirigit, sed immutabilitatem divinam non repraesentat aequaliter.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D8","text":"Conversio fidelium veram lucem iam efficit, sed residua obscuritatis manent donec fides transeat in speciem et corpus redimatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D9","text":"Firmamentum figurat auctoritatem Scripturae, quae per ministros mortales dispensatur sed eorum morte non perit atque inferioribus populis superponitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D10","text":"Mare figurat cupiditates et societatem infidelium divino limite coercitas; arida figurat animas a mari discretas, Deum sitientes et ad opera misericordiae fecundas.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A14","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D11","text":"Sacramenta, miracula et voces corporales necessitati infidelium respondent, dum fideles maturiores per exemplum vitae, continentiam et intelligentiam formantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A14","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D12","text":"Mens renovata transit ab imitatione hominis melioris secundum genus ad probationem voluntatis Dei ad imaginem Dei, manens tamen sub Scriptura.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D13","text":"In beneficio datum est res exterior, fructus autem recta voluntas datoris; minister spiritualis fructu pascitur quia bono operantis gaudet, non quia indigentia sua tantum solvitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D14","text":"Benedictio crescendi piscibus et hominibus attributa figurat multiplicationem signorum corporalium et fecunditatem intellectuum rationalium.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A14","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D15","text":"Creaturam bonam videre nondum idem est ac Deum in ea amare; plenus spiritualis visus fit cum bonitas rei ad auctorem refertur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D16","text":"Opera temporalia bona sunt quia Deus ea in nobis operatur, sed consummatio eorum est requies in qua Deus in nobis quiescit sine propria mutatione.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A10","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD1","text":"Creatio, illuminatio, recta voluntas, cognitio, benefactio et requies constituunt diversos gradus unius gratiae praevenientis, non provincias causalitatis creaturae autonomae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD2","text":"Dualismus ontologicus corruit quia etiam creatura informis bonum essendi a Deo habet, dum malum ex aversione boni creati et non ex substantia aemula oritur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD3","text":"Ecclesiae sanctificatio est recapitulatio temporalis grammaticae creationis: informitas, vocatio, discretio, fecunditas, multiplicatio, regimen et requies fiunt gradus conversionis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A14","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D10","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0130","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD4","text":"Oeconomia ecclesialis distribuit media secundum capacitatem: signa sensibilia initiant, exempla ordinant affectus, dona spiritualia illuminant, mens renovata discernit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A16","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD5","text":"Unitas Scripturae multiplicitatem interpretationum generat sine dissolutione veritatis, quia fecunditas sensuum sub auctoritate textus et cognitione per Spiritum continetur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD6","text":"Divina causalitas humanam operationem non simpliciter substituit, sed eam participative constituit: Deus in homine videt et operatur, homo tamen temporaliter videt, vult et agit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A10","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD7","text":"Finis temporalis ordinis non est perpetuatio operum, sed transitus eorum in requiem; bonitas creationis consummatur non in autosufficientia mundi, sed in fruitione Dei.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A8","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX1","text":"Nulla creatura potest se ipsam efficere, formare, illuminare, satiare aut ad consummationem perducere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX2","text":"Nullus amor est neutralis, quia omnis affectus creaturam aut ad fontem vitae convertit aut ad inferiora conformanda deflectit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX3","text":"Nulla fruitio creaturae ut finis ultimi ordinem bonitatis servat, etiam si res fruenda secundum esse bona est.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX4","text":"Nulla visio humana praesentis status immediata, plena et divinae autocognitioni aequalis est; signa, tempora, fides et aenigma manent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX5","text":"Nulla maturitas spiritualis fit independentia a Verbo vel Scriptura, etiamsi mens ab imitatione magistri humani ad proprium iudicium ascendat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX6","text":"Nulla potestas iudicandi omnia permittit creaturae usurpare occultam divisionem quam Deus solus ante manifesta opera novit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX7","text":"Nulla actio exterior ex sola materia dati fructuosa est, nisi recta voluntas eam in ordinem caritatis inserat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0105","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0106","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX1","text":"Extra causalitatem creatoris nullum residuum ontologicum positivum relinquitur ex quo mundus, malum vel creatura spiritualis independenter proveniat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0116","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0127","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX2","text":"Creaturae mutabili praecluditur prospectus ex quo Deum sicut Deus se ipsum cognoscit cognoscere possit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX3","text":"Consummatio intra ordinem praesentis temporis indisponibilis est; dum fides, signa et opera manent, plena species et quies differuntur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0134","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX4","text":"In Deo impossibilia sunt indigentia, augmentum, successio deliberationis et requies post lassitudinem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5","text":"Sabbato ultimo vespera excluditur, quia requies finalis non est pars alterius cycli mutabilitatis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0134","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:FGS1","text":"Machina ontologica procedit hoc ordine: Deus sibi sufficiens → creatio gratuita ex nihilo → informitas dependens → conversio per Verbum → forma et bonitas ordinata.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:FGS2","text":"Machina affectiva procedit hoc ordine: Spiritus ut donum → infusio caritatis → amor ut pondus → elevatio ad Deum → quies in bono creaturae proprio.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:FGS3","text":"Prima series ecclesialis est: tenebrae ignorantiae → vocatio ad paenitentiam → lux conversionis → firmamentum Scripturae → coercitio maris infidelitatis → apparentia aridae fidelium → fructus misericordiae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A14","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:FGS4","text":"Secunda series ecclesialis est: luminaria donorum et ministrorum → sacramenta, miracula et voces ad initiationem → anima viva per continentiam → mens renovata ad imaginem → iudicium spirituale limitatum → ministerium mutuum per datum et fructum.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A14","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A16","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:FGS5","text":"Machina hermeneutica procedit hoc ordine: enuntiatio corporalis una → intellectus veri multiplices → res intelligibilis una → expressionum corporalium multiplicatio → fecunditas sub auctoritate Scripturae et Spiritu.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:FGS6","text":"Machina consummationis procedit hoc ordine: opera Dei in nobis → bona temporalia et incompleta → perseverantia fidei et spei → transitus ordinis mutabilis → sabbatum sine vespera → Deus quiescens in nobis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A10","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A18","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:AF1","text":"Gratia praeveniens → Deus non indigens → creatura sine merito → informitas → conversio per Verbum → elevatio per Spiritum → requies in Deo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:AF2","text":"Lectio trinitaria Geneseos → translatio creationis in Ecclesiam → distinctio graduum capacitatis → institutio per Scripturam et signa → ordinatio affectuum → renovatio mentis → iudicium spirituale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0130","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:AF3","text":"Multiplicitas signorum et sensuum → visus bonitatis per Spiritum → bonitas singulorum et totius → temporalitas operum → spes consummationis → sabbatum aeternum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0110","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME1","text":"Creatio ex fabricatione indigentiae in donationem plenitudinis reclassificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME2","text":"Lux, tenebrae et informitas ex solis qualitatibus cosmicis in modos conversionis, aversionis et dependentiae ontologicae mutantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME3","text":"Amor ex affectu inter alios in principium gravitatis spiritualis, motus et loci proprii creaturae convertitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME4","text":"Ordo dierum creationis fit tabula formationis Ecclesiae, distinctionis ministeriorum et maturationis fidelium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0130","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME5","text":"Sacramenta, miracula, praedicatio, exemplum et contemplatio non ut media aemula, sed ut operationes diversis capacitatis gradibus congruentes ordinantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME6","text":"Potestas spiritualis ex dominio indefinito in iudicium corrigibile sub auctoritate Scripturae restringitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME7","text":"Multiplicitas interpretationum ex signo ambiguitatis in fecunditatem ordinatam unius veritatis reclassificatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME8","text":"Oppositio boni et mali ab conflictu substantiarum ad oppositionem conversionis et aversionis transfertur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME9","text":"Tempus creationis ex mensura actionis divinae in modum receptionis creaturae et narrationis Scripturae mutatur, cui sabbatum sine vespera terminum imponit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0114","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ALT1","text":"Surface — Littera Geneseos de creatione, Trinitate, bonitate operum et die septimo interpretatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ALT2","text":"Structural — Conversio, Scriptura, sacramenta, dona, opera misericordiae, continentia et iudicium constituunt machinam institutionis Ecclesiae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0130","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Textus dualismum refellit, iudicium spirituale limitat et multiplicem exegesim intra auctoritatem et Spiritum ordinat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Deus immutabilis aeternaliter causat et videt; creatura mutabilis temporaliter recipit, convertitur, operatur et ad requiem sine tempore ordinatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0114","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT1","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad restituendos nexus inter creationem gratuitam, formationem per Verbum, elevationem per Spiritum, Ecclesiam et sabbatum aeternum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT2","text":"Firmissima compages est distinctio inter Deum sibi sufficientem et creaturam cui esse, forma, lumen, bonum opus atque requies donantur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT3","text":"Systema interne cohaeret quatenus conversionem et aversionem ad eandem ontologiam boni creati refert atque principium mali substantiale excludit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0110","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT4","text":"Criterium quo multiplices intelligentiae verae ab interpretationibus falsis discernantur auctoritate, Spiritu et caritate circumscribitur, sed non in regulam plenam formaliter explicatur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT5","text":"Transitus ab aeterno actu Dei ad successionem temporalem creaturae affirmatur per distinctionem Verbi et locutionis temporalis, sed modus relationis causaliter non absolvitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0113","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0114","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT6","text":"Assertio praefatoria universa nullo alio fine condita esse quam formatione Ecclesiae latius patet quam probatio corporis, quae ordinem creationis Ecclesiam figurare demonstrat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0001","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0129","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0130","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT7","text":"Formula spiritualem omnia iudicare per exclusiones restringitur, sed principium generale quo ambitus iudicabilium definitur ex exemplis potius quam ex regula deducitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0081","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0084","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0085","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0088","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT8","text":"Divina operatio in voluntate humana responsabilitatem non tollere praesupponitur, quamvis articulatio inter gratiam causantem et actum proprium incompleta maneat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT9","text":"Aequalitas rationalis feminae et subordinatio corporalis eius per analogiam actionis rationi subiectae componuntur, sed nexus inter aequalitatem naturae et ordinem subiectionis non ulterius solvitur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT10","text":"Restitutio servat verum motum textus ab invocatione et creatione ad allegoriam ecclesialem, hermeneuticam fecunditatis, bonitatem universi et requiem finalem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0110","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T141533745700Z_92d972f1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"BOOK THIRTEEN.","source_sha256":"71aca36a3b4fbe8072a0368646810e7162fe84eff4275bdfa7029cbaf7b84b2b","sha256":"a7d244df7baab06316daa09dc127b6d751134aa6663d65dc7b0205f4f973b22d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:15:33.747891+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS1","text":"The text asks by what connection the goodness of God, who is not in need, the formation of creation, the intimation of the Trinity, the sanctification of the Church, and eternal rest are to be understood from Genesis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS2","text":"Every being, formation, illumination, good living, and resting of creation proceeds from the gratuitous operation of God, who needs no created good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS3","text":"The argument joins the metaphysics of creation, Trinitarian exegesis, ecclesial allegory, and the refutation of dualism into one reconstructive system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS4","text":"The initial movement proceeds from prevenient grace to the distinction between self-sufficient God and dependent creation, then to formation through the Word and elevation through the Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS5","text":"The order of Genesis is converted into ecclesial order: illumination, the authority of Scripture, discernment of the faithful, works of mercy, spiritual ministries, sacraments, continence, and renewal of the mind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0130","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS6","text":"The final movement passes from the goodness of individual things to the goodness of the whole, from temporal works to the sabbath without evening, and from divine operation in us to divine rest in us.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A1","text":"God alone simply and unchangeably is, knows, and wills, and his blessedness and rest do not differ from his essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A2","text":"God needs no created good and is not perfected by the creation or perfection of creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A3","text":"Every created being receives being from the gratuitous goodness of God, with no preceding merit of the creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A4","text":"The creature is produced from nothing, not from the substance of God nor from matter extraneous to God; formless matter itself is also created together with it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0127","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A5","text":"In the creature, being is one thing and being formed another; in created spirit, living is one thing and living wisely and blessedly another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6","text":"Formless creation is recalled to unity through the Word, is formed by conversion, and by illumination becomes conformed to God without equality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7","text":"The Holy Spirit, as gift and charity, infuses the love by which creation is borne either upward toward God or downward toward lower things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A8","text":"The rational creature is not satisfied for blessed rest by any good less than God, not even by itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A9","text":"Whatever in any way is, insofar as it is, is good; individual things are good, and the ordered universe is very good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A10","text":"Things are because God eternally sees them; but the creature sees them temporally because they are.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0140","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A11","text":"Scripture ministers the eternal Word in temporal words and supplies human understanding with a higher authority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A12","text":"Father, Son, and Holy Spirit are read enigmatically in the first words of Genesis, without division of the one Creator.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13","text":"Right knowledge of God's gifts occurs through the Spirit of God, so that God may know, see, and speak in the creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A14","text":"The exposition reads the order of creation and of the narrative of Genesis as a figure of the formation and sanctification of the Church.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0130","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15","text":"Ecclesial sanctification progresses according to capacity from initial conversion through discipline, works, and imitation to the renewed judgment of the mind.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A16","text":"The spiritual person judges corrigible signs, interpretations, and morals under the authority of Scripture, not Scripture itself nor the hidden judgments of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0085","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A17","text":"One intelligible thing can be expressed in many ways, and one expression can be truly understood in many ways.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:A18","text":"Temporal renewal remains under faith and hope until works pass away and creation rests in God on the eternal sabbath.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX1","text":"The worship and ministry of creation neither relieve God's weariness nor supplement his power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX2","text":"The creature is constituted neither from divine substance nor from a hostile, uncreated nature contrary to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0116","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0127","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX3","text":"The creature does not merit being, illumination, or beatification by preceding merit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX4","text":"To be is not the same as to be beautiful, nor is to live the same as to live wisely or blessedly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX5","text":"Evil is not a positive nature coeternal with God, but aversion, privation of light, and the disordered movement of created good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0116","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX6","text":"The Spirit's being borne over the waters does not signify local movement or an eminence belonging to the Spirit alone according to his proper divinity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX7","text":"No abundance that is not God is fullness for the rational creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX8","text":"Being, knowing, and willing in the human mind are not the Trinity itself, but an analogical exercise that shows distance rather than comprehension.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX9","text":"Allegorical reading does not abolish the natures of things that must properly be considered.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0094","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX10","text":"The succession of words and days in Scripture does not impose a succession of knowledge, will, or action upon God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0113","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0114","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX11","text":"The multiplicity of true understandings is not the deception of errors nor a license for indiscriminate meanings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0093","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX12","text":"The formula that the spiritual person judges all things does not extend to the authority of Scripture, the hidden states of human beings, or the destiny of those who are outside.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0086","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX13","text":"God's rest signifies neither cessation of operation nor temporal change in God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0138","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D1","text":"The invocation of God is already a response to the goodness that inspired desire, anticipated the one calling, and converted the one turned away.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D2","text":"The priority of formlessness to form is ontological or expository, not necessarily a temporal interval, because matter and form can be produced without delay.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0127","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D3","text":"By aversion, created spirit does not cease to be or to move, but loses light, and its movement becomes death, darkness, and dissimilarity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D4","text":"The word Fiat lux presupposes illuminable life, but both life and illumination are sustained by the same gratuitous grace.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5","text":"Love is the weight of the creature: cupidity casts it down into restlessness, but charity through the Spirit raises it to its proper place, which is rest in God.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D6","text":"The Spirit alone is said to be borne over, not because Father and Son lack eminence, but because the gift of charity properly expresses the creature's rest and elevation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D7","text":"In one mind, being, knowing, and willing are inseparably distinct; this distinct unity directs toward the Trinity, but does not represent divine immutability equally.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D8","text":"The conversion of the faithful already produces true light, but remnants of darkness remain until faith passes into sight and the body is redeemed.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D9","text":"The firmament figures the authority of Scripture, which is dispensed through mortal ministers but does not perish with their death and is set above inferior peoples.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0044","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D10","text":"The sea figures desires and the society of unbelievers restrained by a divine boundary; dry land figures souls separated from the sea, thirsting for God and fruitful in works of mercy.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A14","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D11","text":"Sacraments, miracles, and bodily voices answer the need of unbelievers, while more mature faithful are formed through the example of life, continence, and understanding.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A14","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0066","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D12","text":"The renewed mind passes from imitation of a better human being according to kind to testing the will of God according to the image of God, while nevertheless remaining under Scripture.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0079","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D13","text":"In a benefit, the external thing is the gift, but the fruit is the right will of the giver; the spiritual minister is nourished by the fruit because he rejoices in the good of the doer, not because only his own need is relieved.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0101","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0105","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0106","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D14","text":"The blessing of increase attributed to fish and human beings figures the multiplication of bodily signs and the fecundity of rational understandings.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A14","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D15","text":"To see a good creature is not yet the same as to love God in it; full spiritual sight occurs when the goodness of the thing is referred to its author.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0120","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:D16","text":"Temporal works are good because God works them in us, but their consummation is the rest in which God rests in us without his own change.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A10","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD1","text":"Creation, illumination, right will, knowledge, beneficence, and rest constitute diverse stages of one prevenient grace, not provinces of autonomous creaturely causality.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD2","text":"Ontological dualism collapses because even formless creation has from God the good of being, while evil arises from the aversion of created good and not from a rival substance.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD3","text":"The sanctification of the Church is a temporal recapitulation of the grammar of creation: formlessness, calling, discernment, fecundity, multiplication, governance, and rest become stages of conversion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A14","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D10","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0130","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD4","text":"Ecclesial economy distributes means according to capacity: sensible signs initiate, examples order affections, spiritual gifts illuminate, and the renewed mind discerns.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A16","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD5","text":"The unity of Scripture generates a multiplicity of interpretations without dissolution of truth, because the fecundity of meanings is contained under the authority of the text and knowledge through the Spirit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD6","text":"Divine causality does not simply replace human operation, but constitutively establishes it by participation: God sees and works in the human being, yet the human being sees, wills, and acts temporally.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A10","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD7","text":"The end of temporal order is not the perpetuation of works, but their passage into rest; the goodness of creation is consummated not in the self-sufficiency of the world, but in the enjoyment of God.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A8","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX1","text":"No creature can make, form, illuminate, satisfy, or bring itself to consummation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX2","text":"No love is neutral, because every affection either converts the creature to the fountain of life or turns it aside to conform to lower things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0021","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX3","text":"No enjoyment of a creature as ultimate end preserves the order of goodness, even if the thing enjoyed is good according to being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0119","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX4","text":"No human vision of the present state is immediate, full, and equal to divine self-knowledge; signs, times, faith, and enigma remain.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX5","text":"No spiritual maturity becomes independence from the Word or Scripture, even if the mind rises from imitation of a human teacher to its own judgment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0080","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX6","text":"No power of judging all things permits the creature to usurp the hidden division which God alone knows before manifest works.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0084","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0085","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX7","text":"No external action is fruitful from the matter of the gift alone, unless right will inserts it into the order of charity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0105","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0106","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX1","text":"Outside the causality of the Creator, no positive ontological residue remains from which the world, evil, or spiritual creature might independently arise.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0116","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0127","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX2","text":"The mutable creature is barred from any perspective by which it could know God as God knows himself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX3","text":"Consummation is unavailable within the order of present time; while faith, signs, and works remain, full sight and rest are deferred.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0134","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX4","text":"In God, need, increase, succession of deliberation, and rest after weariness are impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5","text":"Evening is excluded from the final sabbath, because final rest is not part of another cycle of mutability.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0134","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:FGS1","text":"The ontological machine proceeds in this order: self-sufficient God → gratuitous creation from nothing → dependent formlessness → conversion through the Word → form and ordered goodness.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0127","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:FGS2","text":"The affective machine proceeds in this order: Spirit as gift → infusion of charity → love as weight → elevation to God → rest in the creature's proper good.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:FGS3","text":"The first ecclesial series is: darkness of ignorance → call to repentance → light of conversion → firmament of Scripture → restraint of the sea of unbelief → appearance of the dry land of the faithful → fruit of mercy.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A14","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:FGS4","text":"The second ecclesial series is: luminaries of gifts and ministers → sacraments, miracles, and voices for initiation → living soul through continence → renewed mind according to the image → limited spiritual judgment → mutual ministry through gift and fruit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A14","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A16","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0088","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0105","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:FGS5","text":"The hermeneutical machine proceeds in this order: one bodily utterance → multiple true understandings → one intelligible thing → multiplication of bodily expressions → fecundity under the authority of Scripture and the Spirit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:FGS6","text":"The machine of consummation proceeds in this order: God's works in us → temporal and incomplete goods → perseverance of faith and hope → passage beyond mutable order → sabbath without evening → God resting in us.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A10","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A18","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:AF1","text":"Prevenient grace → God not in need → creature without merit → formlessness → conversion through the Word → elevation through the Spirit → rest in God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:AF2","text":"Trinitarian reading of Genesis → translation of creation into the Church → distinction of degrees of capacity → instruction through Scripture and signs → ordering of affections → renewal of the mind → spiritual judgment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0130","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:AF3","text":"Multiplicity of signs and meanings → sight of goodness through the Spirit → goodness of individual things and of the whole → temporality of works → hope of consummation → eternal sabbath.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0110","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0119","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME1","text":"Creation is reclassified from the fabrication of need into the donation of fullness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME2","text":"Light, darkness, and formlessness are changed from merely cosmic qualities into modes of conversion, aversion, and ontological dependence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME3","text":"Love is converted from one affection among others into the principle of the creature's spiritual gravity, movement, and proper place.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0027","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME4","text":"The order of the days of creation becomes a table of the formation of the Church, the distinction of ministries, and the maturation of the faithful.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0130","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME5","text":"Sacraments, miracles, preaching, example, and contemplation are ordered not as rival means, but as operations suited to different degrees of capacity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0066","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0073","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME6","text":"Spiritual power is restricted from indefinite dominion to corrigible judgment under the authority of Scripture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0084","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0088","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME7","text":"The multiplicity of interpretations is reclassified from a sign of ambiguity into the ordered fecundity of one truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0092","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0093","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0118","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME8","text":"The opposition of good and evil is transferred from a conflict of substances to the opposition of conversion and aversion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0116","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME9","text":"The time of creation is changed from a measure of divine action into a mode of the creature's reception and of Scriptural narration, to which the sabbath without evening sets an end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0114","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0134","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ALT1","text":"Surface — The letter of Genesis is interpreted concerning creation, the Trinity, the goodness of works, and the seventh day.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0110","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0122","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ALT2","text":"Structural — Conversion, Scripture, sacraments, gifts, works of mercy, continence, and judgment constitute the machine of the Church's formation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0130","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The text refutes dualism, limits spiritual judgment, and orders multiple exegesis within authority and the Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0084","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Immutable God eternally causes and sees; mutable creation receives, converts, works temporally, and is ordered toward rest without time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0113","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0114","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0138","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0140","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to restore the connections between gratuitous creation, formation through the Word, elevation through the Spirit, the Church, and the eternal sabbath.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT2","text":"The firmest framework is the distinction between self-sufficient God and the creature to which being, form, light, good work, and rest are given.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT3","text":"The system coheres internally insofar as it refers conversion and aversion to the same ontology of created good and excludes a substantial principle of evil.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0110","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0116","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT4","text":"The criterion by which multiple true understandings are distinguished from false interpretations is circumscribed by authority, Spirit, and charity, but is not formally explained as a complete rule.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0118","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0120","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT5","text":"The passage from the eternal act of God to the temporal succession of creation is affirmed through the distinction between the Word and temporal speech, but the mode of relation is not causally resolved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0113","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0114","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT6","text":"The prefatory assertion that all things were created for no other end than the formation of the Church extends more broadly than the proof of the body, which demonstrates that the order of creation figures the Church.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0001","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0129","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0130","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT7","text":"The formula that the spiritual person judges all things is restricted through exclusions, but the general principle by which the scope of what may be judged is defined is derived from examples rather than from a rule.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0081","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0084","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0085","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0088","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT8","text":"Divine operation in the human will is presumed not to remove responsibility, although the articulation between causing grace and proper act remains incomplete.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0138","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0140","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT9","text":"The rational equality of woman and her bodily subordination are reconciled through the analogy of action subject to reason, but the connection between equality of nature and the order of subjection is not further resolved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0124","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT10","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement of the text from invocation and creation to ecclesial allegory, the hermeneutics of fecundity, the goodness of the universe, and final rest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0127","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0129","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0131","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0093","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0110","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_5P0L_LDT0:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_5P0L_LDT0@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_5P0L_LDT0:v1","source_language_code":"la"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 13","title":"Book XIII.","context":"Chapter 13","original_title":"Liber Decimus Tertius.","original_context":"Chapter 13"},"original_title":"Liber Decimus Tertius.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 01–03","order":1,"parents":["CH_5P0L_LIBP","CH_5P0L_LIBS","CH_5P0L_LIBT"],"revision":"CL_5P0L_01@R001","sha256":"91302909d700bf1beffe94c33c97473e481f4a3029f401b0ff37033cb440efcf","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BAS-01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo homo a principio suo alienatus causam peccati, erroris et inquietudinis agnoscat atque ad Deum, quem imperfecte cognoscit, convertatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BAS-02","text":"Thesis globalis statuit omne bonum a Deo procedere, peccatum autem ex conversione voluntatis ad bonum creatum extra ordinem summi boni oriri.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BAS-03","text":"Argumentatio confessionem autobiographicam, analysim affectuum, criticam institutionum et correctionem ontologicam in unam genealogiam aversionis componit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BAS-04","text":"Motus ab origine memoriae abscondita per infantiam, adolescentiam et errorem doctrinalem progreditur, sed ordinem chronologicum in recursionem eiusdem amoris inordinati transformat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BAS-05","text":"Inordinatio crescit ab appetitu nondum efficaciter moderato ad transgressionem propter ipsam transgressionem, deinde ad captationem intellectus per falsam speciem veritatis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BAS-06","text":"Confessio praeteritum non simpliciter refert, sed memoriam ita reordinat ut culpabilis dispersio intra antecedentem providentiam legatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BAS-07","text":"Misericordia non tantum post lapsum remittit, sed per fidem, correptionem, testimonium, poenam et dilationem ipsam facultatem confessionis praeparat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BAS-08","text":"Clausura est attractiva potius quam consummata: requies in Deo terminum constituit, sed conversio adhuc per dilationem providentialem promittitur, non narratur ut completa.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Deus est principium omnis esse et boni, summum bonum stabile, veritas immutabilis atque rector universi.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-02","text":"[Attractor] Creatura humana ad Deum ordinatur et, sive hoc desiderium agnoscat sive ignoret, extra eum in inquietudine et fame persistit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Bona creata, facultates et signa suam bonitatem retinent, sed neque summum bonum supplere neque rectum usum suum garantire possunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Peccatum est ordinatio amoris qua voluntas a Deo ad bona particularia convertitur, in multa diffluit et partem privatam pro bono universali usurpat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Malum non est substantia positiva, sed deordinatio, defectus et privatio boni quae agentem atque ordinem socialem realiter deformant.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD2","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Vitium operatur parasitice, quia speciem boni divini imitatur et libertatem, potestatem, societatem vel veritatem in formam diminutam convertit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Alienatio a Deo non est distantia localis nec independentia ontologica, sed relatio affectiva deformata intra permanentem dependentiam creaturae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX12","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Species moralis actus ex fine affectus, intentione, usu et tempore iudicatur, dum effectus utiles possunt providentiae tribui sine absolutione agentis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Familia, schola, consortium et communitas doctrinalis appetitus non solum continent, sed etiam praemia, pudorem et criteria veritatis distribuendo amplificant.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Cognitio moraliter ordinatur: eloquentia, rectitudo signorum, sensus et nomina sacra veritatem non praestant, si animus phantasmatibus et superbiae subicitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-11","text":"[Mutating] Memoria confessionalis identitatem ultra recordationem directam restituit et praeteritum ex delectatione vel neutralitate in iudicium atque conversionem transfert.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-12","text":"[Persistent] Misericordia divina confessionem antecedit et errores, correptiones, poenas atque moras ad utilitatem ordinat sine approbatione culpae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-13","text":"[Emergent] Reditus requirit simul conversionem amoris et modi cognoscendi, fide, Christo, humilitate et mediationibus providentiae sustentatam.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-14","text":"[Terminal] Requies, veritas et delectatio secura tantum in Deo stabili inveniuntur; omnis substitutio creata ad egestatem redit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RMD-01","text":"Inquietudo initialiter conditio ontologica est, in adolescentia dispersio affectiva fit, deinde ut fames epistemica veritatem in sensibilibus quaerens redit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RMD-02","text":"Bonum creatum persistit, sed eius functio mutatur ab instrumento male adhibito ad speciem boni vitio imitatam atque tandem ad superficiem per quam error doctrinalis captat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RMD-03","text":"Inordinatio infantilis non identice repetitur: in adolescentia fit voluntaria transgressio, in errore doctrinali autem migrat in intellectum qui falsam veritatem amplectitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RMD-04","text":"Mediatio socialis a disciplina familiae et scholae ad consortium delinquentium, inde ad auctoritatem rhetoricam et sectariam transfertur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RMD-05","text":"Memoria ab instrumento reconstructionis originum in operationem moralem mutatur, qua delectatio criminis vel neutralitas praeteriti excluditur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RMD-06","text":"Libertas, primo sub tensione inter curiositatem et coactionem posita, invertitur in licentiam transgressionis, deinde per humilitatem ut receptivitas veritatis denuo constituitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RMD-07","text":"Dilatio baptismi localiter periculum licentiae auget, sed dilatio correctionis doctrinalis postea in instrumentum providentiae et maturitatis epistemicae mutatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RMD-08","text":"Distinctio inter culpam et effectum utilem amplificatur in duplicem causalitatem historiae, ubi voluntas delinquit et misericordia eandem seriem ad confessionem ordinat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD8","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:CGD-01","text":"Infantia, furtum piri, spectacula et controversiae Manichaeae manent casus locales; hoc gradu valent ut probationes distinctarum formarum unius aversionis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:CGD-02","text":"Negatio innocentiae infantilis sursum amplificatur in thesim continuitatis affectivae, secundum quam instrumenta et ambitus mutantur, non radix appetitus dominandi.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:CGD-03","text":"Inutilitas materialis furti manet probatio singularis, sed efficit transitionem globalem ab explicatione obiecti desiderati ad explicationem status voluntatis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:CGD-04","text":"Correctio Manichaeismi non manet polemica localis, sed explicitat structuram iam implicatam in praesentia Dei non spatiali et in malo non substantiali.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:CGD-05","text":"Dilatio baptismi et dilatio disputationis non aequantur: prior licentiam involuntarie parere potest, altera capacitatem futuram discendi providentialiter tuetur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:CGD-06","text":"Critica scholae, consortii et sectae coniungitur in propositionem praesentis gradus quod formatio socialis ordinem amoris atque criteria veri simul distribuit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GNX-01","text":"Creatura neque sui esse neque suae salutis principium est; omnis autonomia absoluta ontologicam dependentiam negat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX1","CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GNX-02","text":"Deus neque spatium occupat neque corpus aut phantasma est; propinquitas eius mensura locali definiri non potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GNX-03","text":"Malum neque substantia creata neque principium autonomum Deo oppositum est.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GNX-04","text":"Bona creata et instrumenta culturalia neque per se damnantur neque pro fine ultimo haberi possunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GNX-05","text":"Rectitudo grammatica, intensitas affectus, species externa facti et copia nominum sacrorum rectitudinem moralem vel veritatem non probant.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GNX-06","text":"Consuetudo, laus socialis et consortium auctoritatem ultimam non habent, quia finis et lex divina formam moralem societatis iudicant.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SNX4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GNX-07","text":"Transgressio libertatem non constituit, sed dependentiam a bono sub specie autonomiae celat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GNX-08","text":"Providentia effectum utilem ordinare potest, sed utilitas neque intentionem pravum bonam facit neque culpam agentis aufert.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD8","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:DBN-01","text":"Systema corrueret si subiectum sui ipsius auctor, possessor sufficiens aut reparator autonomus esset.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX2","CH_5P0L_LIBS:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:DBN-02","text":"Desiderium, lingua, educatio et societas neutralia esse non possunt, quia unumquodque ordinem amoris vel veritatis efficit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:DBN-03","text":"Peccatum ad necessitatem, ignorantiam vel utilitatem materialem redigi non potest, quia voluntas etiam statum transgressionis quaerit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:DNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:DBN-04","text":"Epistemologia fundata in superficie sensibili, splendore sermonis aut nomine sacro veritatem discernere non potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:DBN-05","text":"Ordo moralis neque conventionalismo locali neque uniformitate materialis praecepti per omnia tempora continetur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:DBN-06","text":"Gratia non potest esse mera responsio posterior subiecto iam ad conversionem sufficienti, quia ipsa excitatio, abstinentia et correctio ei attribuuntur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SNX5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:DBN-07","text":"Praeteritum autobiographicum non est materia moraliter iners, quia recordatio aut veterem delectationem renovat aut causalitatem confessionis constituit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSA-01","text":"Nullum extra Deum spatium ontologicum datur in quo creatura stabilitatem, libertatem aut bonum sibi independenter constituat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSA-02","text":"Principium mali autonomum est ontologice inadmissibile; etiam deformitas indiget bonitate quam imminuit et imitatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSA-03","text":"Reditus sui causa et sermo Deo adaequatus indisponibiles sunt; confessio procedit intra donum fidei et limitationem linguae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBP:SNX5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSA-04","text":"Transparentia totalis originum, intentionum et providentiae homini negatur, unde memoria, testimonium et auctoritas operantur sine comprehensione exhaustiva.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSA-05","text":"Clausura conversionis plena adhuc indisponibilis est: promissio reditus ex somnio, lacrimis et providentia vim accipit, sed legem universalem nondum constituit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:XD-01","text":"Peccatum per aetates eandem structuram aversionis servat, sed ab appetitu elementari ad voluntatem transgressivam et cognitionem captam crescit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-04","CL_5P0L_01:GA-09","CH_5P0L_LIBP:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:XD-02","text":"Schola, sodalitas et secta sunt mutationes unius machinae socialis quae pudorem, gloriam et credibilitatem ita distribuit ut inordinatio se confirmet.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-09","CL_5P0L_01:GA-10","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:XD-03","text":"Bona et signa possunt captationis instrumenta fieri non quia bonitatem amittunt, sed quia eorum similitudo cum bono quaesito substitutionem credibilem efficit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-03","CL_5P0L_01:GA-06","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:XD-04","text":"Furtum et error Manichaeus variantes eiusdem imitationis sunt: alter omnipotentiam per transgressionem, alter veritatem per nomina et phantasmata usurpat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-06","CL_5P0L_01:GA-10","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:XD-05","text":"Cum Deus non spatialiter absit et malum substantia non sit, alienatio necessario fit imminutio relationis, ordinis et participationis potius quam migratio ad alteram realitatem.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-01","CL_5P0L_01:GA-05","CL_5P0L_01:GA-07","CH_5P0L_LIBP:D3","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:XD-06","text":"Confessio causalitatem bifurcat: culpam voluntati restituit, sed facultatem agnoscendi, abstinendi et redeundi misericordiae antecedenti attribuit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-11","CL_5P0L_01:GA-12","CH_5P0L_LIBP:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:XD-07","text":"Dilatio est operator ambivalens: sine recta ordinatione spatium licentiae aperit, sub providentia autem immaturam disputationem suspendit et correctionem praeparat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-08","CL_5P0L_01:GA-12","CH_5P0L_LIBP:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:XD-08","text":"Universalitas iustitiae non ex identitate factorum externorum, sed ex stabilitate ordinis qui intentiones, officia et tempora distinguit, derivatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-08","CL_5P0L_01:GA-13","CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:XD-09","text":"Conversio intellectus pars conversionis affectus est, quia superbia non solum bonum male eligit, sed etiam instrumenta quibus verum agnoscitur deformat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-10","CL_5P0L_01:GA-13","CH_5P0L_LIBP:D10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSD-01","text":"Subiectum autobiographicum non est conscientia sui transparens, sed ens acceptum, socialiter mediatum et confessione retrospectiva recollectum.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSD-02","text":"Tempus humanum est campus mutationis, distributionis moralium officiorum et dilationis providentialis, totum tamen sub immutabili praesentia divina continetur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSD-03","text":"Causalitas moralis asymmetrica est: homo defectum producit per aversionem, Deus autem bona antecedentia et reordinationem consequentium praebet sine auctoritate mali.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD8","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSD-04","text":"Institutio politica et culturalis efficitur regimen affectuum, quia honorem, pudorem, eloquentiam et auctoritatem ita distribuit ut aliqua desideria probabilia atque laudabilia videantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSD-05","text":"Cognitio Dei non acquiritur sola accumulatione propositionum, sed mutatione subiecti cognoscentis ab exterioritate superba ad humilem capacitatem recipiendi.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSD-06","text":"Forma confessionis ipsa doctrinam perficit, quia eadem memoria quae dispersionem refert eam sub attributione culpae et misericordiae reordinat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSD-07","text":"Vera libertas non est sui fundatio, sed capacitas boni summi recipiendi; licentia contra ordinem fit servitus imagini mutilae potentiae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RLE-01","text":"Fames Dei non agnita bonum creatum absolutum eligit; substitutum insufficiens inanitatem auget, quae novam fugam ad exteriora parit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RLE-02","text":"Laus socialis inordinationem remunerat, remuneratio eius publicam imitationem producit, et imitatio novam laudem atque ampliorem normarum inversionem stabilit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RLE-03","text":"Superbia formam humilem respuit, cognitio ad corpora restringitur, phantasma pro veritate accipitur, et falsa doctrina superbiam initialem doctrinaliter confirmat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RLE-04","text":"Correctio sequitur circuitum quo delectatio illicita amaritudinem parit, amaritudo memoriam excitat, memoria confessionem, confessio autem novam ordinationem desiderii.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RLE-05","text":"Memoria est circuitus bifurcus: crimen recollectum vel delectationem repetit vel, sub confessione, culpam retinens eius vim affectivam convertit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RLE-06","text":"Requies in Deo est attractor occultus circa quem inquietudo, dispersio et fames negativam suam formam accipiunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FGS-B01","text":"Donum essendi et bonitatis → dependentia creaturae → appetitus constitutivus summi boni.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FGS-B02","text":"Oblivio principii → desiderium non intellectum → quaestus alimenti in rebus insufficientibus.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FGS-B03","text":"Bonum inferius absolutum → aversio a bono universali → dispersio → poena immanens egestatis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FGS-B04","text":"Institutio vel consortium → distributio laudis et pudoris → confirmatio affectus inordinati → amplificatio socialis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FGS-B05","text":"Appetitus elementaris → transgressio volita → imitatio libertatis → captatio intellectus sub specie veritatis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FGS-B06","text":"Negatio mali substantialis et Dei corporei → reclassificatio alienationis → correctio modi cognoscendi et iudicandi.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FGS-B07","text":"Misericordia antecedens → correptio et dilatio → memoria confessionalis → recollectio bonorum → reditus promissus ad requiem.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:AFM-B01","text":"Dependentia creata → oblivio principii → appetitus infantilis → disciplina socialis → dispersio adolescentiae → transgressio gratuita → fames sapientiae → error doctrinalis → praeparatio reditus.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:AFM-B02","text":"Bonum creatum → usus inordinatus → imitatio perversa boni divini → privatio et egestas → correctio ontologica → reordinatio amoris.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:AFM-B03","text":"Misericordia antecedens → fides et testimonium → correptio → memoria → confessio → dilatio formativa → promissio requiei.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MME-01","text":"Peccatum reclassificatur ex serie actuum separatorum in continuum affectivum quod aetates, institutiones et doctrinas per formas crescentes transit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MME-02","text":"Familia, schola, sodalitas, theatrum et secta fiunt species unius agri mediatorii in quo facultates, honores et verisimilitudines ordinantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:ALT2","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MME-03","text":"Libertas transfertur ab immunitate legis ad participationem recti ordinis, dum transgressio sui fundatrix ut servitus imitationis detegitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX3","CH_5P0L_LIBS:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MME-04","text":"Epistemologia fit pars asceseos moralis, quia modus videndi Deum, malum et Scripturam ab ordine affectus et humilitate cognoscentis pendet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MME-05","text":"Oppositio inter iustitiam universalem et varietatem historicam corruit, quia lex stabilis per officia, personas et tempora distributive operatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MME-06","text":"Malum et providentia non amplius ut causae symmetricae describuntur: privatio ab agente oritur, dum Deus bona servat et consequentia ad correctionem ordinat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B01","text":"Gradus superficiei continet originem, infantiam, scholam, baptismum dilatum, adolescentiam, furtum, spectacula, studia, Manichaeismum et intercessionem Monnicae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:ALT1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:ALT1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B02","text":"Gradus structuralis continet circulationem donorum, appetituum, institutionum, imitationum et correctionum quae sub diversis casibus eandem aversionis machinam efficiunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:ALT2","CH_5P0L_LIBS:ALT2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B03","text":"Gradus metastrategicus iudicium transfert ab honore, utilitate, affectus vehementia et specie externa ad ordinem amoris, intentionem et auctoritatem divinam.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:ALT3","CH_5P0L_LIBS:ALT3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B04","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis realitatem ut dependentiam a Deo incorporeo, malum ut privationem et tempus ut campum providentiae distributivae constituit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:ALT4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:ALT4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B05","text":"Gradus methodologicus et performativus confessionem facit operationem conversionis, quia narratio ipsa culpam, donum et memoriam ad rectas causas refert.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FL-01","text":"Culpabilis voluntas et misericordia decisive antecedens simul servantur, sed modus concursus earum causaliter non explicatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FL-02","text":"Omne vitium speciem boni imitari dicitur, furtum tamen malitiam ipsam appetere videtur; defectus et bonum apparens imperfecte conciliantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FL-03","text":"Providentia ex actibus pravis utilitatem elicit, sed discrimen inter ordinationem effectuum et participationem causalitatis mali formula completa caret.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD8","CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FL-04","text":"Iustitia immutabilis mandata temporaliter diversa sustinet, sed authenticatio mandati divini ab auctoritate pendet cuius criterium intra synthesim incompletum manet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FL-05","text":"Phantasmata corporea ut fontes erroris reiciuntur, somnium tamen vim providentialem accipit; distinctio generali regula epistemica non stabilitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MP-01","text":"Appetitus infantilis in adolescentia mutatur ex impulsu instrumentis infirmo in voluntatem quae ipsam positionem contra legem quaerit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MP-02","text":"Lingua transit ab instrumento socialiter acquisito ad medium gloriae, deinde ad superficiem doctrinalem qua nomina vera errorem tegunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MP-03","text":"Dilatio mutat valorem structuralem: circa baptismum permissionem peccandi minatur, circa disputationem autem correctionem maturam praeparat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MP-04","text":"Eloquentia ab instrumento vanitatis in Hortensio fit excitatio ad sapientiam, sed iterum in splendorem falsae doctrinae labi potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:HSI-01","text":"Realitas implicite est campus participationis non spatialis, in quo omnia a Deo continentur et alienatio intra ipsam dependentiam accidit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBP:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum est appetitus memoriam excedens, per corpora, signa et societates permeabilis, qui se tantum confessione sub gratia recollegit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:HSI-03","text":"Tempus est distributio mutationum sub aeterno Dei hodie, ubi mora potest lapsum amplificare vel facultatem futurae conversionis formare.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:HSI-04","text":"Certamen possibile est navigatio inter bona vera et substitutiones eorum, cuius discrimen requirit ordinationem amoris, humilitatem cognitionis et misericordiam antecedentem.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad restituendum motum ab ontologica dependentia per amplificationes affectivas, sociales et epistemicas ad confessionem reditus dilati.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima est distinctio inter bonum datum et usum inordinatum, una cum malo privativo et veritate quae formam socialem transcendit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT3","CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B03","text":"Cohaerentia praesentis gradus non ordine chronologico solo, sed reditu spirali eiusdem aversionis sub formis affectivis, voluntariis et doctrinalibus sustentatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT9","CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B04","text":"Indeterminata manet relatio exacta inter libertatem culpabilem et misericordiam antecedentem, quam synthesis distinguere potest sed non causaliter absolvere.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B05","text":"Indeterminatum etiam manet criterium generale quo mandatum, somnium vel testimonium providentiale ab imaginatione falsa certo discernatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B06","text":"Reductioni axiomaticae resistit actus confessionis ipse, quia systema non tantum propositiones de conversione enuntiat, sed memoriam narrando causaliter et affective convertit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T142301299276Z_ac8aab7b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 01–03","source_sha256":"91302909d700bf1beffe94c33c97473e481f4a3029f401b0ff37033cb440efcf","sha256":"1d7c16046dbacfb0a7c2f79fcf9dc2f220599edbbd12e044d1bd36878555e4cf","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:23:01.301273+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BAS-01","text":"The system asks how a human being alienated from his origin may recognize the cause of sin, error, and restlessness and turn toward God, whom he knows imperfectly.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BAS-02","text":"The global thesis holds that every good proceeds from God, whereas sin arises from the conversion of the will toward a created good outside the order of the highest good.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BAS-03","text":"The argument combines autobiographical confession, analysis of the affects, critique of institutions, and ontological correction into a single genealogy of aversion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BAS-04","text":"The movement proceeds from the hidden origin of memory through infancy, adolescence, and doctrinal error, but transforms chronological order into a recursion of the same disordered love.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BAS-05","text":"Disorder grows from desire not yet effectively moderated to transgression for the sake of transgression itself, then to the capture of the intellect by a false appearance of truth.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BAS-06","text":"Confession does not simply report the past, but reorders memory so that culpable dispersion is read within antecedent providence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BAS-07","text":"Mercy not only remits after a fall, but through faith, correction, testimony, punishment, and delay prepares the very capacity for confession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BAS-08","text":"The closure is attractive rather than consummated: rest in God establishes the end, but conversion is still promised through providential delay, not narrated as complete.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] God is the principle of all being and good, the stable highest good, immutable truth, and ruler of the universe.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-02","text":"[Attractor] The human creature is ordered toward God and, whether it recognizes or ignores this desire, persists outside him in restlessness and hunger.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Created goods, faculties, and signs retain their goodness, but can neither replace the highest good nor guarantee their own right use.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Sin is an ordering of love by which the will turns from God toward particular goods, flows out into multiplicity, and usurps a private part as a universal good.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Evil is not a positive substance, but disorder, defect, and privation of good that really deform the agent and the social order.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD2","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Vice operates parasitically, because it imitates the appearance of divine good and converts freedom, power, society, or truth into a diminished form.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Alienation from God is neither local distance nor ontological independence, but a deformed affective relation within the creature's enduring dependence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX12","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] The moral species of an act is judged from the end of the affect, intention, use, and time, while useful effects may be attributed to providence without absolving the agent.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Family, school, association, and doctrinal community not only restrain desires, but also amplify them by distributing rewards, shame, and criteria of truth.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Knowledge is morally ordered: eloquence, correctness of signs, meanings, and sacred names do not secure truth if the mind is subject to phantasms and pride.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-11","text":"[Mutating] Confessional memory restores identity beyond direct recollection and transfers the past from delight or neutrality into judgment and conversion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-12","text":"[Persistent] Divine mercy precedes confession and orders errors, corrections, punishments, and delays to benefit without approving guilt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-13","text":"[Emergent] Return requires at once conversion of love and of the mode of knowing, sustained by faith, Christ, humility, and mediations of providence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GA-14","text":"[Terminal] Rest, truth, and secure delight are found only in stable God; every created substitute returns to indigence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RMD-01","text":"Restlessness is initially an ontological condition, becomes affective dispersion in adolescence, then returns as epistemic hunger seeking truth in sensible things.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RMD-02","text":"Created good persists, but its function changes from an instrument badly used to an appearance of good imitated by vice and finally to a surface through which doctrinal error captures.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RMD-03","text":"Infantile disorder is not repeated identically: in adolescence it becomes voluntary transgression, while in doctrinal error it migrates into an intellect that embraces false truth.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RMD-04","text":"Social mediation is transferred from the discipline of family and school to the association of delinquents, thence to rhetorical and sectarian authority.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RMD-05","text":"Memory changes from an instrument of reconstructing origins into a moral operation by which delight in crime or neutrality toward the past is excluded.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RMD-06","text":"Freedom, first placed under tension between curiosity and coercion, is inverted into license for transgression, then reconstituted through humility as receptivity to truth.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RMD-07","text":"Delay of baptism locally increases the danger of license, but delay of doctrinal correction later changes into an instrument of providence and epistemic maturity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RMD-08","text":"The distinction between guilt and useful effect is amplified into a dual causality of history, in which the will sins and mercy orders the same sequence toward confession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD8","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:CGD-01","text":"Infancy, pear theft, spectacles, and Manichaean controversies remain local cases; at this level they function as proofs of distinct forms of one aversion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:CGD-02","text":"The denial of infantile innocence is amplified upward into the thesis of affective continuity, according to which instruments and contexts change, not the root of the desire to dominate.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:CGD-03","text":"The material uselessness of theft remains a particular proof, but effects a global transition from explanation by the desired object to explanation by the state of the will.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:CGD-04","text":"The correction of Manichaeism does not remain a local polemic, but makes explicit the structure already implied in God's non-spatial presence and in non-substantial evil.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:CGD-05","text":"Delay of baptism and delay of disputation are not equivalent: the former can involuntarily engender license, the latter providentially preserves the future capacity to learn.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:CGD-06","text":"Critique of school, association, and sect is joined in the proposition at the present level that social formation distributes together the order of love and criteria of truth.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GNX-01","text":"The creature is the principle neither of its own being nor of its own salvation; every absolute autonomy denies ontological dependence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX1","CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GNX-02","text":"God neither occupies space nor is a body or phantasm; his nearness cannot be defined by local measure.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GNX-03","text":"Evil is neither a created substance nor an autonomous principle opposed to God.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GNX-04","text":"Created goods and cultural instruments are neither condemned in themselves nor can be held as the ultimate end.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GNX-05","text":"Grammatical correctness, intensity of affect, the external appearance of a deed, and an abundance of sacred names do not prove moral rectitude or truth.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:NX11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GNX-06","text":"Custom, social praise, and association possess no ultimate authority, because the end and divine law judge the moral form of society.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SNX4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GNX-07","text":"Transgression does not constitute freedom, but conceals dependence upon good under the appearance of autonomy.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:GNX-08","text":"Providence can order a useful effect, but utility neither makes a depraved intention good nor removes the agent's guilt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD8","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:DBN-01","text":"The system would collapse if the subject were author of itself, a self-sufficient possessor, or an autonomous restorer.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX2","CH_5P0L_LIBS:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:DBN-02","text":"Desire, language, education, and society cannot be neutral, because each effects an order of love or truth.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:DBN-03","text":"Sin cannot be reduced to necessity, ignorance, or material utility, because the will also seeks the state of transgression.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:DNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:DBN-04","text":"An epistemology founded on sensible surface, splendor of speech, or sacred name cannot discern truth.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:DBN-05","text":"Moral order is contained neither by local conventionalism nor by the uniformity of a material precept across all times.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:DBN-06","text":"Grace cannot be a mere subsequent response to a subject already sufficient for conversion, because awakening itself, abstinence, and correction are attributed to it.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SNX5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:DBN-07","text":"The autobiographical past is not morally inert material, because recollection either renews old delight or constitutes the causality of confession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSA-01","text":"No ontological space outside God is given in which the creature might independently establish stability, freedom, or good for itself.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSA-02","text":"An autonomous principle of evil is ontologically inadmissible; even deformity requires the goodness that it diminishes and imitates.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSA-03","text":"Return caused by oneself and speech adequate to God are unavailable; confession proceeds within the gift of faith and the limitation of language.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBP:SNX5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSA-04","text":"Total transparency of origins, intentions, and providence is denied to the human being, whence memory, testimony, and authority operate without exhaustive comprehension.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:DNX6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSA-05","text":"The full closure of conversion is still unavailable: the promise of return receives force from dream, tears, and providence, but does not yet establish a universal law.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:XD-01","text":"Across ages, sin preserves the same structure of aversion, but grows from elementary desire to transgressive will and captured knowledge.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-04","CL_5P0L_01:GA-09","CH_5P0L_LIBP:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:XD-02","text":"School, companionship, and sect are mutations of one social machine that distributes shame, glory, and credibility so that disorder confirms itself.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-09","CL_5P0L_01:GA-10","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:XD-03","text":"Goods and signs can become instruments of capture not because they lose their goodness, but because their likeness to the good sought makes substitution credible.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-03","CL_5P0L_01:GA-06","CH_5P0L_LIBP:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:XD-04","text":"Theft and Manichaean error are variants of the same imitation: the one usurps omnipotence through transgression, the other truth through names and phantasms.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-06","CL_5P0L_01:GA-10","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:XD-05","text":"Since God is not spatially absent and evil is not a substance, alienation necessarily becomes a diminution of relation, order, and participation rather than a migration to another reality.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-01","CL_5P0L_01:GA-05","CL_5P0L_01:GA-07","CH_5P0L_LIBP:D3","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:XD-06","text":"Confession bifurcates causality: it restores guilt to the will, but attributes the capacity to recognize, abstain, and return to antecedent mercy.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-11","CL_5P0L_01:GA-12","CH_5P0L_LIBP:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:XD-07","text":"Delay is an ambivalent operator: without right ordering it opens a space for license, but under providence it suspends immature disputation and prepares correction.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-08","CL_5P0L_01:GA-12","CH_5P0L_LIBP:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:XD-08","text":"The universality of justice is derived not from identity of external deeds, but from the stability of the order that distinguishes intentions, duties, and times.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-08","CL_5P0L_01:GA-13","CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:XD-09","text":"Conversion of the intellect is part of conversion of affect, because pride not only chooses good badly, but also deforms the instruments by which truth is recognized.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-10","CL_5P0L_01:GA-13","CH_5P0L_LIBP:D10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSD-01","text":"The autobiographical subject is not self-transparent consciousness, but a received being, socially mediated and recollected by retrospective confession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSD-02","text":"Human time is a field of change, distribution of moral duties, and providential delay, yet is wholly contained under God's immutable presence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSD-03","text":"Moral causality is asymmetric: the human being produces defect through aversion, while God provides antecedent goods and reordering of consequences without authorship of evil.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD8","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSD-04","text":"Political and cultural institution becomes a governance of the affects, because it distributes honor, shame, eloquence, and authority so that certain desires appear probable and praiseworthy.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSD-05","text":"Knowledge of God is not acquired by accumulation of propositions alone, but by transformation of the knowing subject from proud exteriority to the humble capacity to receive.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSD-06","text":"The form of confession itself performs doctrine, because the same memory that reports dispersion reorders it under the attribution of guilt and mercy.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:BSD-07","text":"True freedom is not self-foundation, but the capacity to receive the highest good; license against order becomes slavery to a mutilated image of power.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RLE-01","text":"Unrecognized hunger for God chooses created good as absolute; the insufficient substitute increases emptiness, which produces a new flight toward external things.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RLE-02","text":"Social praise rewards disorder, its reward produces public imitation, and imitation establishes new praise and a broader inversion of norms.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RLE-03","text":"Pride rejects the humble form, knowledge is restricted to bodies, phantasm is accepted as truth, and false doctrine doctrinally confirms the initial pride.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RLE-04","text":"Correction follows a circuit in which illicit delight produces bitterness, bitterness awakens memory, memory confession, and confession a new ordering of desire.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RLE-05","text":"Memory is a bifurcated circuit: recollected crime either repeats delight or, under confession, retains guilt while transforming its affective force.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:RLE-06","text":"Rest in God is the hidden attractor around which restlessness, dispersion, and hunger assume their negative form.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FGS-B01","text":"Gift of being and goodness → dependence of the creature → constitutive desire for the highest good.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FGS-B02","text":"Forgetting of the principle → desire not understood → pursuit of nourishment in insufficient things.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FGS-B03","text":"Lower good made absolute → aversion from universal good → dispersion → immanent punishment of indigence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FGS-B04","text":"Institution or association → distribution of praise and shame → confirmation of disordered affect → social amplification.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FGS-B05","text":"Elementary desire → willed transgression → imitation of freedom → capture of the intellect under the appearance of truth.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FGS-B06","text":"Denial of substantial evil and corporeal God → reclassification of alienation → correction of the mode of knowing and judging.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FGS-B07","text":"Antecedent mercy → correction and delay → confessional memory → recollection of goods → promised return to rest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:AFM-B01","text":"Created dependence → forgetting of the principle → infantile desire → social discipline → adolescent dispersion → gratuitous transgression → hunger for wisdom → doctrinal error → preparation for return.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:AFM-B02","text":"Created good → disordered use → perverse imitation of divine good → privation and indigence → ontological correction → reordering of love.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:AFM-B03","text":"Antecedent mercy → faith and testimony → correction → memory → confession → formative delay → promise of rest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MME-01","text":"Sin is reclassified from a series of separate acts into an affective continuum that passes through ages, institutions, and doctrines in growing forms.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBS:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MME-02","text":"Family, school, companionship, theater, and sect become forms of one mediating field in which faculties, honors, and verisimilitudes are ordered.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:ALT2","CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MME-03","text":"Freedom is transferred from immunity from law to participation in right order, while self-founding transgression is disclosed as slavery to imitation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:NX3","CH_5P0L_LIBS:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MME-04","text":"Epistemology becomes part of moral ascesis, because the manner of seeing God, evil, and Scripture depends on the order of affect and the humility of the knower.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MME-05","text":"The opposition between universal justice and historical variety collapses, because stable law operates distributively through duties, persons, and times.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MME-06","text":"Evil and providence are no longer described as symmetrical causes: privation arises from the agent, while God preserves goods and orders consequences toward correction.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B01","text":"The surface level contains origin, infancy, school, delayed baptism, adolescence, theft, spectacles, studies, Manichaeism, and Monnica's intercession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:ALT1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:ALT1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B02","text":"The structural level contains the circulation of gifts, desires, institutions, imitations, and corrections that make the same machine of aversion under diverse cases.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:ALT2","CH_5P0L_LIBS:ALT2","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B03","text":"The metastrategic level transfers judgment from honor, utility, intensity of affect, and external appearance to the order of love, intention, and divine authority.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:ALT3","CH_5P0L_LIBS:ALT3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B04","text":"The ontological and temporal level establishes reality as dependence on incorporeal God, evil as privation, and time as a field of distributive providence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:ALT4","CH_5P0L_LIBS:ALT4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B05","text":"The methodological and performative level makes confession an operation of conversion, because narrative itself refers guilt, gift, and memory to their right causes.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FL-01","text":"Culpable will and decisively antecedent mercy are preserved together, but the mode of their concurrence is not causally explained.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FL-02","text":"Every vice is said to imitate an appearance of good, yet theft seems to desire malice itself; defect and apparent good are imperfectly reconciled.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FL-03","text":"Providence draws utility from depraved acts, but the distinction between ordering effects and participation in the causality of evil lacks a complete formula.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD8","CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FL-04","text":"Immutable justice sustains temporally diverse commands, but authentication of the divine command depends on an authority whose criterion remains incomplete within the synthesis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:FL-05","text":"Corporeal phantasms are rejected as sources of error, yet dream receives providential force; the distinction is not established by a general epistemic rule.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:NX6","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MP-01","text":"Infantile desire changes in adolescence from an impulse weak in means into a will that seeks the very position against the law.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MP-02","text":"Language passes from a socially acquired instrument to a medium of glory, then to a doctrinal surface by which true names conceal error.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MP-03","text":"Delay changes structural value: concerning baptism it threatens permission to sin, but concerning disputation it prepares mature correction.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MP-04","text":"Eloquence changes from an instrument of vanity in Hortensius into an awakening to wisdom, but can again slip into the splendor of false doctrine.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:AS4","CH_5P0L_LIBT:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly a field of non-spatial participation, in which all things are contained by God and alienation occurs within dependence itself.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBP:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:HSI-02","text":"The subject is a desire exceeding memory, permeable through bodies, signs, and societies, which recollects itself only by confession under grace.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBS:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:HSI-03","text":"Time is a distribution of changes under God's eternal today, where delay can amplify a fall or form the capacity for future conversion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:HSI-04","text":"Possible struggle is navigation between true goods and their substitutions, the discernment of which requires ordering of love, humility of knowledge, and antecedent mercy.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBS:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B01","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to restore the movement from ontological dependence through affective, social, and epistemic amplifications to confession of delayed return.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT1","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B02","text":"The firmest structure is the distinction between given good and disordered use, together with privative evil and truth that transcends social form.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT3","CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT3","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B03","text":"The coherence of the present level is sustained not by chronological order alone, but by the spiral return of the same aversion under affective, voluntary, and doctrinal forms.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT9","CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B04","text":"The exact relation between culpable freedom and antecedent mercy remains indeterminate, which the synthesis can distinguish but cannot causally resolve.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:MRT6","CH_5P0L_LIBS:MRT5","CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B05","text":"Also indeterminate remains the general criterion by which a command, dream, or providential testimony is certainly distinguished from false imagination.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBT:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B06","text":"The act of confession itself resists axiomatic reduction, because the system not only enunciates propositions about conversion, but by narrating memory transforms it causally and affectively.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBP:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBS:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_5P0L_01@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_5P0L_01:v1","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"Chapters 01–03"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Confessiones","title":"Chapters 01–03","context":"Book I. · Book II. · Book III.","original_title":"Chapters 01–03","original_context":"Liber Primus. · Liber Secundus. · Liber Tertius."},"original_title":"Chapters 01–03","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 04–06","order":2,"parents":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ","CH_5P0L_LI_2","CH_5P0L_LI_3"],"revision":"CL_5P0L_02@R001","sha256":"98b14c644a20b8ab591ff2f5c6220c78a8bc6e24ddcc6e6a808d46b138e18a60","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AS-01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo anima ingenio, veritatibus localibus et bonis creatis praedita simul errore doctrinali, amore inordinato et voluntate servili teneatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AS-02","text":"Quaestio ita restituitur ut error non ex defectu bonorum creatorum, sed ex aversione finis, falsa interpretatione et consuetudine affectiva oriatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AS-03","text":"Argumentatio ab experientia luctus et erroris ad examen auctoritatis, inde ad rehabilitationem fidei atque postremo ad diagnosin voluntatis progreditur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AS-04","text":"Probatio conversionis primum negativa est: certitudo falsa degradatur, obiectio contra fidem dissolvitur, et tantum post hanc purgationem impedimentum morale manifestatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AS-05","text":"Fundamentum totius motus est distinctio inter Creatorem incommutabilem et creaturam mutabilem, cuius mens veritatem non possidet autonome sed participatione et mediatione recipit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AS-06","text":"Motus est recursivus et spiralis: aversio errores novos generat, sed eadem experientia erroris confessione retractata fit materia curationis et novi iudicii.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AS-07","text":"Mutationes loci, magistri et doctrinae non efficiunt conversionem linearem, sed seriem rupturarum quae subiectum a falsa firmitate ad agnitionem propriae infirmitatis cogunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS6","CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AS-08","text":"Clausura huius gregis est limen: falsa auctoritas relicta est, fides rationabiliter necessaria apparet, voluntas autem nondum liberata necessitatem gratiae producit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Ordo Creatoris incommutabilis et creaturae mutabilis simul limites amoris, cognitionis, temporis et quietis constituit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Aversio a Deo non absentiam Dei, sed alienationem animae a se atque corruptionem finis affectivi et intellectualis generat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Unus ordo aversionis mutatur ex fixatione amoris et phantasmate metaphysico in dependentiam ab auctoritate falsa, deinde in consuetudinem voluntatis resistente.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD1","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Veritas localis, facultas intellectualis vel bonum creatum salutare non fit nisi usus eius ad fontem veritatis et finem beatitudinis ordinetur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD4","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Mediatio socialis, rhetorica, sacramentalis, scripturalis et eventuum neque intrinsece corruptiva neque autonome salvifica est, sed secundum ordinem recipientis et providentiae functionem mutat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Conversio incipit per dissolutionem asymmetricam falsi, transit per habitationem provisionalem sub auctoritate, et demum voluntatem sanandam exhibet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Malum neque substantia externa neque necessitas caelestis est, sed vitium agentis mutabilis cui culpa propria restitui debet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] Omnis inquisitio ad quietem in bono incommutabili attrahitur, quia nulla summa bonorum finitorum stabilitatem vel beatitudinem praestat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Auctoritas ex potentia sociali errorem propagante in obiectum examinis mutatur, deinde ut mediatio medicinalis fidei restituitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD8","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Fides et ratio circuitum medicinalem constituunt: aliqua fiducia mentem purgat, mens purgata id quod credit intelligere et iudicare incipit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-11","text":"[Persistent] Reditus non est ascensus autonomus, sed participatio mediationis Christi, cuius incarnatio vera, humilitas et victoria mortis exteriora ad interiora referunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A18","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Correctio doctrinalis, ruptura sectaria et cognitio miseriae conversionem nondum perficiunt, sed insufficientiam virium propriarum et necessitatem gratiae terminative constituunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RMD-01","text":"Praesentia Dei identitatem stabilem retinet, sed eius functio ab fundamento ontologico ad negationem fugae et postremo ad interpretationem absentiae expertae ut caecitatis mutatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RMD-02","text":"Imaginatio corporea redit functione amplificata: primum spiritualia falsificat, deinde dualismum sectarium et caricaturam Catholicismi sustinet, tandem remota impedimentum doctrinale cessat esse principale.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RMD-03","text":"Mediatio socialis mutatur ex circuito laudis et erroris in rhetoricam causaliter ambiguam, deinde in campum ubi idem subiectum corrigi vel captivari potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD8","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RMD-04","text":"Temporalitas ex causa amissionis affectivae in medium inquisitionis dilatae transit atque postremo vim inversionis accipit, quia mora ipsa servitutem auget.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RMD-05","text":"Confessio ab ordinatione retrospectiva donorum et errorum amplificatur in formam quae casum, impedimentum et intentionem perversam sub providentia reclassificat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RMD-06","text":"Dubitatio, initio intervallum productivum post ruinam sectae, functionem terminalem amittit et sub necessitate fidei ac decisionis fit positio non stabilis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RMD-07","text":"Amicitia desinit esse sola relatio dyadica et in structuram latiorem mediationis absorbetur, ubi amor gratuitus ordinem bonorum indicat sed etiam habitum socialem format.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RMD-08","text":"Astrologia post munus locale evanescit, sed eius structura persistit ut exemplar cuiuslibet doctrinae quae causalitatem confundit, culpam externalizat et auctoritatem examinabilem immunem facere conatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:CGD-01","text":"Luctus, astrologia, Faustus, migrationes et casus Alypii manent eventus locales; hoc gradu valent tantum quatenus diversos modos aversionis, mediationis et correctionis efficiunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ALT1","CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:CGD-02","text":"Mors amici ex casu biographico amplificatur in probationem quod permanentia a re temporali exacta miseriam ante ipsam iacturam instituit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME2","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:CGD-03","text":"Imperitia Fausti non sola falsitatem totius sectae probat, sed cum praetensione divina et discrepantia examinabili coniuncta transitum globalem ad discrimen auctoritatis efficit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:CGD-04","text":"Casus Alypii inferiores manent quantum ad personas et eventus, sed sursum amplificantur in legem receptionis non linearis sub habitu, multitudine et providentia.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS6","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:CGD-05","text":"Exegesis spiritalis non constituit hoc gradu probationem positivam plenam, sed commissuram necessariam qua obiectio litteralis solvitur et fides rursus possibilis fit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A12","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:CGD-06","text":"Defensibilitas Catholica localiter nondum est veritas demonstrata; currenti gradu tamen cum necessitate cotidiana credendi coniuncta transit in quaestionem de auctoritate medicinali.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:CGD-07","text":"Artes, scientia et eloquentia autonomiam structuralem amittunt atque sub distinctione inter veritatem, efficaciam causalitatemque, usum et finem denuo codificantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX12","CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME2","CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GNX-01","text":"Nulla creatura mutabilis, relatio temporalis aut compositio bonorum saecularium finem stabilem animae constituere potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GNX-02","text":"Nulla imago corporea, pars sensibilis vel categoria creata ambitum Dei aut substantiae spiritalis exhaurit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX4","CH_5P0L_LI_2:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GNX-03","text":"Malum in substantiam adversam, naturam alienam, sidera aut necessitatem transferri non potest sine dissolutione responsabilitatis et confessionis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GNX-04","text":"Scientia creaturarum, eloquentia, ingenium et veritates locales neque auctoritatem divinam neque beatitudinem per se efficiunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D13","CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX3","CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GNX-05","text":"Credere universaliter repudiari nequit, sed neque certitudo demonstrativa ante omnem transformationem tamquam condicio medicinae postulanda est.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GNX-06","text":"Recta doctrina sola habitum cupiditatis, divisionem voluntatis aut impotentiam continentiae abolere non potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GNX-07","text":"Nulla mutatio loci vel fuga exterior animam a corde suo, praesentia Dei aut ordine amoris quem secum fert separare potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX1","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse oportet subiectum sibi principium veritatis, firmitatis et redemptionis esse posse.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse oportet tempus dilationis medium vacuum esse: idem tempus res dissolvit, memoriam reformat et consuetudinem non interruptam corroborat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse oportet cognitionem veritatis nullo testimonio, magistro, Scriptura, Ecclesia aut fide antecedenti indigere.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse oportet providentiam tantum per intentiones rectas, petitiones statim impletas et causas agentibus perspicuas operari.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:DNX7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse oportet ambitum socialem neutralem esse, cum laus, eloquentia, multitudo et amicitia cognitionem atque appetitum recursive forment.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:DBN-06","text":"Falsum esse oportet novam dispositionem externam eadem cupiditate intacta conversionem efficere posse, quia desiderium perversum se honestis nominibus tegit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:D10","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSA-01","text":"Impossibilis est absentia Dei proprie localis vel ontologica; absentia experta tantum caecitas et aversio animae coram praesentia permanente est.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSA-02","text":"Indisponibilis est positio stabilis inter falsitatem iam relictam et conversionem indefinite recusatam.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSA-03","text":"Indisponibilis est certitudo totalis quae transformationem antecedat, quia ipsa facultas iudicandi indiget medicina quam postulatio certitudinis prohibet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSA-04","text":"Impossibilis est beatitudo intra totalitatem finitorum, etiam si amissio eorum cogitatione removeatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSA-05","text":"Vetitus est reditus per assimilationem superbam, scientiam autonomam aut voluntatem sui iuris; conversio tantum ut participatio medicinae et gratiae cogitatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX7","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:XD-01","text":"Tempus duplicem vim acquirit: obiectum dilectum dissolvit et, ubi conversio differtur, ipsum habitum qui obiecto inhaeret confirmat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GA-01","CL_5P0L_02:GA-08","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:XD-02","text":"Error non residet in propositione singulari, sed distribuitur per imaginationem, auctoritatem, caricaturam doctrinalem et appetitum qui falsas imagines retinere cupit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GA-02","CL_5P0L_02:GA-03","CL_5P0L_02:GA-09","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D11","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:XD-03","text":"Adequatio epistemica non mensuratur copia veritatum localium, sed orientatione cognoscentis et sanatione facultatis qua verum in sapientiam ordinatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GA-04","CL_5P0L_02:GA-10","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD4","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:XD-04","text":"Restitutio culpae toti agenti excusationes externas tollit, sed simul ostendit confessionem responsabilitatis non sufficere sine dono quo voluntas continens fiat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GA-07","CL_5P0L_02:GA-12","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D6","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:XD-05","text":"Nullum medium sociale vim univocam habet: auctoritas et rhetorica secundum habitum recipientis et ordinem superiorem errorem propagare, veritatem inferre aut correctionem producere possunt.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GA-05","CL_5P0L_02:GA-09","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD8","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:XD-06","text":"Providentia causas moraliter mixtas ordinare dicitur sine culpae humanae abolitione, sed nexus inter causalitatem superiorem et responsabilitatem agentis insolutus manet.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GA-05","CL_5P0L_02:GA-07","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD7","CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:XD-07","text":"Auctoritas non simpliciter destruitur neque simpliciter restituitur: examen falsas praetensiones dissolvit, dum necessitas fidei auctoritatem medicinalem sub novo criterio requirit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GA-09","CL_5P0L_02:GA-10","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:XD-08","text":"Dissolutio falsi conversionem tantum negative praeparat; cum obiectio doctrinalis removetur, residuum impeditivum in habitu voluntatis apparet et limen gratiae constituit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GA-06","CL_5P0L_02:GA-12","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D6","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSD-01","text":"Subiectum reclassificatur ex possessore autonomo veritatis in agentem culpabilem, patientem medicinae et participem luminis cuius fontem non constituit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSD-02","text":"Tempus fit simul forma creaturae, medium curationis et periculum strategicum: successione solatur, sed dilatione voluntatem alligat et morti exponit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A18","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSD-03","text":"Causalitas hierarchice ordinatur: intentiones particulares effectus locales producunt, dum providentia earum concursum ad finem agentibus ignotum reponit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSD-04","text":"Cognitio transformativa procedit per refutationem, fiduciam provisionalem, purgationem facultatis et iudicium renovatum, non per demonstrationem totalem uno actu possessam.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD1","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSD-05","text":"Auctoritas et libertas non sunt opposita simpliciter, quia libertas ab errore ipsa mediatione formatur, quam tamen discrepantia, fructus et praetensio veritatis examinabilem faciunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSD-06","text":"Malum ontologice de-substantializatur et strategicam formam accipit: est perversio motus, finis, iudicii et habitus quae bona ipsa contra ordinem eorum convertit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME6","CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME4","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSD-07","text":"Conversio fit mutatio status totius systematis, quae ontologiam, auctoritatem, interpretationem, affectum et voluntatem simul reordinare debet, non mera substitutio opinionis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD4","CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RLE-01","text":"Aversio → inquisitio exterior → phantasma → doctrina falsa → confirmatio aversionis constituit circuitum principalem erroris.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RLE-02","text":"Amor finis temporalis → postulatio firmitatis → iactura vel anxietas → fuga exterior → reditus ad animam vulneratam constituit circuitum miseriae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS2","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RLE-03","text":"Laus vel eloquentia → affectus → auctoritas → transmissio doctrinae → nova laus constituit viam amplificationis socialis, cuius valor epistemicus semper indeterminatus manet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS4","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RLE-04","text":"Fides initialis → purgatio mentis → intellectus auctus → iudicium auctoritatis → fides distinctior constituit circuitum medicinalem cognitionis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RLE-05","text":"Consuetudo → consilium compromissorium → dilatio → consuetudo corroborata → libertas imminuta constituit escalationem voluntatis servilis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RLE-06","text":"Eventus ambiguus → interpretatio confessionalis → recognitio providentiae → humilitas → nova capacitas eventus legendi constituit circuitum curationis retrospectivae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RLE-07","text":"Quietis in Deo attractor lineas amoris, cognitionis, auctoritatis et voluntatis congregat, quia unaquaeque ad defectum firmitatis autonomae reducitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX6","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FGS-B01","text":"Aversio finis → dispersio amoris et cognitionis → bona creata tamquam fines aut principia autonoma usurpata.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FGS-B02","text":"Usurpatio boni creati → phantasma metaphysicum, auctoritas falsa vel appetitus stabilitatis → miseria et error recursive producti.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D11","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FGS-B03","text":"Contradictio experientiae, rationis aut exegesis → degradatio certitudinis → ruptura cum systemate priore sine possessione statim positiva novi.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS2","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FGS-B04","text":"Ruptura certitudinis → habitatio provisionalis → auctoritas medicinalis → fides quae facultatem ulterioris cognitionis purgat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FGS-B05","text":"Correctio intellectus → detectio consuetudinis intactae → translatio impedimenti ad voluntatem → clausura consiliorum compromissoriorum.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FGS-B06","text":"Impotentia voluntatis + mors incerta + mediatio Christi → necessitas gratiae → conversio nondum effecta sed structuraliter inevitabilis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A18","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A18","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AFM-B01","text":"Amor et ingenium aversa → luctus atque falsa metaphysica → examen doctrinae et magistri → ruina auctoritatis sectariae → defensibilitas Catholica → fides rehabilitata → servitus voluntatis → necessitas gratiae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AFM-B02","text":"Phantasma corporeum → dualismus et caricatura fidei → exegesis spiritalis → remotio objectionis → auctoritas medicinalis → cognitio recursiva.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AFM-B03","text":"Appetitus quietis → bona temporalia → anxietas et iactura → consilia media → dilatio → mors ut terminus incertus → gratia ut sola clausura conversionis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MME-01","text":"Veritas propositionis, forma sermonis, rectitudo finis et beatitudo cognoscentis in axes distinctos distribuuntur, quorum confusio errores inferiores generaverat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MME-02","text":"Auctoritas reclassificatur ex dominio vel splendore rhetorico in mediationem examinabilem cuius munus est mentem ad iudicium maturius ducere.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MME-03","text":"Tempus desinit esse scaena neutra eventuum et fit operator qui res temporales dissolvit, curationem differt vel promovet atque consuetudinem auget.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MME-04","text":"Malum ex obiecto substantiali in relationem perversam inter facultatem, obiectum, finem et motum agentis transfertur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MME-05","text":"Conversio ex mutatione doctrinae in reordinationem plurium graduum redescribitur, quia error ontologicus dissolvi potest dum affectus et voluntas manent captivi.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MME-06","text":"Mediatio ex impedimento libertatis in condicionem ambivalentem formationis mutatur, unde lectio semper intentionem agentis, dispositionem recipientis et ordinem providentialem distinguere debet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B01","text":"In gradu superficiei agunt mors amici, astrologia, Faustus, migrationes, Ambrosius, consilia matrimonii et casus Alypii.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ALT1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B02","text":"In gradu structurali aversio, imaginatio, auctoritas, habitus socialis, consuetudo et temporalitas distribuunt errores atque condiciones correctionis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ALT2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B03","text":"In gradu metastrategico quaestio ab electione inter doctrinas ad inventionem criterii, mediationis medicinalis et ordinis quo intellectus atque voluntas curentur transfertur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ALT3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B04","text":"In gradu ontologico et temporali realitas distinguitur inter praesentiam incommutabilem Dei et creaturam successive existentem, mortalem atque incapacem sibi firmitatem tribuendi.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ALT4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B05","text":"In gradu methodologico et performativo confessio ipsa quod asserit efficit, quia fragmenta biographica retractando casum in providentiam, culpam in agnitionem et memoriam in medicinam convertit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FL-01","text":"Providentia causas perversas ordinat et tamen culpam agentibus relinquit, sed modus concursus divini et voluntarii affirmatur potius quam formaliter explicatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT6","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FL-02","text":"Fides rationem sanare debet ad auctoritatem iudicandam, sed auctoritas medicinae partim ipsa fide in institutionem divinam agnoscitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FL-03","text":"Refutatio caricaturae Catholicae et defensibilitas Scripturae probationem veritatis positivae non perficiunt, quamquam motus ad auctoritatem Scripturae vi confessionali acceleratur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX10","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FL-04","text":"Amicitia, matrimonium et bona saecularia legitima manent, sed eadem bona sub cupiditate fiunt vincula; criterium inter usum ordinatum et tegumentum appetitus non semper explicatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX13","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MP-01","text":"Imaginatio corporea mutatur ex causa positiva dualismi in obiectum purgationis exegeticae; post eius dissolutionem locus conflictus ad voluntatem transfertur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MP-02","text":"Rhetorica vim epistemicam amittit sed efficaciam causalem retinet, unde medium repudiatum tamquam criterium redit tamquam via ingressus veritatis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD2","CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MP-03","text":"Scepticismus mutatur ex tutela contra doctrinam falsam in impedimentum, ubi suspensio assensus medicinam fidei indefinite differt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MP-04","text":"Punctum mutationis principale occurrit cum correctione intellectus perfecta relative, impedimentum conversionis non iam in obiecto credendo sed in habitu volendi reperitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:HSI-01","text":"Realitas implicite apparet ut ordo hierarchicus bonorum mutabilium circum praesentiam incommutabilem, in quo nulla creatura sibi principium aut terminum est.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS3","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum est nodus amoris, memoriae, habitus, testimonii et voluntatis, qui secundum id cui adhaeret aut dispergitur aut integratur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:HSI-03","text":"Tempus est fluvius qui obiecta aufert, memoriam format, causas ad fines ignotos vehit et dilationem in servitutem convertit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A16","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:HSI-04","text":"Navigatio possibilis non est fuga ad exteriora, sed reditus interior per mediationes quarum finis est firmare animam in eo quod non transit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad restituendum motum ab aversione affectiva et falsa ontologia per ruinam auctoritatis ad fidem medicinalem atque necessitatem gratiae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT1","CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima est ubi phantasma corporeum doctrinam falsificat, discrepantia examinabilis auctoritatem destruit et correctione doctrinali peracta servitus voluntatis manifestatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT2","CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MRT-B03","text":"Nondum satis determinantur criterium independens verae auctoritatis, concursus providentiae cum culpa et modus quo gratia voluntatem actu liberatura sit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT3","CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MRT-B04","text":"Cohaerentia huius gregis non ordine mere lineari, sed reditu variato aversionis, mediationis et firmitatis impossibilis constat; fragmenta biographica circa conversionem nondum effectam convergunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT9","CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT9","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MRT-B05","text":"Reductioni resistunt singulares ambiguitates luctus, eloquentiae, bonorum coniugalium et providentiae; hae tamen machinam non dissolvunt, sed commissuras ubi transitus a signo ad ontologiam comprimitur indicant.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT3","CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T142344343328Z_b62588d4","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 04–06","source_sha256":"98b14c644a20b8ab591ff2f5c6220c78a8bc6e24ddcc6e6a808d46b138e18a60","sha256":"accbbceda0aa51ce6fa0e08118088c84984e5e4d247aab61548806f7fc341cef","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:23:44.344389+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AS-01","text":"The system asks how the soul, endowed with intellect, local truths, and created goods, is at once held by doctrinal error, disordered love, and servile will.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AS-02","text":"The question is thus restored: error arises not from a defect in created goods, but from a turning away from the end, false interpretation, and affective habit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AS-03","text":"The argument proceeds from the experience of grief and error to an examination of authority, thence to the rehabilitation of faith, and finally to a diagnosis of the will.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AS-04","text":"The proof of conversion is first negative: false certainty is degraded, the objection against faith is dissolved, and only after this purgation does the moral impediment become manifest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AS-05","text":"The foundation of the whole movement is the distinction between the immutable Creator and mutable creature, whose mind does not possess truth autonomously but receives it through participation and mediation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AS-06","text":"The movement is recursive and spiral: turning away generates new errors, yet the same experience of error, reconsidered through confession, becomes material for healing and new judgment.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AS-07","text":"Changes of place, teacher, and doctrine do not produce linear conversion, but a series of ruptures that compel the subject from false firmness to recognition of its own weakness.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS6","CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AS-08","text":"The closure of this cluster is a threshold: false authority has been abandoned, faith appears rationally necessary, but the will, not yet liberated, yields the necessity of grace.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] The order of the immutable Creator and mutable creature simultaneously establishes the limits of love, knowledge, time, and rest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Turning away from God generates not God's absence, but the soul's alienation from itself and the corruption of the affective and intellectual end.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] A single order of turning away changes from fixation of love and metaphysical phantasm into dependence on false authority, then into a habit of resistant will.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD1","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] A local truth, intellectual faculty, or created good becomes salutary only if its use is ordered toward the source of truth and the end of blessedness.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD4","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Social, rhetorical, sacramental, scriptural, and evental mediation is neither intrinsically corrupting nor autonomously salvific, but changes function according to the order of the recipient and of providence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Conversion begins through the asymmetric dissolution of falsity, passes through provisional dwelling under authority, and finally presents the will as requiring healing.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Evil is neither an external substance nor a celestial necessity, but a vice of the mutable agent to which its own guilt must be restored.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] Every inquiry is drawn toward rest in the immutable good, because no sum of finite goods furnishes stability or blessedness.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A10","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Authority changes from a social power propagating error into an object of examination, then is restored as the medicinal mediation of faith.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD8","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Faith and reason constitute a medicinal circuit: some trust purges the mind; the purged mind begins to understand and judge what it believes.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-11","text":"[Persistent] Return is not autonomous ascent, but participation in Christ's mediation, whose true incarnation, humility, and victory over death refer exterior things to interior ones.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A18","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Doctrinal correction, sectarian rupture, and knowledge of misery do not yet complete conversion, but terminally establish the insufficiency of one's own powers and the necessity of grace.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RMD-01","text":"God's presence retains stable identity, but its function changes from ontological foundation to negation of flight and finally to an interpretation of experienced absence as blindness.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RMD-02","text":"Corporeal imagination returns with an amplified function: first it falsifies spiritual things, then sustains sectarian dualism and a caricature of Catholicism, and finally, once removed, ceases to be the principal doctrinal impediment.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RMD-03","text":"Social mediation changes from a circuit of praise and error into causally ambiguous rhetoric, then into a field where the same subject can be corrected or captured.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD8","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RMD-04","text":"Temporality passes from a cause of affective loss into a medium of delayed inquiry and finally acquires the force of inversion, because delay itself increases servitude.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RMD-05","text":"Confession is amplified from retrospective ordering of gifts and errors into a form that reclassifies accident, impediment, and perverse intention under providence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RMD-06","text":"Doubt, initially a productive interval after the collapse of the sect, loses its terminal function and, under the necessity of faith and decision, becomes an unstable position.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RMD-07","text":"Friendship ceases to be a merely dyadic relation and is absorbed into a broader structure of mediation, where gratuitous love indicates the order of goods but also forms social habit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RMD-08","text":"Astrology disappears after a local role, but its structure persists as a model for any doctrine that confuses causality, externalizes guilt, and seeks to render examinable authority immune.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:CGD-01","text":"Grief, astrology, Faustus, migrations, and Alypius's cases remain local events; at this level they matter only insofar as they produce diverse modes of turning away, mediation, and correction.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ALT1","CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:CGD-02","text":"The death of a friend is amplified from a biographical event into proof that permanence demanded from a temporal thing establishes misery before the loss itself.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME2","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:CGD-03","text":"Faustus's incompetence does not alone prove the falsity of the entire sect, but, joined with divine pretension and examinable discrepancy, effects a global transition to a crisis of authority.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:CGD-04","text":"Alypius's cases remain lower with respect to persons and events, but are amplified upward into a law of nonlinear reception under habit, crowd, and providence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS6","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:CGD-05","text":"Spiritual exegesis does not at this level constitute a full positive proof, but a necessary joint by which the literal objection is dissolved and faith again becomes possible.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A12","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:CGD-06","text":"The defensibility of Catholicism is not yet locally demonstrated truth; at the current level, however, joined with the everyday necessity of believing, it becomes a question of medicinal authority.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:CGD-07","text":"Arts, science, and eloquence lose structural autonomy and are recoded under the distinction between truth, efficacy, and causality, use and end.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX12","CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME2","CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GNX-01","text":"No mutable creature, temporal relation, or composition of secular goods can constitute the stable end of the soul.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GNX-02","text":"No corporeal image, sensible part, or created category exhausts the scope of God or of spiritual substance.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX4","CH_5P0L_LI_2:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GNX-03","text":"Evil cannot be transferred to an opposing substance, alien nature, stars, or necessity without dissolving responsibility and confession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GNX-04","text":"Knowledge of creatures, eloquence, intellect, and local truths produce neither divine authority nor blessedness through themselves.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D13","CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX3","CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GNX-05","text":"Believing cannot be universally repudiated, but neither is demonstrative certainty before every transformation to be demanded as a condition of healing.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:D3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GNX-06","text":"Right doctrine alone cannot abolish the habit of desire, division of the will, or impotence of continence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:GNX-07","text":"No change of place or external flight can separate the soul from its own heart, God's presence, or the order of love that it bears with itself.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX1","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that the subject can be for itself the principle of truth, firmness, and redemption.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that the time of delay is an empty medium: that same time dissolves things, reforms memory, and strengthens uninterrupted habit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that knowledge of truth requires no prior testimony, teacher, Scripture, Church, or faith.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that providence operates only through right intentions, immediately fulfilled petitions, and causes transparent to agents.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:DNX7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:DBN-05","text":"It must be false that the social environment is neutral, since praise, eloquence, crowd, and friendship recursively form knowledge and appetite.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:DBN-06","text":"It must be false that a new external arrangement, with the same desire intact, can effect conversion, because perverse desire conceals itself under honorable names.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:D10","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSA-01","text":"The absence of God in a properly local or ontological sense is impossible; experienced absence is only the soul's blindness and turning away before enduring presence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSA-02","text":"A stable position between falsity already abandoned and conversion indefinitely refused is unavailable.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSA-03","text":"Total certainty preceding transformation is unavailable, because the very faculty of judging requires the healing that the demand for certainty prevents.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSA-04","text":"Blessedness within the totality of finite things is impossible, even if their loss is removed in thought.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSA-05","text":"Return through proud assimilation, autonomous knowledge, or self-governing will is forbidden; conversion is conceived only as participation in healing and grace.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX7","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:XD-01","text":"Time acquires a double force: it dissolves the beloved object and, where conversion is deferred, confirms the very habit that clings to the object.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GA-01","CL_5P0L_02:GA-08","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:XD-02","text":"Error does not reside in a single proposition, but is distributed through imagination, authority, doctrinal caricature, and the appetite that wishes to retain false images.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GA-02","CL_5P0L_02:GA-03","CL_5P0L_02:GA-09","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D11","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:XD-03","text":"Epistemic adequacy is not measured by the quantity of local truths, but by the orientation of the knower and the healing of the faculty by which truth is ordered to wisdom.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GA-04","CL_5P0L_02:GA-10","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD4","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:XD-04","text":"The restoration of guilt to the whole agent removes external excuses, but at the same time shows that confession of responsibility does not suffice without the gift by which the will becomes continent.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GA-07","CL_5P0L_02:GA-12","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D6","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:XD-05","text":"No social medium has univocal force: authority and rhetoric can propagate error, convey truth, or produce correction according to the recipient's habit and the higher order.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GA-05","CL_5P0L_02:GA-09","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD8","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:XD-06","text":"Providence is said to order morally mixed causes without abolishing human guilt, but the nexus between higher causality and the responsibility of the agent remains unresolved.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GA-05","CL_5P0L_02:GA-07","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD7","CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:XD-07","text":"Authority is neither simply destroyed nor simply restored: examination dissolves false pretensions, while the necessity of faith requires medicinal authority under a new criterion.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GA-09","CL_5P0L_02:GA-10","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:XD-08","text":"The dissolution of falsity prepares conversion only negatively; when the doctrinal objection is removed, the remaining impediment appears in the habit of the will and constitutes the threshold of grace.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GA-06","CL_5P0L_02:GA-12","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D6","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSD-01","text":"The subject is reclassified from autonomous possessor of truth into a guilty agent, patient of healing, and participant in a light whose source it does not constitute.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_2:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSD-02","text":"Time becomes at once the form of creaturehood, a medium of healing, and a strategic danger: through succession it consoles, but through delay it binds the will and exposes it to death.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A18","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSD-03","text":"Causality is hierarchically ordered: particular intentions produce local effects, while providence places their concurrence toward an end unknown to the agents.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSD-04","text":"Transformative knowledge proceeds through refutation, provisional trust, purgation of faculty, and renewed judgment, not through total demonstration possessed in a single act.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD1","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SNX4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSD-05","text":"Authority and freedom are not simply opposites, because freedom from error is itself formed through mediation, which discrepancy, fruits, and a claim to truth nevertheless render examinable.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSD-06","text":"Evil is ontologically de-substantialized and takes a strategic form: it is a perversion of movement, end, judgment, and habit that turns goods themselves against their order.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME6","CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME4","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:BSD-07","text":"Conversion becomes a change in the state of the whole system, which must reorder ontology, authority, interpretation, affect, and will together, not a mere substitution of opinion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD4","CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RLE-01","text":"Turning away → external inquiry → phantasm → false doctrine → confirmation of turning away constitutes the principal circuit of error.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RLE-02","text":"Love of a temporal end → demand for firmness → loss or anxiety → external flight → return to the wounded soul constitutes the circuit of misery.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS2","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RLE-03","text":"Praise or eloquence → affect → authority → transmission of doctrine → new praise constitutes a path of social amplification, whose epistemic value always remains indeterminate.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS4","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RLE-04","text":"Initial faith → purgation of mind → increased understanding → judgment of authority → more distinct faith constitutes the medicinal circuit of knowledge.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RLE-05","text":"Habit → compromising plan → delay → strengthened habit → diminished freedom constitutes the escalation of servile will.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RLE-06","text":"Ambiguous event → confessional interpretation → recognition of providence → humility → new capacity for reading events constitutes the circuit of retrospective healing.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:RLE-07","text":"The attractor of rest in God gathers the lines of love, knowledge, authority, and will, because each is reduced to the defect of autonomous firmness.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX6","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FGS-B01","text":"Turning away from the end → dispersion of love and knowledge → created goods usurped as autonomous ends or principles.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FGS-B02","text":"Usurpation of a created good → metaphysical phantasm, false authority, or appetite for stability → recursively produced misery and error.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:D11","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FGS-B03","text":"Contradiction by experience, reason, or exegesis → degradation of certainty → rupture with the prior system without immediate positive possession of the new.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS2","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FGS-B04","text":"Rupture of certainty → provisional dwelling → medicinal authority → faith that purges the faculty for further knowledge.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FGS-B05","text":"Correction of intellect → detection of intact habit → transfer of impediment to the will → closure of compromising plans.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FGS-B06","text":"Impotence of the will + uncertain death + mediation of Christ → necessity of grace → conversion not yet effected but structurally inevitable.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A18","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A18","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AFM-B01","text":"Turned-away love and intellect → grief and false metaphysics → examination of doctrine and teacher → collapse of sectarian authority → defensibility of Catholicism → rehabilitated faith → servitude of the will → necessity of grace.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:AS4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AFM-B02","text":"Corporeal phantasm → dualism and caricature of faith → spiritual exegesis → removal of objection → medicinal authority → recursive knowledge.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_2:D7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:AFM-B03","text":"Appetite for rest → temporal goods → anxiety and loss → intermediate plans → delay → death as an uncertain limit → grace as the sole closure of conversion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SD3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MME-01","text":"The truth of a proposition, form of speech, rectitude of the end, and blessedness of the knower are distributed across distinct axes, whose confusion had generated lower errors.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MME-02","text":"Authority is reclassified from dominion or rhetorical splendor into examinable mediation whose role is to lead the mind toward more mature judgment.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:ME1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MME-03","text":"Time ceases to be a neutral stage of events and becomes an operator that dissolves temporal things, delays or advances healing, and increases habit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MME-04","text":"Evil is transferred from a substantial object to a perverse relation among the agent's faculty, object, end, and movement.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MME-05","text":"Conversion is redescribed from a change of doctrine into a reordering of multiple levels, because ontological error can be dissolved while affect and will remain captive.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MME-06","text":"Mediation changes from an impediment to freedom into an ambivalent condition of formation, whence reading must always distinguish the agent's intention, the recipient's disposition, and the providential order.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A13","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level operate the death of the friend, astrology, Faustus, migrations, Ambrose, marriage plans, and Alypius's cases.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ALT1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, turning away, imagination, authority, social habit, custom, and temporality distribute errors and conditions of correction.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ALT2","CH_5P0L_LI_3:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, the question shifts from choosing among doctrines to discovering criterion, medicinal mediation, and the order by which intellect and will are healed.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ALT3","CH_5P0L_LI_3:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, reality is distinguished between God's immutable presence and creature existing successively, mortal, and incapable of bestowing firmness upon itself.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ALT4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological and performative level, confession itself effects what it asserts, because by reconsidering biographical fragments it converts accident into providence, guilt into recognition, and memory into healing.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:FGS7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FL-01","text":"Providence orders perverse causes and yet leaves guilt to agents, but the mode of concurrence between divine and voluntary action is affirmed rather than formally explained.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT6","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FL-02","text":"Faith must heal reason in order to judge authority, but the authority of healing is itself partly recognized through faith in divine institution.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:SD1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FL-03","text":"The refutation of the caricature of Catholicism and the defensibility of Scripture do not accomplish a positive proof of truth, although the movement toward the authority of Scripture is accelerated by confessional force.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:NX10","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:FL-04","text":"Friendship, marriage, and secular goods remain legitimate, but the same goods become bonds under desire; the criterion between ordered use and the covering of appetite is not always explained.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:NX13","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MP-01","text":"Corporeal imagination changes from a positive cause of dualism into an object of exegetical purgation; after its dissolution, the locus of conflict is transferred to the will.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:D5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MP-02","text":"Rhetoric loses epistemic force but retains causal efficacy, whence a repudiated medium returns as criterion and as a path of entry for truth.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD2","CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MP-03","text":"Skepticism changes from protection against false doctrine into an impediment, where suspension of assent indefinitely delays the healing of faith.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD5","CH_5P0L_LI_3:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MP-04","text":"The principal point of mutation occurs when, with correction of intellect relatively complete, the impediment to conversion is found no longer in the object to be believed but in the habit of willing.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_3:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_3:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:HSI-01","text":"Reality implicitly appears as a hierarchical order of mutable goods around immutable presence, in which no creature is its own principle or end.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:AS3","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:HSI-02","text":"The subject is a node of love, memory, habit, testimony, and will, which according to that to which it adheres is either dispersed or integrated.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_2:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:HSI-03","text":"Time is a river that carries away objects, forms memory, bears causes toward unknown ends, and converts delay into servitude.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:A16","CH_5P0L_LI_3:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:HSI-04","text":"Navigation is possible not through flight toward exterior things, but through interior return by mediations whose end is to establish the soul in what does not pass away.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:SNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBQ:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MRT-B01","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement from affective turning away and false ontology through the collapse of authority to medicinal faith and the necessity of grace.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT1","CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT1","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MRT-B02","text":"The structure is strongest where corporeal phantasm falsifies doctrine, examinable discrepancy destroys authority, and, doctrinal correction having been completed, the servitude of the will becomes manifest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT2","CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT4","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MRT-B03","text":"The independent criterion of true authority, the concurrence of providence with guilt, and the manner in which grace will actually liberate the will are not yet sufficiently determined.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT3","CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT8","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MRT-B04","text":"The coherence of this cluster consists not in a merely linear order, but in the varied recurrence of turning away, mediation, and impossible firmness; biographical fragments converge around conversion not yet effected.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT9","CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT9","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_02:MRT-B05","text":"The particular ambiguities of grief, eloquence, marital goods, and providence resist reduction; these nevertheless do not dissolve the mechanism, but indicate the joints where the transition from sign to ontology is compressed.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBQ:MRT3","CH_5P0L_LI_2:MRT7","CH_5P0L_LI_3:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_5P0L_02@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_5P0L_02:v1","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"Chapters 04–06"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Confessiones","title":"Chapters 04–06","context":"Book IV. · Book V. · Book VI.","original_title":"Chapters 04–06","original_context":"Liber Quartus. · Liber Quintus. · Liber Sextus."},"original_title":"Chapters 04–06","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 07–09","order":3,"parents":["CH_5P0L_LI_4","CH_5P0L_LIBO","CH_5P0L_LIBN"],"revision":"CL_5P0L_03@R001","sha256":"039b19f534901082a027c1a47ebf95941e269d649113c47ac4fc1045ab315d89","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AS-B01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo creatura, cui veritas de bono immutabili iam patet, a malo non substantiali sed voluntarie sedimentato liberetur atque libertatem in vita temporali, ecclesiali et mortali perficiat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AS-B02","text":"Thesis globalis malum ex ordine naturarum removet, in privatione et voluntate perverso habitu ligata collocat, liberationem autem gratiae sananti atque mediationibus Christi, Scripturae et Ecclesiae attribuit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AS-B03","text":"Argumentatio diagnostica et reconstructiva falsas ontologias excludit, divisionem voluntatis genealogice explicat, deinde effectus liberationis confessione, sacramento, providentia et intercessione probat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS3","CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AS-B04","text":"Motus ab ascensu ad veritatem incorpoream transit ad detectionem impotentiae practicae, inde ad voluntatem integratam, vitam ecclesialiter formatam et mortem sub spe resurrectionis intellectam.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AS-B05","text":"Progressio est cumulativa et mutatione acta: visio infirmitatem detegit, infirmitas historiam consuetudinis aperit, historia limen gratiae parat, actus autem conversus ulteriorem formationem requirit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:FGS2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AS-B06","text":"Mediatio successive amplificatur ab incarnatione sanante ad allocutionem scripturalem, sacramentum, cantum, communionem et memoriam liturgicam, sine quibus veritas in possessionem temporaliter ordinatam non transit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AS-B07","text":"Conversio simul est eventus punctiformis et processus multistratus: voluntas uno limine integratur, sed intellectus, affectus, professio, consuetudo et relatio socialis temporibus diversis reformantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AS-B08","text":"Clausura non possessionem definitivam sed precem producit: mediatio temporalis ad Sapientiam stabilem ordinatur, dum misericordia et intercessio etiam post vitam laudabilem necessariae manent.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Deus est bonum immutabile et fons omnis naturae; ideo nihil creatum rationem substantiae adversae ex se habet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Quidquid est bonitatem aliquam retinet; malum igitur non est natura positiva, sed diminutio boni et aversio voluntatis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Ordo creatus primo inaequalitatem naturarum complectitur, deinde discordias voluntatis et eventuum intra providentiam ordinantem absorbet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Culpa in voluntate creaturae locatur neque ad naturam contrariam, astra aut effectum providentialiter bonum transferri potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Cognitio veritatis obiectum ostendit, sed neque adhesionem stabilem neque maturitatem voluntatis et intellectus efficit nisi subiectum sanetur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-06","text":"[Attractor] Veritas et Sapientia incommutabiles supra mentem temporalem permanent atque normam iudicii et terminum desiderii praebent.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Gratia voluntatem non delet, sed vincula eius rumpit, consensum excitat et voluntates partiales in actum integrum perducit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Mediatio a Christo et Scriptura ad sacramenta, cantum, communionem et intercessionem extenditur, quia sanatio subiecti formam distributam requirit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Actus voluntarii tempore sedimentantur in consuetudinem necessitatis similem, quae etiam post correctionem rationalem vestigia affectiva relinquere potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Conversio est limen decisivum intra processum longum, cuius effectus voluntatem, intellectum, habitum, statum socialem et incorporationem ecclesialem diversis temporibus mutant.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Providentia effectum salutarem ex eventu adverso vel intentione mala producere potest, quin culpam agentis in bonitatem effectus dissolvat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-12","text":"[Emergent] Confessio causalitatem asymmetrice distribuit: voluntas peccati responsabilitatem gerit, sed initium, medicina et fructus liberationis Deo redduntur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-13","text":"[Terminal] Baptismus conversionem in regenerationem ecclesialem stabilit, non tamen futuram culpam aut permanentem misericordiae necessitatem aufert.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-14","text":"[Attractor] Mens temporaliter Sapientiam tangere potest, sed stabilis praesentiae aeternae possessio intra successionem vitae praesentis indisponibilis manet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-15","text":"[Terminal] Nulla sanctitas humana iudicium claudit; sacrificium Christi, misericordia et intercessio ultimam formam memoriae et spei constituunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-01","text":"Malum ab hypothesi substantiae adversae ad privationem, inde ad voluntatem perversam, consuetudinem et reliquias affectivas transfertur; identitas negativa manet, sed locus operationis temporaliter densatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-02","text":"Voluntas primo locus aversionis est, deinde campus divisionis, postremo consensus a gratia excitatus; eadem facultas culpam et liberationem recipit, non eodem tamen principio causali.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-03","text":"Veritas incorporea identitatem retinet, sed munus mutat: ex termino ascensus fit accusatio impotentiae, deinde norma formationis et attractor eschatologicus.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-04","text":"Consuetudo ex impedimento carnali in genealogiam servitutis explicatur atque post conversionem ut memoria affectiva persistit; non destruitur uno actu, sed ad novum ordinem paulatim traducitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-05","text":"Mediatio a via Christi adversus superbiam ad vocem scripturalem personalem et ad apparatus ecclesiales plurales migrat, dum functio sanandi et adhaesionem stabiliendi permanet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-06","text":"Ascensus interior bis redit functione mutata: primum veritatem demonstrat sed contemplantem infirmum relinquit; postea aeternitatem breviter tangit atque statum viatoris manifestat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-07","text":"Anti-dualismus ab exclusionibus cosmologicis ad unitatem animae et responsabilitatem moralem extenditur, deinde in distinctionem inter intentionem malam et effectum providentialem absorbetur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-08","text":"Exemplum ex comparatione doctrinarum in machinam conversionis mutatur: narrationes alienae dissolvunt excusationes, conversio visibilis autem novas imitationes gignit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-09","text":"Tempus ex successione creata fit medium sedimentationis culpae, discrimen inter nunc et dilationem, atque spatium sacramentalis formationis, luctus et spei.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-10","text":"Ordo universalis mutatur in providentiam narrativam: bonitas totius non solum inconvenientias metaphysicas continet, sed etiam eventus adversos ad salutem convertit sine confusione morali.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-11","text":"Astrologia postquam causalitatem externam infirmavit e campo manifesto recedit; eius opus structuraliter persistit in omni ulteriori recusatione qua culpa ad naturam, necessitatem vel casum transfertur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:CGD-01","text":"Imagines Dei corporeae et astrologia manent refutationes locales; ad gradum praesentem ascendit earum functio communis, scilicet exclusio omnis causalitatis quae bonum immutabile minuat aut responsabilitatem voluntatis extrinsecus solvat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:CGD-02","text":"Distinctio localis inter Platonicos et Scripturam sursum amplificatur in discrimen generale inter cognitionem termini et viam quae subiectum ad fruitionem idoneum reddit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:CGD-03","text":"Delimitationes Christologicae particulares non integrae doctrinae unionem hoc gradu constituunt; earum vis superior est mediatorem nec purum magistrum nec apparentiam sine plena humanitate esse posse.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX9","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:CGD-04","text":"Victorinus, Antonius et aulici casus inferiores manent, sed coniuncti ostendunt exemplum alienum facultatem praesentis mutationis probare, excusationes destruere et conversionem socialiter propagare.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:CGD-05","text":"Vita Monicae non est appendix biographica, sed probatio praesentis gradus qua virtus, correctio, providentia, contemplatio, mors et intercessio sub eadem ratione doni ordinantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:CGD-06","text":"Duo ascensus interiores unitates coniungunt: prior necessitatem mediationis aperit, posterior terminum mediationum praegustat sed eius possessionem adhuc differt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:CGD-07","text":"Actus conversionis qui in discrimine voluntatis localiter clauditur ad gradum praesentem non est finis, sed transitus in formationem, sacramentum, communitatem, disciplinam affectuum et intelligentiam mortis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:CGD-08","text":"Baptismus terminalis est respectu culpae antecedentis et incorporationis ecclesialis, non respectu totius itineris; ulterior culpa, luctus et misericordia vetant eum in clausuram absolutam converti.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-01","text":"Systema nullam materiam increatam aut substantiam malam admittit ex qua defectus voluntatis causaliter derivetur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-02","text":"Pluralitas affectuum et voluntatum neque pluralitatem animarum neque principium ontologice contrarium probat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-03","text":"Deus nec spatio dividitur nec per imaginem, sonum aut mensuram corporalem ut terminus cognitionis definitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-04","text":"Causalitas astralis vel externa culpam non aufert, quia praedictio incerta et necessitas acquisita actum voluntarium antecedentem non abolent.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-05","text":"Cognitio philosophica, certitudo metaphysica et doctrina recta non sunt causa sufficiens adhaesionis, actionis aut maturitatis spiritualis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-06","text":"Voluntas nullum fundamentum autonomum possidet quo consuetudinem suam rumpat aut continentiam ex propria virtute producat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX12","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-07","text":"Dilatio conversionis non est spatium neutrum; promissum futuri indefiniti praesentem retentionem veteris ordinis operatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX13","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-08","text":"Interioritas privata et mediatio exterior separatim sumptae conversionem non perficiunt; sanatio interna incorporationem, confessionem et communionem postulat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-09","text":"Effectus providentialiter bonus intentionem malam non iustificat, neque successus eventus mensuram moralem agentis constituit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-10","text":"Virtus, baptismus et vita laudabilis neque innocentiam absolutam neque ius salutis sine misericordia constituunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-11","text":"Nulla creatura, professio, propinquitas corporalis aut patria terrestris potest terminum ultimum desiderii vel communionis praebere.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse oportet esse cum extensione spatiali converti; aliter Deus incorporeus et veritas supra mentem in nihilum redigerentur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse oportet mentem mutabilem normam sui iudicii producere; aliter ascensus ad veritatem incommutabilem fundamentum amitteret.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse oportet cognitionem termini facultatem perveniendi secum ferre; aliter transitus a metaphysica ad voluntatem et gratiam supervacuus fieret.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse oportet consuetudinem naturam alienam vel necessitatem primariam esse; aliter simul imputabilitas praeterita et sanabilitas praesens corruerent.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse oportet gratiam voluntatem coactione substituere; systema indiget voluntate vere consentiente, quamvis principium liberationis ipsa non praebeat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:DBN-06","text":"Falsum esse oportet conversionem uno decreto omnes ordines subiecti consummare; aliter formatio intellectualis, sacramentalis et affectiva structuram necessariam amitteret.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:DBN-07","text":"Falsum esse oportet bonum effectum bonitatem intentionis demonstrare; aliter providentia et retributio moralis indistinguibiles fierent.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:DBN-08","text":"Falsum esse oportet regenerationem sacramentalem omnem culpam futuram excludere; aliter misericordia post baptismum et intercessio pro laudabilibus incohaerentes essent.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:DBN-09","text":"Falsum esse oportet immediationem Dei mediationes temporales supervacaneas facere; status viatoris signis eget, quamvis terminus eorum transcensum promittat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSA-01","text":"Nulla exterioritas ontologica relinquitur in qua malum, materia aut natura contraria ordini creato coordinari possit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSA-02","text":"Nullum ego neutrum et nullum futurum vacuum inter voluntates contendentes datur; ipsa dilatio iam pars ordinis veteris est.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSA-03","text":"Possibilitas subiecti se ipsum ex nihilo moraliter regenerantis inadmissibilis est; libertas recipitur ut sanata, non producitur ut causa sui.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SNX3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSA-04","text":"Stabilis immediataque possessio Sapientiae intra vitam temporalem abest; haec indisponibilitas mediationibus praesentibus directionem et terminum dat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSA-05","text":"Nulla ratio meritorum potest iudicium claudere aut misericordiam superfluam facere; absentia innocentiae absolutae precem terminalem generat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSA-06","text":"Plena transparentia sui et providentiae indisponibilis manet; confessio causam ultimam Deo tribuit sine cognitione exhaustiva omnium mediorum.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSA-07","text":"Patria ultima nec loco, sepultura, successu nec propinquitate corporali continetur; communionis forma terminalis resurrectionem et memoriam liturgicam postulat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-01","text":"Privatio ontologica, consuetudo moralis et persistentia affectiva componuntur in unam theoriam mali quod essentia propria caret, sed efficaciam temporalem per actus sedimentatos acquirit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A15","CL_5P0L_03:GA-02","CL_5P0L_03:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-02","text":"Ascensus ad veritatem, impotentia conversionis et immaturitas post conversionem demonstrant cognitionem salutarem non simplicem informationem, sed transformationem capacitatis subiecti esse.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D6","CL_5P0L_03:GA-05","CL_5P0L_03:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-03","text":"Responsabilitas et dependentia a gratia cohaerent asymmetrice: subiectum servitutem per actus suos fabricat, sed principium quo vincula rumpuntur sibi non potest praebere.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3","CL_5P0L_03:GA-04","CL_5P0L_03:GA-07","CL_5P0L_03:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-04","text":"Incarnatio, allocutio scripturalis et incorporatio sacramentalis constituunt unam seriem qua veritas superior ad facultates temporales subiecti descendit easque ad se elevat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A11","CL_5P0L_03:GA-08","CL_5P0L_03:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-05","text":"Conversio uno actu divisionem voluntatis claudit, sed non uno tempore omnes eius causas, habitus et effectus; eventus est forma compressionis processus, non negatio processus.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2","CL_5P0L_03:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-06","text":"Ordo universalis et providentia asymmetrica sinunt effectum bonum ex discordia oriri sine substantializatione mali neque absolutione intentionis pravae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4","CL_5P0L_03:GA-03","CL_5P0L_03:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-07","text":"Exemplum conversi et communio ecclesialis efficiunt circuitum propagationis: liberatio visibilis imitationem accendit, communitas eam stabilit, narratio autem novum lectorem intra eundem circuitum trahit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME6","CL_5P0L_03:GA-08","CL_5P0L_03:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-08","text":"Duo ascensus interiores statuunt contemplationem veram sed instabilem esse; brevitas tactus non cognitionem evacuat, sed necessitatem formationis praesentis et possessionis eschatologicae distinguit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2","CL_5P0L_03:GA-06","CL_5P0L_03:GA-14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-09","text":"Liberatio interior separationem externam regere debet, sed conversio privatam invisibilitatem retinere non potest; humilitas spectaculum recusat, communio tamen formam publicam requirit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX9","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX5","CL_5P0L_03:GA-08","CL_5P0L_03:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-10","text":"Baptismus remissionem et regenerationem efficit, sed laus post baptismum in intercessionem transit; sacramentum ordinem misericordiae instituit, non necessitatem eius terminat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D15","CL_5P0L_03:GA-13","CL_5P0L_03:GA-15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-11","text":"Sanatio voluntatis ordinem affectuum mutat, non vulnerabilitatem temporalem delet; consuetudo correcta adhuc in memoria, separatione et luctu operatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D14","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX6","CL_5P0L_03:GA-09","CL_5P0L_03:GA-14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-12","text":"Reiectio astrologiae et dualismi in eandem structuram convergit: causalitas externa non potest voluntatem a culpa eximere, quamvis providentia eventuum ordinem excedat cognitionem agentis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9","CL_5P0L_03:GA-04","CL_5P0L_03:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSD-01","text":"Bonitas ontologica creaturae condicionem sanabilitatis constituit: quia malum naturam propriam non efficit, voluntas aegra restitui potest sine destructione subiecti.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSD-02","text":"Subiectum non est punctum voluntatis atemporale, sed historia actuum, habituum, exemplorum, sacramentorum et affectuum, quae responsabilitatem et transformationem simul portat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSD-03","text":"Causalitas in quattuor ordines distribuitur: intentio mala creaturae, effectus providentialiter ordinatus, liberatio a gratia inchoata et consensus voluntatis ecclesialiter stabilitus.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSD-04","text":"Tempus conversionis est catastrophicum intra accumulationem: diuturna sedimentatio et mediatio in unum nunc comprimuntur, cuius effectus postea per formationem explicantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSD-05","text":"Epistemologia fit soteriologica: veritas cognita statum subiecti iudicat, sed cognitio plena tantum emergit cum voluntas et affectus ad obiectum cognitum formantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSD-06","text":"Ecclesia operatur ut apparatus temporalis transitus ad aeternum, quia propositionem in allocutionem, affectum in cantum, remissionem in sacramentum et memoriam in intercessionem convertit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSD-07","text":"Confessio non solum acta narrat, sed eorum causalitatem performative reordinat et lectorem ex spectatore in gratias agentem, imitatorem atque intercessorem mutat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSD-08","text":"Mors relationem non annihilat, sed eam a consuetudine corporali ad dolorem ordinandum, spem resurrectionis et memoriam liturgicam transfert.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSD-09","text":"Clausura huius gregis aperta manet: conversionem sacramentaliter stabilitam sequuntur vulnerabilitas, iudicium et oratio, dum possessio Sapientiae in terminum eschatologicum differtur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RLE-01","text":"Voluntas perversa libidinem gignit, libido consuetudinem, consuetudo divisionem, divisio dilationem, dilatio autem eandem consuetudinem roborat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RLE-02","text":"Veritas cognita impotentiam manifestat; impotentia exemplis alienis fit inexcusabilis; pudor implorationem aperit; gratia voluntatem ad veritatem iam cognitam reducit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RLE-03","text":"Conversio visibilis imitationem generat, imitatio novos conversos producit, quorum gaudium commune vim exemplarem ulterioris conversionis amplificat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RLE-04","text":"Scriptura a textu generali ad allocutionem praesentem transit; allocutio actum efficit; actus narratus vicissim Scripturam alteri lectori ut possibilem allocutionem restituit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:D9","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RLE-05","text":"Donum Dei confessionem causalitatis generat, confessio gratiarum actionem, gratiarum actio intercessionem; intercessio agnoscit etiam sanctitatem receptum donum manere.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RLE-06","text":"Eventus adversus effectum salutarem parit; effectus ad providentiam refertur, culpa intentioni relinquitur, atque eadem distinctio novos eventus legendi modum format.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RLE-07","text":"Mens a sensibilibus ad se et supra se ascendit, Sapientiam tangit, ad successionem verborum redit atque ex reditu desiderium stabilioris praesentiae auget.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RLE-08","text":"Vinculum familiare per mortem abrumpitur, abruptio dolorem aperit, dolor coram Deo ordinatur, memoria autem in spem resurrectionis et intercessionem convertitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RLE-09","text":"Attractor totius motus est stabilis fruitio Sapientiae: quia nunc indisponibilis manet, omnes mediationes, conversiones et luctus ad praesentiam nondum possessam convergunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FGS-B01","text":"Invariantes statuuntur: bonum immutabile, creatio omnis naturae et bonitas essendi nullam substantiam malam relinquunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FGS-B02","text":"Exemplaria corporea, dualistica et deterministica contra invariantes probantur atque ut modos exteriorizandi defectum eliminantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FGS-B03","text":"Ascensus veritatem supra mentem demonstrat; defectus adhesionis cognitionem ab efficacia salutari separat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FGS-B04","text":"Defectus in historiam voluntatis resolvitur: aversio actus producit, actus consuetudinem, consuetudo necessitatem et voluntatem partialem.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FGS-B05","text":"Exempla et Scriptura divisionem voluntatis ad limen adducunt, ubi dilatio suam vim servilem patefacit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FGS-B06","text":"Gratia vincula rumpit et voluntatem sine substitutione integrat; cognitio iam acquisita in consensum et novum ordinem vitae transit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FGS-B07","text":"Liberatio interna professionem, disciplinam, sacramentum et communionem ordinat, unde conversio punctiformis in processum ecclesialem explicatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FGS-B08","text":"Providentia eventus adversos sine confusione intentionum assumit, dum contemplatio breviter terminum aeternum aperit et ad tempus remittit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FGS-B09","text":"Mors et sanctitas omnem clausuram meritoriam dissolvunt; narratio in misericordiam, sacrificium et intercessionem convertitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:D15","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AFM-B01","text":"Imaginatio corporea → exclusio dualismi → veritas incorporea → malum ut privatio → insufficientia cognitionis → genealogia consuetudinis → voluntas divisa → gratia integrans → conversio.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AF1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AFM-B02","text":"Conversio punctiformis → renuntiatio ordinata → formatio intellectualis → baptismus → communio ecclesialis → providentia narrata → contemplatio brevis → luctus → intercessio.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AFM-B03","text":"Exteriorizatio culpae → responsabilitas voluntatis → impossibilitas autonomiae → mediatio sanans → causalitas Deo restituta → possessio aeterna adhuc dilata.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MME-01","text":"Malum ex classe naturarum in structuram triplicem reclassificatur: privatio ontologica, aversio voluntaria et inertia temporaliter sedimentata.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MME-02","text":"Subiectum ex substantia contra substantiam pugnantem in unam voluntatem historicam, partialem, culpabilem et sanabilem redescribitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MME-03","text":"Conversio ex mutatione opinionis in integrationem voluntatis et processum formationis sacramentalis, affectivae ac socialis expanditur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MME-04","text":"Cognitio dividitur in demonstrationem obiecti, capacitatem adhaerendi et stabilitatem fruitionis; philosophia prioris ordinis sufficientiam amittit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME6","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MME-05","text":"Tempus ex recipiente neutro in machinam moralem mutatur: actus sedimentat, dilatio servitutem auget, momentum decisivum comprimit, formatio autem effectus explicat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MME-06","text":"Scriptura ex deposito propositionum in eventum allocutionis reclassificatur, cuius vis ex tempore, receptione et praeparatione subiecti oritur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MME-07","text":"Ecclesia fit apparatus distribuentis cognitionem, affectum, confessionem, sacramentum, resistentiam communem et memoriam defunctorum.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MME-08","text":"Providentia causalitatem moralem a causalitate eventuum distinguit, ita ut bonum ex malo provenire possit sine conversione malae intentionis in bonam.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MME-09","text":"Mors et vita sancta reordinantur: mors fit separatio temporalis intra resurrectionem, sanctitas autem materia gratiarum actionis et intercessionis, non titulus debiti.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B01","text":"Gradus superficiei coniungit dissolutionem errorum de malo, discrimen conversionis, renuntiationem, baptismum, contemplationem Ostiensem, mortem Monicae et precem pro ea.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:ALT1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:ALT1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B02","text":"Gradus structuralis componit participationem essendi, voluntatem, consuetudinem, gratiam, providentiam et mediationes ecclesiales in unam machinam formationis temporalis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:ALT2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:ALT2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B03","text":"Gradus metastrategicus interpretationem a quaestione obiecti ad quaestionem capacitatis transfert atque exemplum, confessionem et intercessionem modos interventionis efficit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:ALT3","CH_5P0L_LIBO:ALT3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B04","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis realitatem inter creaturas mutabiles et Sapientiam aeternam distinguit, dum subiectum per successionem ligatur, sanatur et ad praesentiam eschatologicam dirigitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:ALT4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B05","text":"Gradus methodologicus et performativus ipsam confessionem adhibet ut redistributionem causalitatis: narratio bonum Deo reddit, culpam voluntati, lectorem autem imitationi et precationi inserit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FL-01","text":"Gratia principium liberationis praebet et voluntas vere consentit, sed modus quo actio divina consensum efficit sine coactione formaliter indeterminatus manet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FL-02","text":"Conversio tamquam actus integer et tamquam processus multistratus cohaeret tantum si limen voluntatis ab ulteriori transformatione intellectus et affectus distinguatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FL-03","text":"Mediationes ecclesiales necessariae sunt, sed immediatio Sapientiae desideratur ut earum terminus; relatio inter necessitatem praesentem et futuram superationem signorum manet tensionis locus.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FL-04","text":"Remissio baptismalis et culpa posterior simul affirmantur, sed limes inter regenerationem, reliquias habitus et novam culpam non perfecte explicatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FL-05","text":"Providentia bonum ex intentione mala producit, sed modus concursus quo effectus Deo et culpa agenti distribuuntur assertione firmatur potius quam analysi exhaustiva.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FL-06","text":"Conversio publicam confessionem requirit, dum renuntiatio Augustini spectaculum magnitudinis recusat; visibilitas necessaria a iactantia distinguenda manet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FL-07","text":"Fides desperationem luctus excludit, non ipsum dolorem; discrimen inter consuetudinem carnalem et lacrimas recte ordinatas mobile manet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX11","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FL-08","text":"Deus invariabilis affirmatur, dum gaudium de conversione sermone affectivo variatur; relatio inter immutabilitatem divinam et variationem gaudii in creaturis compressa manet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MP-01","text":"Malum sensum mutat cum a substantia ad privationem, ab illa ad aversionem voluntatis atque inde ad consuetudinem temporalem transfertur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MP-02","text":"Veritas ex obiecto demonstrabili mutatur in normam quae capacitatem contemplantis iudicat et liberationem ad novum ordinem vitae exigit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MP-03","text":"Voluntas ex pluralitate partialium appetituum ad integrum velle transit; in hoc puncto deliberatio cessat et actus incipit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MP-04","text":"Scriptura functionem mutat cum ex propositione generali in allocutionem temporalem et personalem recipitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MP-05","text":"Conversio a clausura discriminali ad principium formationis mutatur; quod voluntatem terminat, processum sacramentalem et affectivum aperit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MP-06","text":"Vinculum familiare a possessione corporali ad memoriam liturgicam et spem resurrectionis transfertur, sine abolitione doloris separationis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:HSI-01","text":"Realitas implicite est campus ordinatus circa fontem immutabilem, in quo defectus ordinem vulnerare potest sed naturam contrariam producere nequit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum est nodus diachronicus voluntatum, habituum et relationum: se ligat per repetitionem, ab alio principio solvitur et consensu sanato novum ordinem suscipit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:HSI-03","text":"Tempus est simul sedimentum, limen et peregrinatio: praeteritum consuetudinem format, praesens decisionem comprimit, futurum autem possessionem aeternam differt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:HSI-04","text":"Ecclesia est rete mediationum quod veritatem per textum, vocem, aquam, cantum, exemplum et memoriam distribuit atque subiecta singularia in communionem format.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:HSI-05","text":"Navigatio est spiralis: mens ascendit, redit, consuetudinem patitur, iterum per gratiam elevatur et ex singulis reditibus desiderium stabilis praesentiae auget.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:HSI-06","text":"Mors est limen quod communionem corporalem frangit sed relationem non delet; affectum in luctum, luctum in precem et memoriam in spem resurrectionis convertit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad restituendum motum a correctione ontologiae mali per sanationem voluntatis ad incorporationem ecclesialem, mortem et intercessionem.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B02","text":"Systema hoc gradu cohaeret quia bonitatem creaturae, responsabilitatem voluntatis, necessitatem gratiae et permanentem misericordiae rationem sine dualismo componit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B03","text":"Firmissima structura est coniunctio inter genealogiam consuetudinis et redistributionem causalitatis, qua culpa voluntati, liberatio et bonum Deo tribuuntur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B04","text":"Minus determinata manet efficientia qua gratia voluntatem integram producit sine coactione; narratio effectum ostendit, sed nexum causaliter non formalizat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B05","text":"Ordo universalis et providentia firmiter postulantur, sed congruentia omnium particularium et modus quo bonum ex malo elicitur non universaliter demonstrantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B06","text":"Quaedam commissurae auctoritate narrationis, analogia conversionum, testimonio signorum et fide eschatologica nituntur potius quam deductione interna completa.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B07","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat: falsas exterioritates excludit, defectum intra voluntatem temporalem localizat, liberationem per mediationem efficit et clausuram in misericordiam aperit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT9","CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT10","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B08","text":"Reductioni axiomaticae resistunt densitas affectuum, temporalitas allocutionis et singularitas luctus, quia hae non exempla accidentalia sed media sunt quibus systema suam doctrinam efficit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D14","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T142441371579Z_9c70e7b0","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 07–09","source_sha256":"039b19f534901082a027c1a47ebf95941e269d649113c47ac4fc1045ab315d89","sha256":"cc352f4fa7f80ecdc6964dd8808c9ee8e1a571b768b38cac111067510acfebf0","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:24:41.373811+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AS-B01","text":"The system asks how the creature, to whom the truth concerning the immutable good is already manifest, may be freed from evil—not substantial, but voluntarily sedimented—and perfect freedom in temporal, ecclesial, and mortal life.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AS-B02","text":"The global thesis removes evil from the order of natures, situates it in privation and in the will bound by a perverse habit, and attributes liberation to healing grace and to the mediations of Christ, Scripture, and the Church.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AS-B03","text":"The diagnostic and reconstructive argument excludes false ontologies, genealogically explains the division of the will, then demonstrates the effects of liberation through confession, sacrament, providence, and intercession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS3","CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AS-B04","text":"The movement proceeds from ascent to incorporeal truth to the detection of practical impotence, thence to an integrated will, an ecclesially formed life, and death understood under the hope of resurrection.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AS-B05","text":"The progression is cumulative and effected through mutation: vision detects weakness, weakness discloses the history of habit, history prepares the threshold of grace, while the converted act requires further formation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:FGS7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:FGS2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AS-B06","text":"Mediation is progressively amplified from the healing incarnation to scriptural address, sacrament, chant, communion, and liturgical memory, without which truth does not pass into temporally ordered possession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AS-B07","text":"Conversion is at once a point-like event and a multilayered process: the will is integrated at a single threshold, but intellect, affect, profession, habit, and social relation are reformed at different times.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AS-B08","text":"The closure produces not definitive possession but prayer: temporal mediation is ordered toward stable Wisdom, while mercy and intercession remain necessary even after a praiseworthy life.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] God is the immutable good and the source of every nature; therefore nothing created has in itself the character of an opposed substance.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Whatever exists retains some goodness; evil, therefore, is not a positive nature, but a diminution of good and a turning-away of the will.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] The created order first encompasses the inequality of natures, then absorbs the discordances of wills and events within ordering providence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Fault is located in the will of the creature and cannot be transferred to a contrary nature, the stars, or an effect providentially good.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Knowledge of truth shows the object, but produces neither stable adhesion nor maturity of will and intellect unless the subject is healed.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-06","text":"[Attractor] Immutable Truth and Wisdom remain above the temporal mind and furnish the norm of judgment and the end of desire.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Grace does not abolish the will, but breaks its bonds, arouses consent, and brings partial wills into an integral act.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Mediation extends from Christ and Scripture to sacraments, chant, communion, and intercession, because the healing of the subject requires a distributed form.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Voluntary acts are sedimented in time into a habit resembling necessity, which can leave affective traces even after rational correction.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Conversion is a decisive threshold within a long process, whose effects alter will, intellect, habit, social condition, and ecclesial incorporation at different times.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Providence can produce a salutary effect from an adverse event or evil intention without dissolving the agent's fault into the goodness of the effect.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-12","text":"[Emergent] Confession distributes causality asymmetrically: the will bears responsibility for sin, but the beginning, remedy, and fruit of liberation are rendered to God.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-13","text":"[Terminal] Baptism establishes conversion in ecclesial regeneration, yet does not remove future fault or the enduring necessity of mercy.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-14","text":"[Attractor] The mind can touch Wisdom temporally, but stable possession of eternal presence remains unavailable within the succession of present life.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GA-15","text":"[Terminal] No human holiness closes judgment; Christ's sacrifice, mercy, and intercession constitute the ultimate form of memory and hope.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-01","text":"Evil is transferred from the hypothesis of an opposed substance to privation, thence to the perverse will, habit, and affective residues; its negative identity remains, but its locus of operation becomes temporally denser.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-02","text":"The will is first the locus of turning-away, then the field of division, finally consent aroused by grace; the same faculty receives fault and liberation, though not under the same causal principle.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-03","text":"Incorporeal truth retains its identity, but changes its function: from the end of ascent it becomes an accusation of impotence, then a norm of formation and an eschatological attractor.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-04","text":"Habit is unfolded from a carnal impediment into a genealogy of bondage and persists after conversion as affective memory; it is not destroyed by a single act, but gradually transferred to a new order.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-05","text":"Mediation migrates from the way of Christ against pride to the personal scriptural voice and to multiple ecclesial apparatuses, while its function of healing and stabilizing adhesion remains.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-06","text":"Interior ascent returns twice with a changed function: first it demonstrates truth but leaves the contemplator weak; later it briefly touches eternity and reveals the condition of the wayfarer.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-07","text":"Anti-dualism extends from cosmological exclusions to the unity of the soul and moral responsibility, then is absorbed into the distinction between evil intention and providential effect.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-08","text":"Example is transformed from a comparison of doctrines into a machine of conversion: alien narratives dissolve excuses, whereas visible conversion generates new imitations.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-09","text":"Time changes from created succession into the medium of the sedimentation of fault, the crisis between now and delay, and the space of sacramental formation, mourning, and hope.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-10","text":"Universal order changes into narrative providence: the goodness of the whole not only contains metaphysical incongruities, but also turns adverse events toward salvation without moral confusion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RMD-11","text":"After undermining external causality, astrology recedes from the manifest field; its work structurally persists in every subsequent refusal by which fault is transferred to nature, necessity, or chance.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:CGD-01","text":"Corporeal images of God and astrology remain local refutations; at the present level their common function rises, namely, the exclusion of every causality that diminishes the immutable good or extrinsically dissolves the responsibility of the will.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:CGD-02","text":"The local distinction between Platonists and Scripture is amplified upward into the general difference between knowledge of the end and the way that renders the subject fit for fruition.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:CGD-03","text":"Particular Christological delimitations do not constitute the union of the integral doctrine at this level; their higher force is that the mediator can be neither a mere teacher nor an appearance without full humanity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX8","CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX9","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:CGD-04","text":"Victorinus, Anthony, and the courtiers remain lower cases, but together show that another's example can prove the capacity for present change, destroy excuses, and socially propagate conversion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:CGD-05","text":"Monica's life is not a biographical appendix, but a demonstration at the present level by which virtue, correction, providence, contemplation, death, and intercession are ordered under the same rationale of gift.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:CGD-06","text":"The two interior ascents unite the units: the former discloses the necessity of mediation, the latter anticipates the end of mediations but still defers its possession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:CGD-07","text":"The act of conversion that locally closes in the crisis of the will is not, at the present level, an end, but a transition into formation, sacrament, community, discipline of the affects, and an understanding of death.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:CGD-08","text":"Baptism is terminal with respect to antecedent fault and ecclesial incorporation, not with respect to the whole journey; further fault, mourning, and mercy prevent its being turned into an absolute closure.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-01","text":"The system admits no uncreated matter or evil substance from which the defect of the will may be causally derived.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-02","text":"The plurality of affects and wills proves neither a plurality of souls nor an ontologically contrary principle.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-03","text":"God is neither divided by space nor defined as the end of cognition through a bodily image, sound, or measure.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-04","text":"Astral or external causality does not remove fault, because uncertain prediction and acquired necessity do not abolish the antecedent voluntary act.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-05","text":"Philosophical knowledge, metaphysical certainty, and correct doctrine are not a sufficient cause of adhesion, action, or spiritual maturity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-06","text":"The will possesses no autonomous foundation by which it may break its habit or produce continence from its own strength.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX12","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-07","text":"The delay of conversion is not a neutral space; the promise of an indefinite future effects the present retention of the old order.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX13","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-08","text":"Private interiority and external mediation, taken separately, do not complete conversion; internal healing requires incorporation, confession, and communion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-09","text":"A providentially good effect does not justify an evil intention, nor does the success of an event constitute the moral measure of the agent.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-10","text":"Virtue, baptism, and a praiseworthy life establish neither absolute innocence nor a right to salvation without mercy.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:GNX-11","text":"No creature, profession, bodily proximity, or earthly homeland can provide the ultimate end of desire or communion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that being is convertible with spatial extension; otherwise incorporeal God and truth above the mind would be reduced to nothing.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that the mutable mind produces the norm of its own judgment; otherwise ascent to immutable truth would lose its foundation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that knowledge of the end carries with it the capacity to attain it; otherwise the transition from metaphysics to will and grace would become superfluous.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:DNX6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that habit is an alien nature or primary necessity; otherwise both past imputability and present healability would collapse.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:DBN-05","text":"It must be false that grace replaces the will by compulsion; the system requires a will that truly consents, although it does not itself furnish the principle of liberation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:DNX4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:DBN-06","text":"It must be false that conversion consummates all orders of the subject by a single decree; otherwise intellectual, sacramental, and affective formation would lose their necessary structure.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:DBN-07","text":"It must be false that a good effect demonstrates the goodness of intention; otherwise providence and moral recompense would become indistinguishable.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:DBN-08","text":"It must be false that sacramental regeneration excludes every future fault; otherwise post-baptismal mercy and intercession for the praiseworthy would be incoherent.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:DBN-09","text":"It must be false that God's immediacy makes temporal mediations superfluous; the state of the wayfarer needs signs, although their end promises transcendence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSA-01","text":"No ontological exteriority remains in which evil, matter, or a contrary nature could be coordinated with the created order.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSA-02","text":"There is no neutral self and no empty future between contending wills; delay itself is already part of the old order.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSA-03","text":"The possibility of a subject morally regenerating itself from nothing is inadmissible; freedom is received as healed, not produced as its own cause.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SNX3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSA-04","text":"Stable and immediate possession of Wisdom is absent within temporal life; this unavailability gives direction and an end to present mediations.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSA-05","text":"No account of merits can close judgment or make mercy superfluous; the absence of absolute innocence generates terminal prayer.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSA-06","text":"Full transparency of self and providence remains unavailable; confession attributes the ultimate cause to God without exhaustive knowledge of all means.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSA-07","text":"The ultimate homeland is contained neither in place, burial, success, nor bodily proximity; the terminal form of communion requires resurrection and liturgical memory.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-01","text":"Ontological privation, moral habit, and affective persistence are composed into one theory of evil that lacks its own essence but acquires temporal efficacy through sedimented acts.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A15","CL_5P0L_03:GA-02","CL_5P0L_03:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-02","text":"Ascent to truth, the impotence of conversion, and immaturity after conversion demonstrate that salvific knowledge is not mere information, but transformation of the subject's capacity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D6","CL_5P0L_03:GA-05","CL_5P0L_03:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-03","text":"Responsibility and dependence on grace cohere asymmetrically: the subject fabricates bondage through its own acts, but cannot provide for itself the principle by which its bonds are broken.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3","CL_5P0L_03:GA-04","CL_5P0L_03:GA-07","CL_5P0L_03:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-04","text":"Incarnation, scriptural address, and sacramental incorporation constitute one series by which higher truth descends to the temporal capacities of the subject and raises them to itself.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A11","CL_5P0L_03:GA-08","CL_5P0L_03:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-05","text":"Conversion closes the division of the will in one act, but not all its causes, habits, and effects at one time; the event is a form of compression of a process, not the negation of a process.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2","CL_5P0L_03:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-06","text":"Universal order and asymmetric providence allow a good effect to arise from discord without substantializing evil or absolving perverse intention.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4","CL_5P0L_03:GA-03","CL_5P0L_03:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-07","text":"The example of the convert and ecclesial communion effect a circuit of propagation: visible liberation kindles imitation, community stabilizes it, and narrative draws a new reader into the same circuit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME6","CL_5P0L_03:GA-08","CL_5P0L_03:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-08","text":"The two interior ascents establish contemplation as true but unstable; the brevity of the touch does not empty knowledge, but distinguishes the necessity of present formation from eschatological possession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2","CL_5P0L_03:GA-06","CL_5P0L_03:GA-14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-09","text":"Interior liberation must govern external separation, but conversion cannot retain private invisibility; humility refuses spectacle, yet communion requires a public form.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:NX9","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:DNX5","CL_5P0L_03:GA-08","CL_5P0L_03:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-10","text":"Baptism effects remission and regeneration, but praise after baptism passes into intercession; sacrament establishes the order of mercy, not the end of its necessity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D15","CL_5P0L_03:GA-13","CL_5P0L_03:GA-15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-11","text":"The healing of the will changes the order of affects, not temporal vulnerability; corrected habit still operates in memory, separation, and mourning.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D14","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX6","CL_5P0L_03:GA-09","CL_5P0L_03:GA-14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:XD-12","text":"The rejection of astrology and dualism converges in the same structure: external causality cannot exempt the will from fault, even though the providence of events exceeds the agent's knowledge.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9","CL_5P0L_03:GA-04","CL_5P0L_03:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSD-01","text":"The ontological goodness of the creature constitutes the condition of healability: because evil does not produce a nature of its own, the sick will can be restored without the destruction of the subject.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSD-02","text":"The subject is not an atemporal point of will, but a history of acts, habits, examples, sacraments, and affects, which bears responsibility and transformation together.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSD-03","text":"Causality is distributed across four orders: the evil intention of the creature, the providentially ordered effect, liberation initiated by grace, and the consent of the will stabilized ecclesially.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSD-04","text":"The time of conversion is catastrophic within accumulation: prolonged sedimentation and mediation are compressed into a single now, whose effects are subsequently unfolded through formation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSD-05","text":"Epistemology becomes soteriological: known truth judges the condition of the subject, but full knowledge emerges only when will and affect are formed toward the known object.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSD-06","text":"The Church operates as a temporal apparatus of passage to the eternal, because it turns proposition into address, affect into chant, remission into sacrament, and memory into intercession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSD-07","text":"Confession not only narrates deeds, but performatively reorders their causality and changes the reader from spectator into one giving thanks, an imitator, and an intercessor.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSD-08","text":"Death does not annihilate relation, but transfers it from bodily habit to ordered grief, the hope of resurrection, and liturgical memory.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:BSD-09","text":"The closure of this group remains open: sacramentally stabilized conversion is followed by vulnerability, judgment, and prayer, while possession of Wisdom is deferred to the eschatological end.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RLE-01","text":"A perverse will generates lust, lust habit, habit division, division delay, and delay in turn strengthens the same habit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RLE-02","text":"Known truth reveals impotence; through the examples of others impotence becomes inexcusable; shame opens supplication; grace returns the will to truth already known.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RLE-03","text":"Visible conversion generates imitation; imitation produces new converts, whose common joy amplifies the exemplary force of further conversion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RLE-04","text":"Scripture passes from a general text to a present address; the address effects an act; the narrated act in turn restores Scripture to another reader as a possible address.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:D9","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RLE-05","text":"God's gift generates confession of causality, confession thanksgiving, thanksgiving intercession; intercession recognizes that even holiness remains a received gift.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RLE-06","text":"An adverse event produces a salutary effect; the effect is referred to providence, fault is left to intention, and the same distinction forms a way of reading new events.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RLE-07","text":"The mind ascends from sensible things to itself and above itself, touches Wisdom, returns to the succession of words, and through that return increases its desire for a more stable presence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RLE-08","text":"The familial bond is broken by death, the break opens grief, grief is ordered before God, while memory is transformed into hope of resurrection and intercession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:RLE-09","text":"The attractor of the entire movement is stable fruition of Wisdom: because it remains unavailable now, all mediations, conversions, and griefs converge upon a presence not yet possessed.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FGS-B01","text":"The invariants are established: the immutable good, the creation of every nature, and the goodness of being leave no evil substance.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:A1","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A4","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FGS-B02","text":"Corporeal, dualistic, and deterministic models are tested against the invariants and eliminated as modes of externalizing defect.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS3","CH_5P0L_LI_4:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FGS-B03","text":"Ascent demonstrates truth above the mind; the failure of adhesion separates knowledge from salvific efficacy.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","CH_5P0L_LI_4:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FGS-B04","text":"Defect is resolved into the history of the will: turning-away produces act, act habit, habit necessity and a partial will.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FGS-B05","text":"Examples and Scripture bring the division of the will to a threshold, where delay reveals its servile force.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A9","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FGS-B06","text":"Grace breaks bonds and integrates the will without substitution; knowledge already acquired passes into consent and a new order of life.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FGS-B07","text":"Internal liberation orders profession, discipline, sacrament, and communion, whence point-like conversion is unfolded into an ecclesial process.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FGS-B08","text":"Providence assumes adverse events without confusion of intentions, while contemplation briefly opens the eternal end and sends one back to time.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FGS-B09","text":"Death and holiness dissolve every meritorious closure; narrative turns into mercy, sacrifice, and intercession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:D15","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AFM-B01","text":"Corporeal imagination → exclusion of dualism → incorporeal truth → evil as privation → insufficiency of knowledge → genealogy of habit → divided will → integrating grace → conversion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AF1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AFM-B02","text":"Point-like conversion → ordered renunciation → intellectual formation → baptism → ecclesial communion → narrated providence → brief contemplation → mourning → intercession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:AS4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:AFM-B03","text":"Externalization of fault → responsibility of the will → impossibility of autonomy → healing mediation → causality restored to God → eternal possession still deferred.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:D4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MME-01","text":"Evil is reclassified from the class of natures into a threefold structure: ontological privation, voluntary turning-away, and temporally sedimented inertia.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MME-02","text":"The subject is redescribed from a substance struggling against a substance into one historical, partial, culpable, and healable will.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MME-03","text":"Conversion is expanded from a change of opinion into integration of the will and a process of sacramental, affective, and social formation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:AS2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MME-04","text":"Knowledge is divided into demonstration of the object, capacity for adhesion, and stability of fruition; philosophy loses the sufficiency of the first order.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME6","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MME-05","text":"Time changes from a neutral receptacle into a moral machine: act sediments, delay increases bondage, the decisive moment compresses, while formation unfolds the effects.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME7","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MME-06","text":"Scripture is reclassified from a deposit of propositions into an event of address, whose force arises from time, reception, and the preparation of the subject.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MME-07","text":"The Church becomes an apparatus distributing knowledge, affect, confession, sacrament, common resistance, and the memory of the dead.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MME-08","text":"Providence distinguishes moral causality from the causality of events, such that good can result from evil without the conversion of evil intention into good.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MME-09","text":"Death and holy life are reordered: death becomes temporal separation within resurrection, while holiness becomes matter for thanksgiving and intercession, not a title of debt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B01","text":"The surface level joins the dissolution of errors concerning evil, the crisis of conversion, renunciation, baptism, the Ostian contemplation, Monica's death, and prayer for her.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:ALT1","CH_5P0L_LIBO:ALT1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B02","text":"The structural level composes participation in being, will, habit, grace, providence, and ecclesial mediations into a single machine of temporal formation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:ALT2","CH_5P0L_LIBO:ALT2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B03","text":"The metastrategic level transfers interpretation from the question of the object to the question of capacity and makes example, confession, and intercession modes of intervention.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:ALT3","CH_5P0L_LIBO:ALT3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B04","text":"The ontological and temporal level distinguishes reality between mutable creatures and eternal Wisdom, while the subject is bound, healed, and directed toward eschatological presence through succession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:ALT4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B05","text":"The methodological and performative level employs confession itself as a redistribution of causality: narrative renders good to God, fault to the will, and inserts the reader into imitation and prayer.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FL-01","text":"Grace provides the principle of liberation and the will truly consents, but the manner in which divine action effects consent without compulsion remains formally indeterminate.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FL-02","text":"Conversion as an integral act and as a multilayered process cohere only if the threshold of the will is distinguished from the further transformation of intellect and affect.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FL-03","text":"Ecclesial mediations are necessary, but the immediacy of Wisdom is desired as their end; the relation between present necessity and the future overcoming of signs remains a locus of tension.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FL-04","text":"Baptismal remission and subsequent fault are simultaneously affirmed, but the boundary between regeneration, residuals of habit, and new fault is not perfectly explained.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FL-05","text":"Providence produces good from evil intention, but the mode of concurrence by which effect is distributed to God and fault to the agent is affirmed rather than exhaustively analyzed.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FL-06","text":"Conversion requires public confession, while Augustine's renunciation refuses a spectacle of greatness; necessary visibility remains to be distinguished from boastfulness.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FL-07","text":"Faith excludes the despair of mourning, not pain itself; the distinction between carnal habit and rightly ordered tears remains mobile.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:NX11","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:FL-08","text":"God is affirmed as invariable, while joy concerning conversion is varied in affective discourse; the relation between divine immutability and variation of joy in creatures remains compressed.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MP-01","text":"Evil changes meaning when it is transferred from substance to privation, from that to turning-away of the will, and thence to temporal habit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:AS2","CH_5P0L_LI_4:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MP-02","text":"Truth changes from a demonstrable object into a norm that judges the capacity of the contemplator and demands liberation toward a new order of life.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:ME6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MP-03","text":"The will passes from a plurality of partial desires to integral willing; at this point deliberation ceases and action begins.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MP-04","text":"Scripture changes function when it is received from a general proposition into a temporal and personal address.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:ME6","CH_5P0L_LIBO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MP-05","text":"Conversion changes from crisis closure into the beginning of formation; what ends the will opens the sacramental and affective process.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MP-06","text":"The familial bond is transferred from bodily possession to liturgical memory and the hope of resurrection, without abolition of the pain of separation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly an ordered field around an immutable source, in which defect can wound order but cannot produce a contrary nature.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:SD5","CH_5P0L_LI_4:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:HSI-02","text":"The subject is a diachronic node of wills, habits, and relations: it binds itself through repetition, is loosed by another principle, and receives a new order through healed consent.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:HSI-03","text":"Time is at once sediment, threshold, and pilgrimage: the past forms habit, the present compresses decision, while the future defers eternal possession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD6","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:HSI-04","text":"The Church is a network of mediations that distributes truth through text, voice, water, chant, example, and memory, and forms individual subjects into communion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:HSI-05","text":"Navigation is spiral: the mind ascends, returns, suffers habit, is again raised through grace, and from individual returns increases its desire for stable presence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:HSI-06","text":"Death is a threshold that breaks bodily communion but does not destroy relation; it transforms affect into mourning, mourning into prayer, and memory into hope of resurrection.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBN:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBN:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B01","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to restore the movement from the correction of the ontology of evil through the healing of the will to ecclesial incorporation, death, and intercession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT1","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B02","text":"The system coheres at this level because it combines the goodness of the creature, responsibility of the will, the necessity of grace, and the enduring rationale of mercy without dualism.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT3","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B03","text":"The strongest structure is the conjunction between the genealogy of habit and the redistribution of causality, by which fault is attributed to the will, liberation and good to God.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT2","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B04","text":"Less determined remains the efficacy by which grace produces an integral will without compulsion; the narrative shows the effect, but does not formalize the causal nexus.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT4","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B05","text":"Universal order and providence are firmly posited, but the congruity of all particulars and the manner in which good is elicited from evil are not universally demonstrated.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B06","text":"Certain joints rely on the authority of narrative, the analogy of conversions, the testimony of signs, and eschatological faith rather than on complete internal deduction.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B07","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement: it excludes false exteriorities, locates defect within the temporal will, effects liberation through mediation, and opens closure into mercy.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_4:MRT9","CH_5P0L_LIBO:MRT10","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B08","text":"The density of affects, the temporality of address, and the singularity of mourning resist axiomatic reduction, because these are not accidental examples but the media through which the system effects its doctrine.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBO:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBN:D14","CH_5P0L_LIBN:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_5P0L_03@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_5P0L_03:v1","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"Chapters 07–09"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Confessiones","title":"Chapters 07–09","context":"Book VII. · Book VIII. · Book IX.","original_title":"Chapters 07–09","original_context":"Liber Septimus. · Liber Octavus. · Liber Nonus."},"original_title":"Chapters 07–09","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 10–11","order":4,"parents":["CH_5P0L_LIBD","CH_5P0L_LIBU"],"revision":"CL_5P0L_04@R001","sha256":"7e32cb58e367b3f78c9226893fb2697e122913cd66b0ac1e42798f48b3a633bd","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BAS-01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo subiectum, sibi opacum et successione distractum, intra cognitionem Dei omniscientis veritatem de se, mundo et tempore recipere possit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BAS-02","text":"Introspectio non autonomiam constituit, sed dependentiam epistemicam, ontologicam et soteriologicam a veritate immutabili detegit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BAS-03","text":"Argumentatio confessionem, exclusionem apophaticam, analysim experientiae et reconstructionem metaphysicam coniungit, ut errores voluntatis et errores grammaticae sub eadem disciplina veritatis corrigantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS8","CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BAS-04","text":"Motus a signis exterioribus in memoriam et operationes animi descendit, sed interioritatem transcendit versus veritatem, aeternitatem et unitatem divinam.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BAS-05","text":"Progressio est recursiva et spiralis: confessio atque analysis solvunt falsas clausuras, sed singulae solutiones novam opacitatem et ulteriorem conversionem aperiunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BAS-06","text":"Dispersio moraliter ut cupiditas et temporaliter ut distentio apparet; utraque attentionem a fine uno in multa obiecta vel momenta distribuit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BAS-07","text":"Introspectio distantiam inter creaturam mutabilem et Deum immutabilem detegit, sed sola mediatio Christi eam in viam reconciliationis et collectionis convertit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BAS-08","text":"Clausura definitiva differtur: subiectum manet inter sanationem incohatam, cognitionem non exhaustam, praesentem distentionem et pacem futuram.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD8","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Veritas divina immutabilis et aeternitas tota praesens mensuram praebent qua mens mutabilis, voluntas divisa et successio creata iudicantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Creatura, quia mutabilis et facta, nec causa sui nec principium sufficiens cognitionis, ordinis aut collectionis suae est.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Confessio Deo scientiam non addit, sed confitentem et audientem intra ordinem veritatis, illuminationis et affectus recti constituit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Memoria ex campo imaginum, notionum et agnitionis in operationem praesentem convertitur, qua praeteritum absentem vitam temporalem adhuc format.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Interiorem sequi non est in mente claudi: interioritas est limes ubi signa creata, vestigia temporalia et iudicium veritatis supra subiectum concurrunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Proximitas animi sibi ipsi nec plenam sui comprehensionem nec integrum sui praesentem efficit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Dispersio est una structura moraliter et temporaliter expressa: amor in multa dividitur sicut vita inter memoriam, attentionem et exspectationem distenditur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Attentio transit a facultate praesentem successionem metiente ad locum strategicum ubi amor aut finem ordinat aut a bono creato captivatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBD:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] Res creatae, corpus, motus et tempus bona dependentia sunt; error incipit cum medium in finem, signum in rem ultimam aut creaturam in principium autonomum mutatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-10","text":"[Persistent] Gratia et illuminatio actionem creatam non annihilant, sed facultatem cognoscendi, resistendi et ordinandi praebent quam subiectum sibi dare nequit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Unitas ad Deum est attractor communis continentiae et intentionis: amores dispersi atque tempora animi non delentur, sed ad unum finem colliguntur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Christus mediator coniungit mortalitatem cum iustitia atque vitam distentam ad Deum dirigit, sine confusione distantiae Creatoris et creaturae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-13","text":"[Emergent] Eadem forma transitionis per gradus recurrit: pars in totum transit, praesentia in vestigium, appetitus in consuetudinem, actus in vitam.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-14","text":"[Terminal] Cognitio fidelis non comprehensione exhaustiva clauditur, sed confessione limitis, petitione illuminationis et spe consummationis nondum praesentis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD7","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-01","text":"Confessio identitatem functionalem retinet: in utroque campo informatio Dei excluditur, dum actus confitentis ad veritatem et affectum rectum convertitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-02","text":"Memoria mutatur ab amplitudine contentorum interiorum in praesentem operationem temporalem; functio agnitionis persistit, sed eius obiectum fit vestigium rei absentis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-03","text":"Veritas interior identitatem stabilem servat, sed a mensura amoris et beatitudinis ad criterium exegeseos, causalitatis et sermonis de tempore extenditur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-04","text":"Dispersio migrat ex campo cupiditatis in structuram temporis: quod prius divisio amoris erat, fit divisio praesentiae inter multa tempora animi.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-05","text":"Continentia functionem mutat in intentionem: privatio voluptatis iam recusata in recollectionem amorum, deinde in collectionem vitae temporalis convertitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D13","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-06","text":"Mediator ab agente reconciliationis ad principium directionis temporalis amplificatur; mortalitas eius ad creaturam distentam pertinet, iustitia ad finem immutabilem.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-07","text":"Praesens mutatur a statu morali examinando in operationem quae memoriam et exspectationem coniungit; examinatio conscientiae fit examinatio ipsius praesentiae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-08","text":"Veritas beatitudinem definiens in Verbum creatorium absorbetur: finis desiderii et principium essendi non confunduntur, sed eadem stabilitate divina ordinantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-09","text":"Creaturae a signis Conditoris in universum ordinem temporalem migrant; significatio earum nunc etiam dependentiam causalitatis, loci et temporis ostendit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-10","text":"Applicatio anti-Donatistica munere locali peracto evanescit: regulam contra iudicium cordis confirmat, sed structuram creationis et temporis non gubernat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D17","CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:CGD-01","text":"Taxonomia imaginum, affectionum et disciplinarum memoriae localis manet; ad gradum praesentem ascendit sola functio memoriae ut retentio, agnitio et relatio ad absentiam.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:CGD-02","text":"Triplex cupiditas, localiter per genera tentationis ordinata, sursum amplificatur in legem generalem captationis attentionis atque dispersionis vitae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D10","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:CGD-03","text":"Aporiae de longitudine praesentis et motu corporali localiter tempus examinant; praesentis gradus conclusio est nullam praesentiam creatam integre possideri.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX8","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:CGD-04","text":"Enumeratio angelorum, daemonum et artium falsarum localis est; ad gradum praesentem ascendit exclusio omnis mediationis quae distantiam sine coniunctione mortalitatis et iustitiae superare praetendit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX14","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:CGD-05","text":"Analysis beatitudinis non manet argumentum separatum, sed attractorem collectionis definit: gaudium verum est finis ad quem attentio et vita distenta ordinantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:CGD-06","text":"Refutatio circuituum caelestium ut essentiae temporis localis manet; effectus superior est demotio omnis creaturae visibilis a munere mensurae ultimae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX9","CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:CGD-07","text":"Polemica adversus iudicium ad hominem structuram confessionis illustrat, sed novo campo temporis non integratur atque ideo praemissa generatrix gregis non fit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D17","CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:CGD-08","text":"Creatio ex nihilo argumentum localiter cosmologicum est, sed sursum transit in principium universale dependentiae, quod etiam cognitionem et facultatem moralem ordinat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:D3","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:CGD-09","text":"Auditores caritate coniuncti et lectores affectu excitati duas figuras locales praebent; gradus praesens eas coniungit in communitatem cui confessio cognitionem performative ordinat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GNX-01","text":"Confessio neque informatio Dei neque narratio externa est; eius veritas in conversione affectus et subiecti consistit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GNX-02","text":"Subiectum nec sibi plene transparens nec sibi integraliter praesens est; introspectio igitur iudicium ultimum sui praebere non potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GNX-03","text":"Deus non continetur memoria sicut obiectum locale, nec tempus continet Deum sicut receptaculum universale.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GNX-04","text":"Sensus, sonus exterior et auctoritas locutoris veritatem ultimam non constituunt; omnia iudicio veritatis interioris subiciuntur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GNX-05","text":"Corpus et creaturae non sunt per se mala, sed neque principia coaeterna aut fines ultimi; malum ex inordinatione dependentiae oritur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GNX-06","text":"Tempus neque motus corporis neque series rerum in regionibus praeteriti et futuri reposita est.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GNX-07","text":"Nec oboedientia autonoma nec superioritas spiritualis reconciliationem efficit; utraque gratiam et structuram verae mediationis praeterit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX6","CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GNX-08","text":"Vita praesens neque perfectionem stabilem neque praesens sine transitu admittit; omnis clausura intra statum mortalem revocatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:DBN-01","text":"Ut systema constet, falsum esse debet subiectum sui causam, mensuram, medicum et iudicem sufficientem esse.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse debet veritatem immutabilem ex consensu, affectu vel operatione mentis mutabilis produci.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse debet tempus esse campum neutralem et independentem in quo Deus, mundus et anima eodem modo collocentur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse debet pluralitatem bonorum vel momentorum per se ordinem efficere; sine fine uno multiplicitas in dispersionem transit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse debet desiderium veri aut familiaritatem vocabuli sufficere ad cognitionem rectam; voluntas et ratio illuminatione atque correctione egent.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:DBN-06","text":"Falsum esse debet praesentiam rei apud animum possessionem rei vel transparantiam animi efficere; mensuratio et agnitio per vestigia operantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:DBN-07","text":"Falsum esse debet transitum a mutabilitate ad immutabilitatem ex sola introspectione vel analysi temporis deduci posse; utrumque mediatorem theologice requirit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSA-01","text":"Possibilitas maxime indisponibilis est praesens creatum quod se totum possideat: vita semper iam memoratur, adhuc exspectatur aut attentione transit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX3","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSA-02","text":"Systema circum absentiam originis propriae ordinatur: subiectum neque esse, veritatem, bonum neque perseverantiam ex se producit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSA-03","text":"Omne alterum coaeternum Deo excluditur; neque materia, tempus, locus, memoria neque mens potest intervallum independentem praebere.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSA-04","text":"Comprehensio positiva plena animae, temporis et aeternitatis inadmissibilis manet; cognitio vera potest limitem constituere quem transcendere non potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSA-05","text":"Salus ut fuga autonoma ex corpore, successione aut relatione sociali impossibilis est; navigatio manet intra mortalitatem, gratiam et mediationem.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSA-06","text":"Absentia ordinans est pax plena nondum possessa: eam confessio, continentia, intentio et mediatio appetunt sine praesentem statum pro consummatione sumendo.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD8","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-01","text":"Confessio est operatio epistemico-affectiva quae opacitatem subiecti et ignorantiam temporis sub iudicio veritatis ponit, non simplex relatio factorum.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-03","CL_5P0L_04:GA-14","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-02","text":"Memoria identitatem personalem non ut archivum clausum sed ut retentionem praesentem constituit, qua agnitio et temporalitas eodem vestigio operantur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-04","CL_5P0L_04:GA-05","CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX3","CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-03","text":"Cupiditas est distentio moraliter qualificata: multa non tantum successionem vitae componunt, sed attentionem a fine uno captivam faciunt.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-07","CL_5P0L_04:GA-08","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-04","text":"Continentia est forma temporalis intentionis, quia amores colligere idem fit ac exspectationem, attentionem et memoriam ad unum finem ordinare.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-07","CL_5P0L_04:GA-11","CH_5P0L_LIBD:D13","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-05","text":"Veritas interior simul errores amoris et errores interpretationis corrigit; ideo epistemologia et disciplina voluntatis structuram iudicii communem habent.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-01","CL_5P0L_04:GA-10","CH_5P0L_LIBD:D9","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-06","text":"Bonum creatum et tempus creatum eadem lege dependentiae reguntur: neutrum malum est, sed utrumque falsum principium fit si a causa et fine separatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-02","CL_5P0L_04:GA-09","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-07","text":"Interioritas tensionem constitutivam gerit: ibi veritas certissime iudicat, quamvis animus qui iudicatur neque se totum comprehendat neque sibi totus praesens sit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-05","CL_5P0L_04:GA-06","CH_5P0L_LIBD:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-08","text":"Mediatio Christi non solum culpam reconciliat, sed mortalitatem temporalem ad iustitiam et praesentiam divinam dirigit, sine successionis abolitione immediata.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-12","CL_5P0L_04:GA-14","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-09","text":"Forma minima transitionis per totum systema replicatur: quod futurum est per attentionem transit, quod appetitur per usum transit, et uterque transitus memoriam vel consuetudinem format.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-08","CL_5P0L_04:GA-13","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBD:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-10","text":"Ignorantia virium moralium et aporia temporis eandem disciplinam exigunt: simulatio certitudinis excluditur, dum actio sub illuminatione et misericordia continuatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-10","CL_5P0L_04:GA-14","CH_5P0L_LIBD:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSD-01","text":"Subiectum non est punctum simplex conscientiae, sed nexus appetitus, memoriae, attentionis et exspectationis, quem veritas transcendens iudicat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSD-02","text":"Tempus fit medium ethicum, quia qualitas vitae pendet non solum ab obiectis electis, sed a modo quo attentio inter praesentia, vestigia et fines distribuitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSD-03","text":"Sanatio est reconfiguratio temporalis voluntatis: gratia non praeteritum delet aut successionem sistit, sed memoriam, usum praesentem et exspectationem ad unum ordinat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSD-04","text":"Confessio praesentem statum contra duas falsas temporalitates tuetur: defensionem per praeteritum meritum et praesumptionem futurae perseverantiae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSD-05","text":"Creatio et gratia analogam, non identicam, asymmetriam exhibent: sicut creatura esse sibi non dat, ita voluntas dispersa collectionem sibi sufficienter non confert.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSD-06","text":"Mediatio distantiam Creatoris et creaturae non aufert, sed eam in relationem traversabilem mutat, quia idem mediator mortalitatem participat et ad iustitiam immutabilem refert.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSD-07","text":"Certitudo veritatis et provisionalitas sui-examinis simul constant: mens certum principium iudicii recipit, sed applicationem eius ad motiva et durationes imperfecte metitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D3","CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSD-08","text":"Historia personalis et historia creata eadem forma transitus leguntur: exspectata per praesentem actionem in memoriam transeunt, dum finis aeternus successionem sine successione ordinat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:D11","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RLE-01","text":"Opacitas sui confessionem generat; confessio illuminationem petit; illuminatio subtiliorem opacitatem detegit; nova cognitio igitur ad confessionem redit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RLE-02","text":"Bonum creatum attentionem allicit; attentio finem ei concedit; finis falsus animam dispergit; dispersio infirmitatem manifestat; infirmitas misericordiam petit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D10","CH_5P0L_LIBD:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RLE-03","text":"Exspectatio per attentionem in memoriam transit; multiplicatio transituum distentionem vitae producit; distentio desiderium collectionis auget.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RLE-04","text":"Gratia resistendi facultatem dat; resistentia vulnus residuum manifestat; vulnus petitionem renovat; petitio dependentiam a gratia confirmat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD6","CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RLE-05","text":"Sonus exterior ad iudicium interius remittitur; iudicium Verbum aeternum quaerit; Verbum rursus sonum Scripturae interpretandum restituit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RLE-06","text":"Quaestio agnitionem praesupponit, agnitio memoriam, memoria vestigium, vestigium rem absentem; quaerere igitur praesentiam per absentiam recursive operatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RLE-07","text":"Attractor totius gregis est unum immutabile, ad quod amores per continentiam et tempora animi per intentionem colliguntur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RLE-08","text":"Superbia circuitum fugae impedit: subiectum etiam de negatione laudis gloriatur atque mediatorem secundum propriam excellentiam fingit, separationem sic reproducens.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D15","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FGS-B01","text":"Creatura mutabilis + veritas immutabilis → differentia ontologica quae introspectionem, confessionem et analysim temporis necessarias facit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FGS-B02","text":"Signum exterior → iudicium interior → exclusio falsae ontologiae → agnitio principii transcendentis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FGS-B03","text":"Memoria + exspectatio + attentio → praesentia vestigiorum → identitas temporalis sine possessione plena sui.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FGS-B04","text":"Bonum creatum + attentio inordinata → mutatio medii in finem → cupiditas → dispersio moraliter et temporaliter amplificata.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D10","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FGS-B05","text":"Dispersio + opacitas → confessio limitis → petitio illuminationis et misericordiae → facultas partialis correctionis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FGS-B06","text":"Gratia + attentio rectificata → continentia/intentione → recollectio plurium sub fine uno → renovata probatio per successionem.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D13","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FGS-B07","text":"Distantia irreducibilis + mediator mortalis et iustus → reconciliatio sine confusione → sanatio incohata → consummatio extra clausuram praesentis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:AFM-B01","text":"Omniscientia divina → inutilitas informationis → confessio performativa → interioritatis exploratio → memoria et vestigia → opacitas sui → analysis praesentiae → distentio temporalis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:AFM-B02","text":"Distentio → captatio attentionis a bonis creatis → triplex cupiditas → confessio infirmitatis → gratia et illuminatio → continentia sive intentio → collectio ad unum.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D13","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:AFM-B03","text":"Distinctio Creatoris et creaturae → exclusio autocausationis et temporis coaeterni → impossibilitas ascensus autonomi → mediatio Christi → sanatio temporalis → pax futura sine clausura exhaustiva.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MME-01","text":"Interiority ex spatio autonomiae in locum relationis reclassificatur, ubi subiectum a veritate quam non producit iudicatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MME-02","text":"Memoria ex receptaculo contentorum in infrastructuram agnitionis, identitatis et temporalitatis mutatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MME-03","text":"Tempus ex receptaculo cosmico in distributionem praesentium operationum animi transfertur, sine reductione ad fictionem privatam.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MME-04","text":"Peccatum ex proprietate rei sensibilis in modum captationis attentionis reclassificatur, quo usus, cognitio vel societas finem usurpat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX10","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MME-05","text":"Continentia ex suppressione voluptatis in artem collectionis amorum et temporum sub uno fine convertitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D13","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MME-06","text":"Confessio ex relatione praeteritorum in methodum cognitionis praesentis mutatur, quae affectum, lecturam et iudicium intentionum simul exercet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MME-07","text":"Mediatio ex scala superioritatis spiritualis in structuram coniunctionis reconstituitur, quae mortalitatem, iustitiam et directionem ad aeternitatem complectitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME8","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MME-08","text":"Distinctio Creatoris et creaturae agrum integrum reordinat: eadem asymmetria esse, causalitatem, cognitionem, voluntatem et tempus permeat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:ALT-B01","text":"Gradus superficiei confessionem praesentis status, memoriam, tentationes, creationem et naturam temporis tamquam quaestiones expressas proponit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:ALT1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:ALT-B02","text":"Gradus structuralis memoriam, attentionem, exspectationem, appetitum et gratiam tamquam distributiones quibus subiectum dispergitur aut colligitur coordinat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:ALT2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:ALT-B03","text":"Gradus metastrategicus quaestiones non intra praesuppositiones adversas solvit, sed curiositatem, autonomiam et tempus praevium tamquam falsas constitutiones quaestionis destruit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:ALT-B04","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis realitatem creatam ut dependentiam mutabilem, subiectum ut distentionem praesentium operationum et Deum ut praesentiam sine successione constituit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:ALT4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:ALT-B05","text":"Gradus methodologicus et performativus ipsam formam confessionis efficacem facit: reditus, aporiae et negationes lectorem ab informatione ad illuminationem atque ab dispersione ad intentionem transferunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FL-01","text":"Deus in memoria agnoscitur, sed memoria eum localiter non continet; relatio inter notitiam retentam et praesentiam transcendentem manet structuraliter ambigua.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FL-02","text":"Veritas interior certitudinem praebet, quamvis animus interior sibi opacus maneat; systema criterium certum cum applicatione fallibili componere debet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FL-03","text":"Incertum manet utrum tempus sit ipsa affectio animi an res distincta quae tantum per affectionem praesentem mensuratur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FL-04","text":"Praesens omni spatio carens cum attentione perdurante componitur, sed modus quo attentio transitionem sustineat sine extensione praesentis non absolvitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FL-05","text":"Gratia omne bonum facultatis tribuit, dum subiectum responsabilitatem resistendi vel cedendi retinet; modus cooperationis non formaliter determinatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD6","CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FL-06","text":"Analysis distentionis collectionem desiderabilem reddit, sed necessitatem mediatoris ex sola phaenomenologia temporis non demonstrat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT8","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MP-01","text":"Punctum mutationis memoriae occurrit cum contenta interiora in operationem praesentem retinentem res absentes convertuntur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MP-02","text":"Punctum mutationis dispersionis occurrit cum triplex cupiditas desinit esse sola divisio moralium obiectarum et fit forma temporalis vitae in multa.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MP-03","text":"Punctum mutationis attentionis occurrit cum functio mensurationis temporalis in intentionem normativam ad Deum convertitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MP-04","text":"Punctum mutationis mediationis occurrit cum reconciliatio peccatoris etiam collectionem vitae temporalis ad aeternum finem sustinere incipit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:HSI-01","text":"Realitas implicite est machina dependentiarum mutabilium circa centrum immutabile, non planum entium sibi aequaliter praesentium.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD2","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum est nodus appetitus, memoriae, attentionis et exspectationis, cuius unitas effecta potius quam naturaliter possessa est.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:HSI-03","text":"Tempus est fluvius non exterior, sed translatio continua qua exspectatum per attentionem in memoratum transit et praesentiam in vestigium mutat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:HSI-04","text":"Certamen principale est distributio attentionis inter multa bona captantia et unum finem ordinantem; cupiditas et distentio sunt duae imagines eiusdem discerptionis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:HSI-05","text":"Navigatio possibilis procedit per confessionem, illuminationem, gratiam et mediatorem; fuga ex condicione creata substituitur directione eius ad Deum.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata praesentia sufficiunt ad restituendam structuram communem confessionis, interioritatis, memoriae, dispersionis, temporis, gratiae et mediationis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima est coniunctio opacitatis sui cum confessione, mutabilitatis cum dependentia et dispersionis cum collectione gratiae sustentata.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B03","text":"Nondum satis determinatur quomodo prima cognitio Dei in memoria adsit neque quomodo tempus ad affectionem animi ontologice referatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT3","CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B04","text":"Cooperatio inter gratiam et voluntatem manet insufficiens ad formulam reducta, quamvis dependentia doni et responsabilitas subiecti simul necessariae sint.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B05","text":"Clausura christologica cohaeret cum condicionibus mediationis, sed ex analysi memoriae et temporis sola non sequitur atque praemissis revelatis nititur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT9","CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B06","text":"Cohaerentia gregis ordine lineari minus quam forma recursiva nititur: transitus localis in memoriam, consuetudinem vel vestigium per gradus maiores replicatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B07","text":"Reductioni axiomaticae resistunt paradoxum oblivionis et productio successionis ex causa non successiva; utraque limitem explicationis positivae servat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B08","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat si confessionem, exclusionem, recursionem et mediationem tamquam operationes generatrices retinet, non tamquam argumenta iuxta posita.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT10","CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T142535022977Z_50ec2705","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 10–11","source_sha256":"7e32cb58e367b3f78c9226893fb2697e122913cd66b0ac1e42798f48b3a633bd","sha256":"07a12093e82baabbb11a7edd83d3c265d77a07b0c1d3b2de7b6fa04eca962b68","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:25:35.024725+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BAS-01","text":"The system asks how a subject, opaque to itself and dispersed by succession, can receive within the knowledge of an omniscient God truth about itself, the world, and time.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BAS-02","text":"Introspection establishes not autonomy, but uncovers epistemic, ontological, and soteriological dependence upon immutable truth.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BAS-03","text":"The argumentation joins confession, apophatic exclusion, analysis of experience, and metaphysical reconstruction, so that errors of will and errors of grammar may be corrected under the same discipline of truth.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS8","CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BAS-04","text":"The movement descends from external signs into memory and the operations of the mind, but transcends interiority toward divine truth, eternity, and unity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BAS-05","text":"The progression is recursive and spiral: confession and analysis dissolve false closures, but each solution opens a new opacity and a further conversion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BAS-06","text":"Dispersion appears morally as cupidity and temporally as distention; both distribute attention from one end among many objects or moments.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BAS-07","text":"Introspection uncovers the distance between mutable creature and immutable God, but only Christ's mediation transforms it into a path of reconciliation and gathering.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BAS-08","text":"Definitive closure is deferred: the subject remains between begun healing, unexhausted knowledge, present distention, and future peace.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD8","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Immutable divine truth and eternity wholly present provide the measure by which mutable mind, divided will, and created succession are judged.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The creature, because mutable and made, is neither the cause of itself nor a sufficient principle of its own knowledge, order, or gathering.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Confession adds no knowledge to God, but places the confessor and hearer within the order of truth, illumination, and right affection.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Memory is transformed from a field of images, notions, and recognition into a present operation by which the past continues to shape absent temporal life.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] To follow the inner is not to be shut up in the mind: interiority is the boundary where created signs, temporal traces, and the judgment of truth above the subject converge.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] The mind's proximity to itself produces neither full comprehension of itself nor its complete presence to itself.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Dispersion is one structure expressed morally and temporally: love is divided among many things just as life is distended among memory, attention, and expectation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Attention passes from a faculty measuring present succession to the strategic place where love either orders an end or is captivated by a created good.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBD:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] Created things, body, motion, and time are dependent goods; error begins when a means is transformed into an end, a sign into the ultimate thing, or a creature into an autonomous principle.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-10","text":"[Persistent] Grace and illumination do not annihilate created action, but provide a capacity for knowing, resisting, and ordering which the subject cannot give itself.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Unity toward God is the common attractor of continence and intention: dispersed loves and the times of the mind are not erased, but gathered toward one end.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Christ the mediator joins mortality with justice and directs distended life toward God, without confusing the distance between Creator and creature.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-13","text":"[Emergent] The same form of transition recurs through degrees: part passes into whole, presence into trace, appetite into habit, act into life.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GA-14","text":"[Terminal] Faithful knowledge is not closed by exhaustive comprehension, but by confession of limit, petition for illumination, and hope for a consummation not yet present.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD7","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-01","text":"Confession retains its functional identity: in both fields information about God is excluded, while the act of the confessor is turned toward truth and right affection.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-02","text":"Memory is transformed from an amplitude of inner contents into a present temporal operation; the function of recognition persists, but its object becomes the trace of an absent thing.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-03","text":"Inner truth maintains a stable identity, but is extended from a measure of love and blessedness to a criterion of exegesis, causality, and discourse about time.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-04","text":"Dispersion migrates from the field of cupidity into the structure of time: what was formerly a division of love becomes a division of presence among the many times of the mind.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-05","text":"Continence changes function into intention: the previously rejected privation of pleasure is transformed into recollection of loves, then into the gathering of temporal life.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D13","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-06","text":"The mediator is enlarged from an agent of reconciliation into a principle of temporal direction; his mortality pertains to the distended creature, justice to the immutable end.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-07","text":"The present is transformed from a moral state to be examined into an operation joining memory and expectation; examination of conscience becomes examination of presence itself.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-08","text":"Truth defining blessedness is absorbed into the creative Word: the end of desire and the principle of being are not confused, but are ordered by the same divine stability.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A10","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-09","text":"Creatures migrate from signs of the Creator into the universal temporal order; their significance now also shows the dependence of causality, place, and time.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RMD-10","text":"The anti-Donatist application vanishes once its local role has been performed: it confirms the rule against judgment of the heart, but does not govern the structure of creation and time.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D17","CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:CGD-01","text":"The taxonomy of images, affections, and disciplines of local memory remains; only the function of memory as retention, recognition, and relation to absence rises to the present level.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:CGD-02","text":"The triple cupidity, locally ordered through kinds of temptation, is amplified upward into a general law of the capture of attention and the dispersion of life.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D10","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:CGD-03","text":"Aporias concerning the length of the present and bodily motion examine time locally; the conclusion of the present level is that no created presence is possessed integrally.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX8","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:CGD-04","text":"The enumeration of angels, demons, and false arts is local; what rises to the present level is the exclusion of every mediation claiming to overcome distance without the conjunction of mortality and justice.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX14","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:CGD-05","text":"The analysis of blessedness does not remain a separate argument, but defines the attractor of gathering: true joy is the end toward which attention and distended life are ordered.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD3","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:CGD-06","text":"The refutation of celestial circuits as the essence of time remains local; the higher effect is the demotion of every visible creature from the role of ultimate measure.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX9","CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:CGD-07","text":"The polemic against judgment of a person illustrates the structure of confession, but is not integrated into the new field of time and therefore does not become a generative premise of the cluster.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D17","CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:CGD-08","text":"Creation from nothing is locally a cosmological argument, but passes upward into a universal principle of dependence, which also orders knowledge and moral capacity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:D3","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:CGD-09","text":"Hearers joined by charity and readers stirred by affection furnish two local figures; the present level joins them in a community for which confession performatively orders knowledge.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A3","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GNX-01","text":"Confession is neither information about God nor an external narrative; its truth consists in the conversion of affection and subject.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GNX-02","text":"The subject is neither fully transparent to itself nor integrally present to itself; introspection therefore cannot provide its final judgment of itself.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GNX-03","text":"God is not contained in memory like a local object, nor does time contain God like a universal receptacle.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GNX-04","text":"Sense, external sound, and the authority of the speaker do not establish ultimate truth; all are subjected to the judgment of inner truth.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GNX-05","text":"Body and creatures are not evil in themselves, but neither are they coeternal principles or ultimate ends; evil arises from the disordering of dependence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GNX-06","text":"Time is neither the motion of a body nor a series of things stored in the regions of past and future.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A11","CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GNX-07","text":"Neither autonomous obedience nor spiritual superiority produces reconciliation; both bypass grace and the structure of true mediation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX6","CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:GNX-08","text":"Present life admits neither stable perfection nor a present without passage; every closure within the mortal state is revoked.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:DBN-01","text":"For the system to stand, it must be false that the subject is its own sufficient cause, measure, physician, and judge.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that immutable truth is produced from the consensus, affection, or operation of mutable mind.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that time is a neutral and independent field in which God, world, and soul are situated in the same manner.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that a plurality of goods or moments produces order in itself; without one end, multiplicity passes into dispersion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:DBN-05","text":"It must be false that desire for truth or familiarity with a word suffices for right knowledge; will and reason need illumination and correction.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:DBN-06","text":"It must be false that the presence of a thing to the mind produces possession of the thing or transparency of mind; measurement and recognition operate through traces.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:DBN-07","text":"It must be false that passage from mutability to immutability can be deduced from introspection or analysis of time alone; both theologically require a mediator.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSA-01","text":"The most unavailable possibility is a created present that possesses itself whole: life is always already remembered, still expected, or passes through attention.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX3","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSA-02","text":"The system is ordered around the absence of its own origin: the subject produces neither being, truth, good, nor perseverance from itself.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSA-03","text":"Every other thing coeternal with God is excluded; neither matter, time, place, memory, nor mind can furnish an independent interval.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSA-04","text":"Full positive comprehension of soul, time, and eternity remains inadmissible; true knowledge can establish a limit which it cannot transcend.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSA-05","text":"Salvation as an autonomous escape from body, succession, or social relation is impossible; navigation remains within mortality, grace, and mediation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSA-06","text":"The ordering absence is full peace not yet possessed: confession, continence, intention, and mediation seek it without taking the present state for consummation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD8","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-01","text":"Confession is an epistemic-affective operation that places the opacity of the subject and ignorance of time under the judgment of truth, not a simple report of facts.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-03","CL_5P0L_04:GA-14","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-02","text":"Memory constitutes personal identity not as a closed archive but as present retention, through which recognition and temporality operate by the same trace.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-04","CL_5P0L_04:GA-05","CH_5P0L_LIBD:DNX3","CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-03","text":"Cupidity is morally qualified distention: the many do not merely compose the succession of life, but make attention captive away from the one end.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-07","CL_5P0L_04:GA-08","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-04","text":"Continence is a temporal form of intention, because gathering loves is the same as ordering expectation, attention, and memory toward one end.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-07","CL_5P0L_04:GA-11","CH_5P0L_LIBD:D13","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-05","text":"Inner truth simultaneously corrects errors of love and errors of interpretation; therefore epistemology and discipline of the will have a common structure of judgment.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-01","CL_5P0L_04:GA-10","CH_5P0L_LIBD:D9","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-06","text":"Created good and created time are governed by the same law of dependence: neither is evil, but each becomes a false principle if separated from cause and end.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-02","CL_5P0L_04:GA-09","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-07","text":"Interiority bears a constitutive tension: there truth judges most certainly, although the mind that is judged neither comprehends itself wholly nor is wholly present to itself.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-05","CL_5P0L_04:GA-06","CH_5P0L_LIBD:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-08","text":"Christ's mediation not only reconciles guilt, but directs temporal mortality toward justice and divine presence, without immediate abolition of succession.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-12","CL_5P0L_04:GA-14","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-09","text":"The minimal form of transition is replicated throughout the whole system: what is future passes through attention, what is desired passes through use, and each transition forms memory or habit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-08","CL_5P0L_04:GA-13","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBD:D10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:XD-10","text":"Ignorance of moral powers and the aporia of time demand the same discipline: the simulation of certainty is excluded, while action continues under illumination and mercy.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-10","CL_5P0L_04:GA-14","CH_5P0L_LIBD:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSD-01","text":"The subject is not a simple point of consciousness, but a nexus of appetite, memory, attention, and expectation, judged by transcendent truth.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSD-02","text":"Time becomes an ethical medium, because the quality of life depends not only on chosen objects, but on the manner in which attention is distributed among presences, traces, and ends.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSD-03","text":"Healing is a temporal reconfiguration of the will: grace does not erase the past or stop succession, but orders memory, present use, and expectation toward one.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSD-04","text":"Confession protects the present state against two false temporalities: self-defense through past merit and presumption of future perseverance.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX13","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSD-05","text":"Creation and grace exhibit an analogous, not identical, asymmetry: just as the creature does not give being to itself, so the dispersed will does not sufficiently confer gathering upon itself.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSD-06","text":"Mediation does not remove the distance between Creator and creature, but transforms it into a traversable relation, because the same mediator participates in mortality and refers it to immutable justice.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A18","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSD-07","text":"Certainty of truth and the provisionality of self-examination coexist: the mind receives a certain principle of judgment, but measures its application to motives and durations imperfectly.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D3","CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:BSD-08","text":"Personal history and created history are read in the same form of transition: what is expected passes through present action into memory, while the eternal end orders succession without succession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:D11","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RLE-01","text":"Opacity of self generates confession; confession seeks illumination; illumination uncovers a subtler opacity; new knowledge therefore returns to confession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RLE-02","text":"Created good attracts attention; attention grants it the status of end; the false end disperses the soul; dispersion manifests weakness; weakness seeks mercy.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D10","CH_5P0L_LIBD:D12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RLE-03","text":"Expectation passes through attention into memory; multiplication of transitions produces the distention of life; distention increases the desire for gathering.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RLE-04","text":"Grace gives the capacity to resist; resistance manifests the remaining wound; the wound renews petition; petition confirms dependence upon grace.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD6","CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RLE-05","text":"External sound is referred back to inner judgment; judgment seeks the eternal Word; the Word in turn restores the sound of Scripture to be interpreted.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:NX2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RLE-06","text":"Questioning presupposes recognition, recognition memory, memory a trace, a trace an absent thing; therefore seeking operates recursively through presence by absence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A8","CH_5P0L_LIBU:DNX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RLE-07","text":"The attractor of the whole cluster is the one immutable, toward which loves are gathered through continence and the times of the mind through intention.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A15","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:RLE-08","text":"Pride obstructs the circuit of escape: the subject glories even in the denial of praise and fashions the mediator according to its own excellence, thereby reproducing separation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D15","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SNX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FGS-B01","text":"Mutable creature + immutable truth → ontological difference that makes introspection, confession, and analysis of time necessary.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FGS-B02","text":"External sign → inner judgment → exclusion of false ontology → recognition of transcendent principle.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FGS-B03","text":"Memory + expectation + attention → presence of traces → temporal identity without full possession of self.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FGS-B04","text":"Created good + disordered attention → transformation of means into end → cupidity → dispersion amplified morally and temporally.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D10","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FGS-B05","text":"Dispersion + opacity → confession of limit → petition for illumination and mercy → partial capacity for correction.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D12","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FGS-B06","text":"Grace + rectified attention → continence/intention → recollection of the many under one end → renewed trial through succession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D13","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FGS-B07","text":"Irreducible distance + mortal and just mediator → reconciliation without confusion → begun healing → consummation beyond the closure of the present.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:AFM-B01","text":"Divine omniscience → uselessness of information → performative confession → exploration of interiority → memory and traces → opacity of self → analysis of the present → temporal distention.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:AS1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:AFM-B02","text":"Distention → capture of attention by created goods → triple cupidity → confession of weakness → grace and illumination → continence or intention → gathering toward one.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D13","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:AFM-B03","text":"Distinction between Creator and creature → exclusion of self-causation and coeternal time → impossibility of autonomous ascent → mediation of Christ → temporal healing → future peace without exhaustive closure.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SNX2","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MME-01","text":"Interiority is reclassified from a space of autonomy into a place of relation, where the subject is judged by a truth it does not produce.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MME-02","text":"Memory is transformed from a receptacle of contents into an infrastructure of recognition, identity, and temporality.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MME-03","text":"Time is transferred from a cosmic receptacle into the distribution of present operations of the mind, without reduction to a private fiction.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MME-04","text":"Sin is reclassified from a property of the sensible thing into a mode of capturing attention, by which use, knowledge, or society usurps the status of end.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX10","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MME-05","text":"Continence is transformed from suppression of pleasure into an art of gathering loves and times under one end.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D13","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MME-06","text":"Confession is transformed from a report of past things into a method of present knowledge, which simultaneously exercises affection, reading, and judgment of intentions.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MME-07","text":"Mediation is reconstituted from a scale of spiritual superiority into a structure of conjunction, encompassing mortality, justice, and direction toward eternity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:ME8","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MME-08","text":"The distinction between Creator and creature reorders the entire field: the same asymmetry permeates being, causality, knowledge, will, and time.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:ALT-B01","text":"The surface level presents confession of the present state, memory, temptations, creation, and the nature of time as explicit questions.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:ALT1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:ALT-B02","text":"The structural level coordinates memory, attention, expectation, appetite, and grace as distributions through which the subject is dispersed or gathered.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:ALT2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:ALT-B03","text":"The metastrategic level solves questions not within opposing presuppositions, but by destroying curiosity, autonomy, and prior time as false constructions of the question.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:ALT-B04","text":"The ontological and temporal level establishes created reality as mutable dependence, the subject as distention of present operations, and God as presence without succession.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:ALT4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:ALT-B05","text":"The methodological and performative level renders the very form of confession effective: returns, aporias, and negations transfer the reader from information to illumination and from dispersion to intention.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:AS4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FL-01","text":"God is recognized in memory, but memory does not contain him locally; the relation between retained knowledge and transcendent presence remains structurally ambiguous.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D7","CH_5P0L_LIBD:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FL-02","text":"Inner truth provides certainty, although the inner mind remains opaque to itself; the system must reconcile a certain criterion with fallible application.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:D6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FL-03","text":"It remains uncertain whether time is the very affection of the mind or a distinct thing measured only through present affection.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FL-04","text":"The present lacking all extension is reconciled with enduring attention, but the manner in which attention sustains transition without extension of the present is not resolved.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FL-05","text":"Grace grants every good of capacity, while the subject retains responsibility for resisting or yielding; the mode of cooperation is not formally determined.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD6","CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:FL-06","text":"The analysis of distention renders gathering desirable, but does not demonstrate the necessity of a mediator from the phenomenology of time alone.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT8","CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MP-01","text":"The mutation point of memory occurs when inner contents are transformed into a present operation retaining absent things.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A6","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MP-02","text":"The mutation point of dispersion occurs when triple cupidity ceases to be merely a division of moral objects and becomes the temporal form of life among many things.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MP-03","text":"The mutation point of attention occurs when the function of temporal measurement is transformed into normative intention toward God.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBU:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MP-04","text":"The mutation point of mediation occurs when reconciliation of the sinner also begins to sustain the gathering of temporal life toward the eternal end.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:A17","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly a machine of mutable dependencies around an immutable center, not a plane of beings equally present to themselves.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD2","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:HSI-02","text":"The subject is a node of appetite, memory, attention, and expectation, whose unity is effected rather than naturally possessed.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A12","CH_5P0L_LIBD:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:HSI-03","text":"Time is a river not external, but a continuous translation through which what is expected passes through attention into what is remembered and transforms presence into trace.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBU:A14","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:HSI-04","text":"The principal conflict is the distribution of attention between many captivating goods and one ordering end; cupidity and distention are two images of the same tearing apart.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:HSI-05","text":"Possible navigation proceeds through confession, illumination, grace, and the mediator; escape from the created condition is replaced by its direction toward God.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:SD5","CH_5P0L_LIBU:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B01","text":"The present axioms suffice to restore the common structure of confession, interiority, memory, dispersion, time, grace, and mediation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT1","CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B02","text":"The firmest structure is the conjunction of opacity of self with confession, mutability with dependence, and dispersion with gathering sustained by grace.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT2","CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B03","text":"It is not yet sufficiently determined how the first knowledge of God is present in memory, nor how time is ontologically related to affection of the mind.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT3","CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B04","text":"Cooperation between grace and will remains reduced to an insufficient formula, although dependence upon gift and responsibility of the subject are simultaneously necessary.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B05","text":"The Christological closure coheres with the conditions of mediation, but does not follow from analysis of memory and time alone and rests upon revealed premises.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT9","CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B06","text":"The coherence of the cluster rests less on linear order than on recursive form: local transition into memory, habit, or trace is replicated through larger degrees.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:FGS7","CH_5P0L_LIBU:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B07","text":"The paradox of forgetting and the production of succession from a non-successive cause resist axiomatic reduction; both preserve the limit of positive explanation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT4","CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B08","text":"Reconstruction preserves the true movement if it retains confession, exclusion, recursion, and mediation as generative operations, not as juxtaposed arguments.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LIBD:MRT10","CH_5P0L_LIBU:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_5P0L_04@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_5P0L_04:v1","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"Chapters 10–11"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Confessiones","title":"Chapters 10–11","context":"Book X. · Book XI.","original_title":"Chapters 10–11","original_context":"Liber Decimus. · Liber Undecimus."},"original_title":"Chapters 10–11","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 12–13","order":5,"parents":["CH_5P0L_LI_5","CH_5P0L_LDT0"],"revision":"CL_5P0L_05@R001","sha256":"840b41ceb602a1cfb5b55541ce005e4c2ff86195d3be02e9197f3e335f070405","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BAS-01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo dependentia creationis ante omnem successionem in historiam formationis temporalis, ecclesialis et hermeneuticae transeat atque in requiem aeternam terminetur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BAS-02","text":"Omne esse, formari, illuminari, intelligere, bene operari et quiescere fit distributio unius donationis divinae, cui grammatica creationis per diversos ordines creaturae recurrit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BAS-03","text":"Argumentatio est reconstructio transversalis quae metaphysicam creationis, disciplinam interpretationis, formationem Ecclesiae et consummationem coniungit sine horum graduum aequatione.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BAS-04","text":"Motus ab origine ontologica non chronologica per formationem et tempus ad ordinem dierum ecclesialiter recodificatum procedit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BAS-05","text":"Multiplicitas rerum et multiplicitas sensuum eandem structuram participant: unitas fontis diversitatem ordinatam generat, veritate exclusiones eius circumscribente.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BAS-06","text":"Motus verus est recursivus et spiralis, quia narratio creationis regulam formationis Ecclesiae gignit, dum Ecclesia finem latentem ordinis creati retrospecte manifestat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BAS-07","text":"Caritas axem communem constituit quo interpretatio ad veritatem ordinatur et creatura rationalis ad locum quietis suae fertur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A17","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BAS-08","text":"Clausura systematis non est exhaustio sensuum, sed sabbatum sine vespera, ubi opera temporalia cessant sine reditu ad novum cyclum mutabilitatis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SNX4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Deus aeternus, incommutabilis et sibi sufficiens neque creatione augetur neque temporalibus actibus perficitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Omnis creatura ex nihilo procedit, nulla substantia divina, materia coaeterna aut natura hostili tamquam principio secundo admissa.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Esse creatum a forma, sapientia et beatitudine distinguitur; ideo omnis creatura mutabilis est et ulterioris formationis capax.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Informitas a capacitate ontologica prope nihil ad statum spiritualem aversionis, obscuritatis et formationis nondum completae extenditur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Tempus non creationem continet, sed ex mutationibus ordinatis et ex modo temporali quo creatura formam recipit emergit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A8","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-06","text":"[Attractor] Creatura rationalis stabilitatem participat non per immutabilitatem propriam, sed per inhaesionem continuatam et satiationem in Deo.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Verbum increatum est principium creationis et vocatio formativa qua creatura dispersa ad unitatem revocatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Spiritus a plenitudine intentionis divinae in Scriptura ad donum cognitionis, caritatis et elevationis creaturae explicatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A18","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] Caritas simul est norma interpretationis, pondus motus spiritualis et principium quietis in bono proprio creaturae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A17","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-10","text":"[Persistent] Unitas fontis potest multiplicitatem veram rerum, enuntiationum et intellectuum generare sine divisione veritatis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Scriptura est medium temporale et humile Verbi aeterni quod auctoritatem stabilem cum accommodatione multiplici coniungit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A14","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-12","text":"[Mutating] Pluralitas sensuum transit a concordia interpretum ad oeconomiam ecclesialem quae media et intellectus secundum diversas capacitates distribuit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-13","text":"[Terminal] Fides, signa et opera temporalia ad statum transeuntem pertinent cui sabbatum aeternum sine vespera terminum imponit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A18","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-14","text":"[Emergent] Divina causalitas operationem creaturae participative constituit, ita ut Deus in creatura agat neque actum creatum simpliciter supprimat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-15","text":"[Attractor] Bonitas singulorum ad bonitatem ordinatam totius et inde ad fruitionem Dei colligitur, non ad autosufficientiam universi.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RMD-01","text":"Creatio ex nihilo identitatem stabilem retinet et tam cosmologiam quam refutationem dualismi regit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RMD-02","text":"Informitas functionem mutat: primo capacitatem formarum designat, deinde modum aversionis et dependentiae spiritualis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RMD-03","text":"Lux ab effectu formationis ontologicae ad conversionem ecclesialem migrat, obscuritate residua statum nondum consummatum indicante.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:D1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RMD-04","text":"Tempus ab effectu mutationis ad modum receptionis et institutionis creaturae amplificatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RMD-05","text":"Inhaesio intellectualis in caritatem gravitantem mutatur: stabilitas super vicissitudinem fit motus recte directus ad requiem.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:D5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RMD-06","text":"Pluralitas sensuum retinet veritatem multiplicem, sed ex concordia defensiva in fecunditatem activam sub auctoritate Scripturae extenditur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RMD-07","text":"Intentio conscia ministri humani in ampliorem operationem Spiritus absorbetur, qui in creatura cognoscit et loquitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:D13","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RMD-08","text":"Ordo dierum a structura originis non chronologica in figuram formationis Ecclesiae transfertur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RMD-09","text":"Duplex carentia temporis transformationem terminalem patitur: plenitudo per inhaesionem in sabbatum sine vespera colligitur, defectus formae in initium formationis transit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:CGD-01","text":"Status metaphysicus materiae informis manet quaestio localis, dum gradu praesenti capacitas nondum formata fit conditio generalis omnis formationis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:CGD-02","text":"Correspondentiae singulorum dierum cum ministeriis manent locales; distributio mediorum secundum capacitatem sola ad structuram gregis ascendit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:CGD-03","text":"Prioritas originis sine intervallo temporali e quaestione de materia amplificatur in regulam generalem causalitatis divinae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:D6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:CGD-04","text":"Distinctio inter veritatem rei et intentionem humanam cum multiplici intelligibilitate enuntiationis pontem inter ontologiam et hermeneuticam constituit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A16","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:CGD-05","text":"Recapitulatio ecclesialis grammaticae creationis est emergentia propria huius gradus, non simplex allegoriarum localium aggregatio.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:CGD-06","text":"Limites particularis iudicii spiritualis in axiomate superiore auctoritatem participatam, corrigibilem et Scripturae subiectam constituunt.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A16","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:CGD-07","text":"Tenebrae cosmologicae ut privatio formae opere structuraliter peracto non evanescunt, sed in obscuritatem aversionis et conversionis nondum plenae recodificantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GNX-01","text":"Systema excludit Deum temporaliter deliberantem, nova voluntate motum, indigentem aut post laborem quiescentem.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX10","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GNX-02","text":"Creatio neque emanatio substantiae divinae neque ordinatio materiae aut naturae hostilis coaeternae est.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GNX-03","text":"Malum et informitas principia positiva Deo adversa esse non possunt, sed privationem et aversionem boni creati significant.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GNX-04","text":"Tempus non est receptaculum in quo Deus, informitas et creatura formata aequaliter locentur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GNX-05","text":"Nulla creatura se ipsam efficere, illuminare, satiare aut bono creato tamquam fine ultimo compleri potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GNX-06","text":"Pluralitas hermeneutica neque univocitatem exclusivam neque licentiam sensuum falsorum vel indiscriminatorum admittit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GNX-07","text":"Iudicium spirituale non potest auctoritatem Scripturae, occulta hominum aut destinum exteriorum sibi subicere.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX12","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GNX-08","text":"Nulla fruitio temporalium neque perpetuatio operum praesentium consummationem creaturae constituit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:DBN-01","text":"Aequatio essendi cum forma actuali falsa esse debet, alioquin neque materia informis neque vita nondum sapiens cogitari posset.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:DBN-02","text":"Omnis mutabilitas possibilis in mutationem actualem converti non potest, quia inhaesio impedit lapsum sine naturae creatae abolitione.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX2","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:DBN-03","text":"Differentia a Deo non potest rivalitatem substantialem efficere; alioquin malum et materia in principia ontologica independentia converterentur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:DBN-04","text":"Causalitas divina et actio humana relatione aemula contineri non possunt, quia gratia operationem participative constituit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:DBN-05","text":"Significatio divina non potest ambitu intentionis consciae ministri humani terminari.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:DBN-06","text":"Mediatio per verba, signa, fidem et gradus capacitatis non est merus defectus tollendus, sed modus ordinarius formationis temporalis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A14","CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:DBN-07","text":"Successio narrationis non potest successionem cognitionis aut voluntatis divinae probare, quamvis relationem actus aeterni ad effectus temporales systema non absolvat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX10","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSA-01","text":"Origo ante tempus nullo schemate successionis repraesentari potest, sicut requies ultima nullo die posteriori clauditur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SNX3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSA-02","text":"Nullus locus ontologicus extra causalitatem creatoris relinquitur ex quo res aut malum independentem originem accipiant.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX1","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSA-03","text":"Informitas pura cogitationi imaginativae indisponibilis manet et tantum per subtractionem formarum attingitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSA-04","text":"Prospectus qui omnem sensum Scripturae aut cognitionem Dei exhauriat creaturae praecluditur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SNX4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSA-05","text":"Orientatio affectiva neutralis indisponibilis est, quia omnis amor aut ad fontem convertit aut ad inferiora deicit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSA-06","text":"Consummatio quae in novum cyclum laboris, vesperae et mutabilitatis redeat ontologice inadmissibilis est.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:XD-01","text":"Capacitas materiae ad formas et capacitas verborum ad plures intellectus structuram homologam constituunt: unitas receptiva diversitatem ordinatam sustinet sine indeterminatione absoluta.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:GA-03","CL_5P0L_05:GA-10","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:XD-02","text":"Tempus inter duos limites non temporales tenditur: originem quae successionem antecedit et requiem terminalem cui nulla vespera succedit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:GA-05","CL_5P0L_05:GA-13","CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:XD-03","text":"Stabilitas creaturae rationalis non est immobilitas absoluta, sed directio continenter renovata qua mutabilitas ad inhaesionem et requiem ordinatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:GA-06","CL_5P0L_05:GA-09","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:XD-04","text":"Caritas idem principium in duobus campis exercet: motum creaturae ad Deum dirigit et pluralitatem interpretum ad veritatem communem ordinat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:GA-09","CL_5P0L_05:GA-10","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A17","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:XD-05","text":"Incertitudo de intentione Moysi in cognitionem participativam transfertur: plenitudo Spiritus non statum mentalem auctoris replicat, sed veritatem in creatura operatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:GA-08","CL_5P0L_05:GA-14","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A18","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:XD-06","text":"Sicut differentia creaturae a Deo substantiam adversam non gignit, ita multiplicitas intellectuum errorem necessario non gignit; utrumque ordine positivo continetur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:GA-02","CL_5P0L_05:GA-10","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:XD-07","text":"Historia temporalis est apparatus formationis cui propria obsolescentia inscribitur, quia mutationes opera producunt quae in requiem transire debent.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:GA-05","CL_5P0L_05:GA-13","CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:XD-08","text":"Scriptura ut firmamentum stabilitatem supra ministros servat, sed eadem stabilitas accommodationem et pluralitatem sensuum generat potius quam interpretationem unicam immobilit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:GA-11","CL_5P0L_05:GA-12","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:XD-09","text":"Bonitas totius non simplicitate vacua, sed compositione ordinata plurium rerum, facultatum et intellectuum efficitur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:GA-10","CL_5P0L_05:GA-15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A9","CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSD-01","text":"Realitas creata est participatio dependens: accipit esse, formam et stabilitatem sine conversione in substantiam divinam.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:D5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSD-02","text":"Tempus est index interior formationis creaturae et medium historiae salutis, non mensura actus creatoris; eius finis est propria transcensio in requiem.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSD-03","text":"Actio finita non est regio causaliter relicta a Deo, sed effectus in quo causalitas divina voluntatem et operationem creatam participative producit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSD-04","text":"Cognitio vera est communis et participata, sed semper signis, fide, auctoritate et gradu capacitatis mediatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX8","CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSD-05","text":"Auctoritas ecclesialis distribuitur secundum capacitatem et corrigibilitatem; maturitas auget iudicium sine productione autonomiae a Scriptura.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSD-06","text":"Allegoria legitima non naturas delet, sed grammaticam creationis in formationem ecclesialem transfert servata distinctione graduum.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSD-07","text":"Subiectum non est centrum sibi sufficiens, sed capacitas mutabilis cuius status ab orientatione amoris et a gratia formante constituitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSD-08","text":"Visio bonitatis consummatur cum bonum singulare ad auctorem et ad ordinem totius refertur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RLE-01","text":"Bonitas desiderium inspirat, desiderium invocationem parit, invocatio conversionem aperit, conversio ampliorem receptionem eiusdem gratiae efficit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:D1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RLE-02","text":"Vita illuminabilis lucem recipit, lux visum bonitatis producit, visus bonum ad auctorem refert et relatio ulteriorem conformitatem generat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:D4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RLE-03","text":"Verbum unum plures sensus candidatos generat, veritas falsos excludit, caritas veros componit, compositio fecunditatem textus iterum auget.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RLE-04","text":"Genesis Ecclesiam figurat, Ecclesia ordinem Geneseos in se recapitulat, et haec recapitulatio creationem ut historiam sanctificationis denuo legibilem facit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RLE-05","text":"Via amplificationis a conversione initiali per signa, disciplinam et exempla ad iudicium renovatae mentis ascendit, auctoritate Scripturae permanente.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RLE-06","text":"Amor est attractor dynamicus: cupiditas inferiora repetit et inquietudinem auget, caritas ad Deum elevat et requiem appropinquat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RLE-07","text":"Requies sine vespera est attractor terminalis qui totam seriem operum ordinat neque in aliam vicissitudinem reingreditur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RLE-08","text":"Exclusio autonomiae recurrit ad singulos gradus, quia neque initium, formatio, illuminatio neque consummatio merito antecedente aut virtute propria producitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FGS-B01","text":"Deus sibi sufficiens + nulla materia coaeterna → donatio gratuita essendi → dependentia universalis creati.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FGS-B02","text":"Capacitas informis → vocatio Verbi → conversio ad unitatem → forma, lumen et conformitas sine aequalitate.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FGS-B03","text":"Forma recepta → mutationes ordinatae → tempus → historia graduum formationis secundum capacitatem.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A8","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FGS-B04","text":"Verbum aeternum per verba temporalia → sensus veri multiplices → examen veritatis → exclusio falsi → concordia caritatis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FGS-B05","text":"Ordo creationis lectus → translatio ecclesialis → distributio signorum, ministeriorum et intellectuum → renovatio iudicii.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FGS-B06","text":"Spiritus ut donum → caritas ut pondus → operatio divina participata → motus creaturae ad locum quietis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FGS-B07","text":"Opera temporalia ordinata → bonitas totius → transitus operum → sabbatum sine vespera.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:AFM-B01","text":"Deus incommutabilis → creatio ex nihilo → informitas capax → formatio per Verbum → mutationes ordinatae → tempus creatum → quies non temporalis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A8","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:AFM-B02","text":"Sermo humilis → sensus veri multiplices → distinctio veritatis ab intentione humana → exclusio falsi → concordia caritatis → fecunditas sub auctoritate.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:AFM-B03","text":"Creatio recapitulate lecta → conversio ecclesialis → distributio mediorum secundum capacitatem → renovatio mentis → transitus operum → sabbatum aeternum.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MME-01","text":"Tempus ex continente universali in effectum mutationis et modum receptionis creaturae reclassificatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MME-02","text":"Carentia temporis duplicem tabulam aperit: stabilitatem per plenitudinem inhaesionis et terminum eschatologicum sine vespera.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MME-03","text":"Multiplicitas interpretativa ex ambiguitate suspecta in fecunditatem veram, ordinatam et auctoritate limitatam convertitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MME-04","text":"Oppositio boni et mali a conflictu substantiarum ad directiones conversionis et aversionis intra bonum creatum transfertur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME8","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MME-05","text":"Ecclesia fit non thema additum creationi, sed locus in quo grammatica creationis temporaliter recapitulari potest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MME-06","text":"Oppositio inter gratiam et actionem propriam reordinatur ut causalitas participativa, quamvis ratio responsabilitatis incompleta maneat.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MME-07","text":"Auctoritas canonica ex clausura semantica in firmamentum generativum mutatur quod ministros transcendit et intellectus multiplices sustinet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME8","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MME-08","text":"Bonitas universi non in perpetuitate operum, sed in ordine quo bona temporalia ad fruitionem Dei transeunt collocatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:ALT-B01","text":"In gradu superficiei vocabula caeli, terrae, tenebrarum, lucis, dierum et sabbati ut obiecta narrationis Geneseos interpretantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ALT1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:ALT-B02","text":"In gradu structurali capacitas, forma, mutatio, tempus, conversio, media institutionis et iudicium in unam machinam formationis connectuntur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ALT2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:ALT-B03","text":"In gradu metastrategico certamen de sensu mutatur in disciplinam pluralitatis verae, dum potestas ecclesialis intra auctoritatem et corrigibilitatem restringitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ALT3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:ALT-B04","text":"In gradu ontologico et temporali Deus aeternaliter causat, creatura temporaliter recipit et mutabilitas per conversionem ad requiem ordinatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ALT4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:ALT-B05","text":"In gradu methodologico et performativo textus eadem vocabula per campos metaphysicos, hermeneuticos et ecclesiales variat, atque sic fecunditatem quam affirmat actu efficit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FL-01","text":"Materia informis aliquid et tamen omni forma actuali carens dicitur; capacitas hanc medietatem sustinet, sed eius status ulterius non resolvitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FL-02","text":"Creatura intellectualis naturaliter mutabilis manet, quamvis inhaesio eius mutationem actualem impediat; nexus inter potentiam permanentem et immobilitatem participatam fragilis est.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX2","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FL-03","text":"Actus aeternus Dei successionem creatam producit sine successione divina, sed modus huius causalitatis non plene formalizatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FL-04","text":"Operatio divina voluntatem humanam constituit, dum responsabilitas actus proprii retinetur; articulatio utriusque causalitatis incompleta manet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT8","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FL-05","text":"Pluralitas sensuum verorum auctoritate, Spiritu et caritate circumscribitur, sed criterium compatibilitatis plurium sensuum non in regulam plenam convertitur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FL-06","text":"Allegoria naturas proprias servare profitetur, sed propositio creationem universaliter ad Ecclesiam ordinans latius patet quam demonstratio singularium correspondentiarum.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FL-07","text":"Intentio Moysi quaerenda manet, quamvis plenitudo Spiritus et possibilitas unius tantum sensus conscii eius necessitatem structuralem imminuant.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT5","CH_5P0L_LI_5:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FL-08","text":"Ambitus iudicii spiritualis exemplis et exclusionibus restringitur, sed regula generalis quae omnia iudicabilia definit non explicatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MP-01","text":"Informitas mutatur ex limite privativo cosmologico in statum conversionis, aversionis et dependentiae spiritualis.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MP-02","text":"Caritas mutatur ex norma finis hermeneutici in principium gravitatis ontologicae et motus creaturae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A17","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MP-03","text":"Tempus mutatur ex effectu mutationum formatarum in intervallum pedagogicum receptionis, fidei et operum transeuntium.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MP-04","text":"Spiritus mutatur ex amplitudine intentionis divinae in principium quo Deus in creatura cognoscit, amat et operatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A18","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MP-05","text":"Requies mutatur ex stabilitate creaturae inhaerentis in transformationem terminalem totius ordinis temporalium operum.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:HSI-01","text":"Realitas implicite est machina donationis et conversionis: esse effluit non ex indigentia, forma revocat dispersum, amor dirigit et requies colligit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum intra hanc machinam est capacitas mutabilis pondere amoris mota, non substantia sibi sufficiens aut centrum causalitatis clausum.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:HSI-03","text":"Tempus est vestigium motus formativi: cum formae variantur historia aperitur, cum opera in requiem transeunt eius functio terminatur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:HSI-04","text":"Scriptura est firmamentum et prisma: auctoritatem stabilem ministrat, sed unitatem suam in pluralitatem intellectuum verorum refringit.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:D9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:HSI-05","text":"Certamen fundamentale non est inter duas substantias, sed inter conversionem boni creati ad fontem et aversionem eius ad inferiora.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata praesentia sufficiunt ad restituendam seriem a creatione ex nihilo per formationem, interpretationem et Ecclesiam ad requiem aeternam.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima est oppositio inter Deum sibi sufficientem et creaturam cui esse, forma, lumen, actio et quies donantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MRT-B03","text":"Restitutio verum motum servat, quia transitum ab ontologia formae et temporis ad fecunditatem hermeneuticam, sanctificationem ecclesialem et consummationem retinet.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT8","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MRT-B04","text":"Status materiae informis et relatio actus aeterni ad successionem creatam nondum satis determinantur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MRT-B05","text":"Systema cohaeret per distinctiones originis a tempore, mutabilitatis a mutatione, unitatis a univocitate et causalitatis divinae ab autonomia creaturae.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MRT-B06","text":"Reductioni axiomaticae resistunt plena regula discernendi sensus multiplices et demonstratio exhaustiva translationis ab ordine creationis ad Ecclesiam; utraque auctoritate et analogia amplius quam formalizatione nititur.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T142626389556Z_43b75de3","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 12–13","source_sha256":"840b41ceb602a1cfb5b55541ce005e4c2ff86195d3be02e9197f3e335f070405","sha256":"4078d1cd326163e0b0d3aad5f075ceae3f2f617fd7827f28af53267a10425ae0","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:26:26.390502+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BAS-01","text":"The system asks how the dependence of creation prior to all succession passes into the history of temporal, ecclesial, and hermeneutical formation and culminates in eternal rest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BAS-02","text":"All being, formation, illumination, understanding, good action, and rest become the distribution of one divine gift, to which the grammar of creation recurs through diverse orders of creature.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BAS-03","text":"The argument is a transversal reconstruction that joins the metaphysics of creation, the discipline of interpretation, the formation of the Church, and consummation without equating these levels.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BAS-04","text":"The movement proceeds from an ontological, non-chronological origin through formation and time to an ecclesially recoded order of days.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BAS-05","text":"The multiplicity of things and the multiplicity of meanings share the same structure: unity of source generates ordered diversity, with truth circumscribing its exclusions.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BAS-06","text":"The movement is genuinely recursive and spiral, because the narrative of creation generates the rule of the Church's formation, while the Church retrospectively discloses the hidden end of the created order.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BAS-07","text":"Charity constitutes the common axis by which interpretation is ordered to truth and the rational creature is borne toward the place of its rest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A17","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BAS-08","text":"The system's closure is not an exhaustion of meanings, but a sabbath without evening, where temporal works cease without return to a new cycle of mutability.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SNX4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] The eternal, immutable, and self-sufficient God is neither increased by creation nor perfected by temporal acts.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Every creature proceeds from nothing, with no divine substance, coeternal matter, or hostile nature admitted as a second principle.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Created being is distinct from form, wisdom, and blessedness; therefore every creature is mutable and capable of further formation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Formlessness extends from an ontological capacity close to nothing to a spiritual state of aversion, darkness, and not-yet-completed formation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Time does not contain creation, but emerges from ordered changes and from the temporal mode by which the creature receives form.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A8","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-06","text":"[Attractor] The rational creature participates in stability not through an immutability of its own, but through continuous adherence to and satiation in God.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] The uncreated Word is the principle of creation and the formative call by which the dispersed creature is recalled to unity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] The Spirit is unfolded from the fullness of divine intention in Scripture into the gift of knowledge, charity, and the elevation of the creature.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A18","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] Charity is at once the norm of interpretation, the weight of spiritual motion, and the principle of rest in the creature's proper good.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A17","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-10","text":"[Persistent] Unity of source can generate a true multiplicity of things, propositions, and understandings without division of truth.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Scripture is the temporal and humble medium of the eternal Word, joining stable authority with manifold accommodation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A14","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-12","text":"[Mutating] The plurality of meanings passes from the concord of interpreters to an ecclesial economy that distributes means and understandings according to diverse capacities.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-13","text":"[Terminal] Faith, signs, and temporal works belong to a transitory state to which the eternal sabbath without evening imposes an end.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A18","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-14","text":"[Emergent] Divine causality participatively constitutes the creature's operation, so that God acts in the creature without simply suppressing the created act.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GA-15","text":"[Attractor] The goodness of individual things is joined to the ordered goodness of the whole and thence to the enjoyment of God, not to the self-sufficiency of the universe.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RMD-01","text":"Creation from nothing retains a stable identity and governs both cosmology and the refutation of dualism.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RMD-02","text":"Formlessness changes function: first it denotes the capacity for forms, then the mode of spiritual aversion and dependence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RMD-03","text":"Light migrates from the effect of ontological formation to ecclesial conversion, with residual darkness indicating a state not yet consummated.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:D1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RMD-04","text":"Time is expanded from an effect of change into a mode of the creature's reception and instruction.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RMD-05","text":"Intellectual adherence changes into gravitating charity: stability above vicissitude becomes motion rightly directed toward rest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:D5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RMD-06","text":"The plurality of meanings retains manifold truth, but extends from defensive concord into active fecundity under the authority of Scripture.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RMD-07","text":"The conscious intention of the human minister is absorbed into the broader operation of the Spirit, who knows and speaks in the creature.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:D13","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RMD-08","text":"The order of days is transferred from a structure of non-chronological origin into a figure of the Church's formation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RMD-09","text":"The twofold absence of time undergoes terminal transformation: fullness through adherence is gathered into the sabbath without evening, while lack of form passes into the beginning of formation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:CGD-01","text":"The metaphysical status of formless matter remains a local question, while at the present level not-yet-formed capacity becomes the general condition of all formation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:CGD-02","text":"Correspondences of individual days with ministries remain local; only the distribution of means according to capacity rises to the structure of the flock.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:CGD-03","text":"The priority of origin without temporal interval is expanded from a question about matter into a general rule of divine causality.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:D6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:CGD-04","text":"The distinction between the truth of the thing and human intention, together with the manifold intelligibility of an utterance, constitutes a bridge between ontology and hermeneutics.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A16","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:CGD-05","text":"The ecclesial recapitulation of the grammar of creation is an emergence proper to this level, not a mere aggregation of local allegories.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:CGD-06","text":"The limits of particular spiritual judgment establish, at the higher axiom, an authority that is participatory, corrigible, and subject to Scripture.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A16","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:CGD-07","text":"Cosmological darkness as privation of form does not vanish when its structural work is completed, but is recoded into the darkness of aversion and not-yet-full conversion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes a God who deliberates temporally, is moved by a new will, is needy, or rests after labor.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX10","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GNX-02","text":"Creation is neither an emanation of divine substance nor an ordering of coeternal matter or hostile nature.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GNX-03","text":"Evil and formlessness cannot be positive principles opposed to God, but signify privation and aversion from created good.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GNX-04","text":"Time is not a receptacle in which God, formlessness, and the formed creature are equally situated.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GNX-05","text":"No creature can make, illuminate, or satisfy itself, or be fulfilled in a created good as its ultimate end.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GNX-06","text":"Hermeneutical plurality admits neither exclusive univocity nor license for false or indiscriminate meanings.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:NX11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GNX-07","text":"Spiritual judgment cannot subject to itself the authority of Scripture, the hidden things of human beings, or the destiny of outsiders.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX12","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:GNX-08","text":"No enjoyment of temporal things or perpetuation of present works constitutes the creature's consummation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:DBN-01","text":"The equation of being with actual form must be false; otherwise neither formless matter nor life not yet wise could be conceived.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:DBN-02","text":"Every possible mutability cannot be converted into actual change, because adherence prevents falling without abolishing created nature.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX2","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:DBN-03","text":"Difference from God cannot produce substantial rivalry; otherwise evil and matter would be converted into independent ontological principles.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:DBN-04","text":"Divine causality and human action cannot be contained in a rival relation, because grace participatively constitutes operation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:DBN-05","text":"Divine signification cannot be delimited by the scope of the conscious intention of the human minister.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:DBN-06","text":"Mediation through words, signs, faith, and degrees of capacity is not a mere defect to be removed, but the ordinary mode of temporal formation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A14","CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:DBN-07","text":"The succession of narrative cannot prove a succession of divine knowledge or will, although the system does not resolve the relation of the eternal act to temporal effects.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX10","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSA-01","text":"Origin before time can be represented by no schema of succession, just as final rest is not closed by any later day.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SNX3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSA-02","text":"No ontological place outside the causality of the creator is left from which things or evil might receive an independent origin.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX1","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSA-03","text":"Pure formlessness remains unavailable to imaginative thought and is reached only through the subtraction of forms.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSA-04","text":"A perspective that would exhaust every meaning of Scripture or knowledge of God is precluded to the creature.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SNX4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSA-05","text":"A neutral affective orientation is unavailable, because every love either turns toward the source or casts down toward lower things.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSA-06","text":"A consummation that returns to a new cycle of labor, evening, and mutability is ontologically inadmissible.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:XD-01","text":"The capacity of matter for forms and the capacity of words for several understandings constitute a homologous structure: receptive unity sustains ordered diversity without absolute indetermination.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:GA-03","CL_5P0L_05:GA-10","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:XD-02","text":"Time is stretched between two non-temporal limits: an origin that precedes succession and a terminal rest to which no evening succeeds.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:GA-05","CL_5P0L_05:GA-13","CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:XD-03","text":"The stability of the rational creature is not absolute immobility, but a continuously renewed direction by which mutability is ordered toward adherence and rest.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:GA-06","CL_5P0L_05:GA-09","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:XD-04","text":"Charity exercises the same principle in two fields: it directs the creature's motion toward God and orders the plurality of interpreters toward common truth.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:GA-09","CL_5P0L_05:GA-10","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A17","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:XD-05","text":"Uncertainty concerning the intention of Moses is transferred into participatory knowledge: the fullness of the Spirit does not replicate the author's mental state, but works truth in the creature.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:GA-08","CL_5P0L_05:GA-14","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A18","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:XD-06","text":"Just as the creature's difference from God does not generate an opposing substance, so the multiplicity of understandings does not necessarily generate error; both are contained in a positive order.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:GA-02","CL_5P0L_05:GA-10","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:XD-07","text":"Temporal history is an apparatus of formation inscribed with its own obsolescence, because changes produce works that must pass into rest.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:GA-05","CL_5P0L_05:GA-13","CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:XD-08","text":"Scripture as firmament preserves stability above ministers, yet this same stability generates accommodation and plurality of meanings rather than immobilizing a single interpretation.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:GA-11","CL_5P0L_05:GA-12","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:XD-09","text":"The goodness of the whole is effected not by empty simplicity, but by the ordered composition of many things, faculties, and understandings.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:GA-10","CL_5P0L_05:GA-15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A9","CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSD-01","text":"Created reality is dependent participation: it receives being, form, and stability without conversion into divine substance.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:D5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSD-02","text":"Time is the inner index of the creature's formation and the medium of the history of salvation, not the measure of the creator's act; its end is its own transcendence into rest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSD-03","text":"Finite action is not a region causally abandoned by God, but an effect in which divine causality participatively produces created will and operation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSD-04","text":"True knowledge is common and participatory, but is always mediated by signs, faith, authority, and degree of capacity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX8","CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSD-05","text":"Ecclesial authority is distributed according to capacity and corrigibility; maturity increases judgment without producing autonomy from Scripture.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSD-06","text":"Legitimate allegory does not erase natures, but transfers the grammar of creation into ecclesial formation while preserving the distinction of levels.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSD-07","text":"The subject is not a self-sufficient center, but a mutable capacity whose state is constituted by the orientation of love and by forming grace.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:BSD-08","text":"The vision of goodness is consummated when a particular good is referred to its author and to the order of the whole.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RLE-01","text":"Goodness inspires desire, desire produces invocation, invocation opens conversion, and conversion effects a broader reception of the same grace.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:D1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RLE-02","text":"Illuminable life receives light, light produces the sight of goodness, sight refers the good to its author, and this relation generates further conformity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:D4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RLE-03","text":"One Word generates several candidate meanings, truth excludes the false, charity composes the true, and the composition again increases the fecundity of the text.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RLE-04","text":"Genesis figures the Church, the Church recapitulates in itself the order of Genesis, and this recapitulation makes creation newly legible as a history of sanctification.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RLE-05","text":"The path of amplification rises from initial conversion through signs, discipline, and examples to the judgment of the renewed mind, with the authority of Scripture remaining.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RLE-06","text":"Love is a dynamic attractor: cupiditas repeats lower things and increases restlessness, while charity elevates toward God and approaches rest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RLE-07","text":"Rest without evening is a terminal attractor that orders the entire series of works and does not re-enter another vicissitude.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:RLE-08","text":"The exclusion of autonomy recurs at every level, because neither beginning, formation, illumination, nor consummation is produced by antecedent merit or one's own power.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FGS-B01","text":"Self-sufficient God + no coeternal matter → gratuitous gift of being → universal dependence of the created.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A2","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FGS-B02","text":"Formless capacity → call of the Word → conversion to unity → form, light, and conformity without equality.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FGS-B03","text":"Received form → ordered changes → time → history of stages of formation according to capacity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A8","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FGS-B04","text":"Eternal Word through temporal words → manifold true meanings → examination of truth → exclusion of the false → concord of charity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A11","CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FGS-B05","text":"Order of creation read → ecclesial translation → distribution of signs, ministries, and understandings → renewal of judgment.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FGS-B06","text":"Spirit as gift → charity as weight → participatory divine operation → motion of the creature toward the place of rest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FGS-B07","text":"Ordered temporal works → goodness of the whole → passage of works → sabbath without evening.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:AFM-B01","text":"Immutable God → creation from nothing → capable formlessness → formation through the Word → ordered changes → created time → non-temporal rest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A6","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A8","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:AFM-B02","text":"Humble speech → manifold true meanings → distinction of truth from human intention → exclusion of the false → concord of charity → fecundity under authority.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A14","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A15","CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:AFM-B03","text":"Creation read recapitulatorily → ecclesial conversion → distribution of means according to capacity → renewal of mind → passage of works → eternal sabbath.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A15","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MME-01","text":"Time is reclassified from a universal container into an effect of change and a mode of the creature's reception.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MME-02","text":"The absence of time opens a twofold tableau: stability through the fullness of adherence and an eschatological end without evening.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MME-03","text":"Interpretative multiplicity is converted from suspect ambiguity into true, ordered fecundity limited by authority.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MME-04","text":"The opposition of good and evil is transferred from a conflict of substances to directions of conversion and aversion within created good.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME8","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MME-05","text":"The Church becomes not a theme added to creation, but the place in which the grammar of creation can be temporally recapitulated.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MME-06","text":"The opposition between grace and one's own action is reordered as participatory causality, although the account of responsibility remains incomplete.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MME-07","text":"Canonical authority changes from semantic closure into a generative firmament that transcends ministers and sustains manifold understandings.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME8","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MME-08","text":"The goodness of the universe is situated not in the perpetuity of works, but in the order by which temporal goods pass into the enjoyment of God.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:A9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, the terms heaven, earth, darkness, light, days, and sabbath are interpreted as objects of the Genesis narrative.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ALT1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, capacity, form, change, time, conversion, means of instruction, and judgment are connected into one machinery of formation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ALT2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, conflict over meaning changes into a discipline of true plurality, while ecclesial power is restricted within authority and corrigibility.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ALT3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, God causes eternally, the creature receives temporally, and mutability is ordered through conversion toward rest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ALT4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological and performative level, the text varies the same terms across metaphysical, hermeneutical, and ecclesial fields, and thus actually effects the fecundity that it affirms.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:AS3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FL-01","text":"Formless matter is said to be something and yet to lack every actual form; capacity sustains this middle position, but its status is not further resolved.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FL-02","text":"The intellectual creature remains naturally mutable, although adherence prevents its actual change; the connection between enduring potentiality and participated immobility is fragile.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:DNX2","CH_5P0L_LI_5:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FL-03","text":"God's eternal act produces created succession without divine succession, but the mode of this causality is not fully formalized.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT5","CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FL-04","text":"Divine operation constitutes human will while responsibility for one's own act is retained; the articulation of the two causalities remains incomplete.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT8","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FL-05","text":"The plurality of true meanings is circumscribed by authority, Spirit, and charity, but the criterion for compatibility among several meanings is not converted into a complete rule.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT6","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FL-06","text":"Allegory professes to preserve proper natures, but the proposition ordering creation universally to the Church extends more broadly than the demonstration of individual correspondences.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FL-07","text":"The intention of Moses remains to be sought, although the fullness of the Spirit and the possibility of only one conscious meaning diminish its structural necessity.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT5","CH_5P0L_LI_5:D13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:FL-08","text":"The scope of spiritual judgment is restricted by examples and exclusions, but the general rule defining all things subject to judgment is not explained.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MP-01","text":"Formlessness changes from a cosmological privative limit into a state of conversion, aversion, and spiritual dependence.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MP-02","text":"Charity changes from a norm of hermeneutical end into a principle of ontological gravity and creaturely motion.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A17","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MP-03","text":"Time changes from an effect of formed changes into a pedagogical interval of reception, faith, and transitory works.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:ME3","CH_5P0L_LDT0:ME9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MP-04","text":"The Spirit changes from the breadth of divine intention into the principle by which God knows, loves, and works in the creature.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A18","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MP-05","text":"Rest changes from the stability of the adhering creature into the terminal transformation of the whole order of temporal works.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A11","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly a machinery of gift and conversion: being flows forth not from need, form recalls what is dispersed, love directs, and rest gathers.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:AS2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:HSI-02","text":"The subject within this machinery is a mutable capacity moved by the weight of love, not a self-sufficient substance or a closed center of causality.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:A4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:HSI-03","text":"Time is the trace of formative motion: when forms vary, history opens; when works pass into rest, its function ends.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:SD1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:HSI-04","text":"Scripture is firmament and prism: it provides stable authority, but refracts its unity into a plurality of true understandings.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:D9","CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:HSI-05","text":"The fundamental conflict is not between two substances, but between the conversion of created good toward the source and its aversion toward lower things.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LDT0:SD2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MRT-B01","text":"The axioms presented suffice to restore the sequence from creation from nothing through formation, interpretation, and the Church to eternal rest.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT1","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MRT-B02","text":"The firmest structure is the opposition between the self-sufficient God and the creature to which being, form, light, action, and rest are given.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MRT-B03","text":"The reconstruction preserves the true movement, because it retains the transition from the ontology of form and time to hermeneutical fecundity, ecclesial sanctification, and consummation.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT8","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MRT-B04","text":"The status of formless matter and the relation of the eternal act to created succession are not yet sufficiently determined.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT4","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MRT-B05","text":"The system coheres through distinctions of origin from time, mutability from change, unity from univocity, and divine causality from creaturely autonomy.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT2","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_5P0L_05:MRT-B06","text":"The full rule for discerning manifold meanings and an exhaustive demonstration of the translation from the order of creation to the Church resist axiomatic reduction; both rely more on authority and analogy than on formalization.","refs":["CH_5P0L_LI_5:MRT7","CH_5P0L_LDT0:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_5P0L_05@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_5P0L_05:v1","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"Chapters 12–13"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · Confessiones","title":"Chapters 12–13","context":"Book XII. · Book XIII.","original_title":"Chapters 12–13","original_context":"Liber Duodecimus. · Liber Decimus Tertius."},"original_title":"Chapters 12–13","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01","layer":"MC","title":"5P0L L1 01","order":1,"parents":["CL_5P0L_01","CL_5P0L_02","CL_5P0L_03"],"revision":"MC_5P0L_L1_01@R001","sha256":"d23760c5fc0a354fa85ea1ddef272b47a4d263904e33266780a04a465b509b67","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BAS-01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo creatura a principio et fine suo alienata culpam affectivam, epistemicam atque voluntariam agnoscat et ad bonum immutabile convertatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BAS-01","CL_5P0L_03:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BAS-02","text":"Thesis globalis statuit omne esse creatum bonum esse, malum autem ex aversione voluntatis oriri atque per consuetudinem efficaciam temporalem sine substantia propria adipisci.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BAS-02","CL_5P0L_03:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BAS-03","text":"Argumentatio confessionem, analysim affectuum, refutationem ontologicam et historiam mediationum componit, ut exteriorizatio mali in genealogiam subiecti culpabilis sed sanabilis convertatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BAS-03","CL_5P0L_03:AS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BAS-04","text":"Motus chronologiam biographicam in recursionem aversionis transformat, cuius formae ab appetitu per errorem doctrinalem et servitutem voluntatis ad formationem ecclesialem mutantur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BAS-04","CL_5P0L_03:AS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BAS-05","text":"Correctio primum falsas certitudines et ontologias dissolvit, deinde ostendit doctrinam emendatam conversionem non efficere dum habitus volendi integer non est.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:AS-04","CL_5P0L_02:MP-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BAS-06","text":"Conversio emergit ut limen punctiforme quod deliberationem claudit, sed simul processum intellectualem, affectivum, sacramentalem et socialem aperit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:AS-B07","CL_5P0L_03:CGD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BAS-07","text":"Confessio doctrinam performative exercet, quia memoriam reordinat, causalitatem inter culpam et gratiam distribuit atque lectorem in imitationem et intercessionem inducit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSD-06","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BAS-08","text":"Clausura est aperta et attractiva: conversio stabilitur, sed plena fruitio Sapientiae differtur, dum mors, misericordia et intercessio omnem consummationem praesentem vetant.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BAS-08","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Deus est fons immutabilis omnis esse et boni; omnis natura creata bonitatem participat nec principium contrarium coordinatum admittit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-01","CL_5P0L_03:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-02","text":"[Attractor] Creatura ad quietem in bono incommutabili ordinatur, unde inquietudo, inquisitio et desiderium formam negativam termini divini gerunt.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-02","CL_5P0L_02:GA-08","CL_5P0L_03:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Bona creata et veritates locales bonitatem retinent, sed salutaria fiunt tantum cum usus, finis et receptio eorum recte ordinantur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-03","CL_5P0L_02:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Malum est privatio boni quae, quamvis essentia propria careat, per aversionem, repetitionem et habitum efficaciam temporalem acquirit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-05","CL_5P0L_03:XD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Una aversionis structura transit ab appetitu disperso ad imitationem libertatis, captationem intellectus, auctoritatem falsam et voluntatem consuetudine ligatam.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:XD-01","CL_5P0L_02:GA-03","CL_5P0L_03:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Subiectum est nodus diachronicus amoris, memoriae, societatis, habitus et actuum, non conscientia sui simpliciter praesens aut transparens.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSD-01","CL_5P0L_02:HSI-02","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Mediationes sociales, rhetoricae, scripturales, sacramentales et ecclesiales neque univoce corrumpunt neque autonome salvant, sed affectum, credibilitatem et receptionem distribuunt.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-09","CL_5P0L_02:GA-05","CL_5P0L_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Cognitio est moraliter et soteriologice ordinata: veritas ad sapientiam non transit nisi facultas cognoscens humilitate, fide et sanatione transformetur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-10","CL_5P0L_02:XD-03","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Tempus est operator moralis qui mutationes distribuit, obiecta dissolvit, habitus sedimentat, dilationem amplificat et curationem explicat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSD-02","CL_5P0L_02:BSD-02","CL_5P0L_03:RMD-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Gratia conversionem antecedit et voluntates partiales in consensum integrum perducit, voluntatem sanans sine eius actu consensuali abolendo.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-12","CL_5P0L_03:GA-07","CL_5P0L_03:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Conversio est limen decisivum intra processum longum: unum nunc divisionem voluntatis claudit, sed formationem plurium ordinum subiecti non consummat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:AS-B07","CL_5P0L_03:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-12","text":"[Emergent] Causalitas confessionalis asymmetrica est: voluntas defectum et culpam gerit, providentia autem bona servat, eventus ordinat et liberationem inchoat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSD-03","CL_5P0L_03:GA-11","CL_5P0L_03:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-13","text":"[Emergent] Confessio memoriam et narrationem in machinam conversionis mutat, quia identitatem restituit, causas redistribuit et lectorem intra eundem motum format.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-11","CL_5P0L_03:GA-12","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-14","text":"[Terminal] Sapientia stabiliter possessa intra vitam temporalem indisponibilis manet; ideo misericordia, sacrificium et intercessio ultimam potius quam meritoria clausuram constituunt.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:GA-15","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-04","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RMD-01","text":"Inquietudo ab indice dependentiae ontologicae in famem epistemicam, desiderium quietis et attractorem Sapientiae nondum possessae mutatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:RMD-01","CL_5P0L_02:RLE-07","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RMD-02","text":"Bonum creatum ab obiecto male usurpato in speciem boni imitabilem et deinde in medium sanationis transit; bonitas persistit, functio relatione mutatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:RMD-02","CL_5P0L_01:XD-03","CL_5P0L_03:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RMD-03","text":"Mediatio migrat a disciplina et consortio ad rhetoricam, magistrum, Scripturam et apparatus ecclesiales, servata potestate formandi receptionem.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:RMD-04","CL_5P0L_02:RMD-03","CL_5P0L_03:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RMD-04","text":"Auctoritas ex potentia sociali captante fit obiectum examinis, deinde mediatio medicinalis quae iudicium format potius quam suspendit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GA-09","CL_5P0L_02:XD-07","CL_5P0L_02:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RMD-05","text":"Dilatio invertitur secundum ordinem: baptismum differens licentiam aperit, doctrinam suspendens correctionem praeparat, conversionem procrastinans consuetudinem roborat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:RMD-07","CL_5P0L_02:RMD-04","CL_5P0L_03:GNX-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RMD-06","text":"Memoria ab reconstructione originum ad iudicium morale et tandem ad operationem performativam transit, qua casus, culpa et providentia reclassificantur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-11","CL_5P0L_02:RMD-05","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RMD-07","text":"Veritas ex obiecto quaesito fit iudicium impotentiae cognoscentis, norma formationis et attractor cui adhaesio stabilis adhuc deest.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:RMD-03","CL_5P0L_03:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RMD-08","text":"Conversio ex clausura biographica in principium formationis mutatur; baptismus eam ecclesialiter stabilit, sed misericordiae et transformationis ulterioris necessitatem non terminat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:AS-B07","CL_5P0L_03:CGD-08","CL_5P0L_03:MP-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:CGD-01","text":"Infantia, furtum, luctus, magistri, astrologia, conversiones exemplares et mors manent casus locales; praesentem gradum constituunt tantum ut mutationes aversionis, mediationis et reditus.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:CGD-01","CL_5P0L_02:CGD-01","CL_5P0L_03:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:CGD-02","text":"Correctiones anti-Manichaeae et exegeticae transcendent polemicam localem, quia constituunt transitum ab exteriorizatione mali ad discrimen inter cognitionem termini et viam sanantem.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:CGD-04","CL_5P0L_02:CGD-05","CL_5P0L_03:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:CGD-03","text":"Schola, sodalitas, multitudo et exemplum singulare amplificantur in unam theoriam receptionis socialiter distributae, qua laus, pudor et imitatio statum subiecti mutant.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:CGD-06","CL_5P0L_02:CGD-04","CL_5P0L_03:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:CGD-04","text":"Astrologia ut doctrina localis evanescit, sed eius functio persistit in omni conatu causalitatem confundendi et culpam ad necessitatem externam transferendi.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:RMD-08","CL_5P0L_03:RMD-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:CGD-05","text":"Ascensus interiores non manent episodicae contemplationes, sed coniunctim distinguunt cognitionem veri, incapacitatem adhaesionis et brevem anticipationem possessionis eschatologicae.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:CGD-06","CL_5P0L_03:XD-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:CGD-06","text":"Baptismus, vita Monicae et mors eius amplificant conversionem ultra actum singularem in regenerationem, disciplinam affectuum, memoriam liturgicam et intercessionem.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:CGD-05","CL_5P0L_03:CGD-08","CL_5P0L_03:MME-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GNX-01","text":"Nulla exterioritas ontologica datur in qua creatura, materia vel malum extra dependentiam a Deo subsistere possit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSA-01","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GNX-02","text":"Malum neque substantia creata neque materia increata neque principium Deo coordinatum est.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GNX-03","CL_5P0L_03:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GNX-03","text":"Nullum bonum finitum per se damnatur, sed nulla creatura mutabilis terminum stabilem desiderii praebere potest.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GNX-04","CL_5P0L_02:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GNX-04","text":"Desiderium, societas, rhetorica et dilatio neutralia esse non possunt, quia statum recipientis et directionem voluntatis iam efficiunt.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:DBN-02","CL_5P0L_02:DBN-05","CL_5P0L_03:GNX-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GNX-05","text":"Eloquentia, scientia, doctrina recta et certitudo metaphysica neque veritatem salutarem neque adhaesionem moralem per se efficiunt.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GNX-05","CL_5P0L_02:GNX-04","CL_5P0L_03:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GNX-06","text":"Subiectum neque reparator autonomus neque fundamentum sui consensus liberantis est.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:DBN-01","CL_5P0L_03:GNX-06","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GNX-07","text":"Virtus, baptismus et vita laudabilis neque innocentiam absolutam neque clausuram meritoriam constituunt.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:GNX-10","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:DBN-01","text":"Falsum esse oportet mentem principium propriae veritatis et normam ultimam sui iudicii esse posse.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:DBN-01","CL_5P0L_03:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:DBN-02","text":"Falsum esse oportet affectus et ambitus sociales materiam neutralem constituere, quia cognitionem et voluntatem recursive formant.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:DBN-02","CL_5P0L_02:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:DBN-03","text":"Falsum esse oportet originum, intentionum et providentiae transparentiam totalem ante confessionem vel fidem praesto esse.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSA-04","CL_5P0L_02:BSA-03","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:DBN-04","text":"Falsum esse oportet cognitionem termini facultatem perveniendi secum ferre, quia recta doctrina habitum cupiditatis intactum relinquere potest.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GNX-06","CL_5P0L_03:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:DBN-05","text":"Falsum esse oportet dilationem medium vacuum esse; inter veterem et novam voluntatem nullum futurum moraliter neutrum datur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:DBN-02","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:DBN-06","text":"Falsum esse oportet gratiam meram responsionem posteriorem aut voluntatis substitutionem coactivam esse; ipsa initium praebet voluntati tamen consentienti.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:DBN-06","CL_5P0L_03:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:DBN-07","text":"Falsum esse oportet effectum bonum bonitatem intentionis probare, aliter providentia et imputatio moralis confunderentur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:GNX-09","CL_5P0L_03:DBN-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSA-01","text":"Systema circum absentiam impossibilem Dei ordinatur: nulla creatura eum localiter fugit nec extra ordinem participationis subsistit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSA-01","CL_5P0L_02:BSA-01","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSA-02","text":"Inter falsitatem relictam et conversionem recusatam nulla positio stabilis aut voluntas neutralis conceditur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:BSA-02","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSA-03","text":"Plena conversio et stabilis possessio Sapientiae intra praesentem temporalitatem indisponibiles manent, unde clausura vim ex futuro nondum possesso accipit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSA-05","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSA-04","text":"Regeneratio subiecti a se ipso producta est possibilitas inadmissibilis; reditus tantum ut participatio medicinae et gratiae cogitatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:BSA-05","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSA-05","text":"Innocentia absoluta, meritum clausum et transparentia providentiae excluduntur; earum absentia confessionem, misericordiam et intercessionem terminales reddit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSA-04","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-05","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:XD-01","text":"Bonitas ontologica creaturae et carentia substantiae propriae mali efficiunt ut servitus temporalis realis sit, sed subiectum sine destructione naturae sanari possit.","refs":["MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-01","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-04","CL_5P0L_01:GA-05","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:XD-02","text":"Aversio non in actu singulari residet, sed per institutiones, imagines, auctoritates et habitus distribuitur, quos subiectum diachronicum simul recipit et corroborat.","refs":["MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-05","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-06","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-07","CL_5P0L_01:CGD-06","CL_5P0L_02:XD-02","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:XD-03","text":"Auctoritas medicinalis circuitum constituit: fides facultatem iudicandi sanat, sed agnitio medicinae ipsa fiducia in auctoritatem iam indiget.","refs":["MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-07","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-08","CL_5P0L_02:XD-07","CL_5P0L_02:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:XD-04","text":"Correctio obiecti cogniti impedimentum ad capacitatem cognoscentis transfert: veritas demonstrata impotentiam manifestat et conversionem facultatis postulat.","refs":["MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-08","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-10","CL_5P0L_02:XD-08","CL_5P0L_03:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:XD-05","text":"Dilatio est causalitas temporalis activa: secundum ordinem potest correctionem maturare, sed voluntati conversionem recusanti consuetudinem et servitutem amplificat.","refs":["MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-05","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-09","CL_5P0L_01:XD-07","CL_5P0L_02:RLE-05","CL_5P0L_03:GNX-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:XD-06","text":"Responsabilitas et gratia cohaerent asymmetrice: subiectum vincula per actus suos fabricat, sed principium quo consentire integre potest sibi non praebet.","refs":["MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-04","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-10","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-12","CL_5P0L_02:XD-04","CL_5P0L_03:XD-03","CL_5P0L_03:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:XD-07","text":"Eventus conversionis processum non tollit sed comprimit: voluntatem uno actu integrat, cuius effectus sacramento, disciplina et communione temporaliter explicantur.","refs":["MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-10","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-11","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-14","CL_5P0L_03:XD-05","CL_5P0L_03:XD-10","CL_5P0L_03:MP-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:XD-08","text":"Confessio providentiam non tantum interpretatur, sed ordinem causalitatis narrando exercet atque lectorem in gratiarum actionem, imitationem et intercessionem inserit.","refs":["MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-12","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-13","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-14","CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B05","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-07","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSD-01","text":"Subiectum autobiographicum fit agens culpabile, patiens medicinae et historia relationum, cuius identitas memoria et confessione potius quam introspectione immediata constituitur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSD-01","CL_5P0L_02:BSD-01","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSD-02","text":"Malum de-substantializatum non fit inefficax, sed vim strategicam ex conversione bonorum in fines falsos et ex sedimentatione actuum haurit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:BSD-06","CL_5P0L_03:XD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSD-03","text":"Tempus reclassificatur ut medium morale in quo obiecta transeunt, habitus augentur, conversio catastrophicum momentum accipit et formatio eius effectus explicat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSD-02","CL_5P0L_02:BSD-02","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSD-04","text":"Epistemologia fit soteriologia: cognitio vera procedit per purgationem facultatis et transformationem affectus, non per solam accumulationem propositionum.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSD-05","CL_5P0L_02:BSD-04","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSD-05","text":"Institutio socialis est regimen affectuum et credibilitatis, cuius media secundum recipientem captivare, corrigere aut conversionem propagare possunt.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSD-04","CL_5P0L_02:XD-05","CL_5P0L_03:MME-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSD-06","text":"Ecclesia emergit ut apparatus temporalis qui veritatem in allocutionem, consensum in sacramentum, affectum in cantum et memoriam in intercessionem transfert.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:BSD-06","CL_5P0L_03:MME-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSD-07","text":"Mors non relationem delet sed formam eius mutat, dum possessionem corporalem in luctum ordinatum, spem resurrectionis et memoriam liturgicam convertit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:BSD-08","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-09","CL_5P0L_03:MME-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RLE-01","text":"Fames boni immutabilis non agnita substitutum finitum absolutizat; insufficientia substituti inanitatem auget et novam fugam ad exteriora parit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:RLE-01","CL_5P0L_02:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RLE-02","text":"Laus socialis auctoritatem generat, auctoritas imitationem movet, imitatio novam laudem stabilit; conversio visibilis eundem circuitum inversum ad liberationem adhibet.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:RLE-02","CL_5P0L_02:RLE-03","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RLE-03","text":"Superbia imaginem corporalem eligit, imago doctrinam falsam sustinet, doctrina aversionem confirmat, et appetitus veritatem correctionis recusat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:RLE-03","CL_5P0L_02:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RLE-04","text":"Actus perversus consuetudinem gignit, consuetudo divisionem, divisio consilium medium, consilium dilationem, dilatio autem libertatem ulterius imminuit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:RLE-05","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RLE-05","text":"Veritas cognita impotentiam detegit, impotentia excusationes dissolvit, dissolutio implorationem aperit, gratia autem voluntatem ad veritatem iam visam reducit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:XD-08","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RLE-06","text":"Eventus confessione retractatus providentiam manifestat, confessio imitationem generat, et narratio conversionis textum alteri lectori in allocutionem praesentem mutat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:RLE-06","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-03","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RLE-07","text":"Stabilis fruitio Sapientiae est attractor communis inquietudinis, cognitionis, conversionis, mediationum et luctus, quia praesentia quaesita vera sed nondum possessa manet.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:RLE-06","CL_5P0L_02:RLE-07","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FGS-B01","text":"Donum essendi et bonitatis → dependentia creaturae → desiderium constitutivum boni immutabilis.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:FGS-B01","CL_5P0L_03:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FGS-B02","text":"Oblivio principii → bonum finitum absolutum → dispersio affectus → egestas et inquietudo.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-02","CL_5P0L_01:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FGS-B03","text":"Dispersio → mediatio socialis et imaginativa → auctoritas falsa → captatio intellectus et confirmatio aversionis.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:RMD-04","CL_5P0L_02:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FGS-B04","text":"Discrepantia experientiae et refutatio ontologica → dissolutio falsi → rehabilitatio fidei → auctoritas medicinalis.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:AS-04","CL_5P0L_02:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FGS-B05","text":"Veritas intellecta → detectio habitus intacti → voluntas divisa → dilatio servilis → necessitas gratiae.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GNX-06","CL_5P0L_02:MP-04","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FGS-B06","text":"Gratia antecedens → consensus integratus → conversio punctiformis → baptismus et formatio ecclesialis → disciplina affectuum.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:GA-07","CL_5P0L_03:XD-05","CL_5P0L_03:XD-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FGS-B07","text":"Confessio causalitatis → gratiae actio → memoria liturgica → intercessio → possessio Sapientiae eschatologice dilata.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:RLE-05","CL_5P0L_03:GA-15","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:AFM-B01","text":"Dependens bonitas creata → aversio affectiva → amplificatio socialis → error doctrinalis → refutatio ontologica → responsabilitas voluntatis.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B01","CL_5P0L_02:XD-02","CL_5P0L_03:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:AFM-B02","text":"Ruina certitudinis falsae → fides provisionalis → veritas incorporea → detectio impotentiae → gratia integrans → conversio.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:AS-04","CL_5P0L_02:BSD-04","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:AFM-B03","text":"Conversio punctiformis → renuntiatio et baptismus → communio ecclesialis → contemplatio instabilis → mors et luctus → misericordia atque intercessio.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:AS-B07","CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B01","CL_5P0L_03:AS-B08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MME-01","text":"Malum reclassificatur ex natura adversa in structuram coniunctam privationis ontologicae, aversionis voluntariae et inertiae temporaliter acquisitae.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B04","CL_5P0L_02:BSD-06","CL_5P0L_03:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MME-02","text":"Subiectum reclassificatur ex anima sibi transparente in historiam culpabilem et sanabilem, per corpora, signa, societates, habitus et sacramenta formatam.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:HSI-02","CL_5P0L_02:BSD-01","CL_5P0L_03:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MME-03","text":"Libertas transfertur ab autonomia et facultate eligendi ad participationem recti ordinis et consensum a gratia sanatum.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:MME-03","CL_5P0L_01:BSD-07","CL_5P0L_03:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MME-04","text":"Auctoritas desinit esse oppositum libertatis et fit mediatio examinabilis, cuius validitas ex ordine, fructu et facultate formandi iudicium pendet.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:BSD-05","CL_5P0L_02:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MME-05","text":"Tempus ex recipiente neutro in machinam moralem mutatur, quae habitum sedimentat, momentum conversionis comprimit et possessionem aeternam differt.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:MME-03","CL_5P0L_03:MME-05","CL_5P0L_03:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MME-06","text":"Conversio ex substitutione opinionis in integrationem voluntatis et processum intellectualem, sacramentalem, affectivum atque socialem expanditur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:MME-05","CL_5P0L_03:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MME-07","text":"Narratio reclassificatur ex relatione praeteriti in interventionem quae memoriam, causalitatem, imitationem et precationem praesentem ordinat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B05","CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:ALT-B01","text":"Gradus superficiei continet infantiam, institutiones, furtum, luctus, sectam, migrationes, ascensus interiores, conversionem, baptismum, mortem Monicae et intercessionem.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B01","CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B01","CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:ALT-B02","text":"Gradus structuralis componit participationem essendi, aversionem, mediationem, habitum, temporalitatem, gratiam et providentiam in unam machinam formationis.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B02","CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B02","CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:ALT-B03","text":"Gradus metastrategicus certamen transfert ab electione inter obiecta vel doctrinas ad formationem facultatis quae amare, credere, iudicare et consentire potest.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B03","CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B03","CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:ALT-B04","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis realitatem ut participationem boni immutabilis constituit, in qua subiectum per successionem ligatur, sanatur et ad aeternitatem dirigitur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:HSI-01","CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B04","CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:ALT-B05","text":"Gradus methodologicus et performativus confessione efficit quod asserit, quia narratione culpam voluntati, bonum Deo et lectorem imitationi atque intercessioni distribuit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSD-06","CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B05","CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FL-01","text":"Voluntas culpabilis et gratia antecedens simul requiruntur, sed modus quo actio divina consensum efficit sine coactione formaliter indeterminatus manet.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:FL-01","CL_5P0L_03:XD-03","CL_5P0L_03:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FL-02","text":"Providentia eventus pravos ad bonum ordinat et culpam agenti relinquit, sed distinctio causalitatum affirmatur firmius quam explicatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:FL-03","CL_5P0L_02:XD-06","CL_5P0L_03:FL-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FL-03","text":"Fides auctoritatem medicinalem recipit ut rationem sanet, ratio autem auctoritatem sanantem iudicare debet; circulus medicinalis criterio omnino externo caret.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:FL-02","CL_5P0L_02:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FL-04","text":"Bona creata legitima manent, sed eadem sub cupiditate vincula fiunt; limes inter usum ordinatum et tegumentum appetitus non semper explicitus est.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B02","CL_5P0L_02:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FL-05","text":"Conversio ut actus integer et processus multistratus cohaeret tantum distinctione inter integrationem voluntatis et transformationem ulteriorem intellectus atque affectus.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:AS-B07","CL_5P0L_03:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MP-01","text":"Malum sensum mutat ab adversario substantiali ad privationem, inde ad aversionem voluntatis et postremo ad consuetudinem temporaliter efficacem.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:RMD-01","CL_5P0L_03:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MP-02","text":"Mediatio mutatur ab instrumento captationis in condicionem medicinae, deinde in rete ecclesiale quod conversionem temporaliter stabilit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:MME-06","CL_5P0L_03:RMD-05","CL_5P0L_03:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MP-03","text":"Veritas mutatur ex obiecto doctrinae in normam quae cognoscentem iudicat, impotentiam detegit et novum ordinem vitae requirit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:RMD-03","CL_5P0L_03:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MP-04","text":"Dilatio mutat valorem a patientia providentiali ad mechanismum servitutis, ubi mora non amplius praeparat sed veterem consuetudinem confirmat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:MP-03","CL_5P0L_02:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MP-05","text":"Clausura conversionis mutatur in principium formationis, et clausura vitae laudabilis in memoriam liturgicam, misericordiam atque spem resurrectionis.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:MP-05","CL_5P0L_03:MP-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:HSI-01","text":"Realitas est campus participationis circa fontem immutabilem, in quo defectus ordinem vulnerat sed naturam contrariam producere nequit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:HSI-01","CL_5P0L_03:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum est nodus diachronicus permeabilis, qui se repetitione ligat, ab alio principio solvitur et memoria confessionali recollegitur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:HSI-02","CL_5P0L_03:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:HSI-03","text":"Tempus est fluvius, sedimentum et limen: aufert obiecta, format consuetudinem, comprimit decisionem et futuram possessionem Sapientiae differt.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:HSI-03","CL_5P0L_03:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:HSI-04","text":"Mediatio est rete navigabile quod veritatem per voces, textus, corpora, exempla, sacramenta et memoriam distribuit, dum iter ab exterioribus ad interiora regit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:HSI-04","CL_5P0L_03:HSI-04","CL_5P0L_03:HSI-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:HSI-05","text":"Mors est limen quod communionem corporalem frangit sine relationis abolitione, eamque in luctum, precem et expectationem stabilis praesentiae transfert.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:HSI-06","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata extracta sufficiunt ad restituendum motum ab ontologica dependentia per aversionem affectivam, captationem doctrinalem et servitutem voluntatis ad conversionem ecclesialiter formatam.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B01","CL_5P0L_02:MRT-B01","CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima coniungit bonitatem creaturae, malum privativum, responsabilitatem voluntatis et redistributionem causalitatis inter culpam atque gratiam.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B02","CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B02","CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MRT-B03","text":"Cohaerentia huius gradus reditu spirali constat: eadem aversio per affectum, intellectum et habitum mutatur, dum mediatio ab instrumento captationis in apparatus liberationis invertitur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B03","CL_5P0L_02:MRT-B04","CL_5P0L_03:HSI-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MRT-B04","text":"Minus determinata manent efficientia gratiae sine coactione, criterium ultimum verae auctoritatis et concursus providentiae cum culpa particulari.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:MRT-B03","CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B04","CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MRT-B05","text":"Reductioni axiomaticae resistunt actus confessionis, densitas affectuum, allocutio temporalis et singularitas luctus, quia ipsa sunt media quibus doctrina conversionis efficitur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B06","CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T142715963469Z_06feee2b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"5P0L L1 01","source_sha256":"d23760c5fc0a354fa85ea1ddef272b47a4d263904e33266780a04a465b509b67","sha256":"c97898ed2a66c72ab9ad372497ae3e4c32bf8998c22d0afe7ab70f7d110009ec","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:27:15.964473+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BAS-01","text":"The system asks how a creature alienated from its beginning and end may acknowledge affective, epistemic, and volitional guilt and turn toward the immutable good.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BAS-01","CL_5P0L_03:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BAS-02","text":"The global thesis holds that all created being is good, whereas evil arises from the will's aversion and, through habit, acquires temporal efficacy without a substance of its own.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BAS-02","CL_5P0L_03:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BAS-03","text":"The argument composes confession, analysis of the affections, ontological refutation, and a history of mediations, so that the externalization of evil may be converted into a genealogy of the culpable yet healable subject.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BAS-03","CL_5P0L_03:AS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BAS-04","text":"The movement transforms biographical chronology into a recursion of aversion, whose forms change from appetite through doctrinal error and servitude of the will to ecclesial formation.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BAS-04","CL_5P0L_03:AS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BAS-05","text":"Correction first dissolves false certainties and ontologies, then shows that corrected doctrine does not effect conversion so long as the habit of willing is not whole.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:AS-04","CL_5P0L_02:MP-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BAS-06","text":"Conversion emerges as a point-like threshold that closes deliberation, yet at the same time opens an intellectual, affective, sacramental, and social process.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:AS-B07","CL_5P0L_03:CGD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BAS-07","text":"Confession performatively enacts doctrine, because it reorders memory, distributes causality between guilt and grace, and leads the reader into imitation and intercession.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSD-06","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BAS-08","text":"The closure is open and attractive: conversion is stabilized, but full enjoyment of Wisdom is deferred, while death, mercy, and intercession prevent every present consummation.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BAS-08","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] God is the immutable source of all being and good; every created nature participates in goodness and admits no coordinated contrary principle.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-01","CL_5P0L_03:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-02","text":"[Attractor] The creature is ordered toward rest in the immutable good, whence restlessness, inquiry, and desire bear the negative form of the divine end.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-02","CL_5P0L_02:GA-08","CL_5P0L_03:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Created goods and local truths retain goodness, but become salvific only when their use, end, and reception are rightly ordered.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-03","CL_5P0L_02:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Evil is a privation of good which, although lacking an essence of its own, acquires temporal efficacy through aversion, repetition, and habit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-05","CL_5P0L_03:XD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] A single structure of aversion passes from dispersed appetite to the imitation of freedom, the capture of intellect, false authority, and a will bound by habit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:XD-01","CL_5P0L_02:GA-03","CL_5P0L_03:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] The subject is a diachronic nexus of love, memory, society, habit, and acts, not a consciousness of itself simply present or transparent.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSD-01","CL_5P0L_02:HSI-02","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Social, rhetorical, scriptural, sacramental, and ecclesial mediations neither corrupt univocally nor save autonomously, but distribute affect, credibility, and reception.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-09","CL_5P0L_02:GA-05","CL_5P0L_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Knowledge is morally and soteriologically ordered: truth does not pass into wisdom unless the knowing faculty is transformed by humility, faith, and healing.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-10","CL_5P0L_02:XD-03","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Time is a moral operator that distributes changes, dissolves objects, sediments habits, amplifies delay, and unfolds healing.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSD-02","CL_5P0L_02:BSD-02","CL_5P0L_03:RMD-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Grace precedes conversion and brings partial wills into integral consent, healing the will without abolishing its consensual act.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-12","CL_5P0L_03:GA-07","CL_5P0L_03:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Conversion is a decisive threshold within a long process: one now closes the division of the will, but does not consummate the formation of the subject's multiple orders.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:AS-B07","CL_5P0L_03:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-12","text":"[Emergent] Confessional causality is asymmetrical: the will bears defect and guilt, whereas providence preserves goods, orders events, and initiates liberation.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSD-03","CL_5P0L_03:GA-11","CL_5P0L_03:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-13","text":"[Emergent] Confession turns memory and narrative into an engine of conversion, because it restores identity, redistributes causes, and forms the reader within the same movement.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-11","CL_5P0L_03:GA-12","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-14","text":"[Terminal] Wisdom stably possessed remains unavailable within temporal life; therefore mercy, sacrifice, and intercession constitute an ultimate rather than a meritorious closure.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:GA-15","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-04","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RMD-01","text":"Restlessness changes from an index of ontological dependence into epistemic hunger, desire for rest, and an attractor of Wisdom not yet possessed.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:RMD-01","CL_5P0L_02:RLE-07","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RMD-02","text":"Created good passes from an object wrongly usurped into an imitable appearance of good and then into a medium of healing; goodness persists, function changes through relation.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:RMD-02","CL_5P0L_01:XD-03","CL_5P0L_03:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RMD-03","text":"Mediation migrates from discipline and fellowship to rhetoric, teacher, Scripture, and ecclesial apparatuses, retaining the power to form reception.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:RMD-04","CL_5P0L_02:RMD-03","CL_5P0L_03:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RMD-04","text":"Authority changes from socially captivating power into an object of examination, then into medicinal mediation that forms judgment rather than suspending it.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GA-09","CL_5P0L_02:XD-07","CL_5P0L_02:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RMD-05","text":"Delay is inverted according to order: delaying baptism opens license, suspending doctrine prepares correction, postponing conversion strengthens habit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:RMD-07","CL_5P0L_02:RMD-04","CL_5P0L_03:GNX-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RMD-06","text":"Memory passes from reconstruction of origins to moral judgment and finally to a performative operation by which fall, guilt, and providence are reclassified.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-11","CL_5P0L_02:RMD-05","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RMD-07","text":"Truth changes from a sought object into a judgment of the knowing subject's impotence, a norm of formation, and an attractor to which stable adherence is still lacking.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:RMD-03","CL_5P0L_03:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RMD-08","text":"Conversion changes from biographical closure into a principle of formation; baptism stabilizes it ecclesially, but does not end the need for further mercy and transformation.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:AS-B07","CL_5P0L_03:CGD-08","CL_5P0L_03:MP-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:CGD-01","text":"Childhood, theft, mourning, teachers, astrology, exemplary conversions, and death remain local cases; they constitute the present level only as mutations of aversion, mediation, and return.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:CGD-01","CL_5P0L_02:CGD-01","CL_5P0L_03:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:CGD-02","text":"Anti-Manichaean and exegetical corrections transcend local polemic, because they constitute the transition from the externalization of evil to the distinction between knowledge of the end and the healing way.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:CGD-04","CL_5P0L_02:CGD-05","CL_5P0L_03:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:CGD-03","text":"School, fellowship, crowd, and singular example are amplified into a single theory of socially distributed reception, by which praise, shame, and imitation alter the subject's state.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:CGD-06","CL_5P0L_02:CGD-04","CL_5P0L_03:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:CGD-04","text":"Astrology as a local doctrine vanishes, but its function persists in every attempt to confuse causality and transfer guilt to external necessity.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:RMD-08","CL_5P0L_03:RMD-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:CGD-05","text":"Interior ascents do not remain episodic contemplations, but jointly distinguish knowledge of truth, incapacity for adherence, and a brief anticipation of eschatological possession.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:CGD-06","CL_5P0L_03:XD-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:CGD-06","text":"Baptism, Monica's life, and her death amplify conversion beyond a singular act into regeneration, discipline of the affections, liturgical memory, and intercession.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:CGD-05","CL_5P0L_03:CGD-08","CL_5P0L_03:MME-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GNX-01","text":"No ontological exteriority is given in which creature, matter, or evil can subsist outside dependence on God.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSA-01","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GNX-02","text":"Evil is neither created substance nor uncreated matter nor a principle coordinated with God.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GNX-03","CL_5P0L_03:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GNX-03","text":"No finite good is condemned in itself, but no mutable creature can provide a stable end of desire.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GNX-04","CL_5P0L_02:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GNX-04","text":"Desire, society, rhetoric, and delay cannot be neutral, because they already effect the recipient's state and the direction of the will.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:DBN-02","CL_5P0L_02:DBN-05","CL_5P0L_03:GNX-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GNX-05","text":"Eloquence, knowledge, right doctrine, and metaphysical certainty do not by themselves effect either salvific truth or moral adherence.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GNX-05","CL_5P0L_02:GNX-04","CL_5P0L_03:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GNX-06","text":"The subject is neither an autonomous repairer nor the foundation of its own liberating consent.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:DBN-01","CL_5P0L_03:GNX-06","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:GNX-07","text":"Virtue, baptism, and praiseworthy life constitute neither absolute innocence nor meritorious closure.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:GNX-10","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that the mind can be the principle of its own truth and the ultimate norm of its own judgment.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:DBN-01","CL_5P0L_03:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that affections and social environments constitute neutral matter, because they recursively form knowledge and will.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:DBN-02","CL_5P0L_02:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that total transparency of origins, intentions, and providence is available before confession or faith.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSA-04","CL_5P0L_02:BSA-03","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that knowledge of the end carries with it the capacity to attain it, because right doctrine can leave the habit of desire untouched.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GNX-06","CL_5P0L_03:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:DBN-05","text":"It must be false that delay is an empty medium; between the old and the new will no morally neutral future is given.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:DBN-02","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:DBN-06","text":"It must be false that grace is a mere subsequent response or a coercive substitution for the will; it itself provides the beginning to a will that nevertheless consents.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:DBN-06","CL_5P0L_03:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:DBN-07","text":"It must be false that a good effect proves the goodness of intention, otherwise providence and moral imputation would be confused.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:GNX-09","CL_5P0L_03:DBN-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSA-01","text":"The system is ordered around God's impossible absence: no creature locally escapes him or subsists outside the order of participation.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSA-01","CL_5P0L_02:BSA-01","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSA-02","text":"Between retained falsehood and refused conversion, no stable position or neutral will is granted.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:BSA-02","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSA-03","text":"Full conversion and stable possession of Wisdom remain unavailable within present temporality, whence closure receives force from a future not yet possessed.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSA-05","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSA-04","text":"Regeneration of the subject produced by itself is an inadmissible possibility; return is conceived only as participation in healing and grace.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:BSA-05","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSA-05","text":"Absolute innocence, closed merit, and transparency of providence are excluded; their absence makes confession, mercy, and intercession terminal.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSA-04","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-05","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:XD-01","text":"The creature's ontological goodness and evil's lack of a substance of its own make temporal servitude real, yet allow the subject to be healed without destruction of nature.","refs":["MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-01","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-04","CL_5P0L_01:GA-05","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:XD-02","text":"Aversion does not reside in a singular act, but is distributed through institutions, images, authorities, and habits, which the diachronic subject both receives and reinforces.","refs":["MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-05","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-06","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-07","CL_5P0L_01:CGD-06","CL_5P0L_02:XD-02","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:XD-03","text":"Medicinal authority constitutes a circuit: faith heals the faculty of judging, but recognition of healing itself already requires trust in authority.","refs":["MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-07","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-08","CL_5P0L_02:XD-07","CL_5P0L_02:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:XD-04","text":"Correction of the known object transfers the impediment to the knowing capacity: demonstrated truth manifests impotence and demands conversion of the faculty.","refs":["MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-08","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-10","CL_5P0L_02:XD-08","CL_5P0L_03:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:XD-05","text":"Delay is active temporal causality: according to order it can mature correction, but for a will refusing conversion it amplifies habit and servitude.","refs":["MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-05","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-09","CL_5P0L_01:XD-07","CL_5P0L_02:RLE-05","CL_5P0L_03:GNX-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:XD-06","text":"Responsibility and grace cohere asymmetrically: the subject fashions bonds through its acts, but does not provide itself the principle by which it can consent integrally.","refs":["MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-04","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-10","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-12","CL_5P0L_02:XD-04","CL_5P0L_03:XD-03","CL_5P0L_03:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:XD-07","text":"The event of conversion does not abolish process but compresses it: it integrates the will in one act, whose effects are unfolded temporally by sacrament, discipline, and communion.","refs":["MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-10","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-11","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-14","CL_5P0L_03:XD-05","CL_5P0L_03:XD-10","CL_5P0L_03:MP-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:XD-08","text":"Confession does not merely interpret providence, but enacts the order of causality by narrating and inserts the reader into thanksgiving, imitation, and intercession.","refs":["MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-12","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-13","MC_5P0L_L1_01:GA-14","CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B05","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-07","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSD-01","text":"The autobiographical subject becomes a culpable agent, a patient of healing, and a history of relations, whose identity is constituted by memory and confession rather than immediate introspection.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSD-01","CL_5P0L_02:BSD-01","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSD-02","text":"De-substantialized evil does not become inefficacious, but draws strategic force from the conversion of goods into false ends and from the sedimentation of acts.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:BSD-06","CL_5P0L_03:XD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSD-03","text":"Time is reclassified as a moral medium in which objects pass away, habits increase, conversion takes on a catastrophic moment, and formation unfolds its effects.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSD-02","CL_5P0L_02:BSD-02","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSD-04","text":"Epistemology becomes soteriology: true knowledge proceeds through purification of the faculty and transformation of affect, not through the mere accumulation of propositions.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSD-05","CL_5P0L_02:BSD-04","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSD-05","text":"Social institution is a governance of affects and credibility, whose media can, according to the recipient, captivate, correct, or propagate conversion.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSD-04","CL_5P0L_02:XD-05","CL_5P0L_03:MME-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSD-06","text":"The Church emerges as a temporal apparatus that transfers truth into address, consent into sacrament, affect into song, and memory into intercession.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:BSD-06","CL_5P0L_03:MME-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:BSD-07","text":"Death does not destroy relation but changes its form, while converting bodily possession into ordered mourning, hope of resurrection, and liturgical memory.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:BSD-08","CL_5P0L_03:BSD-09","CL_5P0L_03:MME-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RLE-01","text":"Unacknowledged hunger for the immutable good absolutizes a finite substitute; the substitute's insufficiency increases emptiness and generates a new flight toward externals.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:RLE-01","CL_5P0L_02:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RLE-02","text":"Social praise generates authority, authority moves imitation, imitation stabilizes new praise; visible conversion applies the same inverted circuit to liberation.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:RLE-02","CL_5P0L_02:RLE-03","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RLE-03","text":"Pride chooses a bodily image, the image sustains false doctrine, doctrine confirms aversion, and appetite refuses the truth of correction.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:RLE-03","CL_5P0L_02:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RLE-04","text":"A perverse act begets habit, habit division, division an intermediate resolve, resolve delay, while delay further diminishes freedom.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:RLE-05","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RLE-05","text":"Known truth discloses impotence, impotence dissolves excuses, dissolution opens supplication, while grace returns the will to truth already seen.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:XD-08","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RLE-06","text":"An event reconsidered in confession manifests providence, confession generates imitation, and the narrative of conversion turns the text into a present address for another reader.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:RLE-06","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-03","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:RLE-07","text":"Stable enjoyment of Wisdom is the common attractor of restlessness, knowledge, conversion, mediations, and mourning, because the sought presence remains true but not yet possessed.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:RLE-06","CL_5P0L_02:RLE-07","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FGS-B01","text":"Gift of being and goodness → dependence of the creature → constitutive desire for the immutable good.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:FGS-B01","CL_5P0L_03:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FGS-B02","text":"Forgetfulness of the principle → finite good made absolute → dispersion of affect → poverty and restlessness.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:GA-02","CL_5P0L_01:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FGS-B03","text":"Dispersion → social and imaginative mediation → false authority → capture of intellect and confirmation of aversion.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:RMD-04","CL_5P0L_02:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FGS-B04","text":"Discrepancy of experience and ontological refutation → dissolution of falsehood → rehabilitation of faith → medicinal authority.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:AS-04","CL_5P0L_02:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FGS-B05","text":"Truth understood → detection of intact habit → divided will → servile delay → necessity of grace.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:GNX-06","CL_5P0L_02:MP-04","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FGS-B06","text":"Prevenient grace → integrated consent → point-like conversion → baptism and ecclesial formation → discipline of the affections.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:GA-07","CL_5P0L_03:XD-05","CL_5P0L_03:XD-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FGS-B07","text":"Confession of causality → thanksgiving → liturgical memory → intercession → eschatologically delayed possession of Wisdom.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:RLE-05","CL_5P0L_03:GA-15","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:AFM-B01","text":"Dependent created goodness → affective aversion → social amplification → doctrinal error → ontological refutation → responsibility of the will.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B01","CL_5P0L_02:XD-02","CL_5P0L_03:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:AFM-B02","text":"Ruin of false certainty → provisional faith → incorporeal truth → detection of impotence → integrating grace → conversion.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:AS-04","CL_5P0L_02:BSD-04","CL_5P0L_03:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:AFM-B03","text":"Point-like conversion → renunciation and baptism → ecclesial communion → unstable contemplation → death and mourning → mercy and intercession.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:AS-B07","CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B01","CL_5P0L_03:AS-B08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MME-01","text":"Evil is reclassified from adverse nature into a structure conjoined of ontological privation, voluntary aversion, and temporally acquired inertia.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B04","CL_5P0L_02:BSD-06","CL_5P0L_03:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MME-02","text":"The subject is reclassified from a soul transparent to itself into a culpable and healable history, formed through bodies, signs, societies, habits, and sacraments.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:HSI-02","CL_5P0L_02:BSD-01","CL_5P0L_03:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MME-03","text":"Freedom is transferred from autonomy and the capacity to choose to participation in right order and consent healed by grace.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:MME-03","CL_5P0L_01:BSD-07","CL_5P0L_03:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MME-04","text":"Authority ceases to be the opposite of freedom and becomes an examinable mediation, whose validity depends on order, fruit, and the capacity to form judgment.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:BSD-05","CL_5P0L_02:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MME-05","text":"Time changes from a neutral receptacle into a moral machine that sediments habit, compresses the moment of conversion, and defers eternal possession.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:MME-03","CL_5P0L_03:MME-05","CL_5P0L_03:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MME-06","text":"Conversion expands from substitution of opinion into integration of the will and an intellectual, sacramental, affective, and social process.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:MME-05","CL_5P0L_03:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MME-07","text":"Narrative is reclassified from an account of the past into an intervention that orders present memory, causality, imitation, and prayer.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B05","CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:ALT-B01","text":"The surface level contains childhood, institutions, theft, mourning, sect, migrations, interior ascents, conversion, baptism, Monica's death, and intercession.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B01","CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B01","CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:ALT-B02","text":"The structural level composes participation in being, aversion, mediation, habit, temporality, grace, and providence into a single machine of formation.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B02","CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B02","CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:ALT-B03","text":"The metastrategic level transfers the contest from choice among objects or doctrines to formation of the faculty able to love, believe, judge, and consent.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:ALT-B03","CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B03","CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:ALT-B04","text":"The ontological and temporal level establishes reality as participation in the immutable good, in which the subject is bound, healed, and directed toward eternity through succession.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:HSI-01","CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B04","CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:ALT-B05","text":"The methodological and performative level accomplishes by confession what it asserts, because by narrative it distributes guilt to the will, good to God, and the reader to imitation and intercession.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:BSD-06","CL_5P0L_02:ALT-B05","CL_5P0L_03:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FL-01","text":"A culpable will and prevenient grace are simultaneously required, but the manner in which divine action effects consent without coercion remains formally indeterminate.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:FL-01","CL_5P0L_03:XD-03","CL_5P0L_03:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FL-02","text":"Providence orders wicked events toward good and leaves guilt to the agent, but the distinction of causalities is asserted more firmly than it is explained.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:FL-03","CL_5P0L_02:XD-06","CL_5P0L_03:FL-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FL-03","text":"Faith receives medicinal authority in order that reason may be healed, but reason must judge healing authority; the medicinal circle lacks an entirely external criterion.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:FL-02","CL_5P0L_02:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FL-04","text":"Created goods remain legitimate, but the same goods become bonds under cupidity; the boundary between ordered use and a covering for appetite is not always explicit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B02","CL_5P0L_02:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:FL-05","text":"Conversion as an integral act and a multilayered process cohere only through the distinction between integration of the will and further transformation of intellect and affect.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:AS-B07","CL_5P0L_03:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MP-01","text":"Evil changes sense from substantial adversary to privation, then to aversion of the will and finally to temporally efficacious habit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:RMD-01","CL_5P0L_03:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MP-02","text":"Mediation changes from an instrument of capture into a condition of healing, then into an ecclesial network that stabilizes conversion temporally.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:MME-06","CL_5P0L_03:RMD-05","CL_5P0L_03:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MP-03","text":"Truth changes from an object of doctrine into a norm that judges the knower, discloses impotence, and requires a new order of life.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:RMD-03","CL_5P0L_03:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MP-04","text":"Delay changes value from providential patience to a mechanism of servitude, where postponement no longer prepares but confirms old habit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:MP-03","CL_5P0L_02:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MP-05","text":"The closure of conversion changes into a principle of formation, and the closure of a praiseworthy life into liturgical memory, mercy, and hope of resurrection.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:MP-05","CL_5P0L_03:MP-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:HSI-01","text":"Reality is a field of participation around an immutable source, in which defect wounds order but cannot produce a contrary nature.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:HSI-01","CL_5P0L_03:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:HSI-02","text":"The subject is a permeable diachronic nexus, which binds itself by repetition, is released by another principle, and is recollected by confessional memory.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:HSI-02","CL_5P0L_03:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:HSI-03","text":"Time is river, sediment, and threshold: it removes objects, forms habit, compresses decision, and defers future possession of Wisdom.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:HSI-03","CL_5P0L_03:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:HSI-04","text":"Mediation is a navigable network that distributes truth through voices, texts, bodies, examples, sacraments, and memory, while governing the path from externals to interiors.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:HSI-04","CL_5P0L_03:HSI-04","CL_5P0L_03:HSI-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:HSI-05","text":"Death is a threshold that breaks bodily communion without abolishing relation, and transfers it into mourning, prayer, and expectation of stable presence.","refs":["CL_5P0L_03:HSI-06","CL_5P0L_03:BSA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MRT-B01","text":"The extracted axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement from ontological dependence through affective aversion, doctrinal capture, and servitude of the will to ecclesially formed conversion.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B01","CL_5P0L_02:MRT-B01","CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MRT-B02","text":"The firmest structure joins the creature's goodness, privative evil, responsibility of the will, and redistribution of causality between guilt and grace.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B02","CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B02","CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MRT-B03","text":"The coherence of this level consists in spiral return: the same aversion changes through affect, intellect, and habit, while mediation is inverted from an instrument of capture into apparatuses of liberation.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B03","CL_5P0L_02:MRT-B04","CL_5P0L_03:HSI-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MRT-B04","text":"The efficacy of grace without coercion, the ultimate criterion of true authority, and the concurrence of providence with particular guilt remain less determined.","refs":["CL_5P0L_02:MRT-B03","CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B04","CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_01:MRT-B05","text":"Acts of confession, the density of affects, temporal address, and the singularity of mourning resist axiomatic reduction, because they are themselves the means by which the doctrine of conversion is effected.","refs":["CL_5P0L_01:MRT-B06","CL_5P0L_03:MRT-B08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"MC_5P0L_L1_01@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:MC_5P0L_L1_01:v1","source_language_code":"la","original_title":"5P0L L1 01"}],"identity":{"layer":"MC","kicker":"Meta-cluster · Confessiones","title":"5P0L L1 01","context":"Chapters 01–09 · Book One. · Book Two. · Book Three. · Book Four. · Book Five. · Book Six. · Book Seven. · Book Eight. · Book Nine.","original_title":"5P0L L1 01","original_context":"Chapters 01–09 · Liber Primus. · Liber Secundus. · Liber Tertius. · Liber Quartus. · Liber Quintus. · Liber Sextus. · Liber Septimus. · Liber Octavus. · Liber Nonus."},"original_title":"5P0L L1 01","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02","layer":"MC","title":"5P0L L1 02","order":2,"parents":["CL_5P0L_04","CL_5P0L_05"],"revision":"MC_5P0L_L1_02@R001","sha256":"6edf688e8a27ec6791c3d2a36a0aa357d77708c0d0cffb887ed230a3733db34e","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ASP-01","text":"Systema quaerit quomodo creatura sibi opaca, mutabilis et temporalis originem praetemporalem, veritatem sui atque directionem ad requiem recipiat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BAS-01","CL_5P0L_05:BAS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ASP-02","text":"Thesis globalis omnem cognitionem, formationem, actionem et quietem sub asymmetria donationis divinae constituit: creatura accipit quod ex se producere non potest.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BAS-02","CL_5P0L_05:BAS-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ASP-03","text":"Argumentatio confessionem apophaticam cum reconstructione metaphysica, hermeneutica et ecclesiali coniungit, ut dependentia ontologica in disciplina temporalis receptionis explicetur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BAS-03","CL_5P0L_05:BAS-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ASP-04","text":"Motus ab origine non chronologica per signa, interioritatem et successionem procedit, deinde interioritatem ad Verbum, communitatem formatam et finem aeternum transcendit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BAS-04","CL_5P0L_05:BAS-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ASP-05","text":"Progressio est spiralis: quaelibet illuminatio novam opacitatem aperit, et quaelibet formatio originem atque finem ex novo prospectu retrospecte reconstituit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BAS-05","CL_5P0L_05:BAS-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ASP-06","text":"Dispersio et informitas sunt modi non identici carentiae unitatis propriae; caritas, intentio et Verbum eos in formationem sine abolitione pluralitatis convertunt.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BAS-06","CL_5P0L_05:BAS-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ASP-07","text":"Tempus fit simul medium vulneris et formationis: in eo attentio dispergitur, dona recipiuntur, opera exercentur et creatura ad propriam temporis transcensionem ordinatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSD-02","CL_5P0L_05:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ASP-08","text":"Clausura praesens semper differtur, sed dilatio non est infinita: pax nondum possessa in sabbatum sine vespera terminaliter colligitur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BAS-08","CL_5P0L_05:BAS-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Deus immutabilis neque tempore continetur neque creatione perficitur, sed mensura veritatis et fons omnis formationis manet.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-01","CL_5P0L_05:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Creatura ex nihilo facta neque causam essendi neque principium cognitionis, ordinis aut perseverantiae in se possidet.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-02","CL_5P0L_05:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Mutabilitas transit a capacitate ontologica formae recipiendae ad successionem, distentionem subiecti et historiam formationis communis.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-13","CL_5P0L_05:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Creatura est capacitas receptiva cui unitas effecta datur; interioritas, materia informis et vita ecclesialis diversos huius receptivitatis gradus exhibent.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-05","CL_5P0L_05:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Veritas interior et Verbum increatum subiectum transcendunt, errores eius iudicant et capacitatem dispersam ad formam vocant.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RMD-03","CL_5P0L_05:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Interioritas ex loco sui-examinationis in commissuram ontologiae et hermeneuticae mutatur, ubi opacitas creaturae cum iudicio veritatis concurrit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-06","CL_5P0L_05:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Tempus est modus creatus receptionis et transitus: mutationibus oritur, operationibus animi mensuratur et historiam formationis sustinet.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:MME-03","CL_5P0L_05:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] Unitas in Deo per caritatem est attractor qui attentionem, amores, sensus et opera colligit sine diversitate creata delenda.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-11","CL_5P0L_05:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Memoria et Scriptura sunt mediationes temporales quibus absentia operativa fit: praeteritum per vestigium, Verbum aeternum per sermonem humilem adest.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RMD-02","CL_5P0L_05:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-10","text":"[Persistent] Bona creata et multiplicitas sunt positiva, sed medium in finem mutatum dispersionem efficit, dum relatio ad fontem bonitatem totius constituit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-09","CL_5P0L_05:GA-15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Confessio et interpretatio non referunt tantum veritatem iam possessam, sed affectum, intellectum et communitatem sub veritate performative reformant.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-03","CL_5P0L_05:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-12","text":"[Persistent] Gratia et causalitas divina actionem finitam non supprimunt, sed facultatem cognoscendi, volendi et operandi participative constituunt.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-10","CL_5P0L_05:GA-14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-13","text":"[Emergent] Principium creatorium Verbi et mediatio Christi unum axem constituunt quo creatura in esse vocatur, reformatur et per mortalitatem ad iustitiam dirigitur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-12","CL_5P0L_05:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-14","text":"[Terminal] Pax nondum praesens et sabbatum sine vespera unam clausuram eschatologicam constituunt, in qua opera transeunt neque successio renovatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSA-06","CL_5P0L_05:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-15","text":"[Attractor] Unitas vera non est univocitas aut simplicitas vacua, sed ordo plurium sub uno fonte, una veritate et uno fine.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:DBN-04","CL_5P0L_05:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-01","text":"Creatio ex nihilo identitatem stabilem retinet, sed ex propositione cosmologica in legem epistemicae, moralis et ecclesialis dependentiae amplificatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:CGD-08","CL_5P0L_05:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-02","text":"Veritas immutabilis manet mensura, sed munus eius a iudicio interiori ad vocationem formativam Verbi creatoris extenditur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RMD-03","CL_5P0L_05:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-03","text":"Memoria ab archivo interiori in mediationem temporalem migrat, cui Scriptura respondet ut medium communitatis ad Verbum aeternum.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RMD-02","CL_5P0L_05:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-04","text":"Dispersio et informitas eandem functionem non explent, sed recurrenter designant capacitatem quae unitatem ex se non habet et formatione indiget.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-07","CL_5P0L_05:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-05","text":"Attentio ex facultate mensurandi in directionem amoris mutatur, deinde in caritate normam hermeneuticam et pondus ontologicum acquirit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-08","CL_5P0L_05:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-06","text":"Iudicium veritatis ex confessione motuum interiorum ad exegesim pluralium sensuum migrat, servata correctione affectus et intellectus.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:XD-05","CL_5P0L_05:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-07","text":"Praesens ex instanti morali examinando in medium pedagogicum historiae mutatur, quo forma recipitur, exercetur et memoriae traditur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RMD-07","CL_5P0L_05:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-08","text":"Mediatio a reconciliatione peccatoris ad structuram universam originis, formationis et directionis temporalis amplificatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RMD-06","CL_5P0L_05:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-09","text":"Multiplicitas vim invertit: sine fine uno dispersiva est, sub unitate fontis vero fecunditatem rerum et intellectuum efficit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:DBN-04","CL_5P0L_05:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-10","text":"Dilatio pacis transformationem terminalem patitur, cum requies ex stabilitate participata in finem irreversibilem totius successionis transit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BAS-08","CL_5P0L_05:MP-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:CGD-01","text":"Taxonomiae memoriae et quaestio materiae informis locales manent; sursum ascendit sola structura capacitatis quae vestigium aut formam recipit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:CGD-01","CL_5P0L_05:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:CGD-02","text":"Triplex cupiditas et correspondentiae singulorum dierum sunt machinae inferiores; gradus praesens retinet legem distributionis attentionis et mediorum secundum capacitatem.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:CGD-02","CL_5P0L_05:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:CGD-03","text":"Creatio ex nihilo et prioritas originis sine intervallo amplificantur in principium universale causalitatis non autonomae.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:CGD-08","CL_5P0L_05:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:CGD-04","text":"Aporiae de praesentis longitudine et mutationis ordine localiter permanent, sed coniunctae demonstrant tempus non esse receptaculum neque plenam sui possessionem.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:CGD-03","CL_5P0L_05:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:CGD-05","text":"Iudicium interius et pluralitas hermeneutica gradus inferiores coniungunt, quia sensus recipiuntur multipliciter sed veritati supra interpretem subiciuntur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GNX-04","CL_5P0L_05:GNX-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:CGD-06","text":"Communitas confessionis et recapitulatio ecclesialis constituunt transitionem praesentis gradus, qua formatio interior in corpus interpretans et exercitum exteriorizatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:CGD-09","CL_5P0L_05:CGD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:CGD-07","text":"Polemica anti-Donatistica et refutatio circuituum caelestium opere locali peracto recedunt, sed earum exclusio iudicii autonomi et mensurae creatae persistit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RMD-10","CL_5P0L_04:CGD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:CGD-08","text":"Christus mediator et Verbum creatorium non manent conclusiones regionales, sed pontem maiorem inter donationem essendi et reformationem vitae efficiunt.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-12","CL_5P0L_05:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:CGD-09","text":"Dubia de affectione temporali et statu materiae informis limites inferiores servant; synthesis ea coordinat, sed in unam ontologiam exhaustivam non solvit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:FL-03","CL_5P0L_05:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GNX-01","text":"Nulla creatura sui causa, mensura, illuminatrix aut consummatrix esse potest.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:DBN-01","CL_5P0L_05:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GNX-02","text":"Nec materia nec tempus nec mens neque alia substantia potest Deo coaeterna aut ab eius causalitate independens constitui.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSA-03","CL_5P0L_05:GNX-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GNX-03","text":"Deus neque memoria continetur neque temporaliter deliberat, mutatur aut per opera creata completur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GNX-03","CL_5P0L_05:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GNX-04","text":"Interioritas nec transparantiam sui nec prospectum exhaustivum veritatis praebet.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GNX-02","CL_5P0L_05:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GNX-05","text":"Multiplicitas neque per se ordinem efficit neque simpliciter falsitati aequatur; univocitas et licentia indiscriminata pariter excluduntur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:DBN-04","CL_5P0L_05:GNX-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GNX-06","text":"Mediatio non est impedimentum quod ascensus autonomus superet, sed modus necessarius formationis intra mortalitatem, signa et gradus capacitatis.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSA-05","CL_5P0L_05:DBN-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GNX-07","text":"Corpus, materia, tempus et bona sensibilia non sunt substantiae malae, sed neque fines ultimi aut principia sui iuris.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GNX-05","CL_5P0L_05:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GNX-08","text":"Nulla clausura intra statum mortalem neque perpetuatio operum temporalium consummationem creaturae constituit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GNX-08","CL_5P0L_05:GNX-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:DBN-01","text":"Causalitas divina et actio creata relatione competitiva explicari non possunt, quia dependentia doni ipsam operationem finitam constituit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSD-05","CL_5P0L_05:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:DBN-02","text":"Immutabilitas divina inertiam significare non potest, quamvis actus aeternus effectus successivos sine mutatione sui producat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-01","CL_5P0L_05:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:DBN-03","text":"Successio non potest causam divinam continere aut eius voluntatem narrare, sed tantum modum quo effectus creati recipiuntur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:DBN-03","CL_5P0L_05:DBN-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:DBN-04","text":"Unitas non potest plenam identitatem partium exigere, quia systema cohaeret tantum si pluralitas vera sub fonte indiviso subsistit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:XD-07","CL_5P0L_05:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:DBN-05","text":"Veritas nec ab affectu interiori nec ab intentione conscia ministri humani producitur aut terminatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:DBN-02","CL_5P0L_05:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:DBN-06","text":"Introspectio, analysis temporis et mediatio signorum non possunt in ascensum immediatum ad immutabilitatem converti.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:DBN-07","CL_5P0L_05:DBN-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:DBN-07","text":"Homologia inter distentionem, informitatem et formationem non demonstrat per se necessitatem mediatoris aut translationem totius creationis in Ecclesiam.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:FL-06","CL_5P0L_05:FL-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSA-01","text":"Possibilitas radicaliter indisponibilis est creatura quae se totam simul possideat atque stabilitatem ex propria natura habeat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSA-01","CL_5P0L_05:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSA-02","text":"Origo ante tempus nec ordine chronologico repraesentari nec per aliquod alterum Deo coaeternum explicari potest.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:BSA-01","CL_5P0L_04:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSA-03","text":"Finis sine vespera non potest tamquam ultimum momentum intra seriem concipi, quia pacem nondum possessam successione ipsa terminat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSA-06","CL_5P0L_05:BSA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSA-04","text":"Nullum extra causalitatem divinam datur ex quo subiectum esse, veritatem aut oppositionem substantialem accipiat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSA-02","CL_5P0L_05:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSA-05","text":"Prospectus creatus qui animam, tempus, Scripturam et intentionem divinam simul exhauriat constitutive praecluditur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSA-04","CL_5P0L_05:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSA-06","text":"Neutralitas attentionis et amoris indisponibilis est: omnis receptio aut ad fontem ordinatur aut medium in finem convertit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-08","CL_5P0L_05:BSA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:XD-01","text":"Dependentia ex nihilo ontologiam excedit atque in cognitione, voluntate et interpretatione recurrit, quia nulla operatio creaturae principium suum sufficiens continet.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:CGD-08","CL_5P0L_05:BAS-02","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-02","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-04","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:XD-02","text":"Informitas et distentio duas magnitudines carentiae unitatis propriae exhibent: prima capacitatem formationis, altera divisionem vitae iam formatae sed nondum collectae.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-07","CL_5P0L_05:GA-04","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-03","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:XD-03","text":"Tempus est simul effectus mutationis creatae et forma interior receptionis eius; ideo neque obiectivum receptaculum neque fictio privata est.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:MME-03","CL_5P0L_05:BSD-02","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:XD-04","text":"Memoria et Scriptura absentiam in praesentem efficaciam convertunt: una vestigia vitae, altera Verbum per verba temporalia operari facit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-04","CL_5P0L_05:GA-11","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-09","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:XD-05","text":"Caritas est forma superior attentionis, quia simul obiecta desiderii, sensus textus et opera communitatis ad finem communem dirigit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-08","CL_5P0L_05:XD-04","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-08","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:XD-06","text":"Confessio et exegesis sunt machinae correctionis recursivae: utrumque actum sub veritate ponit, falsam clausuram excludit et ampliorem receptionem aperit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GNX-01","CL_5P0L_05:ALT-B05","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-05","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:XD-07","text":"Gratia actionem creatam constituit, sed responsabilitas eiusdem actionis retinetur; dependentia et imputabilitas igitur cohaerent sine modo cooperationis plene formalizato.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-10","CL_5P0L_05:DBN-04","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:XD-08","text":"Verbum creatorium et Christus mediator unam directionem efficiunt: donatio essendi in vocationem formativam, reconciliationem mortalem et reditum ad iustitiam continuatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-12","CL_5P0L_05:GA-07","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-05","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:XD-09","text":"Multiplicitas est bifurcationis locus: a fonte et fine separata dispergit, sub unitate veritatis ordinata fecunditatem rerum et intellectuum constituit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:DBN-04","CL_5P0L_05:GA-10","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-10","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:XD-10","text":"Opera praesentia propriam obsolescentiam continent, quia sanationem incohant sed ad pacem et sabbatum quae successionem claudunt ordinantur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BAS-08","CL_5P0L_05:GA-13","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-07","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSD-01","text":"Asymmetria creationis et gratiae unam legem participationis generat: sicut esse donatur, ita sui cognitio, formatio et perseverantia recipiuntur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSD-05","CL_5P0L_05:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSD-02","text":"Subiectum est capacitas temporaliter distributa, cuius identitas ex appetitu, memoria, attentione, signis et orientatione amoris componitur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSD-01","CL_5P0L_05:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSD-03","text":"Historia non est successio neutralis, sed apparatus quo voluntas reformatur, opera transeunt et creatura ad statum non temporalem praeparatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSD-03","CL_5P0L_05:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSD-04","text":"Ecclesia exteriorizat collectionem interiorem, quia communitas confessionis, interpretatio et distributio mediorum eandem formationem quam animus recipit corporaliter exercent.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:CGD-09","CL_5P0L_05:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSD-05","text":"Pluralitas ontologica et pluralitas hermeneutica homologae fiunt: utraque capacitatem determinatam ad plures formas veras recipiendas praesupponit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:XD-01","CL_5P0L_05:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSD-06","text":"Malum ex agro substantiarum removetur et in directionem boni creati transfertur, qua attentio medium usurpat aut caritas illud ad fontem refert.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GNX-05","CL_5P0L_05:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSD-07","text":"Salus est reconfiguratio totius temporalitatis creatae, non fuga ab ea: mediatio successionem assumit, ordinat et ad requiem irreversibilem perducit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSD-06","CL_5P0L_05:RLE-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSD-08","text":"Cognitio participata certitudinem principii cum provisionalitate applicationis coniungit; veritas stabilis manet, dum intellectus et communitas corrigibilia sunt.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSD-07","CL_5P0L_05:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSD-09","text":"Aporia fit disciplina theologica positiva, quia ignorantia virium, temporis et causalitatis a simulatione comprehensionis ad confessionem dependentiae transfertur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:XD-10","CL_5P0L_05:DBN-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RLE-01","text":"Opacitas confessionem generat, confessio illuminationem petit, illuminatio ampliorem capacitatem aperit, et capacitas renovata novam confessionem requirit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RLE-01","CL_5P0L_05:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RLE-02","text":"Donum facultatem operandi constituit, operatio vulnus et receptivitatem manifestat, atque haec manifestatio receptionem ulterioris gratiae amplificat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RLE-04","CL_5P0L_05:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RLE-03","text":"Bonum creatum attentionem allicit; amor inordinatus illud in finem mutat; dispersio crescit; misericordia petita ordinem amoris instaurat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RLE-02","CL_5P0L_05:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RLE-04","text":"Sonus ad iudicium interius remittitur, iudicium Verbum quaerit, Verbum plures sensus veros aperit, et hi rursus examen caritatis postulant.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RLE-05","CL_5P0L_05:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RLE-05","text":"Interior formatio communitatem gignit, communitas ordinem creationis recapitulat, et recapitulatio conditionem interiorem sub ampliori historia iterum interpretatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:CGD-09","CL_5P0L_05:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RLE-06","text":"Pluralitas sensuum examen veritatis excitat; exclusio falsi concordiam caritatis format; concordia novam fecunditatem semanticam producit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:DBN-04","CL_5P0L_05:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RLE-07","text":"Exspectatio per attentionem in memoriam transit, transitus repetiti historiam formationis efficiunt, et historia desiderium suae consummationis auget.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RLE-03","CL_5P0L_05:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RLE-08","text":"Unitas divina est attractor recursivus intra tempus, sed requies sine vespera attractor terminalis est qui recursionem operum tandem claudit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RLE-07","CL_5P0L_05:RLE-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:FGS-B01","text":"Deus sibi sufficiens + creatio ex nihilo → dependentia universalis → impossibilitas autonomiae ontologicae et epistemicae.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-02","CL_5P0L_05:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:FGS-B02","text":"Capacitas nondum formata + vocatio Verbi → receptio formae → mutatio ordinata → tempus creatum.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:GA-04","CL_5P0L_05:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:FGS-B03","text":"Creatura temporalis + memoria + attentio + exspectatio → identitas distributa → distentio sive historia formationis.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSD-01","CL_5P0L_05:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:FGS-B04","text":"Signum exterior vel Scriptura → iudicium interius → sensus veri multiplices → exclusio falsi → concordia caritatis.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RLE-05","CL_5P0L_05:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:FGS-B05","text":"Bonum creatum + attentio inordinata → captatio → dispersio → confessio limitis → petitio illuminationis.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RLE-02","CL_5P0L_04:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:FGS-B06","text":"Gratia + mediatio + causalitas participativa → actio creata → collectio interior et ecclesialis → renovata capacitas receptionis.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-10","CL_5P0L_05:GA-14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:FGS-B07","text":"Opera temporalia + intentio ad unum → sanatio incohata → pax futura → sabbatum sine vespera.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BAS-08","CL_5P0L_05:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:AFM-B01","text":"Sufficientia divina → origo non chronologica → capacitas creata → vocatio formativa → mutationes ordinatae → tempus.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:BAS-04","CL_5P0L_05:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:AFM-B02","text":"Signa et vestigia → iudicium interius → opacitas et distentio → confessio → illuminatio → caritas → formatio communis.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BAS-04","CL_5P0L_05:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:AFM-B03","text":"Multiplicitas ordinata → opera temporalia → collectio ad unum → mediatio Christi → pax futura → requies sine vespera.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-11","CL_5P0L_05:RLE-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MME-01","text":"Dependentia ontologica fit tabula communis essendi, cognoscendi, volendi, interpretandi et perseverandi.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:CGD-08","CL_5P0L_05:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MME-02","text":"Interioritas ex spatio autonomiae in locum receptionis mutatur, ubi ontologia creaturae et disciplina interpretationis intersecantur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-05","CL_5P0L_05:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MME-03","text":"Tempus ex continente universali in effectum mutationis et distributionem praesentium operationum reclassificatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:MME-03","CL_5P0L_05:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MME-04","text":"Multiplicitas desinit esse aut pura dispersio aut error, quia ordo finis eam in fecunditatem ontologicam et hermeneuticam convertit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:DBN-04","CL_5P0L_05:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MME-05","text":"Auctoritas ex possessione sensus in ministerium corrigibile sub veritate et canone transfertur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GNX-04","CL_5P0L_05:MME-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MME-06","text":"Malum ex proprietate rerum in modum directionis reclassificatur, quo bonum creatum a fonte avertitur et attentionem captivam facit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:MME-04","CL_5P0L_05:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MME-07","text":"Ecclesia fit extensio historica formationis interioris et locus ubi grammatica creationis per signa, ministeria et intellectus recapitulari potest.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:CGD-09","CL_5P0L_05:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MME-08","text":"Bonitas temporalium non ex perpetuitate eorum, sed ex transitu ordinato ad fruitionem et requiem aestimatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GNX-08","CL_5P0L_05:MME-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ALT-B01","text":"Gradus superficiei confessionem, memoriam, tentationem, creationem, verba Geneseos, Ecclesiam et sabbatum tamquam obiecta distincta proponit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:ALT-B01","CL_5P0L_05:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ALT-B02","text":"Gradus structuralis capacitatem, memoriam, attentionem, formam, mutationem, caritatem et gratiam in machinam receptionis atque collectionis componit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:ALT-B02","CL_5P0L_05:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ALT-B03","text":"Gradus metastrategicus certamen de autonomia vel sensu unico in disciplinam dependentiae, pluralitatis verae et auctoritatis corrigibilis transfert.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:ALT-B03","CL_5P0L_05:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ALT-B04","text":"Gradus ontologicus et temporalis Deum ut causam aeternam, creaturam ut receptionem mutabilem et historiam ut ordinem formationis constituit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:ALT-B04","CL_5P0L_05:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ALT-B05","text":"Gradus methodologicus et performativus reditu, variatione et negatione efficit quod affirmat: lectorem a dispersione ad intentionem et a clausura ad corrigibilitatem transfert.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:ALT-B05","CL_5P0L_05:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:FL-01","text":"Tempus oscillat inter affectionem animi, effectum mutationis et medium historiae salutis; relatio ontologica horum trium statuum non plene solvitur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:FL-03","CL_5P0L_05:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:FL-02","text":"Actus aeternus successionem creatam producit, sed transitus ab origine non chronologica ad effectus ordinatos formalizationi resistit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:FL-03","CL_5P0L_05:BAS-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:FL-03","text":"Gratia omnem facultatem bonam constituit, dum voluntas responsabilitatem retinet; nexus causalitatis participativae et imputabilitatis incompletus manet.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:FL-05","CL_5P0L_05:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:FL-04","text":"Veritas interior criterium certum praebet subiecto opaco, dum auctoritas ecclesialis participata et corrigibilis idem iudicium socialiter distribuit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:FL-02","CL_5P0L_05:CGD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:FL-05","text":"Pluralitas sensuum auctoritate, Spiritu et caritate limitatur, sed regula plena compatibilitatis inter sensus veros non exhibetur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:FL-05","CL_5P0L_05:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:FL-06","text":"Analogia inter informitatem et distentionem fecunda est, sed conflationem capacitatis ontologicae cum culpa morali minatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:MP-02","CL_5P0L_05:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:FL-07","text":"Mediatio Christi cum Verbo creatorio structuram globalem claudit, quamquam necessitas huius coniunctionis ex phaenomenologia temporis sola non deducitur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:FL-06","CL_5P0L_04:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:FL-08","text":"Creatura naturaliter mutabilis manet, sed requies terminalis reditum mutationis excludit; modus stabilizationis sine abolitione naturae fragilis est.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:FL-02","CL_5P0L_05:MP-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MP-01","text":"Informitas mutatur ex capacitate privativa in figuram aversionis, deinde cum distentione tamquam indigentia collectionis coniungitur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:MP-01","CL_5P0L_04:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MP-02","text":"Attentio mutatur ex mensura successionis in intentionem normativam, quae sub caritate etiam interpretationem et motum ontologicum regit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:MP-03","CL_5P0L_05:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MP-03","text":"Memoria mutatur ex operatione retinendi in exemplar mediationis, quod Scriptura et communitas ad praesentiam Verbi amplificant.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:MP-01","CL_5P0L_05:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MP-04","text":"Tempus mutatur ex mensuratione transitus interioris in intervallum pedagogicum fidei, actionis et institutionis communis.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSD-02","CL_5P0L_05:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MP-05","text":"Requies mutatur ex directione stabilizante vitae praesentis in transformationem terminalem quae omnia opera temporalia claudit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:MP-04","CL_5P0L_05:MP-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:HSI-01","text":"Realitas est machina donationis et conversionis circa centrum immutabile, in qua dependentiae mutabiles formam, directionem et quietem recipiunt.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:HSI-01","CL_5P0L_05:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:HSI-02","text":"Subiectum est nodus receptivus et porosus, cuius unitas ex memoria, attentione, appetitu, signis et pondere amoris efficitur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:HSI-02","CL_5P0L_05:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:HSI-03","text":"Tempus est simul fluvius transitus et officina formationis, inter originem sine successione et requiem sine vespera extensum.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:HSI-03","CL_5P0L_05:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:HSI-04","text":"Memoria et Scriptura sunt duae superficies prismaticae quibus absentia non removetur, sed in vestigium, sensum et praesentem operationem refringitur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:MME-02","CL_5P0L_05:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:HSI-05","text":"Navigatio possibilis non est fuga a conditione creata, sed directio attentionis et amoris per confessionem, Verbum, gratiam et mediatorem.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:HSI-05","CL_5P0L_05:HSI-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MRT-B01","text":"Axiomata praesentia sufficiunt ad restituendam machinam quae creationem, interioritatem, tempus, interpretationem, Ecclesiam et requiem sub una lege participationis coordinat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B01","CL_5P0L_05:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MRT-B02","text":"Structura firmissima est asymmetria inter Deum sibi sufficientem et creaturam cui esse, veritas, actio, unitas et quies donantur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B02","CL_5P0L_05:MRT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MRT-B03","text":"Nondum satis determinantur relatio temporis ad affectionem animi, status informitatis et causalitas qua actus aeternus successionem producit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B03","CL_5P0L_05:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MRT-B04","text":"Regula plena discernendi sensus multiplices et traducendi ordinem creationis in Ecclesiam axiomaticae reductioni adhuc resistit.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B07","CL_5P0L_05:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MRT-B05","text":"Coordinatio gratiae, actionis et responsabilitatis cohaeret ut postulatum systemicum, sed nondum in formulam causalem completam redigitur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B04","CL_5P0L_05:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MRT-B06","text":"Pons inter Verbum creatorium et mediationem Christi clausuram globalem sustinet, quamvis praemissis revelatis atque analogia plus quam deductione interna nitatur.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B05","CL_5P0L_05:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:MRT-B07","text":"Restitutio motum verum servat si dependentiam, recursionem, pluralitatem ordinatam et terminalem requiem retinet, neque imagines memoriae, informitatis et sabbati in identitatem complanat.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:MRT-B08","CL_5P0L_05:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"la","language_name":"Latina","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261016T142810176965Z_3752f823","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"5P0L L1 02","source_sha256":"6edf688e8a27ec6791c3d2a36a0aa357d77708c0d0cffb887ed230a3733db34e","sha256":"f517c442e477d4a955b8956b6621d4346c5841713e6ec730979bf8eced40e24d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-16T14:28:10.179058+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ASP-01","text":"The system asks how a creature opaque to itself, mutable and temporal, receives a pretemporal origin, the truth of itself, and a direction toward rest.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BAS-01","CL_5P0L_05:BAS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ASP-02","text":"The global thesis places all knowledge, formation, action, and rest under the asymmetry of divine donation: the creature receives what it cannot produce from itself.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BAS-02","CL_5P0L_05:BAS-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ASP-03","text":"The argument joins apophatic confession with metaphysical, hermeneutical, and ecclesial reconstruction, so that ontological dependence may be explained in the discipline of temporal reception.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BAS-03","CL_5P0L_05:BAS-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ASP-04","text":"The movement proceeds from a non-chronological origin through signs, interiority, and succession, then transcends interiority toward the Word, the formed community, and the eternal end.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BAS-04","CL_5P0L_05:BAS-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ASP-05","text":"The progression is spiral: every illumination opens a new opacity, and every formation retrospectively reconstitutes origin and end from a new perspective.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BAS-05","CL_5P0L_05:BAS-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ASP-06","text":"Dispersion and formlessness are non-identical modes of lacking proper unity; charity, intention, and the Word convert them into formation without abolishing plurality.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BAS-06","CL_5P0L_05:BAS-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ASP-07","text":"Time becomes at once the medium of the wound and of formation: within it attention is dispersed, gifts are received, works are performed, and the creature is ordered toward its own transcendence of time.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSD-02","CL_5P0L_05:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:ASP-08","text":"Present closure is always deferred, but the delay is not infinite: peace not yet possessed is terminally gathered into the Sabbath without evening.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BAS-08","CL_5P0L_05:BAS-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] The immutable God is neither contained by time nor perfected by creation, but remains the measure of truth and the source of all formation.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-01","CL_5P0L_05:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The creature, made from nothing, possesses in itself neither the cause of being nor the principle of knowledge, order, or perseverance.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-02","CL_5P0L_05:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Mutability passes from the ontological capacity to receive form to succession, the distention of the subject, and the history of common formation.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-13","CL_5P0L_05:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] The creature is a receptive capacity to which effected unity is given; interiority, formless matter, and ecclesial life exhibit diverse degrees of this receptivity.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-05","CL_5P0L_05:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Interior truth and the uncreated Word transcend the subject, judge its errors, and call dispersed capacity to form.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RMD-03","CL_5P0L_05:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Interiority changes from a site of self-examination into the joint of ontology and hermeneutics, where the creature's opacity encounters the judgment of truth.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-06","CL_5P0L_05:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Time is a created mode of reception and passage: it arises from changes, is measured by the operations of the mind, and sustains the history of formation.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:MME-03","CL_5P0L_05:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] Unity in God through charity is the attractor that gathers attention, loves, meanings, and works without destroying created diversity.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-11","CL_5P0L_05:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Memory and Scripture are temporal mediations through which absence becomes operative: the past is present through trace, the eternal Word through humble speech.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RMD-02","CL_5P0L_05:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-10","text":"[Persistent] Created goods and multiplicity are positive, but a means turned into an end produces dispersion, whereas relation to the source constitutes the goodness of the whole.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-09","CL_5P0L_05:GA-15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Confession and interpretation do not merely report truth already possessed, but performatively reform affection, understanding, and community under truth.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-03","CL_5P0L_05:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-12","text":"[Persistent] Grace and divine causality do not suppress finite action, but participatively constitute the capacity to know, will, and act.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-10","CL_5P0L_05:GA-14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-13","text":"[Emergent] The creative principle of the Word and the mediation of Christ constitute one axis through which the creature is called into being, reformed, and directed through mortality toward justice.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-12","CL_5P0L_05:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-14","text":"[Terminal] Peace not yet present and the Sabbath without evening constitute one eschatological closure, in which works pass away and succession is not renewed.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSA-06","CL_5P0L_05:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-15","text":"[Attractor] True unity is not univocity or empty simplicity, but the order of many under one source, one truth, and one end.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:DBN-04","CL_5P0L_05:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-01","text":"Creation from nothing retains a stable identity, but is amplified from a cosmological proposition into a law of epistemic, moral, and ecclesial dependence.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:CGD-08","CL_5P0L_05:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-02","text":"Immutable truth remains the measure, but its role extends from interior judgment to the formative calling of the creator Word.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RMD-03","CL_5P0L_05:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-03","text":"Memory migrates from an interior archive into temporal mediation, to which Scripture responds as the community's medium toward the eternal Word.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RMD-02","CL_5P0L_05:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-04","text":"Dispersion and formlessness do not fulfill the same function, but recurrently designate a capacity that does not possess unity from itself and needs formation.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-07","CL_5P0L_05:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-05","text":"Attention changes from the faculty of measuring into the direction of love, then in charity acquires a hermeneutical norm and ontological weight.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-08","CL_5P0L_05:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-06","text":"The judgment of truth migrates from confession of interior movements to exegesis of multiple meanings, while preserving the correction of affection and understanding.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:XD-05","CL_5P0L_05:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-07","text":"The present changes from a moral instant to be examined into the pedagogical medium of history, through which form is received, exercised, and handed over to memory.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RMD-07","CL_5P0L_05:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-08","text":"Mediation is amplified from the reconciliation of the sinner to the universal structure of origin, formation, and temporal direction.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RMD-06","CL_5P0L_05:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-09","text":"Multiplicity reverses its force: without one end it is dispersive, but under unity of source it produces the fecundity of things and understandings.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:DBN-04","CL_5P0L_05:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:RMD-10","text":"The delay of peace undergoes terminal transformation, as rest passes from participated stability into the irreversible end of all succession.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BAS-08","CL_5P0L_05:MP-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:CGD-01","text":"Taxonomies of memory and the question of formless matter remain local; only the structure of capacity that receives trace or form ascends.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:CGD-01","CL_5P0L_05:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:CGD-02","text":"The threefold desire and correspondences of individual days are lower mechanisms; the present level retains the law of distributing attention and means according to capacity.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:CGD-02","CL_5P0L_05:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:CGD-03","text":"Creation from nothing and the priority of origin without interval are amplified into a universal principle of non-autonomous causality.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:CGD-08","CL_5P0L_05:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:CGD-04","text":"Aporias concerning the length of the present and the order of change remain locally, but together demonstrate that time is neither a receptacle nor full self-possession.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:CGD-03","CL_5P0L_05:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:CGD-05","text":"Interior judgment and hermeneutical plurality join the lower levels, because meanings are received multiply but subjected to truth above the interpreter.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GNX-04","CL_5P0L_05:GNX-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:CGD-06","text":"The community of confession and ecclesial recapitulation constitute the transition of the present level, by which interior formation is externalized into an interpreting and exercising body.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:CGD-09","CL_5P0L_05:CGD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:CGD-07","text":"Anti-Donatist polemic and the refutation of celestial cycles recede after performing their local work, but their exclusion of autonomous judgment and created measure persists.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:RMD-10","CL_5P0L_04:CGD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:CGD-08","text":"Christ the mediator and the creative Word do not remain regional conclusions, but effect the greater bridge between the donation of being and the reformation of life.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-12","CL_5P0L_05:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:CGD-09","text":"Doubts concerning temporal affection and the state of formless matter preserve lower limits; the synthesis coordinates them but does not resolve them into one exhaustive ontology.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:FL-03","CL_5P0L_05:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GNX-01","text":"No creature can be its own cause, measure, illuminator, or consummator.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:DBN-01","CL_5P0L_05:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GNX-02","text":"Neither matter nor time nor mind nor any other substance can be posited as coeternal with God or independent of his causality.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSA-03","CL_5P0L_05:GNX-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GNX-03","text":"God is neither contained by memory nor deliberates, changes, or is completed through created works temporally.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GNX-03","CL_5P0L_05:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GNX-04","text":"Interiority provides neither self-transparency nor an exhaustive view of truth.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GNX-02","CL_5P0L_05:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GNX-05","text":"Multiplicity neither produces order of itself nor is simply equivalent to falsity; univocity and indiscriminate license are equally excluded.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:DBN-04","CL_5P0L_05:GNX-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GNX-06","text":"Mediation is not an impediment to be overcome by autonomous ascent, but a necessary mode of formation within mortality, signs, and degrees of capacity.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSA-05","CL_5P0L_05:DBN-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GNX-07","text":"Body, matter, time, and sensible goods are not evil substances, but neither are they ultimate ends or self-governing principles.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GNX-05","CL_5P0L_05:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:GNX-08","text":"No closure within the mortal state, nor the perpetuation of temporal works, constitutes the creature's consummation.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GNX-08","CL_5P0L_05:GNX-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:DBN-01","text":"Divine causality and created action cannot be explained by a competitive relation, because dependence on gift constitutes finite operation itself.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSD-05","CL_5P0L_05:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:DBN-02","text":"Divine immutability cannot signify inertia, although eternal act produces successive effects without change in itself.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-01","CL_5P0L_05:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:DBN-03","text":"Succession cannot contain the divine cause or narrate its will, but only the mode in which created effects are received.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:DBN-03","CL_5P0L_05:DBN-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:DBN-04","text":"Unity cannot require the complete identity of parts, because the system coheres only if true plurality subsists under an undivided source.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:XD-07","CL_5P0L_05:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:DBN-05","text":"Truth is neither produced nor terminated by interior affection or the conscious intention of a human minister.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:DBN-02","CL_5P0L_05:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:DBN-06","text":"Introspection, analysis of time, and mediation of signs cannot be converted into immediate ascent to immutability.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:DBN-07","CL_5P0L_05:DBN-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:DBN-07","text":"The homology between distention, formlessness, and formation does not by itself demonstrate the necessity of a mediator or the translation of all creation into the Church.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:FL-06","CL_5P0L_05:FL-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSA-01","text":"Radically unavailable is the possibility of a creature that possesses itself wholly at once and has stability from its own nature.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSA-01","CL_5P0L_05:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSA-02","text":"Origin before time can neither be represented in chronological order nor explained through anything coeternal with God.","refs":["CL_5P0L_05:BSA-01","CL_5P0L_04:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSA-03","text":"The end without evening cannot be conceived as a final moment within a series, because it terminates succession itself with peace not yet possessed.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSA-06","CL_5P0L_05:BSA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSA-04","text":"There is no outside divine causality from which the subject might receive being, truth, or substantial opposition.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSA-02","CL_5P0L_05:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSA-05","text":"A created perspective that exhausts soul, time, Scripture, and divine intention simultaneously is constitutively precluded.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:BSA-04","CL_5P0L_05:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:BSA-06","text":"The neutrality of attention and love is unavailable: every reception is either ordered to the source or turns a means into an end.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-08","CL_5P0L_05:BSA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:XD-01","text":"Dependence from nothing exceeds ontology and recurs in knowledge, will, and interpretation, because no operation of the creature contains its sufficient principle.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:CGD-08","CL_5P0L_05:BAS-02","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-02","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-04","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:XD-02","text":"Formlessness and distention exhibit two magnitudes of the lack of proper unity: the former, capacity for formation; the latter, the division of a life already formed but not yet gathered.","refs":["CL_5P0L_04:GA-07","CL_5P0L_05:GA-04","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-03","MC_5P0L_L1_02:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_5P0L_L1_02:XD-03","text":"Time is at once the effect of created change and the inter